[2812]={"Campeón de Maethad","Has reclamado una de las mazas de Ronkûrz","Lleva la maza de Ronkûrz a Hwati","'¡Maravilloso, lo has logrado! Has demostrado ser ${PLAYERNAME:un guerrero[m]|una guerrera[f]} resistente, lo cual es bueno, porque el mayor desafío aún te espera: derrotar al maestro de Maethad.'","'¡Hemos tenido suerte! Mientras estabas fuera, un enano explorador regresó y nos dijo que vio a Ronkûrz entrando en el campamento orco de Mor Maudhúl. Sin duda ha ido allí para entrenar a los Uruks, pero al estar lejos de la arena, ¡queda vulnerable!\
\
'Espera, espera, me estoy adelantando. Permíteme explicarte mi plan. Verás, para acabar verdaderamente con la amenaza de Maethad, debemos derrotar a su maestro, un Gorthorog llamado \\qKhurrákh.\\q Khurrákh rara vez se muestra, y solo lucha contra quienes considera dignos de su atención. Ronkûrz, otro Gorthorog y actual campeón de Maethad, es su alumno más preciado. Si lo derrotaras y reclamases una de sus mazas, ¡Khurrákh tendría que enfrentarse a ti!\
\
'Mor Maudhúl se encuentra al norte de aquí, al otro lado del lago corrompido en Duvuinen. Ronkûrz debería estar en algún lugar del campamento. ¡Apresúrate!'","Reclama una de las mazas de Ronkûrz","Ronkûrz, el campeón de Maethad, puede encontrarse entrenando Uruks en el campamento orco de Mor Maudhúl, al norte de Gabilshathûr, al otro lado del lago en Duvuinen.\
\
Una vez que hayas reclamado una de las mazas de Ronkûrz, llévala de regreso a Hwati en Gabilshathûr.","Hwati te dijo que para acabar verdaderamente con la amenaza de Maethad, debes derrotar a su maestro, Khurrákh. Sin embargo, este Gorthorog solo luchará contigo si demuestras ser ${PLAYERNAME:digno[m]|digna[f]} de su atención.","'Si queremos acabar con la amenaza de Maethad, debemos derrotar a su maestro, Khurrákh. Sin embargo, para hacerlo salir, debemos derrotar a su alumno más preciado, Ronkûrz, y reclamar una de sus mazas.\
\
'Ronkûrz se encuentra al norte, en el campamento orco de Mor Maudhúl, que está al otro lado del lago corrompido en Duvuinen.'"},
[2813]={"Valthor te ha convocado para continuar tu entrenamiento como ${PLAYERNAME:Campeón[m]|Campeona[f]}.","Campeón: Camino del Campeón Marcial","Valthor está acampado en las Fundaciones de Piedra, en Moria.\
\
Se te ha ordenado buscar la guía del campeón Valthor.","'Bien ${PLAYER:hallado, amigo[m]|hallada, amiga[f]}.\
\
'Debes ser ${PLAYER}. Te estaba esperando.\
\
'Vamos, hablemos un poco. Estoy seguro de que hay mucho que puedo enseñarte.'","Habla con Valthor en las Fundaciones de Piedra","Valthor te ha convocado.","'Según todos los informes, Valthor fue visto por última vez en las Fundaciones de Piedra, en Moria.'"},
[2814]={"Reúnete con Gwesgylliel para recibir más entrenamiento de campeón","Como campeón, has alcanzado tal renombre que has recibido una convocatoria de Gwesgylliel en Lin Giliath, en Meluinen.\
\
Debes buscar a Gwesgylliel para recibir más entrenamiento en tu clase.","Gwesgylliel está en Lin Giliath en Meluinen en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Te han dicho que la doncella elfa Gwesgylliel, ella misma una poderosa campeona, desea hablar contigo.","Las historias de tu audacia se han difundido por todas las tierras de la Tierra Media, y eres ${PLAYERNAME:conocido como un poderoso campeón[m]|conocida como una poderosa campeona[f]} en todas las posadas del camino.","Campeón: El camino más audaz es la disciplina","'Me complace conocerte al fin, ${PLAYER}, pues tus hazañas viajan por delante de ti y hablan bien de tu buen corazón y tu fuerte brazo. Nuestros actos traen esperanza a quienes no tienen ninguna, y ese es el mayor regalo que se puede dar.'"},
[2816]={"Find Gadda at the abandoned farm","'It is terrible, just terrible! Stanric has died! He was healthy as could be, and on a mission to improve things, and for a time things were getting better.\
\
'The men who had supported Sithric slowly began to change their favour...until suddenly, in the dead of night last night, Stanric -- he is gone!\
\
'Gadda has committed treason and abandoned his post here, and Sithric vows to arrest him and those who went with him on sight. They have set up an outpost at the abandoned farm. Gadda wishes very much to speak with you!'","Gadda and a small handful of men loyal to Stanric have escaped Stangard and set up camp at the little farmstead where you planted some hopeful seeds.\
\
You should find Gadda at the abandoned farm in the east of Eorlsmead.","Change for the Worst","You have returned to Stangard to hear some dire news from your friend Sabert at the gate.","'${PLAYER}! You received my message; that is the only good that has come of this mess! You are truly welcome here, my friend.\
\
'Stanric is dead, and I cannot believe it was an accident. He was as healthy a man that ever walked, and Sithric will not give particulars on how he died.\
\
'I suspect treachery, so I escaped while I could. Tatwine and one other came with me....'"},
[2817]={"'I have noticed nothing unusual, though the lands beyond this gate can be dangerous at times. \
\
'Rohirrim and Dunlending roots run deep through Woodhurst, and the lands ahead have the strongest Dunlending influence. Those who live beyond here do not keep hidden their wishes that the Stonedeans were part of Dunland.\
\
'With tensions rising, it would be wise for Rohirrim and their supporters to avoid that place.'","'You have come just in time...you just missed a party of men that I believe are up to no good. They appeared to be following one of the stable-hands at this stable, and they followed him around the corner. He has not come back, and I am worried that they might have hurt or killed him.\
\
'His heritage is mainly Rohirrim, and the party following him were trouble-makers from the lower part of the city. Please check on him.'","Talk to Thurferth, Captain of the Guard","Thurferth suggested other guards posted around the city may be able to help.","'Not many come and go through this gate these days. Occasionally, a waggon of supplies is sent to Brockbridge to aid in their defence; otherwise, it is rather quiet here.\
\
'Smoke rises in the distance and looks to be coming from south of Brockbridge. I worry for that fair town and for our leaders, Herubrand and Herefara, who went to aid in its defence.'","Thurferth is near the centre of Woodhurst.\
\
You should tell Thurferth of what you learned from the guards around town.","'Nothing suspicious happens around this gate. Farmers are busy tending the fields, and two Rohirrim left recently with their waggon packed.\
\
'You are looking for the two who once guarded the Mead Hall? I was good friends with them, but not after what they did. I never wish to speak ill of friends, but they swore off their duty to those they were pledged to protect. And if the rumours are true, good people lost their lives because of it. \
\
'They can usually be found at the inn nearby.'","Talk to guards around Woodhurst and investigate anything suspicious (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Changing of the Guard","'The two men I entrusted with the protection of the Mead Hall are gone. They have not been seen for days, and we assumed they had left for the war, for riches elsewhere, or both.\
\
'I have seen nothing suspicious, but I have orders to give and may not have noticed. The guards around town may have more to offer.'","'I cannot understand why Elda will not trust you. I believe he is concerned for me. He was my father's advisor and is set in his ways. But I am a good judge of character, and you seem trustworthy.\
\
'Arnwi's observation is troubling, and we should be careful not to divulge too much information to the guards. Please speak with Thurferth, Captain of the Guard, about the two men posted at the Mead Hall, and if they have seen anything suspicious lately.'","'There has been nothing suspicious here. They go about their duty, but the miners are tense with worry about war being so close by. \
\
'The Rohirrim seem to be losing this war, and some believe the Stonedeans are better suited to separate from Rohan -- that it should be ruled by its own people and not some fallen king from a far-off land -- while some believe that we should throw in with the Dunlendings and ally with the White Hand.'","Thurferth is near the centre of Woodhurst.\
\
Herubrand told you to speak with Thurferth, Captain of the Guard, about the two men posted at the Mead Hall and whether they have seen anything unusual.","'The two were bribed to leave their post? That is unacceptable. I will inform the others that they should be arrested on sight.\
\
'Loyalty is not what it once was. We are sworn to protect the people...and most of all the Reeve. They were my most trusted men and were posted at the Reeve's door. I will not soon forget this betrayal.'","'Nay, I have seen naught out of the ordinary. With Herubrand gone for Brockbridge, the door is locked and nobody has been up here until you came. It is too quiet up here. I miss my old post.\
\
'I once was stationed down near the mine where I could listen to some of the men talk about their distrust of Rohirrim and that Herubrand was a fool to support them.\
\
'There are terrible rumours about the Rohirrim going around.'","The Mead Hall was attacked by men from Woodhurst for an unknown cause. The Reeve's advisors have worked to keep the attack a secret to help maintain peace."},
[2820]={"'We set forth to reestablish contact with the leader of the canaries in Umbar Baharbêl, but we were ill-prepared. Missteps and affronts to changes in custom abound. Many of our names are etched in their ledgers, and I know they are not written there because of our heroism.\
\
'Through this archway to the east, I saw a sea-hawk perched atop a roof. That is a courier, I am sure of it! Every day, that bird arrives and perches there looking for something. I have seen a scrap of paper affixed to its leg! It likely seeks the eagle that used to watch this outpost, and has a message to deliver.\
\
'I cannot approach it without drawing attention to me, but you have committed no offence and breached no customs. You can act as our eagle here.\
\
'Coax the bird from its perch and obtain that scrap, then return to me.'","The sea-hawk swoops down and enjoys the dinner. Now is your chance!","'Ah, thank you for this, friend! The fall of the Heirs and the rise of the Kindred diminished Achardis's capacity to gather information, yet she persists, and still she awaits requests from us. This bird network of hers... she calls them the Watchers on the Wing.'\
\
He produces a small note and hands it to you.\
\
'We need to send this message back to her. Bind the message to the sea-hawk's leg; it will do the rest. Return to me after the Watcher on the Wing has left.'","The Watcher on the Wing waits dutifully for you to give it a message to bring back to Achardis. Bring the note and tie it to her leg so she may return it to the Order of the Eagle's leader in Umbar Baharbêl.","Speak with Harthabor","Retrieve the message from the sea-hawk","'The threat of the Kindred of the Coins cannot remain unknown. After the fall of the Mâkhda Dahak-'\
\
He shakes his head.\
\
'Forgive me. I am Harthabor, and you should call that place Mâkhda Khorbo, my friend. My folly was not using the local vernacular. Do better than me.'\
\
He begins again.\
\
'After the fall of the Mâkhda Khorbo and the Heirs of Castamir, whispers and warnings from eagles throughout Umbar ceased. Worse, we lost contact with our leader in Umbar City.'\
\
He stops and shakes his head again.\
\
'The citizens call it Umbar Baharbêl, and so should you.\
\
'Can you see why I need your aid?'","Pick up a scrap of meat from the plaza near the sea-hawk","The flat stone on the rampart to the north-east may prove a suitable place to lure the sea-hawk from its perch.","'Now, my friend, we wait. I thank you. Your effort and attention averted the disaster, or worse, that my folly would have wrought.\
\
'I hope to see you again soon.'","'I am sure there is a way to draw the bird down from that height so you can take the message it carries.'","Deliver the message to Harthabor at Jax Phanâl","You gently remove the paper tied to its leg. The sea-hawk does not seem to mind, and in fact appears to be very comfortable exchanging the information for the delicious dinner you set before it.","The sea-hawk flies away over the ramparts, bearing the message","Chapter 1 - The Eyes and Ears of the City","The sea-hawk sits atop a roof through the archway and east of Harthabor in Jax Phanâl. Find a method to draw the bird down, collect its message, and return it to the agent.","'That's the Watcher on the Wing. She's a vigilant bird. She perches at that spot each day she's here. Nary moves unless it's for a scrap of food or a shiny bauble. She's lovely though, isn't she?'","Concern over the new powers in control of Umbar and their potential relationship to the Haradrim or the Church of the All-Seeing cause the Order of the Eagle to maintain watch over threats from Umbar Baharbêl.","Attach the message to the sea-hawk courier","'That sea-hawk? We call her Watcher on the Wing. She's oft up there waiting for a scrap of meat to fall off a careless plate. She doesn't care much what kind of meat it is. She's harmless, as birds go.'","Harthabor is need of assistance to contact his leader in Umbar Baharbêl. Speak with him to learn more.","Perhaps this scrap of meat will entice the sea-hawk from its perch?","The bird is away. Harthabor awaits your return in Jax Phanâl. Go to the agent and inform him that all went well.","Harthabor is waiting to see the message you retrieved.","Place the scrap of meat on the flat stone to the north-east","The sea-hawk looks up expectantly, and you fasten the return message to its leg.","You drew the bird down from its perch and should now remove the message from its leg."},
[2821]={"'My friend! I want to thank you for accompanying Legolas and Gimli on their scouting mission. As you can see, I have at last prevailed at court and now my tour of the kingdom can begin.'\
\
You lower your voice and tell the King what you learned about the Heirs of Castamir and the Kindred of the Coins, concluding at last with the worrisome news that someone near to the King may secretly support the Heirs. He dismisses your worry with a wave.\
\
'I am not troubled by this news, ${PLAYER}. I have brought only those I trust with me on this tour, including my most capable bodyguard.'\
\
You tell Elessar that you already spoke with Legolas and Gimli outside, and he smiles.\
\
'I speak of another, my friend. You will find my fiercest bodyguard somewhere outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, near the top of Imloth Melui.'","King Elessar's most trusted bodyguard greets you with a warm smile.","'I have not heard a song by that name, but songs of every sort have a mysterious power, both upon the singer and upon those who hear them. One of the heralds who travels with the company is a minstrel of some repute; perhaps she has heard this song. Líniel is her name, and she should be outside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui.'","'The riddle proved quite easy in the end, ${PLAYER}. Why should I remain behind in Minas Tirith while my husband sees his kingdom? Is it not now my kingdom also? Any who think to do him harm must first consider the daughter of Elrond, and to those who believe her to be defenceless, I say only this: beware!'\
\
You ask Arwen if she knows anything about a \\qSong of Waves and Wind,\\q and the Queen thinks for a moment.\
\
'I have not heard a song by that name, ${PLAYER}, but songs of every sort have a mysterious power, both upon the singer and upon those who hear them. One of the heralds who travels with the company is a minstrel of some repute; perhaps she has heard this song. Líniel is her name, and she should be outside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui.'","Chapter 1.10: Inside Every Shadow","'I do not speak of Legolas or Gimli. You will find my fiercest bodyguard somewhere outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, near the top of Imloth Melui.'","'I have heard his travelling party will be quite large, so it will take him some time to arrive. The person with whom I spoke said the King intended to first visit Imloth Melui, if you cannot wait for him to reach Linhir.'","Talk to King Elessar's most trusted bodyguard","Legolas and Gimli have come with King Elessar's travelling party to Imloth Melui.","King Elessar told you to find his trusted bodyguard somewhere outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.","'We know little or nothing about this Kindred of the Coins, and that does worry me.'","King Elessar is inside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.","'We returned to Minas Tirith and told the King what we discovered, ${PLAYER}: that the Heirs of Castamir still have their supporters, but Balakhôr himself is likely dead and no leader has the strength to replace him. Those tidings were enough to convince Elessar that his tour of the kingdom could safely proceed.\
\
'But now you tell us there is another group who wishes Gondor ill? He is not going to turn around now, ${PLAYER}.'","'The Song of Waves and Wind? I suppose there are a number of melodies to which that name could apply, but I confess to you that nothing comes at once to mind. I hope I have not disappointed Queen Arwen!\
\
'I will keep my ears attentive as the King tours Gondor, ${PLAYER}. Will you be joining us? I hope you will. The travelling company is a large one, but there will always be room for a friend of the King and Queen such as you, and you a hero in your own right, besides! None will think to threaten them while you stand near.'\
\
You thank Líniel for her time, and wonder if she is right.","According to Pethanar, the gossipmonger of Linhir, King Elessar's travelling party will have reached Imloth Melui by now.","Talk to King Elessar inside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui","Find King Elessar's trusted bodyguard somewhere outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos","'You have returned from your mission of secrecy, ${PLAYER}! What befell you while you walked among the ranks of the enemy?'\
\
You tell Legolas about your experience with the supporters of the Heirs of Castamir and about their conflict with Nakási and Tumúldo, emissaries from the Kindred of the Coins.\
\
'I do not grieve to hear that supporters of the Heirs perished as a result of their own treachery, but they were a known danger and I feel we could manage them easily. We know little or nothing about this Kindred of the Coins, and that does worry me.'","You have found Elessar's most trusted bodyguard","The gossipmonger spoke true: King Elessar's travelling party has come to Imloth Melui","Travel to the entrance of Imloth Melui in King's Gondor","You learned from a gossipmonger in Linhir that King Elessar has begun to tour his kingdom, and indeed has already departed Minas Tirith!","Talk to Legolas at the entrance to Imloth Melui","Talk to Líniel outside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui","Líniel is outside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui.","'Now you tell us there is another group who wishes Gondor ill? The King is not going to turn around now.'","Talk to Gimli at the entrance to Imloth Melui"},
[2822]={"'We have come to the South-gate of the Rammas Echor, through which lies the Harlond, the south-harbour of Minas Tirith. It was held by Orcs of Mordor during the war, and they did not expect the arrival of Elessar aboard the ships of the Corsairs!'\
\
Legolas smiles.\
\
'They did not expect Legolas Greenleaf or Gimli, son of Glóin, either. That much was clear to all!'","Talk to Gimli north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor","Talk to Legolas north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor","Talk to Glindor in Minas Tirith (Midsummer) and go with him to see King Elessar","'My feet are sore already, ${PLAYER}, and we have come to just the first of the places Aragorn told us to visit. His kingdom is larger than it looks on the maps, and Legolas and I have already crossed it once!'\
\
Gimli falls silent.\
\
'I named him Aragorn again, didn't I? He will have as many names as a Wizard next, but he has been a trusted companion through many adventures, and for that I will learn them all.\
\
'He is not the king of any other kingdoms, is he?'","Chapter 1.1: A King Should See His Kingdom","Glindor, King Elessar's herald, is outside the stables in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","'It is to the Tower of Ecthelion we go, there to audience with King Elessar and Queen Arwen, the rulers of victorious Gondor.'","Legolas is north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor.","'There will be fewer Orcs to fight inside the Harlond this time, I wager.'","King Elessar, recently crowned and newly wedded, is eager to heal the hurts of his kingdom and to move Gondor into an age of prosperity.","'A king has returned to Gondor, ${PLAYER}, and all the kingdom celebrates! And yet he is not content to rest on the laurels of his deserved victory over Sauron.\
\
'I was instructed to bring you to see him. Will you come with me?'","Gimli is north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor."},
[2823]={"Talk to Mithrandir just inside the ruin of the Black Gate","Defeat foes in Udûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Rhogrin at Mornaur, in western Udûn","'I must urge caution! Many of the artifacts that might be found within Mordor will be wholly evil, or corrupted beyond any use by good folk. Most of these adventurers do not know the first thing about dealing with such fell entrapments!\
\
'Speak to them, ${PLAYER}, and try to dissuade them from such hasty courses. Or at least give them these warnings, so they will not blunder into their fates all unawares! After they are duly-warned, you should journey ahead and see what foes await us in Udûn. Look too for the forges where the weapons with which Sauron equipped his armies were made.'","Talk to Rhogrin in Cirith Gorgor","Rhogrin is at Mornaur, in western Udûn.","The forges of Mornaur are on the western side of the vale of Udûn.","Rhogrin asked you to push over some of the anvils at Mornaur, rendering them difficult for the Orcs to use.","'Did you find the group of Orcs and trolls I saw from the height?'\
\
You tell Rhogrin that you found a number of dead Orcs and trolls, and it seems they argued among themselves and died from the infighting.\
\
'How very like Orcs, ${PLAYER}. I do not doubt that they would pose more of a threat if they could work together, but their penchant for squabbling leaves them vulnerable to their own fellows! They are weak-minded creatures, and in the absence of Sauron they do not know what to do. Still, we should not underestimate them for they can pose a threat to us in great enough numbers. Ah, that reminds me. Did you see Annoth while you travelled?'\
\
When you tell him you did not, Rhogrin frowns.\
\
'I climbed up here with him, but he left shortly afterward and has not returned. I hope he is all right.'","Sauron has been defeated, but the shroud over Gorgoroth must be pierced if the Free Peoples of Middle-earth are to be made safe of the evils the Dark Lord set in motion before his fall.","'How fared you on the journey into Udûn? I must admit, I faced more foes than I believed I would, but I proved stronger than they. I took the weapon from one of the Orcs I slew, and noted its craftsmanship. I would not have expected such a fine blade in the hands of one such as he; perhaps he was a commander of some sort. Do the Orcs organize their armies and fighting companies in the same fashion as the Men of Gondor?\
\
'Bah, these questions are pointless. What matters is this: he is dead and I am not, and I have come to the forges from which this sword may have been made. Let us ensure that no more of its kind come forth to trouble us! Push over some of the anvils here and render them difficult to use. That will slow down any production of further weapons, and help our efforts in Udûn.'","'Search for the forges of Mornaur on the western side of Udûn. That is where Sauron supplied many of his armies with weapons.'","'Well done, my friend! Let us see those Orcs try to forge new weapons now! We have at least made it more difficult for them to do so, if not outright impossible.\
\
'While you worked to accomplish that task, I stood on the cliff's edge and beheld a rather large movement of Orcs and trolls moving from south to north on the floor of the valley. Perhaps you can see what they are up to, ${PLAYER}? It will be nothing good, that much is certain, but there may be treasure in it, or knowledge worth having. Any enemies you defeat while you search will also help others among our soldiers, and will be no waste of effort!\
\
'I saw that group of Orcs and trolls in the basin of the vale, north-east of the crag on which Durthang stands, if you wish to investigate.'","'Let us ensure that the Orcs have a difficult time trying to use the forges and anvils here to continue the production of their weapons. Push over some of the anvils here and render them difficult to use. That will slow down any production of further weapons, and help our efforts in Udûn.'","'While you worked to accomplish that task, I stood on the cliff's edge and beheld a rather large movement of Orcs and trolls moving from south to north on the floor of the valley. Perhaps you can see what they are up to, ${PLAYER}? It will be nothing good, that much is certain, but there may be treasure in it, or knowledge worth having. Any enemies you defeat while you search will also help others among our soldiers and will be no waste of effort!'","A number of dead Orcs and trolls lie here. What was the cause of the infighting?","'Adventurers have already begun taking hesitant steps through the ruin of the Gate. Let us join them, and I will take their measure. The dangers that await in Mordor will be too great for some of them, I warrant.'","Defeated foes in Udûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Mithrandir asked to meet you just inside the ruin of the Black Gate, there to take the measure of the adventurers that desire to press forward into the land of Mordor.","'It is an honour to meet you, ${PLAYER}, for I have heard tell of the great deeds you have done in service of Middle-earth. I would appreciate your help and your guidance in Mordor, if you would provide it, for I have a task of my own I wish to undertake in the Black Land!\
\
'I am called Annoth, and I am a Ranger of Ithilien; I walked the woods for Faramir, and will again if he commands it. But my heart urges me in another direction, and my feet would follow. For I am a descendent of the Thandrim, Men of Gondor who dwelt within the bounds of Mordor and kept a watch on the evil that stirred there. The Thandrim built the great fortress of Durthand, the Black Shield, and from its high parapet they kept watch over Udûn.\
\
'But in time the watch became less, and their numbers dwindled, and the Thandrim failed. I wish to honour their memory and take vengeance upon the creatures of Sauron that slew them. Will you aid me?'\
\
You give Annoth the warning of Mithrandir, and he nods.\
\
'I do not care for treasure, ${PLAYER}. All I seek is to honour the memory of the Thandrim, for their blood runs in my veins.'","Talk to Covadil in Cirith Gorgor","'I want gold and silver and gems. Those are the spoils I understand, and those are the spoils I seek. The Wizard need not worry on my account. I can take care of myself.'","Adventurers have passed through the ruins of the Black Gate into Cirith Gorgor, and intend to seek treasure and glory in Mordor. Mithrandir asked you to speak to them and warn them against taking brash action.","You have found the Forges of Mornaur, where Sauron equipped his armies","Defeat foes in Udûn while you examine enemy movements (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I respect the warning of Mithrandir, but I do not need it. For I am Harthalín, and this is not my first adventure in the Black Land. I fought at the side of High King Gil-galad during the Battle of Dagorlad, and I know well the subtleties of Mordor. Many of my friends fell before the Black Gate, and many others met their ends on the slopes of Orodruin. I wish to pay my respects to those who fell long ago, and I have one other purpose beyond that.\
\
'I have returned to Mordor with an abundance of caution, for I disbelieve that Sauron can truly be gone. Have we not heard this tale before? I desire to see proof with my own eyes, for he is a master of trickery and deceit, and has escaped death time and again. What is different now?\
\
'I welcome your assistance, ${PLAYER}. We will need to rely upon our friends when we journey in the realm of Sauron, whether he be truly dead or no.'","Search the basin where the group of Orcs travelled, north-east of Durthang","Dangerous foes stalk the vale of Udûn, and Mithrandir asked you to venture forth with caution and defeat them.","Render anvils at Mornaur difficult to use (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Search Udûn for the forges of Mornaur","'Hail, friend, and welcome to Cirith Gorgor! The vale of Udûn lies ahead, beyond Cirith Gorgor, and all its attendant treasures are ready for the taking!\
\
'I am Rhogrin, and I am a soldier of Gondor. I fought on the Pelennor and before the Black Gate, and now I am prepared to seize the spoils of war from the clutches of the vile Orcs who fought for Sauron. They say he is dead, and I believe it. I was fighting at the base of one of the slag-hills when the Mountain of Fire shook all of Mordor, and I felt that blast in my very bones. The Dark Lord was much nearer to the Mountain than that, perhaps on its very slope, and not even he could survive that, could he? No, I think not.\
\
'It is only right that Gondor reaps the rewards of victory.'\
\
You tell Rhogrin of Mithrandir's warning about the artifacts that might remain in Mordor, and he scoffs.\
\
'I know dark magic when I see it, and I will not go near anything of that sort. I want gold and silver and gems. Those are the spoils I understand, and those are the spoils I seek. The Wizard need not worry on my account. I can take care of myself.'","'I do not care for treasure, ${PLAYER}. All I seek is to honour the memory of the Thandrim, for their blood runs in my veins.'","Rhogrin has come to Mornaur, in western Udûn.","Talk to Annoth in Cirith Gorgor","'It is as I thought. Some few of these adventurers are made of stern stuff, but most of them are not prepared for the dangers that await them. Do they think the fall of Sauron has emptied his land of evil? Aye, they believe none remain to guard his treasures, and they hope to have the picking of his coffers!\
\
'But I must urge caution! Many of the artifacts that might be found within Mordor will be wholly evil, or corrupted beyond any use by good folk. Most of these adventurers do not know the first thing about dealing with such fell entrapments!\
\
'Speak to them, ${PLAYER}, and try to dissuade them from such hasty courses. Or at least give them these warnings, so they will not blunder into their fates all unawares! After they are duly-warned, you should journey ahead and see what foes await us in Udûn. Look too for the forges where the weapons with which Sauron equipped his armies were made.'","'I know you, ${PLAYER}! Or rather, I have heard tales of the many great deeds you have performed, and to a scholar that feels like much the same thing! My name is Covadil, and I am a scholar from the Houses of Lore in Minas Tirith. My master sent me to acquire artifacts and knowledge that might be found in Osgiliath following its recapture, but that seemed a bit on the dull side for me.\
\
'I may have gotten a little carried away, but I challenge you to describe a more likely place to find artifacts and knowledge than the Land of Mordor, which has remained closed to us for so long. You cannot do it, can you? Nay, I thought not. That is why I asked the question!'\
\
You give Covadil the warning of Mithrandir, and she smiles eagerly.\
\
'Oh, yes, I will not take anything we find in there for granted! Physically I will take it, of course, pick it up and and carry it gently and carefully, so as to protect anyone else from harm, and bring it back to the Houses of Lore for study. Thank you for the warning! Very useful things to have, warnings. Folk are always giving me warnings, for some reason or another. I think it makes them feel better.'","'Sauron has been defeated, but that is not the end of the evil he stirred into wakefulness, ${PLAYER}. Who can say what lies hidden beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, beyond the wreckage of the Black Gate? The Dark Lord was a master of foul sorceries, and from the height of Barad-dûr he set many terrible plans into motion. I cannot believe that every one ended when he did.\
\
'Adventurers have already begun taking hesitant steps through the ruin of the Gate. Let us join them, and I will take their measure. The dangers that await in Mordor will be too great for some of them, I warrant.'","Talk to Harthalín in Cirith Gorgor","'I wonder what we will find within Mordor? The prospect of untold knowledge is certainly exciting!'","Chapter 1.1: Beyond the Black Gate","From the cliff's edge below Mornaur, Rhogrin saw a large group of Orcs and trolls in the basin of the vale north-east of Durthang, and asked you to investigate in order to make the area safe for other soldiers of Gondor.","'I welcome your assistance, ${PLAYER}. We will need to rely upon our friends when we journey in the realm of Sauron, whether he be truly dead or no.'","Made it difficult to use a Mornaur anvil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2824]={"'Durin wants to know what is to be done? Ha! This Stout-axe has a recommendation or two, but I do not think he is prepared to hear them!\
\
'I am a Stout-axe, ${PLAYER}. Of all the dwarves in this Middle-earth, we have endured the greatest trials; I dare you to say otherwise. Many were the torments Sauron devised for our great king when Drása did not submit, and his people were enslaved. But we kept our honour, though we toiled without end in Mordor, and now that the Dark Lord is gone the Stout-axes have emerged to take what we will, and what we deserve. So I say again to this dwarf-princeling: ha! What authority has he to command any Stout-axe? He fought against the Frost-horde? So did all of us at Skarháld. I count his deeds there no better than any of ours.\
\
'He will need a dozen such victories before he has matched even the least of my own.'","'Durin does not belong here. He is untested and unproven, and should go back to the Lonely Mountain with the rest of the Longbeards.'","Chapter 1.1: The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves","'What have you heard, my friend? Are your tidings as grim as I fear they will be?'\
\
Durin listens to your report of growing unrest among the Stout-axes and Zhélruka, and of Glóin's concerns, and his face falls. He hefts the Red Axe thoughtfully.\
\
'I came here too hastily, ${PLAYER}. Each of our peoples suffered losses when the Frost-horde attacked, but there were never that many loyal Longbeards at Skarháld to begin with. I only assumed command because there was no one else! Without a strong leader to unify each of the dwarf-clans here, I feared the Grey Mountains would prove a grave-cairn for all of us. They might still, but now it is not drakes of the Frost-horde I fear. I fear the disloyalty of the Zhélruka and the Stout-axes. Is there not betrayal in the history of both clans?\
\
'I need more loyal warriors to reinforce me! I ask you to return to my father at the Lonely Mountain and request that he send as many Longbeard warriors as he can spare. Too many were lost when the Frost-horde attacked, and I would not have us outnumbered by... by foes.'","'It seems we share the same affliction, my questing friend! Most of my companions have gone home, satisfied with their adventures, but you and I belong here in the mountains, courting danger and unafraid! I know there is a place of honour set for me beneath the Lonely Mountain, but no matter how great the feast I would still feel the emptiness in my belly. Only adventure can sate my appetite now. My son Gimli will discover this hunger runs in his blood, if he has not already! But from your recent tales I know he has!'\
\
You tell Glóin that Durin is seeking advice from the dwarves at Skarháld.\
\
'I would tell him to treat carefully with the Zhélruka and Stout-axes who have come here, for they are not his people and care little for Longbeards. Each of these kindreds defended Skarháld when the Frost-horde attacked, and each suffered losses. But there are fewer Longbeards here than Zhélruka, and although the Stout-axes were few in number to begin with, it seems to me that more arrive everyday. Durin must be aware of this. Let him keep the Red Axe near at hand.'","<rgb=#00FF00>It is recommended, but not required, that you complete 'The Black Book of Mordor' before beginning 'The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves.'</rgb>\
\
'You have returned, my friend! I did not know when your adventures to the south might release you, but I am pleased it was sooner and not later! It is good to see you!'\
\
Durin claps you heartily on the back. Then he lowers his voice and warily eyes the courtyard.\
\
'Truthfully, things have not been going as well as I might have hoped. I have been trying to ease tensions among the dwarves that have come to Skarháld, but it has not been easy. The Longbeards, Zhélruka, and Stout-axes here all take exception with each other, even on trifling matters of little importance. All three of these dwarf-companies suffered grievous losses at the teeth and claws of the Frost-horde, under Karazgar's direction, but we have seen no sign of the worms since you departed. The Weeping Warrior himself has not reappeared in that time... do you know anything about that, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'But now it falls to me to get these dwarf-clans working together, and that is no easy thing. Perhaps you can ask members of each family what they think I should do on their behalf? Stout-axes, Zhélruka, and Longbeards up the stairs here at Skarháld are sure to give you their opinions on this subject, and it may help me decide how best to proceed.'","Talk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld","Durin asked you to climb the stairs at Skarháld in search of Longbeards, Zhélruka, and Stout-axes who might share their opinions on what he should do for them.","Durin is pleased you have returned to Skarháld, for he has had some difficulty forging a workable alliance between the dwarves who have come to the Grey Mountains and could use your help.","Talk to King Thorin Stonehelm in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","Durin is on the lowest level of Skarháld, near the stable-master, waiting for your report from the three dwarf-clans who inhabit the mountain fortress.","'Things have not been going as well here as I might have hoped. I have been trying to ease tensions among the dwarves that have come to Skarháld, but it has not been easy. The Longbeards, Zhélruka, and Stout-axes here all take exception with each other, mostly for trifling matters. All three of these dwarf-companies suffered grievous losses at the teeth and claws of the Frost-horde, under Karazgar's direction, but we have seen no sign of the worms since you departed. The Weeping Warrior himself has not reappeared in that time... do you know anything about that, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'But now it falls to me to get these dwarf-clans working together, and that is no easy thing. Perhaps you can ask members of each family what they think I should do on their behalf? Stout-axes, Zhélruka, and Longbeards up the stairs here at Skarháld are sure to give you their opinions on this subject, and it may help me decide how best to proceed.'","Talk to Kóvo of the Stout-axes in Skarháld","'I need more loyal warriors to reinforce me! I ask you to return to my father at the Lonely Mountain and request that he send as many Longbeard warriors as he can spare. Too many were lost when the Frost-horde attacked, and I would not have us outnumbered by... by foes.'","Talk to Glóin of the Longbeards in Skarháld","'Durin should keep the Red Axe close. There are too few Longbeards at Skarháld for me to sleep comfortably, and he should not either.'","Durin's father, King Thorin Stonehelm, is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain in Erebor.","'Durin sent you to ask what should be done? He is no Zhélruka, that much is clear. If Bótuz Frostblood were still alive, he would not ask such a thing. He would simply tell us, and in no uncertain terms; woe be to the dwarf who did not comply with his command!\
\
'The Longbeard prince is still as green as Spring in the low-lands. He would do well to keep to himself, and leave the Zhélruka alone. We are not his to command, though we must inhabit Skarháld together for now. That will be for a short time only. Durin will soon tire of adventure and return to his father's halls. Beneath the Lonely Mountain he will live well, while we Zhélruka remain here, sleeping on the cold stone and dreaming of Gundabad, the home that has been kept from us.\
\
'He knows little of the Zhélruka, and cares for us less. I find it distasteful for him to pretend otherwise.'","'Welcome back, my adventuring friend! What news of my son? What news do you bring of Durin? Has he brought to heel the Zhélruka that travelled without leave across my lands?'","Talk to Bórnek of the Zhélruka in Skarháld","'I have said my say. If Durin does not like the truth I speak, he is welcome to tell me himself.'"},
[2825]={"Talk to Annoth outside Durthang","Annoth went to the fortress of Durthand, in Udûn, and has not returned.","'And so it was that only one of the Thandrim came alive out of Mordor that day. Halannon survived, but he was ever changed, and he swore to avenge his fallen friends and kin. He never did, but on his deathbed he asked his sons to remember what had happened at Durthand, and to swear that they would do what he had not.\
\
'But the years passed, and the sons became fathers, and their sons became fathers, and they told the story of the Thandrim, but they did nothing to avenge them. It seemed that Mordor, and Ugrukhôr, would escape judgment.'\
\
Annoth's eyes are lit by a bright fire.\
\
'But then it happened, ${PLAYER}. The Host of the West arose and defeated Sauron's armies in battle. The borders of Mordor were breached. Sauron was destroyed. Can this be anything other than the vengeance of the Thandrim, long-delayed but finally delivered?'","Annoth is consumed by his desire to avenge his ancestors, the Thandrim, and Rhogrin worries that his friend has fallen into trouble on account of it.","Talk to Annoth outside Durthang and listen to his tale of the Thandrim","Talk to Annoth outside Durthand, once the fortress of the Thandrim","'You must find Annoth, if he still lives, and try to dissuade him from attacking Durthand. This course strikes me now as foolish in the extreme!\
\
'The fortress of the Thandrim is to the south-east of us. See it there, towering over the vale? It was called Durthand once, but I do not know what the Orcs call it now.'","'After the Last Alliance of Men and Elves defeated Sauron and razed his tower to the ground, a watch was placed on Gorgoroth. The Men of Gondor built many fortifications within Mordor, such as the towers at the Black Gate, the Shadowguard of Ost Daethír, and Durthand.\
\
'For more than a thousand years, the Thandrim maintained the vigil on Mordor, but even the most important watches must wane...'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Find Annoth outside Durthand, once the fortress of the Thandrim","Annoth is outside the fortress that once belonged to the Thandrim, and was called Durthand.","'Careful, ${PLAYER}. I have already drawn the ire of the Orcs that defend this fortress, and they have sent a number of arrows my way. I returned the favour, and slew two of the beasts from great range; they are remaining watchful.\
\
'This was once Durthand, the fortress from which the Thandrim kept watch on Udûn. It is called Durthang now, in mockery of its original name. That is another insult for me to avenge, and I will do it!\
\
'Would you hear the tale of the Thandrim? I would recount it to you so you will know why I want Durthang taken from the Orcs. The tale is emblazoned in my memory; it will be a simple matter for me to tell it to you, so well is it known to me.'","'Did you speak to Annoth in Cirith Gorgor? As we travelled into Udûn, he spoke to me of his ancestors, the Thandrim, and told me all their sad history. He holds in his heart the grief of their deaths, though most of them died more than a thousand years ago. He desired to go to the fortress of Durthand, which was their watch-post, and reclaim it from any Orcs who possess it.\
\
'I thought they were courageous words, but as I look out at the dark skies over Gorgoroth I wonder if there was a touch of the fool in them. Annoth may be in the right, but he is one man only, and Durthand could be filled with Orcs. Yes, you must find him, if he still lives, and try to dissuade him from this course. I told you before: I desire wealth and treasure, and I do not understand those who seek anything else. This course of Annoth's strikes me now as foolish in the extreme!\
\
'The fortress of the Thandrim is to the south-east of us. See it there, towering over the vale? It was called Durthand once, but I do not know what the Orcs call it now. Find Annoth and render him what aid you can! I will go to rejoin the men of my company, and we will see what treasures await further within Mordor!'","Chapter 1.2: The Cruel History of Durthang","Annoth is outside the fortress of Durthang, in southern Udûn.","You have found Annoth. He lives still"},
[2826]={"'You are here to help? That is good. We turn none away who desire to help cleanse the South-harbour of the filth left behind by the Orcs of Mordor! The land remembers the scars, but it is up to its people to stitch them up and allow them to heal. Despite many offers of help, there is still plenty to be done.\
\
'Begin by cleaning up rubble piles throughout the Harlond. Earlier today some folk offered to pick up loose wooden planks around the port, and left them leaning upright at several locations to the south-west; if you can gather those for me I would appreciate it.\
\
'There has also been an increase in rats here of late... I think they fled the Corsair ships for new homes, which I would not ordinarily begrudge them, but now the creatures trouble the food-stores we keep here for the workers, and I need them gone. Will you and your fellows complete these tasks for me? You will on behalf of the King? I do not see him, but very well. I care not for whom you do these tasks, so long as they are done.'","'See that gathering of Gondorians to the east? Approach them and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation, and you will see I have not invented this worry!'","'That went well, ${PLAYER}.'","Legolas is working along the docks south-east of Othanar in the Harlond.","A small crowd of Gondorians speaks in hushed tones to the east of Legolas and Gimli. You should get closer to them and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation.","The crowd glares at you with distrust","Approach the small crowd and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation","Berthon glares at you with suspicion and dislike writ on his face","'How goes the work, ${PLAYER}? Gimli and I have made ourselves useful.\
\
'Some of the folk here seem... distrusting... of Elves and dwarves. It may be caused by fear or by superstition, but most have given us a wide berth even as they keep one eye upon us. It is nothing to me, but Gimli is bothered by it.'","'Most of these folk have given us a wide berth even as they keep one eye upon us. It is nothing to me, but Gimli is bothered by it.'","Cleaned up rubble piles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Clean up rubble piles inside the Harlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Othanar oversees the rebuilding of the Harlond by the north-eastern entrance.","Gimli is in the Harlond, helping Legolas with the rebuilding effort.","Othanar asked you to clean up rubble piles, collect wooden planks, and defeat the rats that now infest the Harlond.","Bring the wooden planks to Othanar in the Harlond","Legolas stands to the west of the whispering Gondorians by the docks of the Harlond.","Defeat rats throughout the Harlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I do not think this expedition of ours will take very long, ${PLAYER}. If there are folk here who believe the Heirs of Castamir will return, they will soon see that King Elessar holds their fortunes dear and seeks to repair the damage done during the war. They will leave the Heirs of Castamir in the past, where they belong, and Gondor will move forward.\
\
'Let us find someone inside the Harlond, to the south-west, who will tell us how we can help repair the damage done to the South-harbour.'","Talk to Berthon in the Harlond","Chapter 1.2: The Land Remembers It All","Defeated rats throughout the Harlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected wooden planks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Let us find someone inside the Harlond, to the south-west, who will tell us how we can help repair the damage done to the South-harbour.'","The War of the Ring left much of Gondor in ruin, and now its people work to restore their lands.","'Now move on. I don't like the smell of you.'","Talk to Legolas in the Harlond","Talk to Gimli in the Harlond","'You almost had me believing that King Elessar himself would bring these wooden planks to me, stranger. I am disappointed to see that is not the case.\
\
'But you have my thanks for this work, all the same. Your friends work still, by the docks to the south-east.'","'Is this true? Do they really speak of Balakhôr the Scourge?'","'What do you want, stranger? Don't like what you hear, do you? It doesn't matter to me what you like and what you don't. Gondor changed once, and it can change again; folk like you might want to watch where you stick your noses.\
\
'Friend of mine in Arnach heard the Heirs of Castamir are gathering in strength and will soon return. Their leader Balakhôr survived the fighting and slipped away to safety before he could be executed... such a pity for the upstart king! Now Balakhôr plans to overthrow the new king and his foreign bride. It was them, and people like them, that brought the war upon us: the land remembers it all. Won't be long before it has its revenge upon them, using Balakhôr as its instrument.'\
\
You insist that Balakhôr is very dead, and Berthon snorts.\
\
'That's not what my friend in Arnach says, and I think I'll be listening to him and not to you, stranger.'","'Begin by cleaning up rubble piles throughout the Harlond. Earlier today some folk offered to pick up loose wooden planks around the port, and left them leaning upright at several locations to the south-west; if you can gather those for me I would appreciate it. And also take care of the rat problem, if you would.'","'Bothered by it? You wound me, Legolas! I am no delicate crystal, and can give insult better than any of these cowards... should the need arise, which King Elessar should hope it does not, since we are here on an errand of peace and restoration.\
\
'But has the Elf-hearing of which you often boast abandoned you? For I heard those men speak the name \\qBalakhôr,\\q and it is not so common a name that it could belong to anyone but the leader of the Heirs of Castamir, about whom we seek tidings!'","'Your friends work still, by the docks to the south-east.'","Collect wooden planks in the Harlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Berthon speaks to a small crowd of Gondorians by the docks of the Harlond.","Talk to Othanar inside the Harlond","Legolas suggested that someone to the south-west must be overseeing the repairs of the Harlond."},
[2827]={"'The Greymauls were ancient dwarf traitors in the First Age who rebelled against Durin the Deathless, Father of the Dwarves. Their leader was named Mótsog, and he led the Greymauls in a bloody uprising against Durin. For a time they ruled Durin's holdings, but it did not last. Durin returned and put Mótsog to death, and the rebellion was quelled.\
\
'I have been restoring a mosaic of this very event, if you would like to see it. It is over there, against the wall. It was damaged during the residency of Smaug, and once I have finished repairing the stones I will return it to the hall where once it stood. It will once again serve as a reminder that treachery is always rewarded with justice.'","Stáli the Hewer has been restoring a mosaic depicting the death of Mótsog and the end of the Greymaul Rebellion, and he has invited you to admire it. The mosaic is currently in his workshop of Nabgûn-mazaru, but it will be returned to the hall where it came from once his work is finished.","'I do not like this, ${PLAYER}. I do not like this at all! Not every dwarf-clan is good-hearted, and treacherous, wicked dwarves have troubled the Longbeards throughout history. Our cousins in the Blue Mountains could speak at length about the exploits of the villainous Dourhands, and theirs is not the only name of ill repute. Durin will have his reinforcements! I will command the assemblage of a Longbeard army the like of which has not been seen in seventy years!\
\
'Do you think this unnecessary? I assure you it is not. I will not allow my son to be outnumbered by Zhélruka or Stout-axes! The Zhélruka have long quarreled with my people, and the Stout-axes could not have remained thralls to Sauron for so long without it affecting them deeply.\
\
'You remain unconvinced? Go then to Nabgûn-mazaru, the home of Stáli the Hewer, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls, and ask him about the Greymauls. Then you will see the importance of caution, even among dwarves. Especially among dwarves.'","This is the home of Stáli the Hewer, Longbeard artist and sculptor of some renown","'That mosaic stood in the Hall Under the Mountain with many others for hundreds of years, but the coming of Smaug was not kind to any of them. Many of the stones were lost, and it has been a time-consuming process to recreate the mosaic as it was.\
\
'But when Stáli the Hewer commits to such a project, he sees it through to the end!'","'I will not allow my son to be outnumbered by his foes! Go to the home of Stáli the Hewer, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls, and ask him about the Greymauls. Then you will see the importance of caution, even among dwarves.'","The mosaic depicting the death of Mótsog still needs repair, but its subject is clear","Talk to Stáli the Hewer in Nabgûn-mazaru","Examine the mosaic depicting the death of Mótsog","King Thorin Stonehelm has tasked you with going to Nabgûn-mazaru, the home of Stáli the Hewer, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor, and asking him about 'the Greymauls.'","'Welcome to Nabgûn-mazaru, stranger. Are you a patron of the arts? I must confess to you that my hours are quite full, with a number of half-completed works already. If you desire a painting or statue, perhaps to decorate your home, it will be some time before I am able to get to it. With that understanding set forth, what would you like?'\
\
You tell Stáli that King Thorin did not send you to him with a task, but for information on the Greymaul Dwarves.\
\
'The Greymauls? Why should they occupy his thoughts? Better to forget they ever existed, lest you doubt the decency of your closest friends and your family. But I will not disobey the King Under the Mountain, and will speak of them to you.\
\
'They were ancient dwarf traitors in the First Age who rebelled against Durin the Deathless, Father of the Longbeards. Their leader was named Mótsog, and he led the Greymauls in a bloody uprising against Durin. For a time the Greymauls ruled Durin's holdings, but it did not last. Durin returned and put Mótsog to death, and the rebellion was quelled.\
\
'I have been restoring a mosaic of this very event, if you would like to see it. It is over there, against the wall. It was damaged during the residency of Smaug, and once I have finished repairing the stones I will return it to the hall where once it stood. It will once again serve as a reminder that treachery is always rewarded with justice.'","Stáli the Hewer, a Longbeard artist and sculptor of some renown, lives at Nabgûn-mazaru, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Stáli the Hewer, a Longbeard artist and sculptor of some renown, lives south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Chapter 1.2: Treachery Remembered","Find Nabgûn-mazaru, the home of Stáli the Hewer, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor","King Thorin Stonehelm is displeased to hear of the situation in the Grey Mountains and worries for his son Durin.","'I will not allow my son to be outnumbered by his foes! Go to Nabgûn-mazaru, the home of Stáli the Hewer, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls, and ask him about the Greymauls. Then you will see the importance of caution, even among dwarves.'"},
[2828]={"'Go on, feel free to admire the statue of Durin. I am quite proud of it! See his noble visage? I like to imagine he has just looked into the lake of Kheled-zâram, and has realized he is near to finding a place of great wealth and safety for his people.'","King Thorin Stonehelm sent you to consult with Stáli the Hewer, a Longbeard artist of some renown who might tell you of the treacherous Greymaul dwarves and their rebellion against Durin the Deathless in the First Age.","Stáli the Hewer is in Nabgûn-mazaru, his workshop and home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Examine the statue of Durin the Deathless carved by Stáli the Hewer","Talk to Stáli the Hewer in Nabgûn-mazaru","King Thorin is in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor.","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","The statue of Durin is quite impressive. Stáli is more skilled than he is modest","'Can King Thorin's son really be Durin the Deathless reborn? I hope so! I have been planning a statue of him, and it would be a shame for that work to come to naught. But I have spoken too long already, and should get back to my endeavours. Return to King Thorin with my good wishes.'","Stáli the Hewer has invited you to look at the statue he carved of Durin the Deathless, located in his home and workshop of Nabgûn-mazaru.","'Ah, thank you very much, my friend! I can see you are an astute patron of the arts and have a fine eye for detail. I agree that I have done an excellent job of capturing Durin's heroism and majesty.'\
\
Stáli beams at you. You have clearly won him over.\
\
'Durin the Deathless he was called, for he possessed a great span of years and it seemed he would not die. It was not so, for death comes to all, even to the very greatest of dwarves. And yet: we Longbeards believe that Durin comes back whenever the dwarves have need of him, reborn into a new form. It is true! He has come back to us five times during our long history, and we therefore count each Durin in a single line, from Durin I who awoke beneath Gundabad all the way to Durin VI, who perished in Khazad-dûm to shadow and flame. Some folk believe that the son of King Thorin Stonehelm may prove to be Durin the Deathless reborn, a seventh Durin to lead us into the future.\
\
'I hope it is true, ${PLAYER}. I have been planning a statue of him, and it would be a shame for that work to come to naught. But I have spoken too long already, and should get back to my endeavours. Return to King Thorin with my good wishes.'","Chapter 1.3: Father of the Dwarves","'Long, long ago, before the mountains were shaped as they are now, Durin awoke in the caverns beneath a mighty peak that joined two great mountain-ranges of the north. He looked to the peak and gave it the name we have revered ever since: Gundabad, the Mountain-home.\
\
'The fathers of other dwarf-clans began to awake elsewhere in Middle-earth after that, in pairs, but he had awoken first of all the dwarves, and alone, and we revere him as the father of the Longbeards. We are Durin's Folk, and our claim to these lands springs from he who first awoke beneath Gundabad. In time, other dwarves awoke to accompany Durin, and to serve him, but his closest friend was a mighty warrior who helped delve the great halls beneath Gundabad. Legend tells us this friend was also the first dwarf to brew mead, and later ale, but do not think so well of him! He it was who would take the name Mótsog, and lead the Greymauls in rebellion. But that was still some years away.\
\
'The servants of Morgoth in those days were a constant threat, and together Durin and Mótsog fought bravely to defend the Mountain-home from them, but Durin grew restless. He desired a place where the Longbeards might know peace, and so he set forth in search of such a haven. He named his dear friend Mótsog the Lord of Gundabad, a decision he would come to regret, and departed the sacred mountain.\
\
'Do you see the statue there? It was one of my first pieces, and dare I say one of my finest. I hoped to capture some small portion of Durin's majesty as he set forth on his journey to what would become the site of treasured Khazad-dûm.'","'Stáli spoke to you of Mótsog and the Greymaul Rebellion? Good. Now you see how even good-seeming friends can turn traitor, and why it is so important that my son be surrounded by Longbeards he can trust.\
\
'I have commanded a great force of loyal warriors to go with you to join my son in the Grey Mountains. Durin will have his reinforcements!'"},
[2829]={"'Some folk believe Balakhôr survived the fighting at Pelargir and made camp to the south of Arnach, in view of the river. If you wish to learn the truth of it, I suggest you there begin your search.'","Search for some sign of Balakhôr by the shore south of Arnach, in King's Gondor","'We should follow these whispers of Balakhôr to Arnach. Perhaps there we will learn from where they began. Arnach is to the south-west of here, in Lossarnach.'","Gimli has joined you by the camp-fire south of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","According to Baranor, some folk of Arnach believe Balakhôr survived the fighting at Pelargir and came ashore south of Arnach.","'Balakhôr is dead. Why do the folk of Gondor have such difficulty believing it?'","Examine the bag of dirty clothes","'I will ask around town and see what I can learn of the Corsairs and about Balakhôr. Perhaps while I do, you will take care of some of the foes that do endanger Arnach? There may be some few brigands, as ever, but I speak mainly of wild threats: wolves, avanc, and any beasts that grow bold when unopposed.'","Some folk of Gondor whisper that Balakhôr the Scourge survived the war and will yet trouble Elessar's kingdom.","You found the remnants of an old camp... but how old is it, and who made it?","'Welcome, my friend, to Arnach! What brings you hither?'\
\
You explain that you seek word of Corsair activity along the coast of Lossarnach, and that some folk of Gondor believe Balakhôr and the Heirs of Castamir still threaten the King's peace. Baranor rubs his chin.\
\
'I do not doubt that some Corsairs fled into the wild when the fighting turned against them, but their numbers must be quite small, shouldn't they? I will ask around the town and see what I can learn. Perhaps while I do, you will take care of some of the foes that do endanger Arnach? There may be some few brigands, as ever, but I speak mainly of wild threats: wolves, avanc, and any beasts that grow bold when unopposed.'","Examine the boat among the reeds not far from the camp-fire","The ash of the burnt timbers has cooled, and no embers remain","Defeat wild beasts and other foes of Arnach throughout Lossarnach, in King's Gondor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The clothes inside this bag are of the style favoured by Corsairs","Talk to Baranor in the centre of Arnach","Legolas stands deep in thought near the abandoned camp-fire south of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Defeated foes of Arnach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wild beasts and other dangers to Arnach can be found throughout Lossarnach.","Examine the abandoned camp-fire","Baranor, Captain of the Guardsmen of Arnach, nods in welcome","Baranor stands in the centre of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","'This camp-site might have belonged to anyone. Just because it bears the signs of being a Corsair camp does not mean it was made by Balakhôr. Anyone could have come ashore here.\
\
'Do I need to remind you that we saw him die aboard the Night-jewel? He could not escape from the Dead, and did not. It beggars belief, ${PLAYER}!'","Travel to the village of Arnach, south-west of the Harlond, in King's Gondor","'You upheld your side of the bargain? I have done the same. I asked around Arnach, and... well, it seems that a few of the people here have heard that Balakhôr the Scourge survived the fighting at Pelargir and escaped into the wilderness. Some folk believe they saw him personally, though from a distance.\
\
'He supposedly made camp to the south of Arnach, in view of the river. If you wish to learn the truth of it, I suggest you there begin your search.'","'Balakhôr died on the deck of his banner-ship, the Night-jewel, at the hands of the Army of the Dead. We saw him die. About whom, then, do these rumours speak? Do the Heirs of Castamir have a new leader?\
\
'We should follow these whispers to Arnach. Perhaps there we will learn from where they began. Arnach is to the south-west of here, in Lossarnach.'","Talk to Gimli by the abandoned camp-fire south of Arnach","You found the burnt timbers of an old camp-fire near the shoreline","Legolas believes the three of you should investigate these rumours in the village of Arnach, to the south-west.","Talk to Legolas by the abandoned camp-fire south of Arnach","No longer sea-worthy, this boat served its former occupant well enough","'Gimli is right: this camp might have been made by anyone. Balakhôr did not leave the deck of the Night-jewel alive.\
\
'But this too can be true, ${PLAYER}: it may not matter.'","Chapter 1.3: Sighting of the Scourge"},
[2830]={"The guard of the vault has been recently attacked","Talk to Annoth in the dungeon of Durthang","The prisoner in this cell is already dead, and beyond rescue","'${PLAYER}! I saw Ayorzén fleeing from the fortress, but I was not able to catch him! Some of the archers up above fired at him, and never have I wished for arrows to hit their quarry so much as I wished for it then, but he was nimble... he got away!'\
\
You tell Annoth that Ayorzén stole an artifact of some kind from the vault of Durthang, but you don't know what it was.\
\
'This is bad. We need to find him before he does real harm... and what might he have taken from the vault?'","The guard of the vault of Durthang was attacked by Ayorzén when the Easterling escaped.","Talk to the Vault-guard","Ayorzén fled from the dungeon, but he headed deeper into the fortress of Durthang. Where is he going?\
\
Annoth volunteered to search the western side of the fortress, which leaves the north-eastern corner for you.","'Ugrukhôr betrayed the Thandrim more than a thousand years ago, but my heart tells me that he lives still, either through some dark art of Sauron's or some other vile sorcery. Whatever the means of his persistence, I am glad of it, for it means he will know who is responsible for his undoing.\
\
'But worry not! I have not abandoned my caution, as I know Rhogrin feared. I do not want to ruin this with haste! I have seen Orcs on the walls of Durthang, but not so many as must have been stationed here during the war. I think Durthang does not have as many defenders as the Orcs want us to think.\
\
'Let us enter the fortress and see what is going on inside, ${PLAYER}. Defeat enemies inside Durthang, and if there are prisoners in the dungeons, we should set them free. They may know where I can find Ugrukhôr.'","You have freed a number of prisoners from their cells in the dungeon of Durthang.","Defeat Orc-kind inside Durthang (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Let us enter the fortress and see what is going on inside, ${PLAYER}. Defeat enemies inside Durthang, and if there are prisoners in the dungeons, we should set them free. They may know where Ugrukhôr has gone.'","The fortress of Durthang is in southern Udûn.","Open cell doors in the dungeon of Durthang (2/3)","Talk to Annoth outside Durthang","Find Ayorzén in the north-eastern section of Durthang","Annoth believes that the downfall of Sauron is a sign that the time for the vengeance of the Thandrim has come at last, and he wants to recapture the fortress of Durthang.","Chapter 1.3: Unintentions","'You have to get Ayorzén back! He may still be somewhere in Durthang. If you hurry, you might be able to catch him before he escapes and does further injury to Gondor! Search in the north-east and I will search to the west!'","'These prisoners have all been cruelly treated by their jailors. Such is the way of Orcs!'","The dungeon of Durthang is in the south-eastern corner of the fortress.","Annoth is outside the fortress of Durthang, in southern Udûn.","Open cell doors in the dungeon of Durthang (${CURRENT}/3)","'Wait, ${PLAYER}, what did he say his name was? Ayorzén? I know that name! Ayorzén the Wily was a Khundolar leader who fought against Gondor! It is one thing to free the downtrodden of their captivity, but that was no villager or farmer. That was a battle-hardened Easterling warrior! He has slain soldiers of Gondor and Rangers of Ithilien both!\
\
'You have to get him back! He may still be somewhere in Durthang. Search in the north-east corner of the fortress and I will search to the west! If we hurry we might be able to catch him before he escapes and does further injury to Gondor!'","'That Easterling wretch got the jump on me, but I gave him as good as I got. Not enough to stop him from rooting around in the vault, but he'll be good as dead before he's gone a dozen steps from the fortress. My boys'll stick him full of arrows.\
\
'The trinket he took from the vault won't do him no good. He won't know how to use it. Good riddance to that vile thing and to the Easterling too!\
\
'You must be in league with him, and now you'll die same as he will!'","'If there are prisoners being held in the dungeons of Durthang, we should find them and release them. One of them might know where Ugrukhôr has gone.'","Defeated Orc-kind inside Durthang (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2831]={"Annoth has come to the Isenmouthe in search of Ayorzén.","'What is this? Did Ayorzén come this way?'\
\
You show the message you recovered to Annoth, and he considers it for a moment.\
\
'This is very interesting, ${PLAYER}. Ugrukhôr must have commanded these Orcs to close the Isenmouthe, but the doors were ruined in the blast from Orodruin and the upheavals of Mordor; they could not shut them all the way. Fortuitous enough for us, mayhap, but even more so: it seems that they have turned Easterlings away and not permitted them to pass the gate without the permission of Ugrukhôr! Did they turn Ayorzén away? Is he still in Udûn?\
\
'Search Udûn for an Easterling camp. There is one, Rhûd Vorn, somewhere to the north. He may try to return to his people.'","Bring the corrupted heirloom to Mithrandir, just inside the ruined Black Gate","'I suppose we have to bring our captive out of Mordor. I do not like this, but we don't have much of a choice now.'","'Did the guards of the Isenmouthe turn Ayorzén away? Is he still in the vale? Search Udûn for Rhûd Vorn. He may try to return to his people.'","Annoth believes Ayorzén will try to pass through the Isenmouthe, the gate in Carach Angren that bars passage between Udûn and Dor Amarth.","Many foes occupy the Isenmouthe. Did Ayorzén come this way?","Defeated Easterlings at Rhûd Vorn (${NUMBER}/6)","Show the message you recovered to Annoth near the Isenmouthe <rgb=#00FF00>(The message can be read from your inventory)</rgb>","'The Isenmouthe is held by many foes? Defeat some of them and they may tell you if Ayorzén went that way.'","Mithrandir is just inside the ruined Black Gate, in Cirith Gorgor.","Chapter 1.4: Ayorzén, Twice-Imprisoned","There is no sign of Ayorzén. If he came here, he is gone now","Talk to Annoth by the road south of the Easterling encampment in Udûn","You should search the Easterling camp of Rhûd Vorn for any sign of Ayorzén.","'You don't believe his sad story, do you? He was called Ayorzén the Wily for a reason, no matter what name he takes for himself now!'\
\
Annoth clenches and unclenches his fists with frustration.\
\
'We cannot kill him, ${PLAYER}. He is a surrendered man, and the tale he weaves is one of despair whether I believe it is truthful or not! If we were to slay him now, we would be no better than Ugrukhôr, who betrayed the Thandrim! But we must keep a close eye on him and not forget that he is our enemy. That our other enemies have cast him aside does not absolve him of guilt for his crimes!\
\
'As for the trinket he gave to you, I think any study of it should be reserved for Mithrandir. I feel a great deal of evil emanating from it, and shouldn't the Wizard ensure it is not a devious trick of Ayorzén's before we accept it? It is a small curio, easily held in one hand, and its design is not of Mordor. I think it was fashioned elsewhere. It may be that its stay in the vault of Durthang has imbued it with the unpleasant aura that surrounds it. Bring it to the Wizard and see what he thinks, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Annoth sighs, clearly disappointed with the result of pursuing Ayorzén.\
\
'I suppose we have to bring our captive out of Mordor. I do not like this, but we don't have much of a choice now.'","Talk to Ayorzén the Wily by the side of the road in Udûn","Defeat Easterlings at Rhûd Vorn, in Udûn (5/6)","Find the Isenmouthe, the gate between Udûn and Dor Amarth","'I know you two have followed my trail. Do you rejoice to pursue a man who has done nothing? There is no kindness in your hearts, no forgiveness. I am Ayorzén the Humble, nothing more. When I escaped Durthang, I thought to build my strength, find my allies, and rain destruction upon my jailors and the great multitude of my enemies. But it is not to be!\
\
'I went first to the Isenmouthe, but the guards would not let me pass. I then went to my old camp, home to my servants and my sworn men both, and found it hostile to me! They have given Ortakûl the command, and all my servants and all my sworn men look upon me as a coward, as an unwelcome stain upon the Khundolar! Conspirators and ingrates, all of them!\
\
'I sat down here by the road, once-mighty Ayorzén fallen so low as to have no place in all the world. I am not welcome in Gorgoroth. Even the Orcs spit upon me! And there is no place for me with my own kind, despite my long military service and impressive chain of titles and deeds. Ortakûl has seen to that! And Gondor? Do not make me laugh, vile pursuers! Gondor would not welcome one such as me, and I care not for that invading land anyway.\
\
'I have been waiting here for you to catch up and put an end to this miserable day. I surrender to you; do with me what you will, but if you levy death upon me now, you will shame yourself and all you claim to honour! I am Ayorzén, twice-imprisoned, first by one side and then by the other. What do you call yourself? ${PLAYER}? And he is Annoth? I have heard more impressive names; truly I have worn them myself!\
\
'Do you want this trinket? It is of no use to me. I stole it from the vault of Durthang, for I thought it might be useful. Yes, I wanted a valued artifact to barter with some self-important, greed-blinded fool.\
\
'You can have it, ${PLAYER}.'","'I saw Ayorzén disappear around the rocks to the north-east. He must be heading for the Isenmouthe, the gate in Carach Angren that bars passage from Udûn to Dor Amarth. He must be trying to bring the artifact he stole deeper into Mordor!'","Many foes hold the Isenmouthe.","Defeat enemies near the Isenmouthe (${CURRENT}/5)","'I don't know what good that trinket might do for you, but if you find it useful, remember it was a gift from Ayorzén the Generous.'","Ayorzén may have gone to Rhûd Vorn, an Easterling camp in Udûn. You should defeat its warriors while you search for him.","Wait, is that...? Have you found Ayorzén?","You have found Ayorzén. He is sitting with his back against a rock by the side of the road, south of the Easterling encampment in Udûn.","Annoth was going to follow you to the Easterling camp. Walk down the slope south of the Easterling camp and tell him there was no sign of Ayorzén.","'I don't know what good that trinket might do for you, but if you find it useful remember it was a gift from Ayorzén the Generous.'","Many foes hold the gate of Isenmouthe.","'It's him! We have found our quarry, ${PLAYER}! He is just sitting here by the road!'","'I do not know why Ayorzén was being held captive in the dungeon of Durthang, but it doesn't change the fact that he was responsible for the deaths of many good people during the war, ${PLAYER}. I feel responsible for setting him free, so I need to track him down! I would appreciate your help with this.\
\
'I saw him disappear around the rocks to the north-east. He must be heading for the Isenmouthe, the gate in Carach Angren that bars passage from Udûn to Dor Amarth. He must be trying to bring the artifact he stole deeper into Mordor!'","Annoth is south of the Easterling encampment in Udûn, where Ayorzén waited for you.","'What is this talk of prisoners, ${PLAYER}? You have brought an Easterling out of Mordor?'\
\
You tell Mithrandir about Ayorzén, and hand over the artifact he gave to you. The Wizard studies it closely.\
\
'This is not an heirloom of Mordor, but it is wreathed with corruption. I will see if there is aught to learn from it, but for now you should not trouble yourself with Ayorzén or his purloined gift. Both will be watched, and we will see what might be learned from either.'","You find a crumpled paper covered in a crude scrawl","Ayorzén the Wily fled from Durthang, but not before he stole an artifact of some kind from the fortress vault.","Defeated enemies near the Isenmouthe (${CURRENT}/5)","Defeat Easterlings at Rhûd Vorn, in Udûn (${NUMBER}/6)","Ayorzén gives you the heirloom he stole from Durthang; it has an unpleasant aura about it","Find Annoth along the road south of Rhûd Vorn","'You don't have anything for me?'","Defeat enemies near the Isenmouthe (4/5)"},
[2832]={"Chapter 1.4: Survivors of the Orc Wars","Reithvald Red-ember still burns for battle!","'A chance to test my skills? I welcome it, and promise I will not go easy on you!'","Talk to Lági Helmbiter and measure his combat prowess","Talk to Reithvald Red-ember and measure his combat prowess","'You shall have a fight, then! I may be old, but I remain fierce and eager for battle!'","Talk to Agnar Brokentooth and measure his combat prowess","Agnar Brokentooth proved too much for you!","'Those three remain eager for battle? I did not really expect otherwise, but I thought it best to make certain. Thank you for indulging me in this, ${PLAYER}. May their greatest heroics remain ahead of them, in service to my son Durin!'","Lági Helmbiter proved too much for you!","The passage of years has not slowed Lági Helmbiter one bit!","King Thorin Stonehelm is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor.","King Thorin Stonehelm has ordered a great force of Longbeard warriors to go with you to reinforce Durin in the Grey Mountains, but first he wants you to test the mettle of some of the eldest.","Reithvald Red-ember proved too much for you!","'Seek out Agnar Brokentooth, Lági Helmbiter, and Reithvald Red-ember in the passages to the Dwelling-halls and to the New-lodes, and challenge them to battle. If they still desire to join my son in the Grey Mountains after testing their skills against you, then they shall.'","'You have proven yourself a ${CLASS} of great courage, ${PLAYER}, and I judge that you have an eye for strength and capability in battle. Will you measure your fighting prowess against some of the dwarves I have chosen to join this Longbeard army? I do not question their desire for glory; indeed, these dwarves fought bravely and well in time of war, and achieved much honour thereby.\
\
'But their greatest deeds are many years distant now. These three heroes fought in the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, but that was more than two hundred and twenty years ago, when Durin's Folk last set foot within Gundabad. The Battle of Azanulbizar ended that war, and our losses were too great to pursue the Orcs into Khazad-dûm. I do not doubt the bravery of these three! But I want to know they still possess sufficient weapon-skill to aid my son.\
\
'Seek out Agnar Brokentooth, Lági Helmbiter, and Reithvald Red-ember in the passages to the Dwelling-halls and to the New-lodes, and challenge them to battle. If they still desire to join my son in the Grey Mountains after testing their skills against you, then they shall.'","Agnar Brokentooth remains as eager for battle as ever!","King Thorin Stonehelm asked you to test the combat readiness of three survivors of the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, which occurred more than two hundred and twenty years ago. These three heroes can be found in the passages leading to the Dwelling-halls and the New-lodes, in Erebor.","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","'You had best prepare for a real fight, stranger! I have not lived so long in idleness! Indeed, I test my combat skill every day without exception!'"},
[2833]={"Listen to Glassiel speak of the Five Sisters","'What if someone has taken Balakhôr's place, adopting his name and appearance in an attempt to rally the Heirs of Castamir? We should tell Baranor of this possibility, so he can keep watch and guard against it.'","'I hope I did not miss many other such adventures while I was aboard the ship!'","Travel to the town of Halach in King's Gondor","Legolas sits on a bench by the entrance to Glaniath, in King's Gondor.","Breglang, a sailor at Halach, has called for your attention.","'You say Angbor, the Lord of Lamedon, directed that the armour of the Usurper be sent to Pelargir for safekeeping? That was a wise decision, for Castamir's armour has already proven unable to remain lost. Better to keep it under the watchful eye of Sirgon, Lord of Lebennin.\
\
'But a thought occurs to me. If someone were trying to convince others that he was Castamir's successor, or pretending to be Balakhôr himself, he might make use of artifacts such as armour or weapons that once belonged to the Usurper. We should make sure the armour came to Sirgon as Angbor intended.\
\
'But Elessar also wanted us to help the people. Will you see Glassiel safely back to her home? Gimli and I will meet you at Glaniath when you return, and we will proceed together on to Pelargir.'","Glassiel stands inside the entrance to Halach.","'The King will be pleased to hear how you helped the people of Halach, if such is your intent.'","It is time for you to meet up with Legolas and Gimli in the town of Glaniath, to the north-west.","Glassiel speaks to you of the Five Sisters of Lebennin.","Glassiel has arrived safely at her home of Halach","Legolas stands at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor.","'River-maidens they were, caring and understanding. But one was changed by an evil in the waters.'","'If you wish to be of use to the folk of Lebennin, you can oppose some of the dangers to be found between here and my home of Halach. Wild creatures and the occasional hold-out from the war are still to be found prowling the lands between Erui and Halach.\
\
'Meet me at my home when I have safely arrived and I can put you further to work. I understand you have been given a duty to help us by the King himself?'","Legolas is concerned that the legacy of Balakhôr the Scourge may still threaten King's Gondor.","Return to Breglang in the town of Halach, in King's Gondor","Defeat foes on the way to Halach, in King's Gondor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Legolas and Gimli greet you warmly as you arrive in Glaniath","Talk to Legolas by the entrance to Glaniath, in King's Gondor","Travel to the Crossings of Erui, south-west of Arnach, in King's Gondor","'As the long years passed, the Lady of Erui was infected by that anger.'","'You helped make the lands between the Crossings and Halach more safe? I thank you for it! I was not in any danger, for the blessings of the Five Sisters are upon me, and their influence extends into the lands washed by their rivers. Still, it is a welcome deed.\
\
'King Elessar was good to send you to us.'","Talk to Legolas at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor","'It is good of you to offer to bring me to my home, but I can find my own way.\
\
'Still, if you wish to be of use to the folk of Lebennin, you can oppose some of the dangers to be found between here and my home of Halach. Wild creatures and the occasional hold-out from the war are still to be found prowling the lands between Erui and Halach.\
\
'Meet me at my home when I have safely arrived and I can put you further to work. I understand you have been given a duty to help us by the King himself?'","The Crossings of Erui are located to the south-west of the village of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Glassiel is at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Baranor in the centre of Arnach","Baranor is the Captain of the Guardsmen of Arnach, north of the abandoned camp-site in King's Gondor.","'I hope the Lone Lady of Erui knows she now has the love and belief of all of Lebennin.'","'Castamir the Usurper perished here, long ago, but his rage remained.'","'I speak of the Five Sisters of Lebennin, who protect these lands even now.'","'We will remain alert for any supporters of the Heirs who appear, and I trust you will do the same as you continue south and westward, to the Crossings of Erui. There are several small villages beyond the Erui that may foster similar sentiments as those here in Arnach. Good fortune go with you.'","Breglang is in the town of Halach, waiting for you to return from your errands.","'How went your visit to Halach, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'The Heirs of Castamir may never truly disappear, but I think it is becoming clear that their power wanes. An imposter is not as great a threat to Gondor as Balakhôr himself would have been.\
\
'The time approaches when we can return to King Elessar and tell him his tour can proceed.'","Retrieve fishing nets from near the docks of Halach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect building supply crates within Halach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What have you discovered, ${PLAYER}? Was there any truth to the rumours spoken among the people of Arnach? Did Balakhôr survive the war?'\
\
You recount to Baranor what you discovered, and what Legolas had to say about the fallen leader of the Heirs of Castamir. The guardsman nods grimly.\
\
'Aye, an imposter could cause trouble for King Elessar and for Gondor just as easily as Balakhôr himself might have done. We will remain alert for any who appear, and I trust you will do the same as you continue south and westward, to the Crossings of Erui. There are several small villages beyond the Erui that may foster similar sentiments as those here in Arnach. Good fortune go with you.'","'I thank you for doing the tasks I had set before me, friend! Do not be cross with me, for I put the time you spared me to good use!\
\
'My loyalty is to the King, but some of the men I work beside are not as true to Gondor as I am. I have learned from their speech that the Heirs of Castamir have taken to lighting the beacons of Gondor when they find them unguarded, as a sign to their supporters. I do not know if it is true, but that is what I heard. Look for lit beacons and there will be serpents nearby, snakes who endanger the King and his kingdom.\
\
'At least, that is what I was told. Go from Halach with my thanks, and with the warning I give you!'","Talk to Glassiel at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor","Defeated foes on the way to Halach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Gimli at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor","Talk to Glassiel in her home-town of Halach","Retrieved today's catch from fishing nets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You agreed to aid the folk of Lebennin by defeating foes between the Crossings of Erui and Halach.","'Bring in some fishing nets down by the piers, and gather up a couple crates of building materials around town, and you might fill the King's sails with wind, and leave the Heirs of Castamir without. Do these tasks for me and I'll share what else I know, and that would be a help to the King.'","'The blood spilt in these waters during the Kin-strife of Gondor so changed the Lady of Erui that she became estranged from her sisters, and turned her anger upon the folk who dwelt nearby. Not long ago she raised the Armour of the Usurper from these waters and did battle against her sisters, but at last they were able to soothe her rage and she was healed of her hurts.\
\
'So I float these baskets upon her waters as tokens of both forgiveness and love, and I hope that she takes notice of them.'","'The Five Sisters have always protected us, though we did not always remember it.'","Legolas and Gimli planned to meet up with you in the town of Glaniath","The woman Glassiel floats offerings on the river Erui","At the Crossings of Erui you encountered the woman Glassiel, floating baskets on the river.","A sailor standing nearby calls for your attention","Travel to the town of Glaniath, north-west of Halach in King's Gondor","'These are the Crossings of Erui, where Castamir the Usurper perished long ago during the Kin-strife of Gondor, when his rebellion was at last ended, and the rule of the kingdom was restored. But Kings and Stewards rule from distant castles and towers, and our people need the blessing of nearer protectors.\
\
'And so I and other good people of Lebennin float baskets on the river in memory of the Five Sisters, who protected this land in days gone. Some folk believed they were only a myth, but it is not so!'","Fishing nets can be drawn in along the docks of Halach.","Gimli stands at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor.","'Balakhôr need not have survived to inspire those who believed in his purpose. Is it not possible he might have become, in death, more of a symbol to his people than he could have remained in life? A man can be slain; it is more difficult to fully destroy that for which he stood.\
\
'What if someone has taken his place, ${PLAYER}? What if someone has adopted his name and his appearance in an attempt to rally the Heirs of Castamir? We should tell Baranor of this possibility, so he can keep watch and guard against it.'","'Will you see Glassiel safely back to her home? Gimli and I will meet you at Glaniath when you return, and we will proceed together on to Pelargir.'","Chapter 1.4: The Legacy Lives On","Talk to Breglang in Halach","'Mercy upon me for listening, stranger, but I understand you're here on the King's business? That is a joy to me and mine, for certain, but you might want to know that some of the folk hereabout aren't as true as my family. I've a-heard some talk that the Heirs of Castamir never surrendered, but lie in wait, fostering their strength.\
\
'Seems to me a good way to fight some of these rumours might be to show the King is nearer to us than distance would indicate. Maybe you're here to do just that? If'n you bring in some fishing nets down by the piers, and gather up a couple crates of building materials around town, you might fill the King's sails with wind, and leave the Heirs of Castamir without? Do these tasks for me and I'll share what else I know, and that would be a help to the King.'","'They say the Heirs of Castamir are still around. If you are loyal to the King, as I am, you will remain on your guard in these lands.'","Collected building supply crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It is a good story, so far as it goes. A little unbelievable, I think.'\
\
Gimli stares at you with amazement when you tell him it is true, and you witnessed the end of the tale as you passed through Lebennin during the war.\
\
'Really? I missed more than I thought when I agreed to take the ship from Pelargir with Legolas! What happened to the Armour of the Usurper after the River-maidens calmed their sister of her anger?'","You agreed to make safe the lands between the Crossings of Erui and Glassiel's home of Halach, in King's Gondor. Now you should ensure she arrived safely."},
[2834]={"Glóin stands near the stable-master at Skarháld, pleased to see the Longbeard reinforcements from the Lonely Mountain.","<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Skarháld with a large force of Longbeards when you accept this quest.</rgb>\
\
'Go now to the mountain-fortress where waits my son! Bring him this mighty force, and tell him his father knows he will bring glory for the Longbeards for so long as there is glory there to be had!'","Return to Skarháld with the Longbeard force","Mírkuz eyes the Longbeard force with great suspicion.","Talk to Glóin and go with him to search for Durin","Glóin's brow creases in thought and with worry","'Bring Durin this mighty force, and tell him his father knows he will bring glory for the Longbeards for so long as there is glory there to be had!\
\
'Skarháld awaits your return, ${PLAYER}!'","A warrior of the Zhélruka eyes the large Longbeard force with suspicion","Durin has returned to Skarháld with renewed purpose, his eyes alight with hopeful flame.","King Thorin has asked you to return to Skarháld with the great force of Longbeards he commanded to reinforce his son Durin.","Talk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld","'Finally, my friend! At last I know my purpose, and with this army of Longbeards at my back, I cannot hope but to achieve it! Gundabad awaits, ${PLAYER}!'","Talk to Glóin by the stable-master in Skarháld","Glóin stands near the stable-master at Skarháld. He is worried that Durin left the fortress some time ago and has not returned.","'Now this is a fighting force! I do not suppose my son Gimli joined the company? No, I do not see him. He is far away, having further adventures of his own. A pity.\
\
'But look at these warriors! Why, even Agnar Brokentooth has come! And there is Lági Helmbiter! These are truly great heroes of my people, ${PLAYER}. I fought alongside them at Azanulbizar, you know; I was among the youngest to stand at that battle. I am not so young now, am I?\
\
'What a wonder it is that they have come to aid the prince here in the Grey Mountains! Where is Durin? He will be pleased to see so many fighters. I saw him speaking with Heilar some time ago, and the two of them went away to the north-east. Have they not returned?'","'If the son of Thorin Stonehelm thinks to cheat the Zhélruka of the lands that were promised, he will be sorry. Surely he must know this!'","'Why have you brought all these Longbeards here, ${PLAYER}? I am offended to see so many! The Zhélruka were offered a home in these mountains, but now it seems Durin's Folk think to once again stand in the way of that offer.\
\
'What other meaning can there be for this great force? The son of Thorin Stonehelm thinks to cheat my people of the lands that were promised!'","Talk to Mírkuz at Skarháld","'I do not like that Durin has not yet returned. He did not say where he and Heilar were going, but they were heading north-east when last I saw them, and there is not much in that direction, unless....'\
\
A dark shadow passes across Glóin's face.\
\
'That is the way to the Anvil of Winterstith, ${PLAYER}. You do not think they would be going there, do you? We must hurry!'\
\
Glóin looks around grimly.\
\
'And bring the army, ${PLAYER}. We cannot be too careful.'","King Thorin Stonehelm has commanded a large force of Longbeards to travel with you to reinforce his son Durin in the Grey Mountains.","Chapter 1.5: An Echo in the Mountains"},
[2835]={"Find the foundries of Anglach","Mithrandir has asked you to aid soldiers who might have run afoul of the choking fumes that belch from the mines and foundries of Anglach, in Udûn.","Mithrandir is outside the Black Gate.","'He is impudent, and he is impolite, and he is abrasive, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Mithrandir raises an eyebrow, and the faintest hint of a smile emerges beneath his beard.\
\
'He may also be useful. I have had an idea.'","Talk to Belaith at Anglach","Collected treasure in the mines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Chapter 1.5: The Air of That Place","'Give the draughts I gave to you to any at Anglach who might suffer from breathing the unhealthy air. Tell them, too, that they must withdraw. Every moment they breathe the foul fumes brings them closer to harm, and further from real recovery.'","Bring the treasure you collected to Belaith, at Anglach","Ayorzén sits near Mithrandir outside the Black Gate.","Belaith leads a group of adventurers seeking treasure in at Anglach, in Udûn.","'Does this Easterling have something to say? I might remind him that it is impolite to interrupt the Wise, and I have walked in Middle-earth much longer than he!'","Give restorative draughts to adventurers at Anglach (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'This is all you found? These few baubles are the most treasure you could wrest from the mines beneath Anglach, foundry of the Great Sauron? Ah, places of great shadow will hold greater rewards, and we are on the outskirts of the lands that were his. Perhaps greater treasures will be found where the grip of the shadow is stronger.'\
\
Belaith snorts.\
\
'Or perhaps you did not know where to look, ${PLAYER}. Just as soon as my men have recovered from breathing in the noxious fumes of this place, we will be back. The real treasure must be hidden deeper within the mine! Even so, a deal spoken is a deal done. I will do as I said I would, and my men will have a few days to rest and recover before we return.'","Talk to Ayorzén outside the Black Gate","Defeat Orcs in the mines below Anglach and retrieve treasure (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Just as soon as my men have recovered from breathing in the noxious fumes of this place, we will be back. The real treasure must be hidden deeper within the mine! Even so, a deal spoken is a deal done. I will do as I said I would, and my men will have a few days to rest and recover before we return.'","The foundries of Anglach have filled the air with choking fumes","'What have you done, ${PLAYER}? You have stopped my men from their tasks. I lead this group of adventurers, and if they are not fighting Orcs or searching for treasure, they are not doing their jobs! The air here is foul, that is true, but these are strong men and they cannot use that as an excuse to relax their effort.\
\
'If you wish to be of help, you could make your way into the mine. It is delved behind the foundries here and descends beneath us for a great distance. Who knows what treasures await us in there? If you care so much for the lives of these men, you would be doing them a service if you thinned out some of the foes that lurk in the mine.\
\
'You might find some treasure, too. Bring it out here and I will return with my men back to the gate so they may recover... but not before!'","'I saw a group of treasure-seekers returning from Udûn, so I know you did your duty and compelled them to return. They do not value their lives as greatly as they value their treasure; if they continue on this course they will soon have neither! Treasure makes fools of all men.\
\
'To linger so near the mines and foundries of Anglach is unwise, for these seekers of treasure or indeed for any! Who can say what foul work was undertaken for Sauron at Anglach or what terrible craft was done there in the name of his war?'","'You have not found sufficient treasure for me!'","The foundries and mines of Anglach are in north-eastern Udûn.","Talk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate","'He fancies himself a Wizard, does he? Ayorzén knows about Wizards, and wants nothing to do with them. They are not as wise as they claim to be, nor as impartial.\
\
'He says, \\qNone know what was made at Anglach,\\q but that is already not right, for I know well. The great ram Grond was made there and wreathed about with spells. I saw it destroy the gate of the Tall City myself, and if things had gone otherwise there would have been no stopping it.\
\
'Yes, I was in the war councils, and I heard the plans for Grond. Can this so-called Wizard claim that? No, he cannot. It was a matter of pride for me, Ayorzén the Included, but now I have been replaced. Replaced by Ortakûl, no doubt. He will not last. That at least is cause for comfort!'","'Adventurers who have sojourned in Gorgoroth have reported a great deal of discomfort, not only of the spirit but of the body. The air in Udûn is filled with choking fumes and unhealthy vapours, but nowhere worse than that produced by the mines and foundries of Anglach.\
\
'I have prepared a number of restorative draughts that should bring comfort to adventurers in Udûn. I ask that you go to Anglach and give these draughts to any there who might suffer from these maladies. Tell them, too, that they must withdraw. Every moment they breathe the foul fumes brings them closer to harm, and further from real recovery.'","Belaith asked you to delve into the mines below Anglach in search of treasure and refused to return to the Black Gate with his men until you have brought him some.","Ayorzén, sitting nearby, laughs coldly","'I know well what was made at the foundries of Anglach. The great ram Grond was made there and wreathed about with spells. I saw it destroy the gate of the Tall City myself, and if things had gone otherwise there would have been no stopping it.\
\
'Yes, I was in the war councils, and I heard the plans for Grond. Can this so-called Wizard claim that? No, he cannot. It was a matter of pride for me, Ayorzén the Included, but now I have been replaced. Replaced by Ortakûl, no doubt. He will not last. That at least is cause for comfort!'","Adventurers affected by the choking fumes can be found at the foundries of Anglach, in north-eastern Udûn."},
[2836]={"Sirgon has come to a decision, and is ready to speak with you.","Collect tokens from the boxes in Glaniath (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'I traded for this gem in a seaside market, twenty years ago. It remains as brilliant today!'","'I have taken many an enemy's shield in battle. I display some of them here.'","'The Uruk who wore this boarded my ship just off the Shield Isles. Now it is mine.'","Meet Sirgon in his room of keepsakes, to the north","'So many tokens have been cast in support of my proposal! This is nearly all!\
\
'I want you to understand that folk of Glaniath hold no ill will toward Sirgon in their hearts. His experience was a mournful one, and it is wrong to expect him to carry on without harm. Let him cede the rule of Lebennin to his son Faltharan. That will be best for him, and it will be best for the lands he must govern. I am certain King Elessar will approve, but we must take single steps first. Sirgon served Gondor, and with the war finished he has earned a peaceful rest, and should take it with our gratitude.\
\
'As you are going soon to Pelargir, you will bring these tokens to him and show him the mind of Glaniath's families, yes?'","Talk to Gimli by the entrance to Glaniath, in King's Gondor","'No, I never saw this creature alive! I recovered its bones on a southern voyage.'","The port city of Pelargir is to the south-west of Glaniath, in King's Gondor.","Sirgon's son Faltharan has joined you in the room of keepsakes","Enter Sirgon's Manor in Pelargir and find its lord","Talk to Faltharan inside Sirgon's room of keepsakes","'The armour of my first slain Orc. Had I perished, my armour might be in a case like this one.'","'See the keepsakes I have gathered in my life, and know what I have come to miss.'","Chapter 1.5: The Lord of Lebennin","'It brings me joy to see you return to Pelargir, my friend, with the spectre of war behind us!\
\
'You wish to see Sirgon, Lord of Lebennin? His manor is down the street to the west. He will be pleased to see you, I imagine, but be warned that his captivity during the war left its mark upon him and his spirit is not as vital as once it was.\
\
'He is still strong and stern, do not mistake me! But he is changed, and weariness lies upon his brow.'","Travel to the eastern entrance of Pelargir, south-west of Glaniath, in King's Gondor","Arvellon is in the centre of Glaniath, and Legolas believes you should speak with him.","Captain Thandor is in the square by the eastern entrance to Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","Gimli is by the entrance to Glaniath.","'While Gimli and I waited for you to arrive, a resident of this town came to speak with us. Arvellon, he is called, and he was most interested to learn we plan to continue on to Pelargir. The matter that occupies his thought may be of interest to King Elessar.\
\
'Speak with Arvellon and see what you think. He should be near the centre of town.'","'A friend gave me a number of tapestries depicting friendship between Gondor and Rohan.'","Faltharan stands within his father's room of keepsakes.","'I did not understand this proposal when Arvellon told it to us, and I still do not. He expects Sirgon to simply abandon the lordship of Lebennin because a few families thought he should? No dwarf would do this.\
\
'At any rate, the sooner we go to Pelargir the sooner we will return to Minas Tirith with the tidings we sought. We have heard plenty of whispers and rumours, but little in the way of real danger. I suppose that is good, but it is also a pity, for my axe needs swinging!'","'I found this fellow just off the Langstrand, a few years ago. He sings beautifully.'","Talk to Captain Thandor by the eastern entrance to Pelargir","Collected tokens cast by folk of Glaniath (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Sirgon's Manor is located down the street to the west of the north-east entrance of Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","Wait for Sirgon to speak","'As you are going soon to Pelargir, you will bring these tokens to him and show him the mind of Glaniath's families, yes?'","Talk to Sirgon in his manor","Talk to Sirgon inside his room of keepsakes","'You wish to see Sirgon, Lord of Lebennin? His manor is down the street to the west.'","'Meet me in my room of keepsakes, to the north. I want to show you something.'","'I was once the master of the fleets of Gondor, ${PLAYER}. I sailed across the Bay of Belfalas at the direction of the Steward, and brought the might of Gondor to bear wherever it was needed. I remember the smell of the salt on the spray, the cry of the gulls overhead, the wind in my hair, the rocking of the ship's deck beneath my feet.\
\
'When I was held captive during the war, I feared for my family and for the people in my charge... but I am shamed to admit that I also feared I would die on land. I was a man of the sea, ${PLAYER}, but in recent days I have felt penned up in this city, in this kingdom, in my very title. \\qLord of Lebennin!\\q Rather would I be once again the Lord of Ships, the Lord of Tide and Wave!\
\
'See the keepsakes I have gathered in my life, and know what I have come to miss.'","'So many memories.\
\
'Perhaps my son should succeed me. It took the folk of Glaniath to make me realize something I think I have known for these past few months, but did not express. My heart does not belong on land. I wish to sail again, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'I can better serve King Elessar from the deck of a ship, as I did in prior years. Faltharan should rule in Lebennin.'","'This fellow set one of my ships alight with evil sorcery. Now I keep an eye upon him here.'","'Maybe the people of Glaniath are right, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The days of my youth are far behind me now. Who will follow a leader so easily captured in war, as I was by the Men of Harad? Respect is hard to gain, but easy to lose. There were moments I despaired, and thought Lebennin would be better served if I never returned.'\
\
Sirgon sighs heavily and looks you in the eye.\
\
'This was not supposed to be my life. Meet me in my room of keepsakes, to the north. I want to show you something.'","'My father has been seized by one of his moods again, I see. He has always suffered from the call of the gulls, the pull of the sea, but it has been worse in recent days.\
\
'I do not desire to rule in Lebennin, but I will do so if that is my father's wish, and the will of the King.'","'Welcome to my home, ${PLAYER}. I offer you what hospitality I can, though it cannot hope to match that of the King in Minas Tirith. What brings you so far from the White City?'\
\
You tell Sirgon that King Elessar has sent you to help heal the hurts of the war and to prepare the way for his own tour of the kingdom.\
\
'That is a worthy purpose. The war... the war may be ended, but the scars it left behind cut deep. How fare the towns within my purview?'\
\
Reluctantly, you tell Sirgon the people of Glaniath have proposed that he step down as Lord of Lebennin and leave the lordship to his son Faltharan, and show him the tokens they cast for that purpose.","'This tapestry depicting Folca and the Boar was a gift. The Rohirrim hold him in great esteem.'","Captain Thandor hails you in greeting","Sirgon rests on a bench inside his manor, thinking about the tidings you brought to him.","Talk to Sirgon inside his manor","Arvellon is in the centre of Glaniath, waiting for you to return with the tokens cast in support of his proposal.","Sirgon has asked to meet you in his room of keepsakes, to the north, where he will speak with you further.","Sirgon stands in his room of keepsakes, appraising his treasured memories.","'Faltharan should rule in my stead, if the King will have him.'","Talk to Arvellon in the centre of Glaniath, in King's Gondor","Sirgon has suggested that you examine the keepsakes he acquired over a long life at sea.","'This creature crawled upon my deck while we were in port. Now his head hangs upon my wall!'","Sirgon appears to have come to a decision","Sirgon rests on a bench inside the entrance to his manor.","'Speak with Arvellon and see what you think. He should be near the centre of town.'","'These stuffed birds were a wedding gift from an old friend, drowned at sea.'","Sirgon considers the treasured memories in his room of keepsakes.","'Would you believe I found this bear far to the south, in a land of snow and ice? It is true!'","Examine Sirgon's keepsakes and listen to what he has to say about them","'You are welcome to Glaniath, my friend, and on the King's business, no less! It is remarkable how much can change in the matter of mere months!\
\
'The war left its mark upon Lebennin, and I expect it has done the same in other areas of Gondor. But here it marked us deep, for Sirgon our lord was captured by the Haradrim, and while he was freed from their bonds the experience changed him. I fear he is no longer suited for rule, and it would be just for the King to permit him to step down. Faltharan, his son, is fully capable of following his father as Lord of Lebennin.\
\
'I have called for families of Glaniath to cast tokens in favour of this proposal. Will you gather these tokens from the collection boxes around town so Lord Sirgon will see how many families support my proposal?'","'At any rate, the sooner we go to Pelargir the sooner we will return to Minas Tirith with the tidings we sought. We have heard plenty of whispers and rumours, but little in the way of real danger. I suppose that is good, but it is also a pity, for my axe needs swinging!'","Talk to Sirgon in his room of keepsakes","Legolas and Gimli wish to return soon to Minas Tirith with word of what you discovered, but first they wish to consult with Sirgon, Lord of Lebennin.","Collection boxes can be found beside stone buildings on the outskirts of Glaniath.\
\
Arvellon asked you to gather the tokens cast by townspeople of Glaniath in support of his proposal.","'Will you gather tokens from the collection boxes around town so Lord Sirgon will see how many families support my proposal?'","Sirgon nods at you as you approach"},
[2837]={"'My father's reinforcements from the Lonely Mountain have brought their own weapons, but those will not be enough if we are to truly assault Gundabad. Can I ask you to climb the stairs and find the armoury in the Skarháld keep? Bring back some of the swords and axes that are stored there, and we can better supply this fighting force.'","You hear a horn blowing in the distance east of Skarháld, but it ends abruptly","'You are looking for weapons? You will find none here. Several parties of my people armed themselves with swords and axes from the armouries here and set out into the mountains in search of the remaining drakes of the Frost-horde. It is a proud tradition of the Zhélruka to hunt such creatures... but I might have advised against it if I had known an army of Longbeards was soon to arrive!\
\
'Tell the Longbeard prince that if he wants those weapons he will have to wait for my Zhélruka brothers to return victorious from their hunt.'","One of the Zhélruka hunting parties went to the east of Skarháld.","Collect weapons from the eastern armoury inside the Skarháld keep","This armoury has also been emptied of weapons. Tomókh calls you to him","The armoury has been picked clean of weapons by persons unknown","'Tell the Longbeard prince that if he wants those weapons he will have to wait for my Zhélruka brothers to return victorious from their hunt.'","You found the second Zhélruka hunting-party, but they are already slain","Find the second Zhélruka hunting-party somewhere to the north-east","Talk to Tomókh in the eastern armoury inside the Skarháld keep","One of the Zhélruka hunting parties went east of Skarháld.","'There were no weapons in the armoury? Did you try the other one?'","Return the \\qborrowed\\q weapons to Durin at the stable-master in Skarháld","Talk to the Zhélruka drake-hunter east of Skarháld","Durin is waiting by the stable-master in Skarháld for you to return with the weapons the Zhélruka \\qborrowed.\\q","Collected abandoned weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect the abandoned weapons from the slain hunting-party (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durin is waiting by the Skarháld stable-master for you to return with weapons from the armouries.","The Zhélruka cheer the victory","Reinvigourated by the arrival of the Longbeard reinforcements from the Lonely Mountain, Durin wishes to prepare for an assault upon Gundabad, the Mountain-home of Durin's Folk.","Talk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld","'Did you hear that horn blowing? It ended suddenly. I think the Zhélruka hunting parties may have run into some trouble after all, ${PLAYER}. You had better go and bring back their weapons, for it seems they may not need them any longer!\
\
'The horn sounded to the east of Skarháld. I think that is where you will find them.'","The first armoury was empty of weapons. Perhaps some implements of war remain in the other armoury on the eastern side of the Skarháld keep.","'Yes, drake-hunting is a dangerous endeavour. They knew the risks when they set out from Skarháld, the same as us.\
\
'Where did you find them? To the north-east?'","'Some of the Zhélruka have gone into the mountains to hunt the remaining drakes of the Frost-horde? I would say to let them go, and good riddance, but we need those weapons!\
\
'You had better go after them, ${PLAYER}, and save them from their own foolishness. I want them alive so they can hear my reprimands, but more importantly I want the weapons they stole. I have spoken with some of the reinforcements from the Lonely Mountain, and many of their weapons are of poor quality, damaged either from disuse or entirely too much use; there is no middle ground.\
\
'Find the Zhélruka hunting-parties outside Skarháld and bring back those weapons!'","Find the Zhélruka hunting party east of Skarháld and help them slay a drake of the Frost-horde","The western armoury is up the stairs inside the Skarháld keep.","Chapter 1.6: A Proud, But Dangerous, Tradition","'Sound the traditional drake-hunting horn and help us slay whatever answers the call, ${PLAYER}. It waits there for you.'","'Thank you for your help, friend. We will return to Skarháld, but there was another party of drake-hunters with us, and they have not yet come back. We heard their horn blowing some time ago, but it stopped abruptly.\
\
'They continued on to the north-east, if you wish to search in that direction.'","'¿Sí? ¿Qué quieres?'","The second Zhélruka hunting-party continued their hunt to the north-east of the first.","'The second party continued on to the north-east, but I fear they are dead. You had better find out for certain.'","Collect weapons from the western armoury up the stairs inside the Skarháld keep","'Thank you for these, ${PLAYER}. My Longbeards are going to need every weapon on which they can get their hands, and I do not appreciate these Zhélruka raiding the armouries without notice. That practice must end, or they will face my wrath and that of my Longbeards.\
\
'But there is trouble brewing in Skarháld, and I need my most trusted ${CLASS} to help deal with it before the situation gets worse.'","Tomókh has called for your attention inside the eastern armoury inside the Skarháld keep.","The second Zhélruka hunting-party ran afoul of the drakes they sought, and now you should collect the weapons they took from Skarháld."},
[2838]={"The Armour of the Usurper remains where it was left","Faltharan agrees that the Heirs of Castamir might try to steal the Armour of the Usurper, but believes the relic is safe.","Convince Legolas that you are truly <rgb=#00FF00>angry</rgb>","'That day is not yet here, but still you must tell me what brings you to Pelargir. The Armour of the Usurper? Aye, I know it. Angbor of Lamedon sent it to us several moons ago, charging my father with its safekeeping, and so it is kept safe.\
\
'You are welcome to see for yourself, ${PLAYER}. The armoury of Pelargir is to the south of the manor; with my permission the guards will allow you to pass. They are men and women of true hearts and proven loyalty, and they guard the armoury day and night.'","'I have had an idea, ${PLAYER}. If we stage a performance for the benefit of this spy, we might be able to learn if she works for the Heirs of Castamir, and turn that knowledge to our benefit.'\
\
Legolas smiles at you briefly before the Elf adopts a pained expression.","The suspicious onlooker is to the south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Legolas outside the Pelargir Armoury","Legolas stands outside the Pelargir Armoury, pretending to be angry with you.","'The skulking woman watches us from afar.'","Legolas stares at you with his eyes aflame and his fists clenched. He needs your help to show that you are truly <rgb=#00FF00>angry</rgb>.\
\
You will be most convincing if you target the Elf and use the <rgb=#00FF00>Angry</rgb> emote.","Chapter 1.6: True Hearts and Proven Loyalties","Legolas has had an idea.","Cuguril invited you to check on the Armour of the Usurper inside the Pelargir Armoury, as long as you also deal with any of the pests you might find inside.","Cuguril stands watch outside the Pelargir Armoury.","'Gimli and I will meet you back at Sirgon's manor after you have spoken with the spy. Good fortune go with you!'","'I beg your pardon, stranger, but I could not help but notice your argument with that Elf over the way. Did he give you insult? I have seen such as he treat others with disrespect, and often enough that it has become to me a sad indicator that all of that folk believe themselves to be our betters.'\
\
You tell the woman that he took issue with some statements you made about the new Queen of Gondor, and she studies you closely.\
\
'Is that so?' she asks. 'Perhaps you would like to hear my own thoughts on the subject?'","The Pelargir Armoury is to the south of Sirgon's Manor.","'Is that so?' Legolas demands angrily","Walk by the suspicious onlooker to the south-east and see if she speaks to you","'Ho there, halt.'","'You have come at the request of Lord Sirgon and his son? What brings three such as you here?'\
\
You tell Cuguril that supporters of the Heirs of Castamir may seek to steal his armour for their own purposes, and the Lord of Lebennin wants to ensure it is kept safe.\
\
'He need not fear on that account, friend! We take great care to keep unknown folk from entering the armoury. Why, a suspicious woman has been watching us from a distance for the past few days; I have yet to see her today. Rest assured we keep an eye upon her when we do see her skulking about.\
\
'You are welcome to go inside and check on the armour yourself. You and your companions would stick in my memory well enough that I do not think you are the sort we need suspect! In gratitude perhaps you will deal with some of the pests within? We have had something of a rat and crawler problem in recent days.'","Find the Pelargir Armoury south of Sirgon's Manor, in King's Gondor","'You are welcome to go inside and check on the armour yourself. Perhaps you will deal with some of the pests within? We have had something of a rat and crawler problem in recent days.'","Check that the Armour of the Usurper remains inside the Pelargir Armoury","Talk to Aithil south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor","The armoury is watched day and night by a rotating shift of guards","Legolas has begun a dramatic argument for the benefit of the nearby onlooker, and he needs your help to show that you are truly <rgb=#00FF00>angry</rgb>.\
\
You will be most convincing if you target the Elf and use the <rgb=#00FF00>Angry</rgb> emote.","Talk to Cuguril outside the Pelargir Armoury","'You are welcome to see for yourself. The Armoury of Pelargir is to the south of the manor, and is guarded day and night, but with my permission the guards will allow you to pass.'","Defeat pests within the Pelargir Armoury (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Castamir's armour remains where it was left? I told you it was so. But look here!\
\
'The skulking woman is back. She watches us from yonder, pretending that we are not the object of her attention... but it is clear to me she spies upon us even now.'","The guardswoman Cuguril stands watch outside the Pelargir Armoury.","The woman eyes you curiously","Defeated pests within the Pelargir Armoury (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I should have expected no less from such as you!' Legolas exclaims. Then he lowers his voice.\
\
'Now you should stroll most casually in the direction of the skulking spy, my friend. Perhaps she will be interested to speak to you, and if you can draw from her some knowledge of the Heirs of Castamir or their supporters, we will be aided.\
\
'And let there be no hard feelings between us, ${PLAYER}! Such a performance did not come easily for me, but if it serves as effective bait for this suspicious fish it will prove worthwhile. Gimli and I will meet you back at Sirgon's manor after you have spoken with this onlooker. Good fortune go with you!'","The woman Aithil is south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor.","'How dare you?' Legolas exclaims"},
[2839]={"Talk to Arâm at the Black Gate","You should tell Ayorzén that he will have a place in Gondor","'Ayorzén will be given a new start in Gondor in return for the knowledge he can give to us of Mordor. Speak to the waggon-driver Rathnor, and arrange for Ayorzén's passage to the city.'","'Aye, one more passenger to the city should not be hard to manage.'","Mithrandir is outside the Black Gate.","Ayorzén has given you the names of especial terrors in Mordor, and wants you to speak those names to some of the freed Nurnhoth at the Black Gate.","'Sauron may be gone, but his servants were many and they were beings of power and terror. I have not seen anything of Gondor that can hope to stand against even these three, and that is not the full extent of his lieutenants.\
\
'And so I become Ayorzén the Unwilling, and refuse this so-called king's offer of pardon. I will remain between the realms until I taste which way the wind blows, ${PLAYER}. Right now, the breeze is rank, and it comes from Gorgoroth.'","Itli shudders when you ask him about Dulgabêth and clenches his fists.\
\
'I can tell you nothing of him that a dozen others could not. He was the Mouth of Sauron, and his knights rode at his command. They plucked me from my village by the Sea and marched me long leagues to Udûn, where I was put to work at the forges. I only saw the Mouth once, from afar, for he was too busy with Sauron's errands to spend time tormenting the Nurnhoth.\
\
'But Sauron is gone, and if the Mouth had a leash, it is now off him. We should not... we should not be speaking of him here, so close to Mordor. It will bring ill fortune. Speak no more to me of him!'","Aragorn is outside the Black Gate.","'Mordor has been closed to the eyes of Gondor for more than a thousand years, ever since the fall of Durthand and the expulsion of the Thandrim. What transpired beneath the shroud of Gorgoroth remained unknown to us, and it brewed a bitter cup of rumour, and worry, and fear. That was in aid of Sauron's plans, as ever, for he knew the uses of fear better than any creature in this Middle-earth.\
\
'But we have one in our keeping who witnessed the last days of the War of the Ring from the other side. Ayorzén walked in Mordor when the peoples of Gondor and indeed of all Middle-earth could not pass the bounds of that land. What did he see? What does he know? He claims he was involved in high councils of war. Perhaps that is true, and perhaps it is not, but there is no question that he may have knowledge of Sauron's lieutenants that we simply do not.\
\
'Can he be forgiven of his crimes? If he can be so forgiven, he might be given a new life in Gondor in exchange for the information he possesses about Mordor and the power structure in the Black Land after the downfall of Sauron. Speak to Aragorn. It must be he who will forgive Ayorzén of these crimes, if any will.'","'Do you see now? Sauron may be gone, but his servants were many, and they were beings of power and terror. I have not seen anything of Gondor that can hope to stand against even these three, and that is not the full extent of his lieutenants.\
\
'And so I become Ayorzén the Unwilling, and refuse this so-called king's offer of pardon. I will remain between the realms until I taste which way the wind blows, ${PLAYER}. Right now, the breeze is rank, and it comes from Gorgoroth.'","Talk to Hujâ at the Black Gate","Chapter 1.6: Whispers from the Other Side","The waggon-driver Rathnor can be found near the Black Gate.","Talk to Ayorzén outside the Black Gate","Talk to Rathnor the waggon-driver","'I hold that Ayorzén will still be useful to us; indeed, he has already been so, for I think the artifact he stole from Durthang can be made to serve our purposes.\
\
'And further, he has given us an idea of the evils that wait within Gorgoroth. The shadow that hangs on Mordor is too deep for you to pierce it without powerful help, but pierce it you must if you are to combat the villains of whom he spoke.'","Talk to Itli at the Black Gate","'I have already been approached about making a place for the Nurnhoth in Gondor, for their enslavement in Mordor has stirred the hearts of the folk who freed them. I do not know if Ayorzén merits the same treatment, ${PLAYER}. The Nurnhoth were cruelly mistreated by their overlords in Udûn and elsewhere; freedom was just a distant, half-remembered tale to them.\
\
'But Ayorzén led armies against us. He commanded his people to fight during the war, and many good men died on Khundolar blades before the White City. This is not an easy choice to make.'\
\
Aragorn is silent for a moment, considering. Then he comes to a decision.\
\
'The words of Mithrandir have not oft led me astray, ${PLAYER}. Ayorzén will be given a new start in Gondor, in return for the knowledge he can give to us of Mordor. Speak to the waggon-driver, Rathnor, and arrange for Ayorzén's passage to the city.'","Talk to Aragorn outside the Black Gate","'Your people have brought Nurnhoth through the Black Gate and freed them from captivity. I have an exercise for you! Speak these names to them, and ask yourself why I would side with Gondor when there are foes in Gorgoroth such as these still alive, still active, and still angry?\
\
'Speak the name Dulgabêth. Speak the name Ugrukhôr. Speak the name Urudanî. Does Gondor possess such terrors as these? I think it does not.'","Arâm stares at you coldly.\
\
'You should not speak of Urudanî. They say if you speak her name, she hears it and will come. Her kiss is death, her embrace torment. Have we not suffered enough? Let the Stonemaiden slumber, and awaken her not!'","'What is it?'\
\
You tell Ayorzén that the King of Gondor has agreed to a bargain: Ayorzén will be given a home in Gondor and his crimes washed away in exchange for what he knows about the situation in Mordor. The Easterling studies you carefully, and then he breaks into laughter.\
\
'How grand, ${PLAYER}! An offer of pardon from Gondor? I spit at this offer. I am not interested in the charity of this king. I have not yet decided which side in this contest will be the victor. Why then, would I ally myself with any of you? I have seen nothing to prove that Gondor will triumph in the days to come, but I know of many dangers that lurk still in Gorgoroth, waiting.\
\
'Your people have brought Nurnhoth through the Black Gate and freed them from captivity. I have an exercise for you! Speak these names to them, and ask yourself why I would side with Gondor when there are foes in Gorgoroth such as these still alive, still active, and still angry?\
\
'Speak the name Dulgabêth. Speak the name Ugrukhôr. Speak the name Urudanî. Does Gondor possess such terrors as these? I think it does not.'","Ayorzén is outside the Black Gate.","'We have one in our keeping who witnessed the last days of the War of the Ring from the other side. Ayorzén walked in Mordor when the peoples of Gondor and indeed of all Middle-earth could not pass the bounds of that land. What did he see? What does he know? He claims he was involved in high councils of war. Perhaps that is true, and perhaps it is not, but there is no question that he may have knowledge of Sauron's lieutenants that we simply do not.\
\
'Can he be forgiven of his crimes? If he can be so forgiven, he might be given a new life in Gondor in exchange for the information he possesses about Mordor and the power structure in the Black Land after the downfall of Sauron. Speak to Aragorn. It must be he who will forgive Ayorzén of these crimes, if any will.'","Talk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate","Mithrandir believes that Ayorzén's knowledge of Mordor might be made useful by those who adventure within its bounds.","'What's that? There's another fellow that needs passage back to the city? Aye, I'll accommodate him. There won't be much room, but I've got a little more space if folk are willing to sit close.'","Hujâ stares at you with wide eyes, and when he speaks it is no more than a whisper.\
\
'Ugrukhôr... he is the Captain of the Pit. He knows no mercy. He delights in death.'\
\
Tears well in his eyes as he speaks.\
\
'His face... terribly scarred... but not always! They say Sauron punished him... punished him for something. Held him... held him to the Fire!'\
\
Hujâ falls silent and will speak no more, but his trembling persists for some time."},
[2840]={"<rgb=#00FF00>Agree</rgb> with Aithil to preserve your deception","'My scouts have reported smoke on the horizon to the north-west. It is possible Amon Anglebed could be the source of it. That is where you should go if you think to find more supporters of the Heirs. But use caution! These could well prove to be dangerous folk, if they suspect your beliefs do not align with theirs. You should continue to convince them you stand beside them, until you have learned what you need.'","Travel to Amon Anglebed, the beacon outside Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor","'I do not begrudge Elessar his choice of wife! Were he not King, he could marry anyone he wished, and he would have my blessing. But if he is to be King, he should put the needs of Gondor ahead of his heart's call. If Gondor is to have a Queen, she should be a woman of Gondor. Does he not know the history of his own kingdom? Eldacar married a north-woman and caused much bloodshed. Does Elessar desire another Kin-strife?\
\
'The scribes named Castamir \\qthe Usurper\\q for trying to restore Gondor, and he perished for it. But even today there are some who believe in that for which he stood. If you join with them, you may be well-rewarded, and see the return of a King who prizes what Gondor should be.\
\
'One of the beacons of Gondor remains lit, and it casts Castamir's shadow long and far. If you are a friend to those who wish to see it remain so, you will <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb> with us. We must act in the shadows, for now, and keep down our voices; you never know who might be watching us.'","The man raises an eyebrow and stares at you appraisingly","'If it were up to me, I would have shown this woman the blade of my axe and gotten just as many answers, if not more! But Legolas says that would not be wise. Hmmph. Does it matter where the wisdom comes from, if it might be gotten more swiftly one way than by another?\
\
'If you must be the play-acting spy today, so be it! But when it comes to fighting, as it always does, don't be too slow to set aside the lies and pick up your weapon!\
\
'Legolas and I will return to Minas Tirith to tell the King what we learned on this journey, but you won't be coming with us. You have somewhere else to go, I understand!'","Faltharan told you that Amon Anglebed has been kept burning, and may be the beacon about which the skulking woman spoke.","Aithil nods, smiling discreetly","'Gimli and I will return to Minas Tirith with news of what we have learned, but you still have work to do here.'","The beacon remains lit, as Faltharan suspected","Chapter 1.7: Castamir's Shadow","Faltharan is inside his father's manor.","Talk to Maethon by the lit beacon, in King's Gondor","A man stands by the beacon. Perhaps he is the contact about whom you were told, and if you <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb> with him he will reveal himself.","Convinced by your argument with Legolas, the woman Aithil has welcomed you as a supporter of the Heirs of Castamir.","Sirgon's Manor is located to the north of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor.","Return to Sirgon's Manor with what you have learned","'One of the beacons of Gondor remains lit, and it casts Castamir's shadow long and far. If you are a friend to those who wish to see it remain so, you will <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb> with us.'","Legolas and Gimli have come to Sirgon's Manor to await your tidings.","Talk to Legolas inside Sirgon's Manor","<rgb=#00FF00>Agree</rgb> with the man and determine his loyalties","Maethon stands by the burning beacon of Amon Anglebed, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Gimli inside Sirgon's Manor","'Legolas and Gimli told me about the woman you met. What were her words? \\qOne of the beacons of Gondor remains lit, and it casts Castamir's shadow long and far?\\q She may have been speaking in riddles, but I think it is more likely she meant her people keep one of the beacons lit even in the aftermath of the war.\
\
'My scouts have reported smoke on the horizon to the north-west. It is possible Amon Anglebed could be the source of it. That is where you should go if you think to find more supporters of the Heirs.\
\
'But use caution! These could well prove to be dangerous folk, if they suspect your beliefs do not align with theirs. You should continue to convince them you stand beside them, until you have learned what you need.'","Talk to Faltharan in his father's manor","'I have two questions for you, my friend. First, was she convinced by our display, and second, is she a supporter of the Heirs of Castamir, as we supposed?\
\
'Yes to both? Very good, ${PLAYER}. I am sorry it fell to you to play this part, but if she believes your interests are aligned with hers, we may be able to follow this thread to its very source, and learn who now leads the Heirs of Castamir.\
\
'You must keep these folk convinced, my friend, for as long as you are able to do so.'","The woman Aithil, south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, is convinced that you <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb> with the Heirs of Castamir. You should ensure she continues to believe it.","'We will see you after you have learned what you can of these folk, ${PLAYER}.'","'Can I help you with something?' he asks carefully, and you respond by noting that the beacon casts a long shadow, like Castamir did in years past. The man smiles broadly.\
\
'You must be the kindred spirit I was told to expect! What a pleasant surprise! Aithil described you to me, but I did not foresee that one of the King's close personal friends could possibly support our mission... and yet here you are! I need not tell you how useful it would be to have you with us, especially if you still have the ear of the King! I hope you have not aired your true feelings and endangered your friendship with him?\
\
'My name is Maethon, and I have been keeping this beacon lit. It is to be a sign that although the war is over, the fighting is not yet done. The guards at Ost Anglebed try to extinguish it as often as they can, but my friends and I re-light it when their attention wanes; they cannot guard it at all hours.'"},
[2841]={"The ale-keg ran dry after filling two of the mugs, and now you need to find another keg or risk making the dwarves' quarrel worse instead of better!","A keg of ale stands south of the quarrelling dwarves in Skarháld. You have gathered four (mostly) clean mugs and should now fill them from an ale-keg.","Find Imák and calm him down","'It appears nothing was settled after all! You go find these unruly dwarves and get to the bottom of this, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps they will listen to you. If they do not, well... we will swing that axe when we get there!'","Chapter 1.7: Close Quarters","Fill mugs of ale from another ale-keg (2/4)","You remember seeing a keg of ale and clean mugs on this level of Skarháld","Fill mugs of ale from the ale-keg south of the quarrelling dwarves (1/4)","After filling the second mug, the ale-keg runs dry!","Heilar dusts himself off and scowls at Imák","Talk to Imák","Imák the Stout-axe still glowers at Heilar the Longbeard. Durin asked you to ease the tensions among these dwarves, if such a thing is possible.","Bring the mugs of ale to the quarrelling dwarves in the north-west corner","Help Heilar to his feet and find out what happened","'I do not know anything about these Greymauls he mentioned, but his tone of voice was clear. He intended for it to be insulting, so I was insulted. This story of treacherous dwarves must be some fable of the Longbeards. We Stout-axes have our own tales, and no shortage of villains to which I might compare such as he, who speak without thinking!\
\
'He would do well to remember the force of my punch, for if he says anything of the sort to me again he will face my fists once more, and this time I will hold nothing back!'\
\
You ask Imák if there is anything that might be done to put this quarrel behind them, and he nods in the direction of Heilar and the interested onlookers.\
\
'I would accept an apology over a mug of ale, if you were to fetch enough for the four of us. I find that usually helps.'","'You want to know what happened? I said two words, little more than that, and turned to go. That treacherous slime knocked me down when my back was turned! He calls himself a Stout-axe, but I know what he really is! He spent so long in Mordor... he was a willing servant of Sauron, or I am an Elf!\
\
'I called him a Greymaul, what of it? He shows his true nature with such a cowardly strike! I wager all the Stout-axes have some Greymaul blood in them, and it wouldn't surprise me if the Zhélruka did too! Yes, some of the Greymauls must have escaped Durin's judgement, and their descendants probably intermingled with the other dwarf families. It would not surprise me to learn that Greymaul blood might have led to the crimes and failings of even the Dourhands!'","Tensions run high as Stout-axes, Zhélruka, and Longbeards quarrel at Skarháld. Durin tasked you with easing these tensions, if such a thing is possible.","Talk to Heilar","You fill one of the mugs with ale","You pass out the mugs of ale, and the dwarves set aside their differences (for now)","Find Gílpi and calm him down","Talk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld","'You were able to smooth things over with the quarrelling dwarves? I expected no less, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'But now there is something else. Isn't there always?'","'You say you have it well in hand? I expected nothing else, my friend!\
\
'If you cannot make these dwarves forget their quarrel, I fear no one can.'","Fill mugs of ale from another ale-keg (3/4)","You found another ale-keg in Skarháld and can now fill the last of the mugs you collected.","The quarrelling dwarves are two levels up from the stable-master at Skarháld, in the north-west corner, waiting for you to return with the mugs of ale you promised.","Collected clean mugs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tensions run high as Stout-axes, Zhélruka, and Longbeards quarrel at Skarháld.","Talk to Venko","'While you were away, a brawl broke out on the upper level. I do not know the precise cause of it, but it seems there is some resentment on the part of the Zhélruka and the Stout-axes here at Skarháld. When I climbed up to investigate, the matter had been resolved, but....'\
\
Even as Durin speaks, you hear shouting from up the stairs.\
\
'There! You hear them? It appears nothing was settled after all! You go find these unruly dwarves and get to the bottom of this, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps they will listen to you. If they do not, well... we will swing that axe when we get there!'","In order to help ease the tensions among the quarrelling dwarves, you have decided to fetch four clean mugs and fill them with ale from one of the kegs at Skarháld.","The brawling dwarves can be found to the north-west and up two levels from the stable-master in Skarháld.","'Find these unruly dwarves and get to the bottom of this, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps they will listen to you. If they do not, well... we will swing that axe when we get there!'","Happily, this ale-keg is nearly full and you are able to pour a third mug","Fill mugs of ale from the ale-keg south of the quarrelling dwarves (0/4)","'I saw it all. They were grumbling at each other for a good while, mostly about imagined slights, I expect, but before long they were each at a full bellow. Heilar called Imák \\qGreymaul filth\\q as he turned to go, and that is when Imák knocked him down.\
\
'I do not know what he meant by that, but he is fortunate Imák used his fists and not his axe. I might have done worse.'","A keg of ale stands south of the quarrelling dwarves in Skarháld. You have gathered four (mostly) clean mugs and should now fill them from the ale-keg.","You fill the last of your mugs from the ale-keg","Durin is waiting by the stable-master in Skarháld for you to return.","'Mugs of ale? Aye, that should help them set aside their differences... while they are drinking, anyway.'","The arrival of the large Longbeard force has escalated the tensions between the dwarf-clans at Skarháld, and Durin has asked you to try and resolve the brewing conflict.","Collect clean mugs at Skarháld (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2842]={"'Glóin is right. The two of you have leave to go with them in search of the Gundabad raiding-party. But you will need to collect some supplies before you depart.'","Imák and Venko can be found two levels up from the stable-master in Skarháld, in the north-west corner.","Bring the supplies to Glóin by the stable-master at Skarháld","'Ah, there you are.'","'In the interest of setting aside our differences, I will do as Durin requests, if Imák desires to do the same. I will venture to the Wells of the Langflood in pursuit of this raiding party... but only if you come with us as well, ${PLAYER}. Let Durin's trusted friend be a part of this errand too, and perhaps he will be more interested in its successful outcome, and our survival.'","'So you are ready to depart for the Wells of the Langflood? I know very little of that region, but I understand Glóin journeyed there during the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, when he was very young. I am sure he will tell you anything you may need to know of that land.\
\
'I will await word of the raiding-party when you find it, and then we will turn our attention to the place from which it came: Gundabad, the Mountain-home of my people. For too long has it been kept by the Orcs, but their residency will soon come to an end!\
\
'One more thing, ${PLAYER}. Keep a watchful eye on the Stout-axe and Zhélruka with whom you travel. They may not wish you ill, not directly, but they may treat you dishonestly if it serves their purposes. The Wells of Langflood are west of here, accessible by a narrow pass in the southern cliffs, east of the broken Rushgate. Journey there boldly, but with caution in your eye, and find this raiding-party before it can do more harm.'","Talk to Glóin by the path leading into Misthallow","Talk to Imák of the Stout-axes in Skarháld","Durin's scouts have reported the presence of a raiding-party from Gundabad near the Wells of Langflood, and he thinks he may have found a solution to more than one of the problems that troubles him.","Chapter 1.8: A Watchful Eye","'Speak first to Durin, and then we will depart for the Wells of the Langflood.'","'Durin wants us to go face a raiding-party from Gundabad? I see the workings of his mind, and I tell you they are not as subtle as he thinks them to be! If Imák and I prove victorious against these Orcs, then the few folk who live along the Langflood will be made safer, and if we do not, well, Durin has only lost a Stout-axe and a Zhélruka in the effort. He will not mourn us overmuch, Imák, will he?\
\
'In the interest of setting aside our differences, I will do as Durin requests, if Imák will do the same. I will venture to the Wells of the Langflood in pursuit of this raiding party... with two conditions only.\
\
'The first is this: you must come with us, ${PLAYER}. You are a close friend of the Longbeard prince, and he would not send you into danger without reason. If you were to perish, I believe he would be aggrieved. So I ask that you come with us in search of this raiding-party. My second condition is that Durin send a Longbeard as well. Why should Stout-axes and Zhélruka go into danger when Durin's Folk remain behind in safety?\
\
'Those are my conditions. Bring them to Durin with haste, ${PLAYER}, and see what this Longbeard prince has to say.'","'Why has the Longbeard prince not charged any of his people with this mission, Venko? That is what I want to know.'","'You found the supplies for our expedition? Very good. At a young age I learned the importance of preparing for a journey, and my appreciation of such preparation has only increased with every passing year. You do not want to lack some crucial tool in the middle of the wilderness, I can tell you that! But you know that as well as I, my friend.\
\
'I spoke to Imák and Venko while you were gathering up the supplies, and they said they will meet us at the pass that leads to the Wells of Langflood, far to the west of Skarháld, east and south of the broken Rushgate. They were not very happy about it; they believed their conditions would change Durin's mind and keep anyone from seeking out this raiding-party, but it was not so. Speak to Durin and then we will join our new companions.'","You have met up with your travelling companions near the pass to the Wells of Langflood","'We are all arrived, my friend. This is the path that will take us to the foggy basin of Misthallow, through which runs the tributaries of a familiar river. The folk of these northern lands named it Langflood, but you would call it the Great River, or Anduin.\
\
'The raiding-party from Gundabad was spotted somewhere near the Wells of Langflood. That is where we must go.'","Glóin is by the stable-master in Skarháld.","A bag of foodstuffs can be found two levels above the Skarháld stable-master.\
Climbing gear can be found three levels above the Skarháld stable-master\
Flint and camping supplies can be found two levels above the Skarháld stable-master.","'Durin expects the two of us to go in search of a raiding-party from Gundabad? Is that what you are saying, ${PLAYER}? I cannot fail to notice that he has charged a Stout-axe and a Zhélruka with this mission, rather than any of the large number of his own folk that have come to Skarháld. I find that most curious, Venko, do you not?\
\
'I believe the Longbeard prince is seeking to get rid of us!'","Glóin has made it known he wishes to speak with you and Durin at the stable-master in Skarháld.","'My scouts bring word of a raiding-party set loose from Gundabad upon the inhabitants of Misthallow and the Floodfells. There are few enough of those, but if the Orcs move in those lands they will trouble any army that seeks to advance upon Gundabad. Someone must deal with this raiding-party... and I believe we might solve two problems with a single stroke! Why not send some of the troublesome Zhélruka or Stout-axes to confront this raiding-party? They will realize their true quarrel is with the Orcs, and during their absence some measure of peace may return to Skarháld. What were their names? Imák? Venko? Bring them this news of this task, and invite them to adventure on behalf of their people.'","Talk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld","The way to the Wells of Langflood from the Grey Mountains is west of Skarháld, accessible by a narrow pass in the southern cliffs east of the broken Rushgate.","Collected the bag of climbing gear","'They will only undertake this errand if you go with them? This is outrageous, ${PLAYER}! No one else has assumed the mantle of leadership here at Skarháld, and I do so only unwillingly, but if I make such a command as this it should be followed, and without question! These dwarves will cause only trouble for me and mine, and if I want them well away from Skarháld then away from it they shall be, without negotiation!\
\
'But what is it, Glóin? You have something to say?'","Imák of the Stout-axes is in the north-west corner, two levels up from the stable-master in Skarháld.","Talk to Glóin by the stable-master in Skarháld","Imák and Venko stop drinking as you approach","Venko of the Zhélruka is in the north-west corner, two levels up from the stable-master in Skarháld.","'Yes, Durin, I have something to say. I have seen a thing or two during my long life, and it has taught me much. I was among the youngest of the dwarves to fight at Azanulbizar... did you know that? Every dwarf-clan sent representatives to fight in that war, Durin, not just the Longbeards. Even so youthful as I was, I knew that each family fought for more than just their own glory; they fought for the survival of all dwarves.\
\
'You should not send Zhélruka only, or Stout-axes only, in pursuit of this Orc raiding-party. Neither should you keep your Longbeards in reserve, for that speaks poorly both of you and of them! A Longbeard should go, and I volunteer myself. Let ${PLAYER} adventure there too, not just because Imák and Venko request it but because ${PLAYER} is a loyal friend and true, and will see this raiding-party destroyed. These are words of wisdom, Durin, and with age and experience they will come naturally to you. For now let them come from your friends and allies, for they want the same as you and will not lead you astray.\
\
'${PLAYER}, will you gather the supplies we will need for an excursion into the Wells of Langflood? You will find satchels of foodstuffs, climbing gear, and assorted other supplies two or three levels up in Skarháld. While you do that I will tell Imák and Venko that we will be travelling companions, for the good of Skarháld and all the dwarves.'","Glóin is at the entrance to the pass that leads to the Wells of Langflood from the Grey Mountains, east and south of the broken Rushgate.","Return to Imák and Venko in the north-west corner, two levels up from the Skarháld stable-master","Find your travelling companions to the west of Skarháld, at the pass to the Wells of Langflood east and south of the broken Rushgate","Talk to Venko of the Zhélruka in Skarháld","Collect the bag of camping gear in Skarháld, two levels up","Durin is by the stable-master in Skarháld.","'You know I desire to take back Gundabad for my people, and it will not be long before I drive the Orcs from that sacred mountain. But I am no fool, ${PLAYER}! Too often the hasty stroke goes astray, or so they say, and I know any assault upon the Mountain-home must be carefully planned. To that end, I sent a number of scouts to the Wells of the Langflood, swift and true, and they have now returned.\
\
'But they return with news not from the foot of Gundabad, but from the lands to the south! They bring word of a raiding-party set loose from Gundabad upon the inhabitants of Misthallow and the Floodfells. There are few enough of those, but if the Orcs move in those lands they will trouble any army that seeks to advance upon Gundabad. Someone must deal with this raiding-party.\
\
'Do you know something, ${PLAYER}? I believe we might solve two problems with a single stroke! Why not send some of the troublesome Zhélruka or Stout-axes to confront this raiding-party? They will realize their true quarrel is with the Orcs, and during their absence some measure of peace may return to Skarháld. What were their names? Imák? Venko? Bring them the news of this task, and invite them to adventure on behalf of their people.'","'I will await word of the raiding-party when you find it, and then we will turn our attention to the place from which it came: Gundabad, the Mountain-home of my people. For too long has it been kept by the Orcs, but their residency will soon come to an end!\
\
'One more thing, ${PLAYER}. Keep a watchful eye on the Stout-axe and Zhélruka with whom you travel. They may not wish you ill, not directly, but they may treat you dishonestly if it serves their purposes. The Wells of Langflood are west of here, accessible by a narrow pass in the southern cliffs, east of the broken Rushgate. Journey there boldly, but with caution in your eye, and find this raiding-party before it can do more harm.'","Collected the bag of camping gear","Collect the bag of climbing gear in Skarháld, three levels up","Collect the bag of foodstuffs in Skarháld, two levels up","Durin is waiting by the Skarháld stable-master to hear that Imák and Venko will go in search of the raiding-party in the Wells of Langflood.","Collected the bag of foodstuffs","'What is it, Glóin? You have my respect and for that I give you my ear.'"},
[2843]={"Residents of Ost Anglebed can be found throughout the city if you wish to hand out the parchments, <rgb=#00FF00>or</rgb> you can burn Maethon's parchments in the nearby brazier.","Pick up <rgb=#00FF00>either</rgb> of the barrels north of the fountain and carry it to Maethon, below the cliffs south of the eastern entrance to the city","Wait for Maethon to leave before you begin his errand","Chapter 1.8: The Imposter","Ladben asked you to bring the container of beacon oil to Halwen for safekeeping. Halwen keeps watch over the supplies near the north-east fountain in Ost Anglebed.","Pick up the beacon oil at Amon Anglebed","'What do you need, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Halwen that Ladben asked for you to bring him a barrel of weapons so he could rearm the guards of Ost Anglebed and keep troublemakers from re-lighting the beacon. Halwen nods.\
\
'That has been a real problem of late, and they're using so much oil! What if we had need of it? You can of course bring him the weapons, my friend. There's a barrel of high quality weapons just on the other side of the fountain. Wait, don't go just yet! There's also a barrel of rusty old implements right next to it. Be careful not to bring the wrong one!'","Talk to Halwen by the supplies near the north-east fountain in Ost Anglebed","Collect Maethon's parchments from the crate outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed","After you deliver the beacon oil, you hear someone whispering your name","Return to Maethon at the lit beacon of Amon Anglebed","'Of course you can bring him the weapons, my friend. There's a barrel of high quality weapons just on the other side of the fountain. Wait, don't go just yet! There's also a barrel of rusty old implements right next to it. Be careful not to bring the wrong one!'","'We need to distribute those papers! I stashed them in a crate outside the steps to the Hall of Ost Anglebed. Retrieve them and hand them out to the people of the city!'","A guardsman of Ost Anglebed, Ladben, stands by the lit beacon.","Maethon is missing. In his place stands a guard of Ost Anglebed","'I am grateful for your assistance, my friend, as we all are, or will be, when you meet the rest of us. And I think it will be soon, for there is to be a meeting!\
\
'Our plans have accelerated, and the time to act is approaching!'","'¡Aquí!'","'Maybe you can do me a favour? Bring this beacon oil to Halwen for safekeeping. If we store the oil further away, that may prevent these villains from lighting the beacon every time we douse it. At least it will be made more inconvenient for them.\
\
'Halwen guards the stores by the north-east fountain, in Ost Anglebed.'","Maethon admires the high quality weapons you have brought for the Heirs of Castamir","Talk to Maethon below the cliff south of the eastern entrance of Ost Anglebed","Maethon sees the rusty implements and shrugs. 'Better than nothing!' he says","'Sorry I didn't meet you at the beacon, but Ladben was sniffing around.\
\
'The guards really trust you, don't they? It was truly a stroke of good fortune that sent you to us! If you tell Halwen you need a barrel of weapons, I am certain she would give it to you, and happily! Delivering papers is one thing, but we will need weapons if we are to carry out our plans; eventually it will come to fighting. It always does! At least we will know we are in the right, when it comes.\
\
'When you have the barrel of weapons, bring it to me outside the eastern entrance of the city, below the cliffs to the south. Hold on! Wait for me to leave before you speak to Halwen. We do not want to be too suspicious.'","Halwen believed your story that Ladben needs a barrel of weapons, and she told you to take one from the other side of the fountain. She warned you that there is a barrel of rusty weapons there as well, so be careful not to bring Ladben weapons of poor quality.","Eager to make use of the help you have offered, Maethon has a number of tasks for you to complete on behalf of the Heirs of Castamir.","Maethon stashed a number of parchments to distribute on behalf of the Heirs of Castamir in a crate outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed, to the north-east.","'I know you! You performed a great many deeds throughout the kingdom during the war, and your name is spoken of with reverence. It's... that ${RACE}... something. ${PLAYER}? Yes, that's right.\
\
'You don't know anything about the lighting of this beacon, do you? No, you wouldn't. It's just that these troublemakers keep setting it afire whenever we extinguish it, and it's not supposed to be lit except in dire need. Has no one told these miscreants the war is over?\
\
'Maybe you can do me a favour? Bring this beacon oil to Halwen for safekeeping. If we store the oil further away, that may prevent these villains from lighting the beacon every time we douse it. At least it will be made more inconvenient for them.\
\
'Halwen guards the stores by the north-east fountain, in Ost Anglebed.'","Distribute Maethon's parchments in support of the Heirs of Castamir to residents of Ost Anglebed, or burn the parchments in the nearby brazier","Talk to Maethon by the stairs","Maethon stands below the cliff south of the eastern entrance to Ost Anglebed.","Maethon stands beside the stairs to the Hall of Ost Anglebed, calling for you in hushed tones.","Talk to Ladben at the lit beacon of Amon Anglebed","Maethon makes himself scarce so you can accomplish his goal.","Residents of Ost Anglebed can be found throughout the city if you wish to hand out the parchments, or you can burn Maethon's parchments in the nearby brazier.","Halwen stands by the supplies near the north-east fountain in Ost Anglebed.","'If we are to advance this cause, we need people to know that Elessar does not speak for all of Gondor. I have written a number of parchments proclaiming that Balakhôr survived the war, and he marshals a force that will rise up against Elessar and his Elf-queen; the people of Gondor need to ready themselves for the coming conflict.'\
\
You ask Maethon where Balakhôr has hidden himself to prepare, and he waves away your question.\
\
'There will be time later to discuss it. For now we need to distribute those papers! I stashed them in a crate outside the steps to the Hall of Ost Anglebed. Retrieve them and hand them out to the people of the city!'","Maethon's parchments quickly turn to ash in the heat of the brazier","Maethon will want to hear about your efforts on behalf of the Heirs of Castamir. He should still be at the lit beacon of Amon Anglebed.","Distribute Maethon's parchments in support of the Heirs of Castamir to residents of Ost Anglebed, <rgb=#00FF00>or</rgb> burn the parchments in the nearby brazier"},
[2844]={"Enter the building by the fountain in the northern half of Linhir and attend the meeting","'What tidings have I of King Elessar? Can it be you have not already heard?\
\
'He has departed the White City and begins a tour of his kingdom. It may be a few weeks, but he will be coming here if you wish to see him!'","You should find a gossipmonger in Linhir and learn if Elessar has left Minas Tirith","'Go to the northern half of the town of Linhir and knock on the bronze door opposite the fountain. My name will get you inside. I will see you there!'","This is the building Maethon described","You should enter the building by the fountain in the northern half of Linhir and attend the meeting.","Talk to the gossipmonger inside the eastern entrance to Linhir","'Today we were allies, ${PLAYER}. The next time we meet it will not be so. This is the only warning I will give to you. Gondor will pay for the death of Tumúldo. A thousand times over it will pay. Do not stand in my way.'","'My husband and I were at sea when Balakhôr summoned us to join his fleet as he besieged Gondor. Instead we quit the war and sailed for home, and so were we robbed of our chance to spit upon his corpse; but not before he took something else from me, for my youngest brother died there in service to the Scourge. It meant we were near at hand when the uprising began, and when the waves receded, the Kindred of the Coins ruled in Umbar, and the Heirs of Castamir were only a foetid memory.\
\
'Tumúldo and I swore to fight for the Kindred, and fight we have, but I was not certain that Gondor would have to die until this day. Now, however... I am sure of it. The Sea Shadow hates Gondor, and he has chosen the manner of its doom: the Song of Waves and Wind will spell the end of Elessar's Gondor, and you would be wise to leave the kingdom before it does.'\
\
Nakási falls briefly silent, as if waiting for Tumúldo to speak, but he is dead. She turns cold eyes upon you.\
\
'Today we were allies, ${PLAYER}. The next time we meet it will not be so. This is the only warning I will give to you. Gondor will pay for the death of Tumúldo. A thousand times over it will pay. Do not stand in my way.'","Maethon described the location where the supporters of the Heirs of Castamir intend to meet. It is a dwelling in the northern half of the city of Linhir, opposite a fountain and with a bronze door.","Talk to Nakási outside Linhir","Find the entrance to the dwelling in the northern half of Linhir where supporters of the Heirs of Castamir intend to meet","The Linhir gossipmonger has news, and can be found just inside the eastern entrance to Linhir, in King's Gondor.","Chapter 1.9: Kindred Spirits","Maethon told you supporters of the Heirs of Castamir are to meet soon in a secret place in Linhir, and he invited you to attend. This may be a chance to learn more of their plans!","'You are welcome to attend the meeting, my new friend. Many of those who share our way of thinking will be in attendance, and they will be eager to meet you!\
\
'Go to the northern half of the town of Linhir and knock on the bronze door opposite the fountain. My name will get you inside. I will see you there!'","Nakási is outside Linhir, south of the eastern entrance."},
[2846]={"Bring the scorpion stingers to Girhâzi in Iridír","Join Khôltekh outside the brigand camp of Bidrokh-nûn","Defeat Ordâkhai in Ambarûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have agreed to help my brother with the task given to him by the ruler of Iridír, ${PLAYER}, but I wanted first to speak to you about another matter.\
\
'I heard from the Dumûri warrior Surdûsha that you and her friend Rahâzi protected the life of an Elf-warden in the northern reaches of Ambarûl. Is it true?'\
\
You describe your meeting with the Elf-warden Shanthar at the grove of Arwáth, and what he said to you about his people, the Kintai.\
\
'I would be most interested to learn more about the Kintai. Did he say others of his kind live along the Ikorbân River? Perhaps we will encounter more of them as we continue our journey.'","Talk to Sigileth in Iridír","Only at this bridge may the Ikorbân River be safely crossed, lending it much importance","'I have given the members of your travelling company a number of tasks to complete that will prove their friendship to the Ikorbâni. Speak to them around the village and you will see that these tasks are not for the benefit of Iridír alone, but will also serve you well on your own mission.\
\
'As for you, ${PLAYER}, I would ask that you scout the eastern side of the Wrackwade, the crossing of the Ikorbân River at the camp of Sûru to the south. The Ordâkhai fled that way when we reclaimed Iridír, but they might threaten to return if it is not watched.'","Girhâzi's trust is not easily gained, for she and her people have long memories.","Girhâzi gave a number of tasks to your travelling companions for them to complete in order to earn the trust of her people, and to learn valuable information that will benefit your own mission in Ambarûl.","'Girhâzi assigned to each member of the company a task by which they might prove they are friends to Iridír, but she gave me no such challenge. What am I supposed to do while everyone else proves their worth, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'I cannot simply wait for everyone to complete their tasks! I have spoken already with Sirgon, and the two of us will scout the south-eastern road that leads out of Ambarûl. You are welcome to come with us and see if Azagath and Nakási took that road. Perhaps we will find them and shorten the duration of our journey, bringing about an unexpected but satisfying conclusion while it has still just begun!'","'I understand the tasks I gave to you and your travelling companions have been completed? Perhaps the rulers of Umbar will prove useful allies to me after all.'\
\
Girhâzi takes the scorpion stingers from you and lightly tests one of them with her teeth. She spits a drop of glistening venom onto the ground.\
\
'I am satisfied, ${PLAYER}. I will help you in any way I can. My folk are at your service, and you will have the hospitality of Iridír, such as it is in these days of strife.'","Scout the road from Ambarûl to Urash Dâr, south-east of Iridír","Defeated Ordâkhai in Ambarûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated brigands in Ambarûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Your companions have been given a number of places to scout and enemies to defeat there: at the eastern side of the Wrackwade in the camp of Sûru, an Ordâkhai camp at Eshadur across the river, a brigand camp to the south-east, and the road to Urash Dâr.","Defeat brigands in Ambarûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Eshadur has been occupied by the Ordâkhai, and they prepare for war","Chapter 10.11: The Lessons of Memory","Recent quakes have blocked the road to Urash Dâr","Brigands established camps along the path that climbs the rocky slope","Talk to Rothog in Iridír","Talk to Khôltekh in Iridír","Girhâzi waits for your successful return in Iridír.","'The warrior-woman who rules this village knows strength when she sees it before her, ${PLAYER}. She has challenged Rothog to slay Ordâkhai at their encampment across the river to the south-west, from where they might threaten her people. She says that place was called Eshadur.\
\
'I told her it will be done, quickly and well. My khopeshes hunger for the blood of Ordâkhai, for they tasted it during the Sea-stone Mutiny and it has been too long since they drank their fill! Húrshauk, too, will rejoice to be set loose within the encampment, but he will have to move with speed if he thinks to outpace his master!'","Collect stingers from usan-kûni scorpions in Ambarûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Join Rothog outside the Ordâkhai camp at Eshadur","'You expected me to chafe against the task assigned to me by the chieftain of Iridír? No, I will not, for I understand the reasoning that lies behind it.\
\
'Girhâzi tests whether the Kindred of the Coins will respond to her own needs, or if we seek only to do what personally benefits each of us. This is something with which I am familiar, for I have conducted similar tests of my own to assess the loyalty of those who serve me and my various interests.\
\
'Girhâzi is troubled by brigands to the south-east of Iridír, at a place named Bidrokh-nûn. It will be advantageous to us to help her with this problem, and we can also keep open our eyes when there we venture. If Balakhâd or his potential helper Sadûkh came this way, they might be hiding among the brigands. Do you see how completing Girhâzi's task might help us with our own?'","'I have given the members of your travelling company a number of tasks to complete that will prove their friendship to the Ikorbâni. Speak to them around the village and you will see that these tasks are not for the benefit of Iridír alone, but will also serve you well on your own mission.\
\
'As for you, ${PLAYER}, I would ask that you scout the eastern side of the Wrackwade, the crossing of the Ikorbân River by the camp of Sûru to the south. The Ordâkhai fled that way when we reclaimed Iridír, but they might threaten to return if it is not watched.'","Talk to Belondor in Iridír","'I have given the members of your travelling company a number of tasks to complete that will prove their friendship to the Ikorbâni. Speak to them around the village and you will see that these tasks are not for the benefit of Iridír alone, but will also serve you well on your own mission.\
\
'As for you, ${PLAYER}, I would ask that you scout the eastern side of the Wrackwade to the south, in the camp of Sûru. The Ordâkhai fled that way when we reclaimed Iridír, but they might threaten to return if it is not watched.'","Collected scorpion stingers in Ambarûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Corudan in Iridír","'The ruler of Iridír tasked me and my sister with collecting stingers from the usan-kûni scorpions that lurk to the east of the village or across the river to the south-west. It seems such stingers can be put to a number of medicinal uses by the Ikorbâni, and Girhâzi desires to restock their supply. She cautioned us that the creatures possess great reserves of patience; they might lie in wait for hours, hidden from careless observation, and strike without any warning.\
\
'Despite the danger, we are, of course, willing to help.'","Scout the eastern side of the Wrackwade in the camp of Sûru to the south"},
[2847]={"Sigileth refuses the gift","Offer a pillow to Khôltekh","Chapter 10.12: The Short Road and the Long","Your task complete, you can now rest for the night in the village of Iridír. Sleeping mats for this purpose can be found on the western side of the lodge.","Prepare your sleeping mat on the western side of the lodge in the village of Iridír","'I did not sleep well in the night, ${PLAYER}, but I have determined it will not adversely affect my morning. We have a long day of travel ahead of us, for Azagath must be ahead of us. He gets further away with every passing hour, and we have already spent enough of them sleeping, or trying to sleep.'","'It has been years since I slept among pillows, ${PLAYER}. I do not think I would find that as comfortable as once I did. You may keep them. Perhaps my brother will accept an extra.'","Your own sleep disturbed by troubled dreams, you hope that your companions are feeling more rested than you. They can be found at the entrance of Iridír to the north of the lodge.","'I have already given my thanks to Girhâzi for the accommodations, ${PLAYER}. I have not awoken so refreshed in many months! Did you sleep as well as I?'\
\
You tell Corudan that you managed to rest for a few hours. You ask him if he dreamed at all, and he shakes his head.\
\
'At the very least I remember nothing. I believe my sleep was untroubled.'","Offer a pillow to Rothog","Offer a pillow to Corudan","Rothog refuses the gift","Rahâzi gives you a number of pillows to distribute among your companions","You awaken from disturbing dreams, the memory of them fading into nothingness","Rahâzi is on the eastern side of her mother's lodge in Iridír.","Your sleeping mat awaits on the western side of the lodge in the village of Iridír.","Talk to Sigileth at the entrance of Iridír","You set down the excess pillows and prepare your sleeping mat for the night, making it as comfortable as you can.","Corudan accepts the gift","'We will not speak of it here. Let us later discuss our dreams in private.'","Your own sleep disturbed by troubling dreams, you hope that your companions are feeling more rested than you. They can be found at the entrance of Iridír to the north of the lodge.","'I believe my sleep was untroubled.'","'My mother says you are to rest for the night before leaving Iridír? The sleeping mats on the west side of the lodge have been prepared for the use of your company, but I cannot promise they will be comfortable!\
\
'Here, I will give you feather pillows to distribute among your companions. I gave one to the man Sirgon already, for he stood near when my mother gave me the command. He was grateful for it; so grateful my face reddened with embarrassment. They are just pillows, and I would not describe them as soft! Still, they should be better than nothing at all, and help you and your friends awake rested for your journey. The road through Khûd Zagin is rocky, hot, and uncomfortable; spending one night in Iridír as my mother's guests should not be!'","Talk to Rahâzi on the eastern side of the lodge in Iridír","Offer a pillow to Sigileth","Your companions throughout the village of Iridír may welcome the gift of pillows, or they may not.","'Speak with Rahâzi on the eastern side of the lodge and she will tell you where your companions can rest, and rest well, before you depart. If you should dream, rue it not! The dreamless sleep holds no wisdom.'","Rest for the night on your sleeping mat in the lodge within Iridír","Offer a pillow to Belondor","Khôltekh refuses the gift","Girhâzi has agreed to provide you with supplies and assistance as you prepare to take the necessary longer road in pursuit of Azagath.","Talk to Sirgon at the entrance of Iridír","'A feather pillow? That is very kind of our hosts, ${PLAYER}. Thank you very much for this. I have not had much occasion to rest comfortably in recent weeks.\
\
'How odd to speak so, my friend! I have not forgotten how I rued the time of my recovery in Leafshade's grove, when I awoke from my wounded stupor as Nestinanessornë! Then I had nothing but time to rest, and the inactivity cut deeply! Now there is little time to rest, but this pillow will help me to make the most of it.'","Talk to Corudan at the entrance of Iridír to the north of the lodge","'Something has troubled you, ${PLAYER}; I see it on your face. Your sleep was troubled by dreams?'\
\
You nod and ask if it was the same for Sigileth. She looks around at the folk gathered nearby.\
\
'We will not speak of it here. Let us later discuss our dreams in private.'","'Here, I will give you feather pillows to distribute among your companions. I would not describe them as soft, but they should be better than nothing at all, and help you and your friends awake rested for your journey. The road through Khûd Zagin is rocky, hot, and uncomfortable; spending one night in Iridír as my mother's guests should not be!'","Belondor accepts the gift","'If your prey was set upon journeying further east, he will have found the road into Urash Dâr blocked by landslides caused by the recent quake. He would need to travel south instead, a longer road and a harder one through the rocky land beside the desert, but necessary. If you go that way in pursuit of him, I will see that you have the provisions and supplies you need for the journey.\
\
'Speak with Rahâzi on the eastern side of the lodge and she will tell you where your companions can rest, and rest well, before you depart. If you should dream, rue it not! The dreamless sleep holds no wisdom.'","'Feather pillows? Huh.'\
\
Rothog takes a pillow from you and tests it with one hand. The burlap material tears and a few brown feathers fall from the rip. The half-troll stuffs the feathers back inside and hands it back to you.\
\
'I do not think I have much use for such a thing as this, ${PLAYER}. You can keep it. I will follow the example of my friend Húrshauk, who sleeps anywhere he wishes and requires nothing.'","'A feather pillow? Perhaps some others among the Temámir would accept such a gift, but I do not look for comfort when I rest during the evening hours.\
\
'I sleep with an eye open when at home in the Shoreward Stone. I cannot imagine sleeping in an unfamiliar land with more than that eye closed, ${PLAYER}. Keep your pillows!'","You lie down on the sleeping mat and prepare to rest, giving your journey south into Khûd Zagin a good beginning.","'Thank you for this pillow, ${PLAYER}. My manor-house in Umbar Baharbêl has dozens of pillows, artfully arranged by Mêshka throughout every room, but they are far away. This one will transport me back home while I sleep, and no doubt give to me pleasant dreams of my home and my hearth. I will see Mêshka when I close my eyes.\
\
'You may need to shake me awake in the morning with some force, ${PLAYER}. I may not want to leave her embrace, awakening on the hard ground of Iridír. This is not to speak poorly of the hospitality of its people, you understand. But none can compete with even the most fleeting dream of my wife!'"},
[2848]={"Make your way through Eryn Lasgalen to the Forest Gate in the west","Gandalf stands at the Forest Gate on the western edge of Eryn Lasgalen, waiting to speak with you.","'Take care on your journey, my friend, and beware!'","Make your way to the entrance of the Beorninghús south-west of the Forest Gate","'I propose that we travel together, ${PLAYER}, and bring the Black Book with us on a new journey away from the stones of Skarháld. But where shall we take it? I suggest a place of both comfort and strength, perhaps a lodge warmed by a roaring hearth and guarded by a family of stern temperament, but who deal kindly with their friends?\
\
'Yes, I speak of Grimbeorn and his folk, ${PLAYER}! The Beorninghús will be well-suited for my study of the Black Book, and we shall be assuredly very safe within its wooden walls. Grimbeorn will require some convincing before he allows us to stay, but like his father Beorn before him, if we spark his curiosity he will open his doors to us.\
\
'The direct road south is not open to us, but that is no great hindrance. Let us return to Eryn Lasgalen on our way to the Beorning-lands, for I wish to consult with Thranduil of the wood about several small matters. If he has not already done so, we should ask him to open the Forest Gate once again.\
\
'You should bid farewell to Durin before we leave for Felegoth. And ${PLAYER}? Tell the young prince to ignore the voice in his heart that compels him to seek Thafar-gathol. That place is lost, if ever it existed at all, and he should put it from his mind. It is not for him.'","Talk to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","Talk to Gandalf at the Forest Gate in Eryn Lasgalen","The Beorninghús is located in the Beorning-lands, south-west of the Forest Gate.","'We should make for Felegoth, in Eryn Lasgalen, and ask Thranduil to open the Forest Gate.'","The Forest Gate stands open, as King Thranduil commanded","King Thranduil is in the throne room of Felegoth, in Eryn Lasgalen.","'We have arrived. Now we will see if we are welcome!'","'I am sorry to see you go, ${PLAYER}, but I understand Gandalf's reasoning. To keep such an artifact here as the Black Book of Mordor must be considered unwise, and doubly-so if it is sought by one such as Karazgar! The Weeping Warrior has been shamed by our Wizard, true, but such a humbling is bound to last only a short while. He will recover from it. If he still desires to get his claws on the Black Book, as it seems he must, he will follow its trail away from here. Take care on your journey, my friend, and beware!'\
\
You bid Durin a warm farewell, but before you depart his company you give him Gandalf's warning not to seek for Thafar-gathol. Durin looks at you thoughtfully and hefts the Red Axe in one hand.\
\
'Ah, you need not worry on that score, my friend. There is so much to be done here at Skarháld without adding Thafar-gathol to our list of problems! Longbeards, Zhélruka, and Stout-axes must all work to steady our foothold in the Grey Mountains, and to launch such an expedition so soon would be folly! Perhaps one day, ${PLAYER}. But certainly not today!'\
\
Durin's words are reassuring, but after taking your leave you turn back and see him gazing at the distant peaks of the Ered Mithrin, and wonder.","Gandalf believes that Karazgar will remain a threat to the dwarves at Skarháld for as long as the Black Book remains there, and he wants to bring it on a journey away from the Ered Mithrin.","'I sent Wood-elves to open the Forest Gate on the western bounds of Eryn Lasgalen. You will find it unsealed, your path to the Beorning-lands open.'","'The Forest Gate is open, and our path to the Beorning-lands is clear. That is good. If we do not tarry, we should reach the Beorninghús today.\
\
'The Vales of Anduin are home to a number of hearty folk, ${PLAYER}. The Woodmen make their homes on the edge of the forest; you will find them rustic and superstitious, but do not mistake either of these qualities for weakness! To dwell within the shadow of Mirkwood for so long has made them strong, and while the wood now has a fairer name, the Woodmen endured when it did not.\
\
'Grimbeorn's folk, the Beornings, have also weathered hardship in the Vales. Long ago they learned the secret art of skin-changing, and other denizens of the Vales hunted them nearly to extinction. But they survived, and now they are a sturdy folk, slow to trust outsiders but worthy allies of those they name friend.\
\
'Let us go to the Beorninghús, south-west of here, and see if Grimbeorn will count us among that lucky number.'","'You should bid farewell to Durin before we leave for Felegoth. And ${PLAYER}? Tell the young prince to ignore the voice in his heart that compels him to seek Thafar-gathol. That place is lost, if ever it existed at all, and he should put it from his mind. It is not for him.'","'¡Aquí!'","Durin is on the upper level of Skarháld, waiting to speak with you following Karazgar's defeat.","Grimbeorn stands at the Beorninghús.","'You have returned to my halls, ${PLAYER}, as has Mithrandir. Am I to understand your search for the Bugdatish, the artifact sought by Ugrukhôr and Karazgar of the Gúrzyul, has come to naught?'\
\
You briefly recount your adventures with the dwarves and your several confrontations with Karazgar. Thranduil smiles grimly.\
\
'It is often thus,' he replies, 'that servants of the Enemy outreach themselves, and their fall is all the further for it. I applaud Mithrandir for reminding Karazgar that not every Power in this world has fallen to evil.\
\
'As for the Forest Gate, I have already sent Wood-elves to open it. Trade has not yet been continued, but that too should soon follow. I will speak with Mithrandir for a time, and then the two of you should continue on to the Forest Gate on the western bounds of Eryn Lasgalen. You will find it unsealed, your path to the Beorning-lands open.'","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld","The Forest Gate is located on the western edge of Eryn Lasgalen, along the forest road.","'Do you expect me to welcome you to my home, ${PLAYER}? These days are dire enough without Wizards and their travelling companions darkening my doorstep! Why should I make room for the two of you, and whatever trouble likely follows behind?\
\
'You say this is Gandalf? Tell me no such lies! I have met Gandalf, and this cannot be he. Gandalf is a man old and bent, dressed in grey. Kind of temperament is he, and not like this imperious stranger! Gandalf? Bah! If this truly is Gandalf, I say that trouble follows him wherever he goes, and these days are dire enough already without such as he darkening my doorstep!\
\
'I will take care of my own kind, first. If you will stay at my home, you will have the poorest rooms, and the smallest servings at dinner, and in all other things you will come second, and last. Is this understood? Be glad I do not turn you away, as is my right! But I am feeling generous.'","The sound of buzzing bees and sweet smell of clover welcome you to the Beorninghús","Chapter 10.1: A New Journey","'Grimbeorn's folk, the Beornings, have also weathered hardship in the Vales. Long ago they learned the secret art of skin-changing, and other denizens of the Vales hunted them nearly to extinction. But they survived, and now they are a sturdy folk, slow to trust outsiders but worthy allies of those they name friend.\
\
'Let us go to the Beorninghús, south-west of here, and see if Grimbeorn will count us among that lucky number.'","Talk to King Thranduil at his throne in Felegoth","'I sent Wood-elves to open the Forest Gate. Trade has not yet been continued, but that too should soon follow. I will speak with Mithrandir for a time, and then the two of you should continue on to the Forest Gate on the western bounds of Eryn Lasgalen. You will find it unsealed, your path to the Beorning-lands open.'"},
[2849]={"'I have been itching to return home and tell Orgolas and all my friends about the adventures I have had since coming here! They will not believe me, but perhaps when you come back to Pinnath Gelin you will tell them it is all true? They will be astounded!'","'The Elf warrior Sigileth advised me to set aside my desire for vengeance, and while I refused to do so forever, I told her I would not delay returning my son to his home to achieve it. But that was not all. I enlisted her promise not to forget the injustices done to my family, and if she has the opportunity to make hated Nakási pay for them, she will do so. I have only known Sigileth for a short time, but I believe she will do as I have requested. It is only this that allows me to leave behind this city, and its treacherous rulers.'","Talk to Nimrodel in the Sail-haven","You send them off with a proud salute","Many of your friends, including the crew of the Wave-hunter, prepare to depart Umbar Baharbêl from the Sail-haven. Jaith told you to find them not far from the Beacon-gate on the west side of the city.","'A number of your friends have agreed to escort me home. I hope you will forgive my taking them from you.'","Talk to Legolas in the Sail-haven","The child Thorongil stands by his mother in the Sail-haven in Umbar Baharbêl, east of the Beacon-gate.","'Queen Arwen and King Elessar would never forgive us if we allowed any harm to befall Nimrodel during her journey back to her home. I volunteered at once to accompany her, and Elladan and Elrohir also wished to do their part. To my surprise Gimli has also asked to come along, and I am glad of it, but his reasoning is clouded to me: he wants to hear from Nimrodel about the caves in which her people dwell, for some project upon which he wishes to set his mind.\
\
'The thinking of dwarves is beyond me, ${PLAYER}, but I am happy for his company all the same.'","'Gimli and I will guard Nimrodel as she returns home to Belfalas.'","Talk to Thorongil in the Sail-haven","'Oh, I am not leaving with them, ${PLAYER}. I feel that I still have work to do here, and I would appreciate your continued help. Together I hope we might ease the tensions between Gondor and Umbar, and further the cause of peace between King Elessar and the Kindred of the Coins.'","'Queen Arwen and King Elessar would never forgive us if we allowed any harm to befall Nimrodel during her journey back to her home. I volunteered at once to accompany her, of course, but to my surprise Gimli has also asked to come along. I am glad of it, but his reasoning is clouded to me: he wants to hear from Nimrodel about the caves in which her people dwell, for some project upon which he wishes to set his mind.\
\
'The thinking of dwarves is beyond me, ${PLAYER}, but I am happy for his company all the same.'","Talk to Sirgon in the Sail-haven","With solemn reverence, Nimrodel's chosen bodyguards salute you","The crew of the Wave-hunter, and others of your friends, make ready to leave the city","'We are leaving, ${PLAYER}, and it is just as well. Ever since Azagath Sea-shadow and Nakási Wave-reaper fled from the Citadel of the Winds, I have been itching to return home and tell Orgolas and all my friends about the adventures I have had since coming here! They will not believe me, but perhaps when you come back to Pinnath Gelin you will tell them it is all true? They will be astounded!\
\
'My mother refuses to tell me much about what befell your own ship when it ran aground upon the Shield Isles as you journeyed to Umbar, but I overheard the captain of the vessel we are taking back to Gondor discussing the voyage ahead. He believes the currents and the winds will be favourable, and the journey should not take very long, or be very dangerous. That is a shame. I imagine being shipwrecked can be pretty exciting, and I would like to see for myself, just once!'","'It is time for me to return to the Caves of the Avorrim in Belfalas, but I have made a decision. I will bring my people from the cavern that has been their home, and we will no longer mourn, but rejoice in the light of the sun and the feel of the breeze.'\
\
Nimrodel smiles gently at you.\
\
'Perhaps by the time we arrive I will be ready to do this, my friend. It is one thing to speak it, and another to see it done! But that is the wish of my heart. Lothíriel will help me in this, I am certain of it.\
\
'A number of your friends have agreed to escort me home, ${PLAYER}; I hope you will forgive my taking them from you.'","'Your friends have engaged the services of a merchant vessel and plan to return to their own lands, but they wish to bid you farewell before they depart. They asked for me to send you on to them in the Sail-haven, by the Beacon-gate on the west side of the city. They assured me they would not leave until you spoke with them, but the honour of my station begs that you will not delay.'","'Gimli and the sons of Elrond, and myself, will be fine guardians for Nimrodel as she returns home to Belfalas.'","Talk to Lady Nauriel in the Sail-haven","Find your friends and crew in the Sail-haven, not far from the Beacon-gate on the west side of Umbar Baharbêl","Talk to Gimli in the Sail-haven","'There you are. I was not certain the guard posted at the Meeting-hall would give you our message in time, but it seems he proved worthy. I am surprised; still, I welcome it. Has my mood been lightened by our success? How could it not? The purpose that brought us to these shores has been satisfied: my son Thorongil has been rescued from the clutches of the Kindred of the Coins, and we must go now to the Green Hills of Pinnath Gelin. My husband Carandolion will be pleased to see his son's safe return, and his wife's triumph.\
\
'Yes, I say \\qtriumph,\\q though my vengeance be incomplete and those responsible for the hurts done to my family remain unpunished. The Elf warrior Sigileth advised me to set aside my desire for vengeance, and while I refused to do so forever, I told her I would not delay returning my son to his home to achieve it. But that was not all. I enlisted her promise not to forget the injustices done to my family, and if she has the opportunity to make hated Nakási pay for them, she will do so.\
\
'I have only known Sigileth for a short time, but I believe she will do as I have requested. It is only this that allows me to leave behind this city, and its treacherous rulers.'","'A number of unusual folk were looking for you, ${PLAYER}: some Elves, a dwarf, and a few others I deemed travellers from Gondor. I trust they were friends of yours? They asked if I had seen you of late, and when I told them you often have business within the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, they gave me a message to pass on to you.'\
\
Jaith rests his weapon against one shoulder while he tries to remember the message.\
\
'Yes, I recall the words, fear not. They said they have engaged the services of a merchant vessel and plan to return to their own lands, but they wish to bid you farewell before they depart. They asked for me to send you on to them in the Sail-haven, by the Beacon-gate on the west side of the city. They assured me they would not leave until you spoke with them, but the honour of my station begs that you will not delay.'","'Ahí está.'","Sirgon is not yet prepared to leave Umbar Baharbêl, and wishes to speak with you about the days to come.","Chapter 10.1: Different Roads","'I will guard the Elf Nimrodel as she returns home. I also wish to ask her some questions about the caves in which she dwells.'","You send them off with an understanding wave","Nimrodel's guardians are preparing to depart, and you should acknowledge them with a <rgb=#00FF00>salute</rgb> or a <rgb=#00FF00>wave</rgb>.","Nimrodel stands among your friends in the Sail-haven in Umbar Baharbêl, east of the Beacon-gate.","<rgb=#00FF00>Salute</rgb> or <rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> at your assembled friends","Nauriel shakes her head disapprovingly","The guard outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja has received word that some of your friends have made preparations to depart Umbar Baharbêl.","Legolas stands ready to depart for Gondor on a merchant vessel leaving Umbar Baharbêl.","You send them off with a particularly flashy salute","Gimli stands ready to depart for Gondor on a merchant vessel leaving Umbar Baharbêl.","'I do not know why Legolas is so surprised that I wish to accompany him as he escorts the Elf Nimrodel back to her home. I have been moved by what he has shared of her story, and it brings to my mind some of the greatest love stories ever told among the dwarves of Durin's Folk: beautiful tales, lovely and sad...'\
\
Gimli coughs and sputters. When he has recovered, he continues gruffly.\
\
'Legolas and I vowed to travel with each other to see places dear to each of us: for me the Glittering Caves, and for he the forest of Fangorn, then to compare the relative beauty of each. I should fear to let him out of my sight, lest he forget this promise!'\
\
Gimli looks down at his boots and speaks more quietly.\
\
'But of course I would feel more at ease if Nimrodel was protected by the axe of a hale dwarf-warrior. She reminds me of the Lady Galadriel, and I would see no harm come to her.'","Lady Nauriel of Pinnath Gelin stands in the Sail-haven in Umbar Baharbêl, east of the Beacon-gate."},
[2850]={"A number of Longbeards stand in Zul-mazal, studying the broken mosaic and the curious stone block in the centre of the chamber.","'Welcome back to Zul-mazal, ${PLAYER}! I understand that you helped dear Bróin collect stones and pebbles for me? Thank you for taking the time to do so... it can't have been easy!\
\
'My master Stáli is very pleased that he may be able to complete this mosaic, although he tries not to show it. When I presented to him the pouch of colourful pebbles that Bróin gifted to me, he said he might begin my instruction in sculpture-carving sometime in the next ten years.\
\
'That is quite soon, ${PLAYER}! Yesterday he said he would teach me sometime in the next hundred!'","Talk to Durin in Zul-mazal","'Lead on, ${PLAYER}. I would see the chamber where the hammer was found.'","Return to Zul-mazal by the upper crypts on the western side of the Pit of Stonejaws","Zul-mazal is by the upper crypts on the western side of the Pit of Stonejaws.","Talk to Bróin in Zul-mazal","'For what purpose was this room constructed, ${PLAYER}? Is it a tomb or memorial of some kind? And yet it shares little with the crypts outside. I do feel the presence of an enchantment of some sort... it puts me in mind of a net draped upon stone.'\
\
You tell Durin that Imák sensed something similar in the chamber, but dismissed it as a product of the Angmarim cultists in Gundabad. Durin shakes his head.\
\
'I do not think this is the work of the Angmarim: this enchantment feels dwarf-made to me. There is a secret in this chamber, ${PLAYER}. A dwarf secret.'","Chapter 10.1: Fitting the Pieces","With the mithril hammer in his possession, Prince Durin is interested to learn from where it came, and what significance it might hold for his conquest of the Mountain-home.","Talk to Stáli the Hewer in Zul-mazal","'Oh, it's you again. Do not forget that you owe me a favour! I did not have to release Eskil from his agreement with me, and chose to do so from benevolence only! You have surely noticed that my new apprentice has not retrieved the Zabad'ibîn for me, as you promised she would! You did not promise that? Well, someone did.\
\
'But I do confess she has a better eye for artistry than her brother ever possessed. See this mosaic Fastrith brought to my attention? It is the perfect match to one that decorated the Hall Under the Mountain in Erebor, and which I was restoring before departing for Gundabad.\
\
'My apprentice has somehow come into possession of numerous colourful stones with which I may be able to complete the mosaic. It will be another triumph by Stáli the Hewer, master sculptor!'","'Fastrith was delighted by the gift, ${PLAYER}! Thank you again for collecting those stones!'\
\
Reminded of the pouch of stones you found on an Orc in the Welkin-lofts, you tell Bróin of your discovery and hand it over. He beams happily at you.\
\
'Perfect, my friend! This will surely be enough stones to complete the mosaic in this chamber!'","Durin stands in Zul-mazal, deep in thought.","Talk to Fastrith in Zul-mazal","'It was with the help of Glúrkub that Gorgar first acquired this hammer from Zul-mazal. If Hrímil fears it, I would see the chamber from where it came. Some clue to her fear might remain within, and this understanding may help us use it against her.\
\
'Lead on, ${PLAYER}. I have not yet seen Zul-mazal, but you know where it lies.'"},
[2851]={"Durin stands beside a secret stair deep beneath Gundabad, marvelling at the long-hidden passage.","Durin believes that Zul-mazal holds some secret, and he is determined to learn what it may be.","Durin is in Zul-mazal, determined to unravel whatever mystery lies within the curious chamber's walls.","'I can hardly believe it, ${PLAYER}. For how long has this secret stair remained hidden? And where does it lead?'","'Then let us begin. This chamber will reveal its secrets to me!'","Talk to Durin deep beneath Gundabad","'Will you help me uncover this secret, ${PLAYER}? According to Glúrkub, this is the room from which Gorgar acquired the mithril hammer. Revealing this secret may help us understand why Hrímil Frost-heart so fears this weapon, and how we may use it against her.'","Chapter 10.2: The Mystery of Zul-mazal","Talk to Durin and help him uncover the secret of Zul-mazal"},
[2852]={"Talk to Sigileth in the Sail-haven","Sirgon is waiting in the Sail-haven east of the Beacon-gate to go with you to meet with the Kindred of the Coins.","Talk to Sirgon in the Sail-haven and go with him to meet the Kindred","Corudan and Sigileth are in the Sail-haven, east of the Beacon-gate in Umbar Baharbêl.","'Your friends will be safe on their journey back to Gondor, ${PLAYER}, I doubt it not. It is my belief, and my sister's, that we remain closer to danger than they!\
\
'We have achieved a tenuous peace with those who rule in Umbar, for now, but we should not forget that the Kindred of the Coins may have secret purposes of its own. Azagath kept the evil in his heart hidden from those with whom he ruled the city; might the members of the Kindred who remain act similarly?\
\
'Sigileth and I have decided to stay here in Umbar and help you in the days to come, but heed our words now: remain cautious when you speak with the Kindred of the Coins! The gravest threat among their number may have fled the city... but I believe those who remain could still pose a danger to you, and to Gondor.'","Talk to Corudan in the Sail-haven","'It is true, ${PLAYER}: I cautioned Nauriel against pursuing her vengeance against the Kindred. It was the lesson of Cruel Dancer, who was once Galatâni, that caused me to speak such words to Nauriel. If she followed the road of vengeance to its end, as did Galatâni, would she ever return from it? Or would the road curve and bend, with retribution following her back to Pinnath Gelin?\
\
'I do not remember the name of Nauriel's husband, but if she achieves her vengeance would it stop there, or would he be endangered? Their son, too, for whom this was done... would he be threatened anew?\
\
'The lesson of Cruel Dancer inspired me to steer Nauriel from this course. I have accepted the burden of vengeance on her behalf. She has my promise that my sword Baugliltir will seek the blood of Azagath Sea-shadow and Nakási Wave-reaper.'","'My brother is right in this: you should remain wary of the Kindred of the Coins, despite their benign words.'","'Are you ready to go? Let us meet with Belondor about what awaits Gondor and Umbar in the days ahead. He has invited us to the Citadel of the Winds, and assured us of safe passage there.'","'After you have spoken with your friends, let us go to meet with Belondor about the days to come.'","'Remember our words of caution when you meet with the Kindred!'","Belondor has requested that you and Sirgon meet with him and the rest of the Kindred of the Coins in the Citadel of the Winds to discuss your next course of action.","Talk to Sirgon outside the Lords' Gate in the Fleetfast","Sirgon stands in the Fleetfast outside the Lords' Gate, waiting to discuss your meeting with the Kindred of the Coins.","'We will begin today, if you are willing! When you have bid farewell to the crew of the Wave-hunter and your other friends, there is something I must ask of you. Belondor desires to meet with the two of us in the Citadel of Winds, the better to discuss our next course of action.'","'Near Harad! I know very little of these lands, ${PLAYER}, but I will not turn away from the mission that awaits us. If the capture of Azagath and Nakási will help maintain the peace between Gondor and Umbar, I would pursue them to lands both distant and dangerous, no matter how far the chase takes me from the Sea where my heart dwells, or from my home and family in Lebennin.'","Chapter 10.2: The Next Move"},
[2853]={"Cleared brush from the roads (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has recogido leña (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect firewood in the Beorning-lands near the Beorninghús (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have given you my price. Speak to Gandalf and learn if he appreciates this favour!'","Bring the useful pieces of flint to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","'I will allow you to stay, for I know the dangers that lie beyond my walls and I will not make you face them alone. But I do not give you this lodging for free. It will cost you nothing in coin; rather, the price will be the sweat of your brow. Many are the tasks that need doing, and in return for a safe place to stay you will see them done. Do you agree?\
\
'Very good. The road through my lands has become choked in some places with brush. Clear four patches of brush, and you will have made a start on opening the way. We always have need of flint and firewood. Gather four suitable logs and search patches of soil until you find three pieces of flint. Orcs and wargs have been troubling my family ever since my sire came down from the mountains. Slay four Orcs and three wargs, and let them know that these lands are not safe for them!\
\
'That will be a start, ${PLAYER}. That is my price. Speak to Gandalf and learn if he appreciates this favour!'","'You have done more than I asked, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Grimbeorn squints at you suspiciously.\
\
'Why? Is this the Wizard's doing? Why would you do more than I asked? What are you trying to prove, ${CLASS}?'","Gandalf wishes to speak with you. The Wizard stands near the entrance to the Beorninghús.","Chapter 10.2: The Price of Lodging","'Grimbeorn has let us off lightly, ${PLAYER}. Four patches of brush and logs for firewood? Three pieces of flint? And this is not to mention the paltry number of Orcs and wargs he asked that you slay in the fields and meads around his home.\
\
'Grimbeorn, like his sire before him, does not appreciate surprises. Oh, he will warm up to them, in time, but at the outset he looks upon any unexpected arrival with disapproval. You will need to trust me, ${PLAYER}: if Grimbeorn asks that you clear four patches of brush, you should instead clear eight! If he asks for three pieces of flint, I suggest that you bring him six! In point of fact, I think you should double the quantities of every task he set before you!\
\
'Why? Let us just say that it is important for us to be on the good side of the Beorninghús's master. You will thank me for it, when all is said and done.'","Defeat Orcs in the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You don't have what I need?'","Grimbeorn is at the Beorninghús, in the Beorning-lands.","'I think you should double the quantities of every task Grimbeorn set before you! Why? Let us just say that it is important for us to be on the good side of the Beorninghús's master. You will thank me for it, when all is said and done.'","Defeated Orcs in the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Grimbeorn has tasked you with a number of errands to undertake in the Beorning-lands, and Gandalf has helpfully doubled the required quantities of each.","Search patches of soil for flint (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected useful pieces of flint (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat wargs in the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Grimbeorn has demanded that if you and Gandalf are to stay at the Beorninghús, you must work for your keep.","Talk to Gandalf at the Beorninghús","Defeated wargs in the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Clear brush from roads in the Beorning-lands near the Beorninghús (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2854]={"Durin believes that none have travelled these secret stairs for an age, but he will not allow that to dissuade him from seeking whatever may lie at the bottom.","You enter a long-forgotten chamber deep below Gundabad","Chapter 10.3: Buried Secrets","'What is this place?'\
\
Durin stares in disbelief at the statue on the opposite side of the chamber.\
\
'That is a statue of Mótsog the Traitor, who led the Greymauls against Durin the Deathless in the First Age! He was slain at the conclusion of his rebellion... why would he be given the dignity of a tomb?'\
\
Durin fumes, his eyes flashing angrily and his fists clenched.\
\
'What is the meaning of this?'","'Let us meet outside this shameful crypt and decide what next can be done.'","'What is the meaning of this? Mótsog was slain for his treachery. He should never have been given the dignity of such a tomb!'","The statue of Mótsog has changed. Where once it was worked in grey stone, now the statue is given the colour he might have had in life. So too is there another change: the statue is now shorn of any beard.\
\
Despite its lifelike colour, the statue remains unmoving and bereft of life.","The secret stairs have not been travelled for an age, descending far below Gundabad.\
\
What lies beyond their lowest step?","Durin has asked you to meet him on the stairs outside the long-forgotten chamber.","'What was that? Something changed, ${PLAYER}! What enchantment is this?'","A statue of Mótsog stands in the long-forgotten chamber.","Descend the secret stairs far below Gundabad and explore the deepest caverns","Wait for Durin to catch up with you","Something about the air feels different. But what?","Return to Durin and learn what has disturbed him","'Tread carefully, ${PLAYER}. I will meet you at the bottom of the stairs... for surely there must be an end to them. Is it not so?'","Durin looks around the chamber with wide eyes","Durin runs into the long-forgotten chamber.","Talk to Durin in the long-forgotten chamber","Meet up with Durin at the bottom of the stairs outside","Durin stands in the long-forgotten chamber deep below Gundabad.","'Even these stairs have an end, ${PLAYER}. But look there: a path leads to a chamber of some kind!'","Examine the statue of Mótsog","A cool breeze blows past you, and Durin cries out in surprise","'I cannot believe that a traitor such as Mótsog would be given the dignity of a tomb beneath the Mountain-home, ${PLAYER}. One of his followers must have built this place in secret after Durin's judgement. Did they spirit his body here? Does it lie behind one of these walls, enjoying the undeserved rest of a traitorous worm?\
\
'I am disgusted. Such a place should not be. I thought we would find some secret to opposing Hrímil Frost-heart? There is no such secret here. Let us meet outside this shameful crypt and decide what next can be done.'","This statue of Mótsog is very detailed; someone crafted it with care","'My breath is stolen away by the sight of this cavern, and by the knowledge that none have traversed these steps for an age. The stair snakes along the wall, descending out of sight; how far below Gundabad will we find its lowest step?\
\
'Tread carefully, ${PLAYER}. I will meet you at the bottom of the stairs... for surely there must be an end to them. Is it not so?'","Durin stands in the long-forgotten chamber beneath Gundabad."},
[2855]={"Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Gultheg is at Vegbár, the watch-fort west of the Old Ford in the Wolf-denes.","'For how long have my people lived by the side of the wood? Long years indeed, for true deeds have vanished into the haze of memory, taking on the feel of legend or myth. Doubt not that even the most fantastical of these tales must hold some truth within its marrow! Or do you count yourself brave enough to search for Vagári, the ghostly wanderer of the Gladden? Marhairu of the Horse-folk did, and he was forever changed.\
\
'Long ago, the Horse-folk of Rhovanion knew the hardship of war, and they came to the Vales of Anduin in desperate need. The Woodmen that lived in the vales at that time gave them food and shelter, and in return the Horse-folk raised no king and demanded no fealty. Instead they lived as neighbours with the Woodmen, building a fortress of stone and timber on an island south of the Old Ford. This redoubt they named Avabárg, and it housed the Horse-folk for several generations, but they were never comfortable within its confines and they desired a home more to their liking.\
\
'While the Horse-folk remained in the vales, the Woodmen told them of Vagári, a spectral figure that stalked among the fens by the light of the moon. The sight of him filled my people with dread, and they fled in terror, but the Horse-folk were bold, and their blood ran hot. Marhairu, son of the chief, went in search of Vagári. He was not seen for a year and a day, and when he finally returned his hair was stricken white. He was clad in pale garments instead of his armour, and there was a darkness in his eye that had not been there before.\
\
'He claimed to have met the Wanderer and followed him for a time, but whenever he tried to speak to him, the spectral figure faded from view, only to reappear further ahead in the mist. His memory failed in the recounting of what befell him, and he spoke with confusion of an empty dwarf-hold and a sorrowful song. Until the end of his days, Marhairu insisted that he followed the Wanderer for only a short time; he could not explain his long disappearance. The Horse-folk, believing he had been ensorcelled, named him \\qWinter-hair\\q and shunned him as a source of ill fortune. He dwelt in a hut on the edge of the Gladden and lived to be an old man, but one day his hut was found empty, and no one can say what happened to him.\
\
'Listen to the warning of Marhairu Winter-hair, ${PLAYER}! If you encounter Vagári the Wanderer among the mists, turn and flee, before it is too late for you!'","Defeat Orcs in Woodsedge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have arrived at the village of Hultvís. Adalfon nods in greeting","Grimbeorn is at the Beorninghús, waiting for you to return with the collected tolls from Vegbár.","'Thank you for helping with the hunt, my friend. I look forward to seeing you again, and hearing your own stories of the wider world, as you listened to ours. Farewell, and good fortune to you!'","Talk to Gultheg at Vegbár","You should return to the Beorninghús with the delivery Grimbeorn requested","He hands you a small pouch. Now you should continue to Hultvís","Townsfolk throughout Hultvís will speak to you of the legends that have been passed down among the Woodmen.","Talk to Gelfrida in Hultvís","'You are not one of our hunters, but you have found choice cuts to exceed many of their finest takings! Is this the luck of a beginner, or have you hunted prey in far-off lands, and the harts of Woodsedge just the latest? Well done, my friend! You are welcome in Hultvís, for there is much that needs doing. Ask around and you will find no shortage of tasks, I am sure.\
\
'But it is the tradition of our hunters not to depart immediately upon returning from a successful hunt, and I do not ask you to do otherwise! I will salt and prepare these steaks, and while I do you should speak to the men and women of the village and listen to their stories. One such as you must have heard many tales from wandering in distant lands, but I assure you that ours are unique! Legend hangs heavily upon every tree and rock in these vales, and whispers tell that even creatures out of myth can be found among the mists.\
\
'There is a magic about the Vales of Anduin, ${PLAYER}. Listen to the tales of my people and I challenge you to say otherwise!'","'Legends and stories? Aye, we here in Hultvís have our fair share of the things. I myself have seen enough to believe most of what they say about the lands hereabout, and if you spend some time here I do not doubt you will too!\
\
'Have you heard tell of the Maiden that walks the marshland? Her hair is golden, they say, threaded with yellow flowers, and she walks among the pools of Gladden singing songs of sorrow. Even when I was a young girl I heard the stories of her, and strayed further from my home than I ought in hopes of seeing her, but it was for nothing. I convinced myself that the Horse-folk that lived in these lands long ago, from whom came the first stories of the Maiden, must have mistaken the light on the water for her golden hair, the breath of the wind for the sound of her song. I gave up seeking her, and then I was a woman grown, with a family to look after, and I left tales of the Maiden to my childhood.\
\
'But there is magic in the vales, stranger. One afternoon while I sought wildflowers along the river-bank, I was caught out of doors too late. The sun went down, and as the last of the light faded, I saw her standing among the gladdens. Still as a statue she was, but as I sought to look at her closely a great drowsiness fell upon me. I blinked my eyes to clear away the fog, but then she was gone. I searched among the pools until it was too dark to see, at which point I had to return to Hultvís. It would not have been safe to remain in the bog, for then as now there are sometimes monsters about. I have not seen her again, but it lightens my heart to know the Maiden of the Gladden is out there somewhere, singing.\
\
'That is how I know the tales of her are true. Perhaps there is truth in the other tales of my people, as well.'","Collected forest-hart flanks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, there you are. I have been studying the Black Book, but it resists my attempts to dissolve its mysteries. A Wizard does not become frustrated, but I do not deny that my patience is tested. Perhaps I could use some air, ${PLAYER}.'","'The fighting may be done, but we need to rebuild our town and restock our larders. If you seek out and defeat Orc stragglers, and gather flanks from the forest-harts in Woodsedge for our cook Veremund, you will have helped us and we will remember it.'","Talk to Veremund by the cooking fires in Hultvís","Chapter 10.3: Good Fences","Adalfon asked you to help the village of Hultvís recover and rebuild following the recent battle.","You hunted wild harts for the Woodmen of Hultvís, and now Veremund waits by the fires in the village for the meat you obtained.","'Veremund is by the cooking fires in Hultvís. Bring him the flanks and know you have the thanks of all the village.'","Defeated Orcs in Woodsedge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The days have been dark along the Anduin these past few months, and not just for my people. Orcs, goblins, and trolls have long harried the people of the Vales, but their attacks became more frequent of late. We turned them away, my kin and the Woodmen both, and by so doing we each became more friendly with the other. \\qGood fences make for good neighbours,\\q my sire used to say, but to that I now add, \\qand so does shared hardship.\\q\
\
'You stay at the Beorninghús because I allow it, ${PLAYER}, and that means you should do as I say, when I say it. And now I wish for you to go to Hultvís, the village of the Woodmen on the eastern side of Woodsedge, and lend them whatever assistance you are able. They face danger in the Vales of the Anduin, but they are not as hardy as my people and will need your aid.\
\
'Hmm! On your way to Hultvís, stop by the fort of Vegbár and obtain the collected tolls from Gultheg there. Return it to me when you have finished with the folk at Hultvís, and I will count your obligation met.'","'Hultvís is a village of the Woodmen located on the eastern side of Woodsedge. That is where you plan to go next, is it not?'","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, studying the Black Book of Mordor within Grimbeorn's lodge.","Veremund is by the cooking fires of Hultvís, waiting for you to return from speaking with the people of the village.","'I gave you two purposes, ${PLAYER}: to bring back the collected tolls from Vegbár, and to aid my neighbours at the Woodmen village of Hultvís. Have you done this?'\
\
You give Grimbeorn the pouch of money, and he weighs it in his hand.\
\
'We keep safe the road through the mountains and across the Old Ford, and in return for that safety we ask these coins from those who pass. It is a reasonable price, but this pouch feels light in my hand. Are there so few travellers in the vales today, even with the end of the war? Hmmph. War is never truly ended, is it?\
\
'The Wizard is inside the lodge, peering at the book he brought. Speak to him. Perhaps he is ready to leave.'","'There is a magic about the Vales of Anduin, ${PLAYER}. Listen to the tales of my people here in Hultvís and see if you can say otherwise!'","Bring the flanks to Veremund by the cooking fires in Hultvís","Bring the collected tolls to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","'Are you willing to hunt the wild harts for the village of Hultvís? I am glad to hear it, but you will accomplish little if you stay here talking.'","Adalfon has greeted you at the entrance to the village of Hultvís.","'Did you enjoy the peaceful respite of hearing my people's myths and legends, ${PLAYER}? I am pleased the Bear-folk came to our aid during the recent battle, for if they had not and my people were slain, these traditions would surely vanish with us!\
\
'Thank you for helping with the hunt, my friend. I look forward to seeing you again, and hearing your own stories of the wider world, as you listened to ours. Farewell, and good fortune to you!'","'I have asked for you to go to Hultvís, the village of the Woodmen on the eastern side of Woodsedge, and lend them whatever assistance you are able. They face danger in the Vales of the Anduin, but they are not as hardy as my people and will need your aid. On your way to Hultvís, stop by the fort of Vegbár and obtain the collected tolls from Gultheg there. Return it to me when you have finished with the folk at Hultvís, and I will count your obligation met.'","Grimbeorn has another task for you. He wants you to check on the Woodmen, his neighbours to the south, and aid them with their difficulties.","'The Wizard is inside the lodge, peering at the book he brought. Speak to him. Perhaps he is ready to leave.'","Talk to Mavi in Hultvís","Collect flanks from forest-harts in Woodsedge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I love hearing stories, yes I do, and I love telling them too! When I am old enough, I will learn the truth of these legends, and if they are false I will let everyone know. But I hope they are true, yes, yes, I do! I will tell you one of these stories, but which one? The Maiden of the Gladden? Or Marhairu Winter-hair of the Horse-folk? Perhaps the tale of Old Mad Ubb? Nay, that one is too frightening.\
\
'I've got it! Have you heard tell of the Hole-dwellers? They were a small people, shy and tricksy, and it is said they dwelt in holes beneath the ground. Nay, not like dwarves! These folk were smaller than dwarves, it is said, and they would vanish at the first approach! My mother says that she heard fairy stories about the Hole-dwellers when she was a little girl, but none of them have been seen in hundreds and hundreds of years, if not longer! She heard that folk used to leave food and trinkets for them on the river-banks, and that sometimes when they went back to check... the gifts would be gone!\
\
'I wonder where the Hole-dwellers went? I think perhaps they perfected the art of hiding, and now no one can find them. I'd wager they're still somewhere in the vales, just waiting for a child smart and clever enough to see them! I hope that's me, yes, yes I do!'","Talk to Adalfon at the entrance to Hultvís","Hultvís is on the eastern side of Woodsedge, in the Vales of Anduin.","'What brings you to Vegbár, stranger? From this fort my people keep watch on travel and trade across the river and over the mountains. Dwarves and Men find easy passage, as long as they pay the toll. Orcs and wargs are given no such choice, and are turned away with sword and claw, unless they be slain where they stand!'\
\
You explain that Grimbeorn sent you to Vegbár to gather the tolls that have been recently collected, and Gultheg studies your face with suspicion.\
\
'I was supposed to return to the Beorninghús yesterday, it is true, but a raiding-party of goblins demanded my attention and I was delayed. How do I know you can be trusted, and have truly been sent by my chieftain? Perhaps you are a common bandit, and plan to rob us of the coins we have collected!'\
\
Gultheg glares at you for a moment, and then relents.\
\
'The war is done, even if the fighting is fresh in my mind and there are still foes about. I will trust that you have come from Grimbeorn with this request, but if I learn that you are a bandit you will regret this deception. But you will not regret it for long, do you understand me?'","Talk to Eurik in Hultvís","Find the entrance to the village of Hultvís, on the eastern side of Woodsedge","'Welcome to Hultvís, village of the Woodmen. My people have endured much with the passage of time, but no matter the trouble that comes we persist and stand strong. When Orcs burned the walls, we rebuilt them. When wargs stalked our streets, we drove them away. So it has always been, and that was the way of life in Hultvís.\
\
'But in recent weeks something changed. I know not what it was, and neither do the elders of the village, but the Orcs and goblins of the Misty Mountains poured from their holes in numbers we had not seen for a hundred years. The fighting was more fierce than any I had ever seen, and my people and the Bear-folk alike suffered tremendous losses. Grimbeorn and a number of his people finally saw victory at the Old Ford, but none knew if a second attack might be coming. Only when a great Eagle appeared in the southern skies and spoke of the war's ending did we dare hope that the worst was behind us.\
\
'The fighting may be done, but we need to rebuild our town and restock our larders. If you seek out and defeat Orc stragglers, and gather flanks from the forest-harts in Woodsedge for our cook Veremund, you will have helped us and we will remember it.'"},
[2856]={"Chapter 10.3: Leave The City Behind, Part One","Sirgon is by the east gate of Umbar Baharbêl, preparing to depart the city.","Talk to Sirgon by the east gate of Umbar Baharbêl","The leaders of the Kindred await your assistance with their preparations in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja.","'It is not a habit of mine to set forth upon a journey without knowing where it will end, but none of us can say precisely where Azagath and Nakási might be bound. If only Belondor had thought to lay his eyes upon the tapestry map when he first came to the Mâkhda Khorbo... our circumstances now might be rather different, and of a more beneficial flavour.\
\
'But they are not, and the duration of our pursuit cannot be determined. We must prepare for a long journey, and hope to be too well-supplied, rather than not provisioned enough!\
\
'As it happens, I own a controlling interest in a number of warehouses in the city, and I can ensure most favourable rates for the provisioning of our party. Bring this order to Ilbidûn at Stonecliff Market in the Lower Ward, and she will see that it is filled.'","Talk to Rothog in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","'I believe the errant members of my Kindred prepared for an overland journey even before they recovered the tapestry map from within the Mâkhda Khorbo, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps they were aided in this by the secret wealth gathered by Sharûla and others of her sort, scoundrels hiding their true nature behind fair faces. I have seen this before.\
\
'But we must take time to prepare our own pursuit, or we doom it to fail before it is begun. The lands east of the city into which Azagath and Nakási have fled are treacherous and full of danger for the unwary. Caravans leave Umbar Baharbêl and follow the Road of Riches eastward along the Ikorbân River before turning south and crossing the rocky waste that marks the edge of the great sands. From there it is a long, inhospitable trek to the desert kingdoms of the south, from which great wealth flowed to us, and back again. The treasure from the south has slowed in recent months; can it be due to anything but unrest in the Empire of Ordâkh following the war?\
\
'Caravans are now slow to depart from Umbar, and that will make their masters hungry for work. I have written an offer of employment for a caravan driver, his animals, and sufficient supplies for the journey. Bring it to Jakbir outside at the Forum and he should accept its terms without difficulty, but before you depart Dâr Laja you should speak with the other leaders of the Kindred about their own preparations. They may have some tasks for you as well.'","'Did you not listen? I will not repeat my words to you.'","'There you are, my friend. I see that the Kindred of the Coins have kept you busy making arrangements for our departure.\
\
'While I waited, I pondered the road ahead of us and came to a realization: I know very little about the lands and kingdoms to the east and south within the Haradwaith, beyond the Cape of Umbar. I do not want my lack of knowledge about this area to hinder our pursuit, ${PLAYER}.'","Deliver Khôltekh's orders to Ilbidûn at Stonecliff Market in the Lower Ward","Rothog gives you a set of orders to deliver to the arena armourer","'You have a caravan order for me from the Golden Queen?'\
\
Jakbir takes the parchment from you and studies it closely. At last he looks up at you.\
\
'The Road of Riches has always been dangerous for caravans such as mine, remaining a favourite target of brigands and waylayers, but in these times of tumult it has become more treacherous than before. I understand the Ordâkhai fight to maintain their grip on trade with the desert kingdoms, despite their failing empire, and men whisper of merciless phantoms and spirits hiding in the night's darkness, seeking vulnerable prey.\
\
'I will see what I can do for the Lady Hármelak in honour of our long and profitable relationship, but I fear I can promise little. You understand.'","Talk to Belondor in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","'We must prepare for a long journey. As it happens, I own a controlling interest in a number of warehouses in the city, and I can ensure most favourable rates for the provisioning of our party. Bring this order to Ilbidûn at Stonecliff Market in the Lower Ward, and she will see that it is filled.'","Deliver Hármelak's orders to Jakbir at Bith Gabâr, the Forum in the Upper Ward","Talk to Khôltekh in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","'Every day wasted means our quarry gets further and further ahead, and the success of our pursuit becomes less and less likely. Go to the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja and urge them to hurry.'","Mêshka is already on the way to see her husband","The leaders of the Kindred of the Coins have a number of preparations to make before your combined pursuit of Azagath Sea-shadow can begin.","The leaders of the Kindred await your assistance in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja.","'My wife Mêshka did not know this pursuit might take me far from the city and into the wild lands east of Umbar. Will you speak with her and learn if she would have me stay? Whatever she decides will become my course, and I will not gainsay it or act in any fashion opposed to her mind.\
\
'Afterwards, if she gives her approval, I will join you, Sirgon, and the Elves at the east gate of the city.'","'Caravans are now slow to depart from Umbar, and that will make their masters hungry for work. I have written an offer of employment for a caravan driver, his animals, and sufficient supplies for the journey. Bring it to Jakbir at the Forum outside and he should accept its terms without difficulty.'","Deliver Rothog's orders to Mekhamun on the steps of Dahâl Huliz in the Tor-gardens","'What? You have an order for me from Rothog the Storm?'\
\
You hand the parchment to Mekhamun and he slowly reads its contents, sounding each word aloud as he does.\
\
'I am not a learned man, stranger, but providing weapons and armour for Rothog and his Hûliz required me to become a swift pupil; the only thing more quick in all the city must be the rate at which he dulls his khopeshes! When he arrives to see Húrshauk I will sharpen them, and of course we will provide the rest of the items on this list, if they are to be found anywhere within Dahâl Huliz or the storage rooms located beneath the arena.\
\
'But can you tell me this? If Rothog is leaving the city, who will stay behind to feed Húrshauk? None of my fellows dare approach him!'","Talk to Mêshka somewhere within the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","Khôltekh gives you a set of orders to deliver to the warehouse keeper","Talk to Hármelak in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","'Caravans are now slow to depart from Umbar, and that will make their masters hungry for work. I have written an offer of employment for a caravan driver, his animals, and sufficient supplies for the journey. Bring it to Jakbir outside and he should accept its terms without difficulty, but before you depart Dâr Laja you should speak with the other leaders of the Kindred about their own preparations. They may have some tasks for you as well.'","You assure Mekhamun that you do not have the answer to that question","'Hármelak spoke of the need for many preparations before our travelling party can depart. I hope it will not take too long before we are ready to leave! Every day wasted means our quarry gets further and further ahead, calling into question the success of our pursuit.\
\
'Go to the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja and urge them to hurry. You may be able to speed their preparations if you offer your assistance.'","Hármelak gives you a set of orders to deliver to the caravan master","'Azagath betrayed the city and its people, ${PLAYER}, but that is not the extent of his evil. The cruel sorceries he wove inflicted terrible pain and death upon the men under my command, and those are the hurts for which I will make him pay. My wife Mêshka knows the direction of my thoughts, and she has encouraged me to follow where my heart leads on this matter.\
\
'Still, she did not know it could take me far from the city and into the wild lands east of Umbar. Will you speak with her and learn if she would have me stay? Whatever she decides will become my course, and I will not gainsay it or act in any fashion opposed to her mind.\
\
'Afterwards, if she gives her approval, I will join you and the others at the east gate of the city.'","'You wished to speak with me?'\
\
You tell Mêshka that her husband asked that you find her and see what she thinks of his plan to pursue Azagath and Nakási into the wild lands east of Umbar.\
\
'I am on my way to see him about this very subject, ${PLAYER}. He has my support, in this as in all things, and I plan to tell him that in person.\
\
'I hope you will stand beside him and protect my Belondor from any dangers the two of you may face upon the eastward road. He will do the same for you and for the others of your company, I am certain of it.'","'My khopeshes have become dulled from recent use: that business with the drake Ragrekhûl. For a journey of this sort I need them sharp! I will go to Dahâl Huliz later today and leave them with Mekhamun for sharpening. He can do the work while I visit with my good friend Húrshauk.\
\
'This parchment contains a list of other things I want to bring with me on the road. Give him that and tell him I will expect everything to be prepared when I arrive.'","'What have you brought me? An order for supplies for a caravan leaving the city?'\
\
Ilbidûn takes the parchment from you and reads it. By the time she has finished, her wordless grunts match the number of times she has shaken her head.\
\
'There was a day I might have fulfilled this order, but it is months gone now. Ever since we accepted Khôltekh's offer of providing guards for the warehouse, items both large and small have gone missing in surprising quantities. I am not blaming the dwarf, you understand... but it is curious. Nothing more than that.\
\
'As a result, we may have some difficulty fulfilling this order. I will see what I can do.'","The Kindred of the Coins have given you orders to deliver to a number of people at various locations within the city: Bith Gabâr, the forum in the Upper Ward, at Stonecliff Market in the Lower Ward, and on the steps of Dahâl Huliz, the arena in the Tor-gardens."},
[2857]={"'Yes?'\
\
You tell Ghâlim that his student Caebar was worried about him, and the man laughs.\
\
'Oh, I am in no danger. I have come to the passages beneath the city in search of a book that has been misplaced. Has my student already finished the task I set before him?'\
\
You assure him that Caebar has done well, and he suggested that Ghâlim might answer your questions about the lands east of Umbar. Ghâlim looks at you appraisingly.\
\
'It is true, I could do that. Unfortunately, there is still the matter of this misplaced book, and I can answer no questions until I have recovered it. If you retrieve it for me I will be happy to instruct you. The book is called 'Kanash-tubu-hârra,' and its author is unknown, which only adds to the tome's allure; it may be somewhere far to the south in the halls of Harkhaphâr, here in Umbar-môkh. The gladiators that roam those halls believe the book possesses some secret sword-art, and they are always stealing it away with the hope they might learn the technique.'","'Scribes and scholars gather upon the terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens. I would there begin the search for our friend Caebar.'","'I had thought Ghâlim would be back by now, but he has not returned. He may still be at Kên Taghlim in the northern reaches of a place called Kamrabezûr, in Umbar-môkh. I overheard him talking about having to go beneath the city for some reason, but his task may be taking longer than he expected. If you find him at Kên Taghlim and tell him I have finished my own task, he may be willing to impart the knowledge you need.\
\
'I hope he is safe. I have heard the passages beneath the city can be dangerous.'","Bring 'Kanash-tubu-hârra' to Ghâlim at Kên Taghlim in Umbar-môkh","Ghâlim is on a terrace in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.","Caebar is on a terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Ghâlim at Kên Taghlim in Umbar-môkh","Retrieve the book 'Kanash-tubu-hârra' from Harkhaphâr in Kamrabezûr, in Umbar-môkh","Chapter 10.4: Scholarly Pursuits","'Yes, thank you, these should provide the amount of pigment for which I was made responsible. The scholars of the Tor-gardens go through a lot of ink and a lot of scrolls as they perform their work. Be glad that today was berry-picking, rather than parchment-making, for that takes much longer!\
\
'I had thought Ghâlim would be back by now, but he has not returned. He may still be at Kên Taghlim in the northern reaches of a place called Kamrabezûr, in Umbar-môkh. I overheard him talking about having to go beneath the city for some reason, but his task may be taking longer than he expected. If you find him at Kên Taghlim and tell him I have finished my own task, he may be willing to impart the knowledge you need.\
\
'I hope he is safe. I have heard the passages beneath the city can be dangerous.'","Find Caebar's teacher Ghâlim at Kên Taghlim in Kamrabezûr, in Umbar-môkh","Ghâlim shakes his head in disapproval","'¿Si?'","'${PLAYER}! It is very good to see you again, my friend!'\
\
Caebar clasps you on the arm and listens to the account of your recent adventures.\
\
'I confess you have made yourself more useful than I. Perhaps it is because I am a man of Gondor and the folk here distrust me, but Ghâlim has been slow to include me in the lessons he administers to his other students. Instead I have been given the duties of a servant: sorting jars of ink, picking berries for pigments, running errands for the scholar and his fellows.\
\
'These are not complaints! When I chose to make a new life for myself here in Umbar, I knew where I must begin. This is merely the first step. If you help me finish my tasks for today I will introduce you to Ghâlim, and he will have much to say about the geography and history of Near Harad.\
\
'Today I have been charged with picking the berries that colour the pigments used for scholars' inks here in the Tor-gardens. I have almost collected enough, but if you help me the work will be sooner done. The berry bushes are just down the steps to the east; I was saving the nearest ones for the task's end, so it would seem to go more quickly as I tired of the errand.'","'What? Have I said something wrong already?'","Given that the preparations for your departure will still take some time, Sirgon believes you should learn what you can about the lands of Near Harad into which you must travel.","Ghâlim tucks the book under one arm and leaves by the door to the surface","'Already you have betrayed your lack of knowledge, young Caebar. You are not to blame for it, but you hail from Gondor, and your words reveal it.\
\
'\\qNear Harad,\\q you name that land, but you speak in error. That is the Gondorian name for that place; indeed, \\qHarad\\q is an Elvish word. It means \\qSouth,\\q for these lands are south of Gondor, and that relationship has been one of uneasy tension, or of war. To the folk who live there it is named Shagâna, the \\qFair Land,\\q but even that makes too simple a more complicated reality.'","Caebar will teach you what he knows, but first he needs your help to finish the chores given to him by his instructor: picking berries from bushes down the steps to the east to be used for the making of inks and pigments.","'I find myself thinking about the Gondorian scribe that sailed with us on the Wave-hunter, ${PLAYER}. Yes, Caebar. When last I spoke with him he said he had found employment in the Tor-gardens performing the duties of a scribe for an esteemed scholar of Umbar. Perhaps he will introduce us to his employer, and this man will tell us what we need to know about the lands of Near Harad into which we must travel?\
\
'Scribes and scholars gather upon the terrace west of the Arena, in the Tor-gardens. I would there begin the search for our friend Caebar.'","Talk to Ghâlim on the terrace in the Tor-gardens","Talk to Caebar on a terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl","Talk to Caebar on the terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens","Caebar is on a terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl, waiting for you to return with the pigment berries you picked.","Pick pigment berries from bushes down the steps to the east (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'This is not the only time the Hûliz from the arena have stolen away 'Kanash-tubu-hârra.' The legend of that tome grows with every passing year, and no amount of study has yet convinced them the arts contained within are beyond their possibility to learn. For me the technique is of no interest; I am attracted to the beauty of its unknown author's prose. He, or she, named it 'Kanash-tubu-hârra,' which means 'Road of Bending Reeds' in the language of Old Shagâni. I thank you for returning it to me.\
\
'But let us climb now to the surface and join my apprentice Caebar where I left him in the Tor-gardens. Then I will answer whatever questions you may have for me. Your recovery of 'Kanash-tubu-hârra' has earned you some of my time.'","Ghâlim is at Kên Taghlim in Umbar-môkh.","Picked pigment berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Caebar's teacher, a man named Ghâlim, is at Kên Taghlim in Kamrabezûr, in Umbar-môkh.","Ghâlim has asked you to retrieve the book 'Kanash-tubu-hârra' from Harkhaphâr, far to the south of Kamrabezûr, in Umbar-môkh.","'There is still the matter of this misplaced book, and I can answer no questions until I have recovered it. If you retrieve it for me I will be happy to instruct you. The book is called Kanash-tubu-hârra, and its author is unknown, which only adds to the tome's allure; it may be somewhere far to the south in the halls of Harkhaphâr, here in Umbar-môkh.'","'Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. My teacher Ghâlim has suggested that I begin the lesson, so I will do the best I can. I must warn you, I do not know a great deal about Near Harad...'","Caebar is on the terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.","'Today I have been charged with picking the berries that colour the pigments used for scholars' inks here in the Tor-gardens. I have almost collected enough, but if you help me the work will be sooner done. The berry bushes are just down the steps to the east; I was saving the nearest ones for the task's end, so it would seem to go more quickly as I tired of the errand.'","You pick up the book 'Kanash-tubu-hârra,' taking care not to damage it","You have found Caebar's teacher Ghâlim","Bring the pigment berries to Caebar on the terrace in the Tor-gardens"},
[2858]={"Chapter 10.4: The Disaster of the Gladden Fields","Meet up with Gandalf further north along the road by the Gladden Fields","Despite the warmth of springtime, you feel a chill in the air","Talk to Gandalf on the road north of Duskenvale, near the Gladden Fields","'Let us continue up the road, ${PLAYER}. We walk in the footsteps of Isildur's company, even three thousand years later.'","'<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around as Isildur did, ${PLAYER}, and imagine the encircling hordes drawing ever nearer.'","As you survey the terrain, you can almost hear the harsh war-cries of the Orcs","Meet up with Gandalf further east along the road, in Laerlad","Gandalf has called a halt alongside the river-bank. He asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> around you as Isildur must have done when he knew the end was near.","Gandalf has called a halt beside the road by the Gladden Fields.","Gandalf asked to meet you on the road north of Duskenvale, near the Gladden Fields.","'Whether they were alerted by the presence of the Ring or not, the Orcs struck as Isildur's company crossed near to the Gladden Fields. The attack came in darkness, with neither sun nor moon in the sky, and in that blackness the Orcs had the greatest advantage.\
\
'<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around us, ${PLAYER}. Isildur and his men were unfamiliar with the lay of the land, but their foes ranged it for years, plundering the towns and villages of Wilderland.'","'I have found that walking can often be the best way to banish troubling distractions, my friend. When I return from such a diversion my thoughts are clear, my mind ready to resolve the problem that had stymied me. It is a habit I picked up from Bilbo, I believe, for his walking-stick was rarely at rest and he thoroughly enjoyed walking the hills and lanes of the Shire. Elrond himself would have his hands full keeping the old hobbit from exploring Imladris on a sunny day, were he not...'\
\
Gandalf trails away, and smiles at you mysteriously.\
\
'But I get ahead of myself, ${PLAYER}. Do you also take enjoyment from strolling in the country? The Gladden Fields are to the south, and it has been some time since there I walked. That is a place of great import, as I am sure you know, for it was there that the Ring lay hidden for many long years. Meet me on the road just north of Duskenvale, near the Gladden Fields, and I will tell you what the Wise can say of the Ring's first great loss. It is gone now, and for good, but the tale is interesting and I will appreciate the diversion.\
\
'But let it not be said that we waste the hours in idleness, ${PLAYER}! Before we speak of the distant past, I ask that you slay Orcs and half-orcs that presently haunt the Gladden Fields. It will be a comfort to the people who dwell in the vales, for such creatures ever pose a threat.'","Gandalf has called a halt along the wooded road in Laerlad. He asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the surrounding countryside and consider the landscape Isildur would have seen as he rode north.","Gandalf has called a halt beside the road alongside the Gladden Fields.","Gandalf desires to walk east along the road into Laerlad, where he will speak further on the subject of Isildur's journey north from Gondor.","'Of his men, only three survived. One of these was Ohtar, Isildur's own esquire, with whom the doomed king entrusted the shards of Narsil. He bade Ohtar bring the broken blade to Rivendell. Did the squire obey his lord's command without complaint, or did he wish to stand by his king and die with him?\
\
'We do not know for certain. What we do know is that Ohtar managed to slip away during the confusion of battle, and after much toil and danger in the wilderness he came to Rivendell safely bearing the shards of Narsil. They became an heirloom of Isildur's line ever after, in Arnor and later among the Rangers in the wild.\
\
'Our account of Isildur ends with the departure of Ohtar. The squire believed Isildur fought on, even without hope of victory, but for long years even the Wise did not know.'","'Here will do.'","Gandalf has called a halt along the river-bank in the Gladden Fields.","'This will do.'","Defeated half-orcs in the Gladden Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around us, ${PLAYER}. Isildur and his men were unfamiliar with the lay of the land, but their foes ranged it for years, plundering the towns and villages of Wilderland.'","'The War of the Last Alliance had ended in victory. Did that success blind Isildur and his men as they rode north? Did they think the Shadow was gone forever, and dark things could trouble them no more? I do not know for certain. They lived in fear of Sauron's evil for so long that it seems to me they may have met his defeat with doubt that it would last.\
\
'Whether they did or did not, it is true that dark things abided still in Middle-earth. The Orcs of Wilderland lay in wait, lurking within the shadows of Mirkwood. Perhaps they heard rumour of Isildur's approach, or perhaps the Ring called out to them.\
\
'Let us continue up the road, ${PLAYER}. We walk in the footsteps of Isildur's company, even three thousand years later.'","'Yes, this place will do.'","'You know of the War of the Last Alliance and the Siege of Barad-dûr that concluded the Second Age. When the fighting was done, the several kindreds that came together for the defeat of Sauron faced long roads back to their respective homelands. With the death of his father Elendil, Isildur ascended to the kingship. After two years of ordering the affairs of Gondor, he set forth to claim his father's throne at Annúminas. He bore the shards of his father's sword, Narsil, which had broken when Sauron was defeated.\
\
'He bore another artifact in secret: the Ruling Ring he had taken from Sauron's hand. Let us walk east along the road into Laerlad, my friend. Further ahead we will speak of Isildur's journey.'","Gandalf has called a halt alongside the river-bank.","Gandalf indicates that he wishes to stop here beside the road","'Onward, ${PLAYER}. The end of the story draws near. It lies to the north-west, down the slope and by the bank of the river.'","'Isildur pressed north, harried by his enemies, but he did not make it far. The Orcs proved relentless, and for every one the Dúnedain killed, two more leapt forward in its stead. Soon the dwindling company could go no further, and Isildur knew there could be no escape.\
\
'He watched as his knights, his captains, and even his own sons fell in the affray. <rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around as he did, ${PLAYER}, and imagine the encircling hordes drawing ever nearer.'","Talk to Gandalf beside the road","Defeated Orcs in the Gladden Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Meet me on the road just north of Duskenvale, near the Gladden Fields, and I will tell you what the Wise can say of the Ring's first great loss. It is gone now, and for good, but the tale is interesting and I will appreciate the diversion.'","'Meet me on the road just north of Duskenvale, near the Gladden Fields, and I will tell you what the Wise can say of the Ring's first great loss. It is gone now, and for good, but the tale is interesting and I will appreciate the diversion.\
\
'But let it not be said that we waste the hours in idleness, ${PLAYER}! Before we speak of the distant past, I ask that you slay the Orcs and half-orcs that presently haunt the the Gladden Fields. It will be a comfort to the people who dwell in the vales, for such creatures ever pose a threat.'","Talk to Gandalf by the wooded road in Laerlad","'<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around us, ${PLAYER}. More than three thousand years have passed since Isildur came this way, but the shape of the land has changed little. This is what he would have seen as he rode, in the company of his sons and his men-at-arms, little suspecting the danger the Ring would draw.'","Gandalf motions for you to stop","Gandalf wants to meet you on the road north of Duskenvale, but first he has asked you to defeat Orcs and half-orcs in the Gladden Fields.","'Isildur rode from Minas Tirith with a small company, including his three eldest sons, following the River Anduin northward. He planned to cross the Misty Mountains, where he would be reunited with his youngest son, Valandil. Being but a child and too young for war, Valandil had remained behind in the safety of Rivendell, and it was for that hidden valley that Isildur intended to ride.\
\
'But the Ring he bore was no mere trinket. Already it yearned to return to its master. It would prove Isildur's undoing.\
\
'<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around us, ${PLAYER}. More than three thousand years have passed since Isildur came this way, but the shape of the land has changed little. This is what he would have seen as he rode, in the company of his sons and his men-at-arms, little suspecting the danger the Ring would draw.'","Gandalf desires to walk north along the road beside the Gladden Fields, where he will speak further on the subject of Isildur's journey north from Gondor.","Gandalf has called a halt beside the road by the Gladden Fields. He asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the surrounding countryside and consider the terrain within which the Orcs attacked Isildur's company.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the surrounding terrain as Gandalf suggested","Defeat Orcs in the Gladden Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gandalf has called a halt along the wooded road in Laerlad.","Gandalf desires to meet you down the slope along the river-bank, further to the north-west.","Talk to Gandalf alongside the river-bank","Meet up with Gandalf by the river-bank, down the slope and to the north-west","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around you as Gandalf suggested","'Emboldened by their advantage in the darkness, the Orcs descended upon Isildur's band with ravenous fury. Even so, it was a hard fight. The Men of Gondor were strong and valiant, and they had much skill at arms. Do not forget that they were survivors of the great war against Mordor, and years of battle had hardened their courage and their resolve.\
\
'But the Orcs were many, and they were treacherous foes, prone to trickery. Their warriors practiced the arts not just of combat, but of deception. The battle that followed was brutal, and blood soaked these hills.\
\
'Onward, ${PLAYER}. The end of the story draws near. It lies to the north-west. Climb down the slope to the bank of the river, and meet me further north.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the countryside nearby as Gandalf suggested","What did Isildur feel as the battle turned against him?","Defeat half-orcs in the Gladden Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gandalf looks around at the countryside with satisfaction","'Let us walk east along the road into Laerlad, my friend. Further ahead we will speak of Isildur's journey.'","Gandalf has run into some difficulty deciphering the mysteries of the Black Book of Mordor, and has decided to walk with you in the Gladden Fields to clear his head."},
[2859]={"There is something strange about this chamber and the statue of Mótsog it contains, but Durin has vowed not to rest until he unravels their mysteries.","Talk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb","Durin contemplates the lifelike statue and the strange chamber in which it stands.","Talk to Durin and unravel the mystery of the long-forgotten chamber","'I am... shaken, I confess it. Why does Mótsog show these visions to us, ${PLAYER}? For what purpose would such a foe of my great ancestor give this knowledge to me? What does Mótsog hope to gain from aiding me thus?'","Something about the lifelike visage compels your eye, but the strange enchantment that encircles the statue of Mótsog resists your study. The feeling that you are being watched by an invisible presence grows stronger and more unwelcome.","Durin stands in Mótsog's Tomb, shaken by what he has seen and experienced.","Chapter 10.4: The Dreaming Dwarf","'Something is not right, ${PLAYER}. We are being watched. Can you sense it?\
\
'Show yourself, villain!'"},
[2860]={"Mótsog stands in a long-forgotten chamber deep below Gundabad.","Talk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb","'I will not be swayed by honeyed words from an enemy's tongue, ${PLAYER}. Did you mark how often he called me his friend? But it is not so. Remain on your guard, and I will do the same.'\
\
Durin stares coldly at the beardless dwarf standing in the ancient crypt.\
\
'I know you for an enemy, Mótsog, and I demand that you account for yourself! Do you deny your treachery?'","'See you now that I deny nothing?\
\
'You who were Durin: you were my friend, and my lord, but I coveted your title and your lands, the respect and the love that was given you. I listened too closely to those of my people who whispered that I might truly be an Eighth Father of the Dwarves.'\
\
Mótsog turns his attention to you.\
\
'Aye, an Eighth Father to join the other Seven. \\qIf there were eight, and not seven,\\q my people whispered, \\qabout what else might they deceive us?\\q Some suggested, falsely, that perhaps I awoke first beneath the mountains, and it was Durin who usurped my rights and privileges! Durin was the usurper!\
\
'They were false whispers, but they echoed loudly in the halls of Gundabad while Durin was away, and I did not speak against them as I should have done. That failure led in direct line to the Greymaul Rebellion.'\
\
Mótsog once again addresses Durin.\
\
'No, my friend. I do not deny my treachery. Neither do I deny the blood spilt by those who followed me.'","Durin wears an impassive expression as he considers Mótsog.\
\
'These crimes are unforgiveable, and they match my understanding of the Greymaul Rebellion. You deserved the death given to you by my ancestor Durin, to whom you owed fealty.\
\
'You claim you were his friend? You say you speak the truth about the Greymaul Rebellion, but I deem you speak falsely on this: you were no friend of Durin. Nor are you a friend of mine.'","Durin has demanded that Mótsog account for himself, and deny his treachery if he can.","Chapter 10.5: The Greymaul Rebellion","'Deny your treachery, if you can!'","Durin stands in Mótsog's Tomb deep beneath Gundabad.","'I do not deny it, Durin who was once my friend.'\
\
Behind you Durin snorts loudly with disgust.\
\
'It is true,' Mótsog continues. 'Once we were great friends, and you trusted me with your kingdom. But I do not deny my treachery. Hear how it was, and you may remember it anew.'","Talk to Mótsog","Talk to Mótsog and hear his account","'I do not deny my treachery.'"},
[2861]={"Gandalf desires to conclude his tale of the Disaster of the Gladden Fields, where Isildur fell and the Ruling Ring was lost.","Gandalf waits on the island of Tol Send, ready to conclude the story of Isildur and his loss of the Ring.","'We believed the Ring had been borne on the current to the Sea, and that it left this Middle-earth. The truth, and the rediscovery of the Ring, has now shown otherwise. <rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around you, ${PLAYER}, and imagine Isildur's despair as he rose from the water without the Enemy's Ring.'","'For many years following the Disaster of the Gladden Fields, none knew what became of Isildur. Most believed he perished in the ambush shortly after Ohtar escaped with the shards of Narsil, for there was no further word of the king. His body was never found, and there was no claim for ransom by the Orcs or their masters.\
\
'But in time, the Wise learned his true fate. After sending Ohtar away, Isildur saw but one hope for his survival. Refusing to allow the Ring to fall back into the hands of the enemy, he put it on and disappeared even amidst the tumult of the battle. Leaving the Orcs to the fury of their confusion, he fled to the river and sought to swim across.\
\
'See the islet over yonder, to the west? I believe that is where the son of Elendil intended to go. Let us follow him, ${PLAYER}, and pick up his story at its ending.'","'See the islet over yonder, to the west? I believe that is where the son of Elendil intended to go. Let us follow him, ${PLAYER}, and pick up his story at its ending.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around you on the isle of Tol Send, as Isildur must have done","Chapter 10.5: The Isle of the Flowers","'Bereft of the safety provided by the Ring's power, Isildur did not live for much longer. The Orcs spied him standing by the water and shot him with arrows. As the tales say, he breathed his last breath here, in the Gladden Fields.\
\
'I believe it happened on this very eyot, which is why these flowers bloom here still, rather than the gladdens that spring to life elsewhere in the fields. \\qSimbelmynë\\q they are called in Rohan, where they cover the grave-mounds of many dead kings.\
\
'And so Isildur at last met his end, betrayed by the Ring and slain by his foes before he could return to the lands he hoped to rule. But his tomb at Annúminas stands empty, for his bones remain unfound to this day.'","The island is covered in small white flowers","Meet Gandalf on Tol Send, a small island in the Anduin to the west","Gandalf has pointed out an island in the Anduin to the west, declaring that the end of Isildur's story can there be told.","The sound of the water rushing by fills your ears, but all else is quiet","'The River Anduin is mighty, and it was no less so when Isildur sought to swim across; the effort nearly killed him, but still he managed to reach the island. But alas! While he was still in the water, the Ring betrayed him. It slipped from his finger and was lost.\
\
'Even when the Wise pieced together this account of the events, we did not know the truth entire. We believed the Ring had been borne on the current to the Sea, and that it left this Middle-earth. The truth, and the rediscovery of the Ring, has now shown otherwise.\
\
'<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around you, ${PLAYER}, and imagine Isildur's despair as he rose from the water without the Enemy's Ring.'","Gandalf asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> around you while standing on the isle of Tol Send, as Isildur must have done after swimming across the river.","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send"},
[2862]={"'I bid you good fortune if your journeys bring you into Shagâna. Farewell.'","'Shagâna, the Fair Land. Yes, it was fair, once. Tales from long ago speak of a green and fertile land, threaded with mighty rivers. The men who came to that place worked the land, their crops thriving, and they harvested valuable spices and rare wood from the forests, and gold and jewels from beneath the hills. But that was long ago. The wealth of Shagâna was like a camp-fire set upon a hill, and covetous men saw it from far away, and hungered for the spices, and the rare woods, and the gold and the jewels. These men came from even further south, in Jarmât, which my student Caebar might call \\qFar Harad,\\q but they came too from Khand in the east.\
\
'They came from other directions, as well: from the west and from the north. They came from Númenor, and later from Gondor. The Shagâni number these among their cruelest oppressors.'","Keeping his eyes upon you, Ghâlim slowly upends the jar. Water spills out onto the ground until the jar is empty.","Caebar wishes to do what he can to help you learn about the lands into which you must travel.","Retrieve a jar of clean water for Ghâlim from the fountain down the stairs to the east of the terrace in the Tor-gardens","Ghâlim stands on the terrace in the Tor-gardens, waiting for you to return with the jar of water he requested.","A jar of clean water can be found down the stairs to the east of the terrace in the Tor-gardens.","Chapter 10.5: The Lands of Shagâna","Ghâlim upends the jar you brought him and spills the water onto the ground","Caebar is on the terrace in the Tor-gardens.","Ghâlim has wasted the clean water you brought to him in service of making a point.","'Throughout the lands of the south he was known as He-Who-Sees-All, or Barkhûsh, and he came to dominate various smaller kingdoms and in time even the great Empire of Ordâkh. Those who opposed his rise were slain, in terrible number, and as the power of those kingdoms grew so too did that of Barkhûsh. Fewer and fewer stood against the might of this Dark Lord and his servants, and more and more believed that his and their strength might serve to drive back their ancestral enemies: the Khandari, the Númenóreans, the Dúnedain, the Gondorians.\
\
'You ask how Barkhûsh came to dominate the Fair Land? That was the foundation: his church ruled through Fear, but so too did it promise something the Shagâni had sought for centuries: victory over their enemies. Was it a lie? Perhaps it was, and the execution of that lie would forever change the face of Shagâna, and the fate of its people.\
\
'But I have grown parched. Bring me a jar of water from the fountain down the stairs to the east and I will tell you how Barkhûsh and the vast Empire he now controlled conquered the Fair Land and transformed it forever.'","Ghâlim is in the Tor-gardens, instructing you about the lands of Shagâna.","Return to Ghâlim with the jar of clean water","Talk to Caebar on the terrace in the Tor-gardens","'Has nothing among these legends spoken of a Song of Waves and Wind?'","Wait for Ghâlim to speak","Talk to Ghâlim on the terrace in the Tor-gardens","'It is the most valuable of all the resources to be found in this part of Middle-earth, more valuable than any of Lady Hármelak's golden coins or the Abâshal prized by Kinsman Khôltekh and the Temámir dwarves.\
\
'Water. Only with it can crops thrive; without it life cannot survive. You will notice its absence within a day; within three days you would kill to acquire it, or perish yourself. But water can be even more valuable than this. Water can protect you from your enemies. It can serve as a barrier, and if that barrier disappears...'\
\
Ghâlim falls silent, considering the ground by his feet where the water he poured has already soaked into the gaps in the cobbles and vanished.\
\
'Two hundred years ago, a terrible drought and famine fell upon the green fields of Sûgedin, where once thrived the Abundant Kingdom of Nísaka. The River Usâl ran dry, leaving only the arid and cracked channel that was once its river-bed. Desert claimed the Khûd, and the fertile land on either side of the Usâl became the Lâkhedin, the Witherlands. This distressing process came to be called the Great Dearth, and the lands through which the Usâl flowed never recovered. They will never be green again.\
\
'The drying of the River Usâl removed the last barrier between Shagâna and the Great Southern Empire of Ordâkh. The armies of the Ordâkhai marched north into Shagâna and brought formerly separate kingdoms under the control of the Hûl of Ordâkh, and the Dark Lord he served.\
\
'Most learned men believe the Great Dearth was not caused by nature, but was the result of Ordâkhai sorcery given to them by Barkhûsh. Ever was the Dark Lord seeking to remove the barriers between the lands under his control and those he sought.'","'I have grown parched. Bring me a jar of water from the fountain down the stairs to the east and I will tell you how Barkhûsh and the vast Empire he now controlled conquered the Fair Land and transformed it forever.'","'The Song of Waves and Wind? No, I am not familiar with such a tale or legend as that.\
\
'The lands to the east and south of the Cape of Umbar contain many mysteries, and the histories of the people who dwell there are complex; it could be the mention of such a thing is simply buried, or lost to time. Water and wind are both of great significance to the people who dwell in Shagâna, for each have greatly affected their lives across the centuries.\
\
'If your travels bring you to these lands, I advise you to listen to the folk who dwell there, for they will be better teachers on such matters than even I can claim to be, with all my renown!\
\
'I sense now that I have given you what instruction you sought, and I must take my leave. Perhaps one day my student Caebar will be able to share such knowledge as this with you, but he is still young and unlearned. It will be some time. Thank you again for the return of 'Kanash-tubu-hârra.'\
\
'I bid you good fortune if your journeys bring you into Shagâna. Farewell.'","You pick up the jar of clean fountain-water","'Thank you for providing this helpful instruction to us, Ghâlim. I appreciate your teachings, and for imparting this knowledge to the both of us!'","Suitably chastened by the words of his instructor, Caebar wishes to do what he can to help you learn about the lands into which you must travel.","'Can this be true? Can the sorceries of the Empire of Ordâkh truly have such an effect upon something so large as a swift-flowing river?'\
\
Caebar immediately puts a hand over his eyes.\
\
'No, I am being foolish. How could I have forgotten the terrible smoke that Sauron sent before his armies during the war? The day without a dawn came to all of Gondor, darkening even distant Ethring, where my family lives. My mother and uncle resented my absence on that terrible day and the weeks that followed, but I witnessed it in Minas Tirith and knew the despair of it even as they did. Of course Sauron could grant to the Ordâkhai such terrible powers, if it served his fell purposes.'\
\
Caebar removes his hand from his eyes, now widened with sudden realization.\
\
'Ghâlim, have you ever heard of something called the Song of Waves and Wind? Could it be some tale or legend of Sauron, or of Ordâkh? Might it be related to the Great Dearth that dried the River Usâl and brought the desert to Shagâna?'","'I understand the actions of Gondor in the south may appear unjustified to the Haradrim, but none who join the armies of Sauron can claim to stand on the side of justice! How can the people of Harad...?'\
\
Caebar sputters to a halt.\
\
'How did the folk of Shagâna come to stand with Sauron, Ghâlim? Did they not oppose his evil? Were there none who fought his domination?'","Ghâlim is on the terrace in the Tor-gardens.","'How did the folk of Shagâna come to stand with Sauron, Ghâlim? Did they not oppose his evil? Were there none who fought his domination?'","'The wealth of Shagâna was like a camp-fire set upon a hill, and covetous men saw it from far away, and hungered for the spices, and the rare woods, and the gold and the jewels. These men came from even further south, in Jarmât, which my student Caebar might call \\qFar Harad,\\q but they came too from Khand in the east. They came from other directions, as well: from the west and from the north. They came from Númenor, and later from Gondor. The Shagâni number these among their cruelest oppressors.'","'Most learned men believe that the Great Dearth was not caused by nature, but was the result of Ordâkhai sorcery given to them by Barkhûsh. Ever was the Dark Lord seeking to remove the barriers between the lands under his control and those he sought.'","Ghâlim has determined that you need some instruction in the geography and history of the land men of Gondor call \\qNear Harad\\q but which the folk who live there call \\qShagâna.\\q","'Thank you for this water. It will prove most helpful with my demonstration.'\
\
He takes a brief sip of water from the jar before continuing.\
\
'East and south of Umbar Baharbêl, beyond the marshlands of Ambarûl, there was a green and fertile plain called Sûgedin, bordered on the south by the River Usâl. That waterway formed a natural barrier between Shagâna and the lands where originated the Great Southern Empire of Ordâkh.'"},
[2863]={"'This is a surprise, ${PLAYER}! I did not expect you to return to our village so soon, but I am pleased that you have done so, and with more flanks for me to salt and season for the village! Oh, these are intended to replace the carcass our hunters left behind? It is good to fill the hole in our food-stores.\
\
'The Woodmen of Hultvís have long relied on Eurik and his son, and other of our hunters, to bring back food for the village. I have never known Eurik to flee like this. Now that he has returned to the village, I know he feels terribly about what happened. If you speak with him about the apparition he saw, please do not chide him overmuch. Many frightening things stalk the woods hereabout, and I know that if a hunter such as he saw fit to run away, there was surely good reason for it!'","'Yes, I knew that Elrond and much of his household would be making the journey across the mountains, ${PLAYER}. Why did you think I suggested doubling the quantities of each errand Grimbeorn requested that you complete? For my own amusement?'\
\
Gandalf chuckles quietly, and his eyes twinkle.\
\
'Nay. That was merely an additional benefit, my friend.'","'If you can hunt more harts in Woodsedge for us we should be able to fill the hole left in our stores. Once you have gathered some replacement flanks, bring them to Veremund as you did before and Hultvís will be grateful.'","'Where is your Wizard now, ${PLAYER}?'","'The creature I saw filled me with such terror! My blood ran cold and I felt rooted to the spot to see it. At first I thought I beheld Vagári, spectral wanderer of the Gladden, but nay; this was something else. I can still see its terrible visage! The apparition stood in the waters of the Old Ford, half-across, and as the courage drained from me I urged my son Badwila to leave our prey behind. Together we fled, and I could not bear to look behind us as we ran, for I expected to see the terrible creature close behind! Bodily it did not follow us, but I can still see its face in my mind, and that seems a far worse pursuit.\
\
'If you go in search of it, go to the Old Ford to the north-west, but bring caution with you and do not fear to flee, as I did! The shame is hard to bear, but on this day at least I hold life more precious than honour.'","'You have nothing to fear from me, ${PLAYER}. Not on this day.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Eurik, a hunter from Hultvís, was frightened away from his prey by a terrible apparition at the Old Ford, located in the Wolf-denes north-west of the village.","'Hold, ${PLAYER}. I do not intend to harm you. I wish only to speak with you. Will you hear my words?'","Adalfon at the village of Hultvís may have a request for you.","Talk to Adalfon at the village of Hultvís","Karazgar stands by the Old Ford. He has declared that he means you no harm, but wishes only to speak with you.","Collected forest-hart flanks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect forest-hart flanks in Woodsedge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Veremund is by the cooking fires in the village of Hultvís.","Eurik is in the village of Hultvís.","'That is the end of the tale, ${PLAYER}, and it has taken many years to piece it together. This unassuming island in the Anduin has shaped the fate of Middle-earth in its own way, has it not? How might things have transpired had Isildur not swam across the river to reach it? Agents of Sauron would have taken the Ring from his body, and the Dark Lord's dominance would be all but assured.\
\
'Be glad it was not so! The Ring worked great evil on its course, but in the end the actions of Isildur enabled its destruction, these many years later.\
\
'I have enjoyed our walk, my friend, and now I will return to the Beorninghús and resume my study of the Black Book. I will meet you there, but before you return I ask that you pay a visit to Hultvís, the village of the Woodmen at Woodsedge. They suffered greatly during the War of the Ring, and their efforts to rebuild and return their lives to normal have not yet borne fruit.\
\
'You say you have already lent your aid to the Woodmen? I know that, ${PLAYER}! Do you think I would ask you to return without reason? If you have the good fortune to know a Wizard, know that he is not to be ignored! Go to Hultvís and ask me no more questions!'","Adalfon asked you to slay forest-harts in Woodsedge for their flanks, in order to help fill the hole left in the town's food-stores.","Chapter 10.6: A Request","'Now that Eurik has returned to the village, I know he feels terribly about what happened. If you speak with him about the apparition he saw, please do not chide him overmuch. Many frightening things stalk the woods hereabout, and I know that if a hunter such as he saw fit to run away, there was surely good reason for it!'","Gandalf stands with Elrond outside the Beorninghús.","Talk to Karazgar, but remain alert for treachery","Karazgar stares at you, his eyes filled with malice.","Investigate the terrible apparition Eurik saw at the Old Ford","Talk to Karazgar and learn of his request","Bring the flanks to Veremund by the cooking fires in Hultvís","Gandalf has asked you to return Hultvís, the village of the Woodmen, and lend them whatever assistance they might require.","'I see you have collected a good number of flanks, ${PLAYER}! These will serve nicely to replace the carcass our hunter left behind.'","You have found the apparition Eurik encountered: Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior!","'Oh, ${PLAYER}, you have returned. I suppose you must have heard tell of my shame from others in the village? It is true that I abandoned my hunt, and now that my son and I have returned to safety I can hardly bear to give voice to the fear I felt. Before today I would never have counted myself a coward, but...'\
\
Eurik shakes his head sadly.\
\
'The creature I saw filled me with such terror! My blood ran cold and I felt rooted to the spot to see it. At first I thought I beheld Vagári, spectral wanderer of the Gladden, but nay; this was something else. I can still see its terrible visage! The apparition stood in the waters of the Old Ford, half-across, and as the courage drained from me I urged my son Badwila to leave our prey behind. Together we fled, and I could not bear to look behind us as we ran, for I expected to see the terrible creature close behind! Bodily it did not follow us, but I can still see its face in my mind, and that seems a far worse pursuit.\
\
'If you go in search of it, go to the Old Ford to the north-west, but bring caution with you and do not fear to flee, as I did! The shame is hard to bear, but on this day at least I hold life more precious than honour.'","'Before you return to the Beorninghús I ask that you pay a visit to Hultvís, the village of the Woodmen at Woodsedge. They suffered greatly during the War of the Ring, and their efforts to rebuild and return their lives to normal have not yet borne fruit.\
\
'You say you have already lent your aid to the Woodmen? I know that, ${PLAYER}! Do you think I would ask you to return without reason? If you have the good fortune to know a Wizard, know that he is not to be ignored! Go to Hultvís and ask me no more questions!'","Talk to Eurik in Hultvís","Talk to Gandalf outside the Beorninghús","'I did not think to see you again, ${PLAYER}, but fortune must smile on Hultvís for you to return to us so quickly; as it happens we do have need of you. Two of our hunters were frightened away from their prey by some apparition, and while no one in the village would wish for them to endanger themselves, they left the carcass behind. Our food-stores are too low to do without such provisions.\
\
'Creatures of the vale have surely found the abandoned carcass by now, but if you can hunt more forest-harts in Woodsedge for us we should be able to fill the hole its loss left in our stores. Once you have gathered some replacement flanks, bring them to Veremund as you did before and Hultvís will be grateful.'"},
[2864]={"Talk to Sirgon by the east gate of Umbar Baharbêl","Talk to Rothog in Dâr Laja","'There has been a miscommunication with the owner of the warehouse that was going to supply this expedition. I will remain and... correct... this error, but as a result it will be some time before I can depart.'\
\
You consider sharing with Khôltekh the words of Caebar, who believed the power of the Kindred would speed along the preparations, but decide to keep them to yourself instead.\
\
'Hármelak has had some difficulties of her own arranging for the caravan, but fewer mouths to feed on the journey will require fewer supplies. Her failure makes my own task more simple, which puts a smile on my face.'\
\
Khôltekh smiles dangerously and you take your leave of him.","'I will remedy the situation with Jakbir, to his detriment, but this matter will not delay your departure. You will travel lighter than we planned. Speak to the others and learn how fare their own preparations.'","'Belondor tells me the rest of our travelling party has been delayed, but they will join us when they can? I confess this small group is more to my liking, but will this endanger the success of our mission?\
\
'I would not want to face Azagath and Nakási in battle without the half-troll at our side!'","Belondor is by the east gate of the city.","Talk to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja","'Rothog and Khôltekh will join us when they can. For now, this will be our travelling company as we venture in pursuit of Azagath and Nakási.\
\
'Onward! To victory and vengeance!'","'This is everyone?'","Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja","With preparations for the journey delayed or otherwise obstructed, the Kindred has suggested that you gather at the east gate of the city and form an advance travelling party.","Talk to Belondor by the east gate of Umbar Baharbêl","'You plan to return to Dâr Laja and see how fare the preparations of the Kindred of the Coins? Such things must happen more swiftly in Umbar than in Gondor, for the Kindred possesses all the power of a King... but there are many more of them!'","You should speak with Hármelak about the status of the preparations. The Golden Queen is inside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja.","'Part of me wishes I could come with you on this journey, ${PLAYER}... but a greater portion knows I cannot. After all, I was quite near to not surviving my last adventure with you, and might have perished among the rocks of the Shield Isles when the Wave-hunter ran aground during the storm!\
\
'I hope some of the good fortune that spared me will attend you on your next adventure, my friend, and I will eagerly await your safe return to Umbar when it is done. You will have to tell me all about it!\
\
'But now you plan to return to Dâr Laja and see how fare the preparations of the Kindred of the Coins? Such things must happen more swiftly in Umbar than in Gondor, for the Kindred possesses all the power of a King... but there are many more of them!'","Sirgon is by the east gate of the city.","'Have I given you the impression that my words are mere suggestions, ${PLAYER}, and not commands? How else can it be that Jakbir has denied the Kindred the use of his caravan for this journey? He thinks to increase the treasure he must be paid from the coffers of Umbar Baharbêl, as if there are no other caravans we might hire for this purpose!\
\
'He is mistaken, and this mistake will be made clear to him. The Kindred of the Coins will not suffer such fools as he. Does he believe I do not punish those who think to take advantage of my mercy, or that of my agents? No caravan will accompany your travelling company, ${PLAYER}. I will remedy the situation with Jakbir, to his detriment, but this matter will not delay your departure. You will travel lighter than we planned. Speak to the others and learn how fare their own preparations.'","Once the preparations for your departure have been made, you will be ready to leave the city of Umbar Baharbêl behind and set forth into the lands of Shagâna.","Meet with your companions at the east gate of the city","Chapter 10.6: Leave The City Behind, Part Two","Talk to Hármelak in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","'This small group is more to my liking, but will this endanger the success of our mission? I would not want to face Azagath and Nakási in battle without the half-troll at our side!'","Hármelak has asked you to speak with the other members of the Kindred of the Coins in Dâr Laja.","'I cannot leave yet. My khopeshes are sharp, for now, but the quality of the weapons I requested from Dahâl Huliz is unsatisfactory. To set forth on an unknown road, into lands that test the might and the will of a warrior, without suitable arms? Unacceptable!\
\
'If we were a-ship I would hold he who disappointed me over the water by one foot until he satisfied the bargain. Alas that remedy is not available here: the fountains of Umbar Baharbêl are not deep enough!'\
\
Rothog rumbles in dissatisfaction.\
\
'There is another problem, but I will not burden you with it. I will say just this: should a friend of yours gift you an animal, ensure that the men who care for it have bravery enough to feed it, or become dinner themselves. Otherwise it may become an annoyance.\
\
'Khôltekh waits as well. I will travel with him when he is ready, and the two of us will meet up with you when we can.'","The advance travelling party has assembled at the east gate","'Hármelak and Khôltekh speak of difficulties, but to my eyes the sun shines upon our road: Mêshka has given her blessing for this journey. My wife came to speak with me on this matter shortly after you left Dâr Laja, and she made clear her approval of this adventure. She wishes me to avenge our family and those of my crew upon the traitor Azagath and his ally Nakási, and put these sorrowful days behind us.\
\
'Mêshka's love will follow me on this road, and it will remain when I return home in triumph. I am ready to depart, the sooner to return! After you have spoken with the others, I will meet you at the east gate of the city, with our eyes turned to the sunrise and the road ahead.'"},
[2866]={"'We should speak with Khashig's fellow guardsman Hûta at his post where the road runs into Ambarûl.'","'I cannot say what will remain a thousand years from now, but from my heart I speak when I say the Umbari must not suffer beneath the heel of a distant power: not Ordâkh, not Mordor, and not Gondor. We must build for ourselves lives of peace and safety that can become the envy of all the world.'\
\
Hûta stands up straighter and taller than before.\
\
'I will not disappoint you, Kinsman Belondor. If I allowed my watchfulness to wane in recent days, I apologize for it! No longer.\
\
'As you pass into Ambarûl, I suggest you follow the road along the marsh until it turns south. That will bring you to the largest settlement of the region, a town built on wooden pilings that the people there call Iridír. I have seen the women warriors of that place from afar, and they appear quite deadly with the weapons they carry. You should introduce yourself to them before they consider you to be strangers and introduce themselves to you, if you take my meaning. It would be wisest for you to approach them on friendly terms while you have the opportunity!'","'As you pass into Ambarûl, I suggest you follow the road along the marsh until it turns south. That will bring you to the largest settlement of the region, a town built on wooden pilings that the people there call Iridír. I have seen the women warriors of that place from afar, and they appear quite deadly with the weapons they carry. You should introduce yourself to them before they consider you to be strangers and introduce themselves to you, if you take my meaning. It would be wisest for you to approach them on friendly terms while you have the opportunity!'","Defeated stinging sand-flies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I can make no such decision today, guardsman Hûta.'\
\
Belondor turns his gaze upon the remains of Telperiën's Wall, and when he speaks again his tone is thoughtful.\
\
'A queen of Númenor ordered the building of this wall, long ago, to protect her coastal holdings from the inland peoples of Shagâna. It was damaged over the centuries by war, by the shifting of the earth, and by the passage of Time. She and the folk she sought to protect have been dead for thousands of years, but Telperiën's Wall still stands, in large part, marking that ancient desire.\
\
'The things we build outlast us, guardsman Hûta. What has Umbar built?'","'Perhaps I can soon return home, Kinsman Belondor?'","Bring the fallen stones to Hûta at his guard-post by Telperiën's Wall","'Khashig is right, ${PLAYER}. The Kindred of the Coins are well-known to the Umbari, but as we travel further away from the city the names and faces of our quarry will be less familiar to the people we meet. Azagath and Nakási may travel more openly in the lands ahead of us.\
\
'But we should speak with Khashig's fellow guardsman Hûta at his post where the road runs into Ambarûl.'","'What brings you this way, travellers?'","Talk to Hûta at his guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall","Journey east to the guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall","'What brings you this way, travellers? The caravans have slowed in recent days, and I have had little company save for the sand-flies... they are drawn by the heat, and make my days a misery.'\
\
Khashig peers at each of your companions in turn, and when his gaze reaches Belondor he spreads his hands in surprise.\
\
'Belondor of the Fleet-fast? This is a pleasure and an honour! The Kindred of the Coins has spared little thought for me or for Hûta since we were sent to man these posts in the days following their rise. I see now I was mistaken!'","Journey to the guard-post east of Umbar Baharbêl","'Hûta might have seen something. I wish I could be more of a help to you and your companions!'","Belondor is at the guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall.","The first step of your journey lies to the east of the city, along the Road of Riches, at the guard-post Belondor suggested.","'¿Si?'","Defeat stinging sand-flies east of the city for Khashig (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Hûta at the guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall","Retrieve fallen stones along Telperiën's Wall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Khashig acknowledges the arrival of your travelling party with a raised eyebrow","'Thank you for collecting these stones. I understand you did not see the people you seek? I am sorry, but I appreciate you following the ruins of the wall to the north and back again. I do not patrol its length as often as perhaps I should.\
\
'Ordâkh is a long way from here, across the southern desert, and their soldiers are in disarray. Even with the wall in such a state of disrepair I do not think the Ordâkhai can pose much of a threat to Umbar. Without the sorcery of their Dark Lord, how can they hope to threaten our soldiers?\
\
'Perhaps I can soon return home, Kinsman Belondor?'","Talk to Corudan at the guard-post east of the city","Patrol northward along Telperiën's Wall","You have arrived beside Telperiën's Wall, where Hûta keeps watch","Khashig is at his guard-post east of the city.","Talk to Khashig at the guard-post east of the city","'The things we build outlast us, guardsman Hûta. What has Umbar built?'","'Thank you for taking care of those insects, my friends. I know they will return, for nothing keeps the pests away for long, but even an hour's reprieve is worth celebrating! Now perhaps you will tell me what brings Belondor of the Fleet-fast to my guard-post? I cannot believe it was only to bring some comfort to poor Khashig, guardian of the road!'\
\
Belondor explains that the four of you are seeking Azagath Sea-shadow and Nakási Wave-reaper, who you believe came this way sometime in the past few days. Khashig gazes into the distance, deep in thought.\
\
'Ah, I wish I could tell you I have seen this travelling party, but you are the only one of that esteemed group to visit poor Khashig outside the city, Kinsman Belondor. Each member of the Kindred is well-known to the Umbari who dwell in these lands, for we count them heroes: the brave men and women who saved us from the Church of the All-seeing and the Empire of Ordâkh. If they wished to remain unseen, they might take pains to stay hidden from the eyes of any Umbari as they travelled. Also, I confess to you that my charge is to watch eastward, not westward, and the sand-flies may have affected my vigilance! But no longer, I assure you!\
\
'If you continue east you will reach my fellow guardsman Hûta, who watches the road where it passes by Telperiën's Wall and into Ambarûl. He may have seen something. The folk of that land do not revere the Kindred as do the Umbari, and your fellows may not feel as much need for secrecy.'","'It is unusual for folk to come this way without a larger caravan behind them, strangers. I must warn you the Road of Riches has become more perilous in recent weeks, and it has never been safe.'\
\
You ask Hûta if Azagath Sea-shadow or Nakási Wave-reaper has come this way, and he stares at you blankly.\
\
'I have not seen Azagath, that I can tell you for certain! I cannot imagine what business could bring him so far outside the city. But I am not familiar with this woman's name, this Nakási. She sounds like a Corsair. There is water and marshland in Ambarûl, along the Ikorbân River, but I have not heard of Corsairs sailing upriver. There is simply nothing there.\
\
'When I was commanded to keep this guard-post, I asked for men to help me guard the length of Telperiën's Wall, but I was denied. It could be the people you seek passed by the wall further to the north. Perhaps you should patrol that way and see if there is any sign of them? If you can pick up some of the fallen stones along the way I would appreciate it. From time to time I collect them and stack them here by my guard-post, but I have not made the walk recently.'","You followed Hûta's suggestion but found nothing out of the ordinary","Chapter 10.7: Beyond Telperiën's Wall","Talk to Rahâzi at the entrance of Iridír","Retrieved fallen stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Corudan is at the guard-post east of the city.","'The caravans have slowed in recent days, and I have had little company but the sand-flies... they are drawn by the heat, and make my days a misery. You will help take care of them for me?'","'It could be the people you seek passed by the wall further to the north. Perhaps you should patrol that way and see if there is any sign of them? If you can pick up some of the fallen stones along the way I would appreciate it. From time to time I collect them and stack them here by my guard-post, but I have not made the walk recently.'","The next step of your journey lies further to the east, by the ruins of Telperiën's Wall.","A young woman leaving the village stops in her tracks at the sight of you","Find the west entrance to the village of Iridír, in Ambarûl","Belondor suggests you help Khashig with the sand-flies that trouble him","Sand-flies can be found in the vicinity of Khashig's guard-post, east of Umbar Baharbêl.","Hûta asked you to patrol northward and retrieve stones that have fallen from the wall.","Hûta gave you directions to the village of Iridír in Ambarûl, east of Telperiën's Wall.","Rahâzi stops in her tracks as you seek to enter the village of Iridír.","While Khôltekh and Rothog remain behind to see to the final preparations, your advance company sets forth toward the Valley of Ikorbân in the lands of Shagâna.","'You are a long way from home, strangers. What brings you to Iridír in Ambarûl? Speak quickly, for I am one of the Dumûri and I will not hesitate to strike you down if you bring evil here!'","'When trade with the southern kingdoms thrived, the flat ground to the east of the city was alive with a colourful assemblage of tents and caravans preparing to depart along the Road of Riches. Now there are few, for such trade has slowed to but a trickle, but theirs is the road upon which we will begin, and follow it eastward until we find some sign of Azagath.\
\
'There should be a guard-post east along the road. Let us go there now and see what its sentries have seen.'","Hûta is at his guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall.","Talk to Belondor at the guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall","'There should be a guard-post east along the road. Let us go there now and see what its sentries have seen.'","'If you continue east you will reach my fellow guardsman Hûta, who watches the road where it passes by Telperiën's Wall and into Ambarûl. He may have seen something. The folk of that land do not revere the Kindred as do the Umbari, and your fellows may not feel as much need for secrecy.'","Talk to Khashig at the guard-post east of Umbar Baharbêl"},
[2867]={"Grimbeorn is waiting to speak with you about the many new arrivals at his home.","Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","'I have never seen the home of the Beornings, ${PLAYER}, but it seems most lovely. The beauty of the flower-fields and the buzzing of the bee-pastures are quite different than the sights and sounds of Imladris and Lórien.\
\
'We will stay here for a short time before continuing on to Lothlórien, where we will meet up with my brothers. Then we will continue on to Gondor and the White City, and by midsummer we will toll the wedding-bells throughout the kingdom. I hope you will attend my wedding, ${PLAYER}, for I understand you have been a help to all of Middle-earth and to my betrothed, and it is his dear wish that you be there with us.\
\
'Will you also ask the Lord of the Beornings to attend? It is very kind of him to offer his hospitality to my father's household while we stay here a time.'","Talk to Elrond at the Beorninghús","Elrond, Arwen, and Glorfindel have come to the Beorninghús on their journey to Gondor.","'This is what happens when I open my doors to a Wizard and his companion, ${PLAYER}! \\qThere will only be two of us,\\q you told me. And then there were more, and more, and more! Now an Elf-lord and his household have taken up residence at my humble home!\
\
'What? Do I wish to attend the wedding of the Elf-maiden and the King of Gondor? Bah! Do you think an invitation will remedy these irritations and inconveniences? They might have consulted with me before their arrival! The Wizard has already given up on entertaining his friends! He has gone inside again. Follow him and convey my displeasure, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Attend the wedding? Bah!'","'Gandalf has assured me my household will be welcome, and that you will speak to Grimbeorn, the Lord of the Beornings, on our behalf.'","Chapter 10.7: The Arrival of the Wise","'Speak to the company and learn how they fared during their passage of the mountains; I trust they encountered no problems. Few creatures in this Middle-earth would dare to trouble either Elrond or Glorfindel when apart, and when together only the most fool-hardy would think of it.\
\
'But there have always been fools in service of the Enemy.'","'The Wizard has already given up on entertaining his friends! He has gone inside again. Follow him and convey my displeasure, ${PLAYER}.'","'Speak to the company and learn how they fared during their passage of the Misty Mountains.'","Elrond and some of his household have made the journey across the Misty Mountains in preparation for his daughter's wedding.","Talk to Glorfindel at the Beorninghús","Gandalf has gone back inside the Beorninghús to study the Black Book of Mordor.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, it is good to see you outside the confines of my library, for ever it seemed I found you there.\
\
'My daughter journeys to Minas Tirith for her wedding to Aragorn Elessar, King of Gondor, and I have brought such of my household as desired to attend her. We found the High Pass clear and the passage of the mountains much easier than it has been at times in the past; it is a balm of the heart for me to find it so.\
\
'We will stay awhile at the Beorninghús. Gandalf has assured me my household will be welcome, and that you will speak to Grimbeorn, the Lord of the Beornings, on our behalf.'","Habla con Grimbeorn","'The mountain passes have not always been as safe as we found them on this journey. Indeed, they have been a source of grief for Elrond and his daughter, for it was in the Misty Mountains that Celebrían, Arwen's mother, was captured by the Orcs.\
\
'That is a sad story and I will not speak more of it now, but I know in my heart that while Arwen is full of joy at the wedding that will come at journey's end, this land holds much sorrow for her. With an abundance of caution I chose to safe-guard the company as they travelled, and I am pleased to report the passage was without incident. After a short rest we will continue on to Lothlórien, but I am confident we should have little to fear before we reach the safety of the Wood.'","'Grimbeorn is displeased with the arrival of Elrond and his household? He is free to tell them they are not welcome, but the Lord of the Beornings surely knows better than to risk the ire of an Elf-lord, let alone several. It is to be hoped he knows not to risk the ire of an Elf-maid planning for her wedding, for that way may lie his truest danger!\
\
'But I will return now to the study of the Black Book of Mordor. I will let you know when I have discovered anything further.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>The Black Book of Mordor continues in a future update!</rgb>","Talk to Arwen at the Beorninghús"},
[2868]={"Talk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb","'Is this some trick? How do you expect me to know the conclusion of your tale, Mótsog? It is an impossibility.'\
\
Durin turns to you, irritation on his face, but before he can voice his dismissal his brow furrows with confusion.\
\
'And yet... there is something strange, ${PLAYER}. As I cast my memory to Sundergrót, I find that I see it not as it was mere weeks ago, but as Mótsog described it during the First Age, when it was the site of Biriz-zahar! How can this be? I... I do know what happened following the Sunder-battle. I was...'\
\
Durin stares at you with amazement in his eyes.\
\
'I was there, ${PLAYER}, as I was in Moria, and at Helegrod, and in Mordor. I am Durin now as I was then, six times before. I will finish your tale, Mótsog. I am the only one still in this world who can.'","'Aye, Durin gave me my life, both mercy and punishment. I have remained in this chamber ever since, casting my dreaming gaze over the mountains, watching from afar the trials of the dwarves. I say it was mercy, for truly I deserved a usurper's death, but so too do I call it punishment, for I was unable to intervene or aid them in their struggles.\
\
'On rare occasions one of those I watched would seem to catch a glimpse of me, but never in my own form. Was this a cruelty of the First Crafter, or some confounding jest? I cannot say. But this I know: only once did he to whom I spoke hear my words.\
\
'It was Durin who heard me, Durin who returned again and again with new visage but the same spirit in his breast. Only Durin heard my words, my friend of old who showed me the mercy I did not deserve. So often had I sought to aid the dwarves in their trials, and so often failed. But when Durin stood before the Anvil of Winterstith I spoke to him of Gundabad and his right to rule the Mountain-home for all dwarves, and he listened. It must mean something. My long penance nears its end, and the prolonged hours of my dream must soon pass away. Soon I will wake, and Mótsog will be no more.'","'Hear then the end of the tale, as I know it to be.\
\
'For I am Durin, Father of Dwarves, first to awaken, and I was there.'","Talk to Durin and hear his remembrance","'Durin knows the rest of the tale. It is not for me to tell.'","Chapter 10.7: The Legacy of Durin","Mótsog stands in a long-forgotten chamber deep beneath Gundabad.","Talk to Mótsog","Mótsog has finished his account, and he has told you that the conclusion is for someone else to tell.","Durin stands in a long-forgotten chamber beneath Gundabad, clearly confused by the words of Mótsog.","Durin looks at you with realization dawning in his eyes."},
[2869]={"Rahâzi was sent to the insect den of Gurakhu, north-west of Iridír, and now her mother Girhâzi wants you to help with her assigned task.","Talk to Surdûsha at Gurakhu","'The words spoken by your companion Belondor are smooth as the stones at the bottom of the Ikorbân River... but that does not mean there is no truth in them.\
\
'I am changed by the months that have passed. My husband and all my sons perished on the fields of the Northern War, slain beneath the banner of the Black Serpent they followed. We were told Ordâkh was invincible; it was not so. When the survivors began to return, all too few, it was made clear to me the cause that had taken most of my family was a lie. I cast down the tools of the field and picked up the tools of war, and under a new name I rallied the people to burn the temple of Iridír. The banner of the Black Serpent no longer flies in Ambarûl. My Dumûri warriors, the Daughters of Iridír, have sworn to keep the peace and hunt the remnants of Ordâkh wherever they hide.\
\
'I have sent my daughter Rahâzi to the insect den of Gurakhu, north-west of Iridír. Go there and assist her with her task while I speak with Belondor concerning how he came to cast the Ordâkhai from his city. I am most interested to hear how it was done, and what brings he and you into Ambarûl.'","Rahâzi has asked you to collect the bristles she was sent to retrieve from the insects at Gurakhu, west of Iridír. In the interest of continued collaboration, you should do what you can to help Girhâzi's daughter.","Collected zizanu bristles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Well? What have you to say?'\
\
You assure the warrior that you and your companions have come to Ambarûl with no intention to cause harm to any of the folk who live here.\
\
'So might say any foe of the Ikorbâni who live alongside the river, but from the look of you I believe the Dumûri need not fear you. My mother will be the judge of that. Present yourself to Girhâzi inside the lodge, but know this: if she finds your motive suspect or your words untrustworthy, you will not leave this village.\
\
'Had I not a task of my own I would stay to see what befalls you, but duty awaits me outside Iridír.'","'Your people and mine have long been enemies. What now is different?'","The distraction writ upon Rahâzi's face is clear to you as you report finishing the task.\
\
'Good enough,' she answers you.\
\
'Surdûsha has brought wondrous tidings to me! Speak to her and hear them!'","A young woman named Rahâzi has directed you to speak with her mother Girhâzi, leader of the village of Iridír in Ambarûl.","Girhâzi watches you carefully as you approach","'I would be honoured to speak to Girhâzi of the relationship between Umbar and the folk who live in Ambarûl.'","Rahâzi is at Gurakhu, north-west of Iridír, waiting for you to return to her with her task complete.","Talk to Girhâzi inside her lodge within Iridír","'While hunting to the north-east of Iridír, I found a scouting party of Ordâkhai setting up a small encampment from which they might threaten the village! They were few in number, but not so few I thought I should attack them on my own.\
\
'With Rahâzi I knew I could face them, so I hurried here to bring her back with me. I trust you are a friend?'","'Surdûsha has brought wondrous tidings to me! Speak to her and hear them!'","Girhâzi is inside her lodge within the village of Iridír, in Ambarûl.","'I was born in Gondor, Girhâzi of Iridír, but I am now a man of Umbar, and that is where my loyalties lie. Are you the same as you were when you were young? I deem not. We are not who we were, and could that be different for any of us? This is an age of great change.\
\
'I would be honoured to speak to you of the relationship between Umbar and the folk who live in Ambarûl, for we are neighbours now, as you say.'","Talk to Rahâzi at the insect den of Gurakhu, north-west of Iridír","Girhâzi is inside her lodge in the village of Iridír, in Ambarûl.","Talk to Rahâzi at Gurakhu","Rahâzi is at Gurakhu in Ambarûl.","Rahâzi runs into the wild, leaving you to speak to her mother Girhâzi.","'I found a scouting party of Ordâkhai setting up a small encampment from which they might threaten the village! They were few in number, but not so few I thought I should attack them on my own. With Rahâzi I knew I could face them, so I hurried here to bring her back with me. I trust you are a friend?'","Collect zizanu bristles for Rahâzi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You still live! Your reasons for coming to Ambarûl must have satisfied my mother. But why have you come to Gurakhu?'\
\
You tell Rahâzi that her mother asked you to help with her task while Girhâzi discusses the relationship between Umbar and Iridír with Belondor.\
\
'Help? I need no help crushing insects! I am one of the Dumûri, the women warriors of Iridír! These zizanu insects were unworthy of my attention to begin, and I only accepted the task out of deference to my mother, and so the craftswomen of Iridír will have the bristles they need for their work.\
\
'Now that you are here, you can do it instead. I will see how you perform and measure your skill. Collect the zizanu bristles as quickly as you can. Perhaps that is why my mother sent you here?'","Belondor is in Girhâzi's lodge within the village of Iridír.","Wait for Rahâzi to depart the village","Talk to Belondor inside Girhâzi's lodge within Iridír","'Now that you are here, you can do this task instead. I will see how you perform and measure your skill. Collect the zizanu bristles as quickly as you can. Perhaps that is why my mother sent you here?'","Find Girhâzi within the lodge inside the village of Iridír","According to Rahâzi, her mother Girhâzi will be interested in speaking with you within her lodge to the south.","'Our choice is clear! The Ordâkhai must be defeated, and driven from Ambarûl!'","Rahâzi's fellow Dumûri warrior, Surdûsha, is at Gurakhu, north-west of Iridír.","'I have sent my daughter Rahâzi to the insect den of Gurakhu, north-west of Iridír. Go there and assist her with her task while I speak with Belondor concerning how he came to cast the Ordâkhai from his city. I am most interested to hear how it was done, and what brings he and you into Ambarûl.'","Chapter 10.8: The Daughters of Iridír","'The eyes of my Dumûri have been upon you ever since you entered Ambarûl. Speak now and relate what brings you to the lands under my protection.'\
\
You introduce yourself and your companions, and when you identify Belondor as a member of the Kindred of the Coins, Girhâzi eyes him appraisingly.\
\
'Word has come to me of your ruling body, Belondor, but I would learn more of the rebellion that pried your city from the grip of Barkhûsh and the Ordâkhai. We are neighbours now, my people and yours, and our interests may be aligned.'\
\
Girhâzi lowers her voice almost to a whisper.\
\
'I say \\qmay,\\q for you say you hail from Umbar, but I take you for a man of Gondor who keeps company with Elves. Your people have long been enemies of mine. What now is different?'","Bring the zizanu bristles to Rahâzi at Gurakhu"},
[2870]={"Talk to Surdûsha outside Omboha","Surdûsha told you that Rahâzi pursued fleeing Ordâkhai warriors to the north.","Pick up the weapon of the slain Ordâkhai","'I heard sounds of fighting without the grove. Was there danger? Has it dispersed?'\
\
You tell the Elf that a warrior from the nearby village defeated a number of Ordâkhai soldiers beyond the ring of trees, and the danger has passed. He contemplates your words and nods slowly.\
\
'So often that is the way for the Avabár-kintai,' he says to you. 'We struggle to maintain our wooded groves in a land that was once fair, but they remain shrinking oases as dearth and danger press in on all sides.\
\
'I am Shanthar, and I count myself among the Kintai, wandering Elves who settled in this fertile country of forests and wetlands, long ago. We are fewer in number now, and we who remain tend our homes as the lands around them fail.'\
\
You ask Shanthar if he lives in this grove by himself, and he smiles sadly.\
\
'The Kintai have no interest in departing the circles of the world, as I have heard other Elves may. When my people reach old age, they become... untethered... in spirit. They begin to fade, and in time they belong to the natural world. Some even now remain in this grove, and if you <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> beneath the scarlet leaves of the Sarláshi trees you might hear them.'","Chapter 10.9: Hunting the Remnants","'We should search this wooded grove to the north and ensure no others of the Ordâkhai hide within.'","The Elf-warden Shanthar stands within the grove of Arwáth.","An Elf-warden stands watch within the grove of Arwáth","On the body of the slain warrior you find a token of the Church of the All-seeing","Shanthar suggested that you <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for the faded Kintai in the grove of Arwáth.","Rahâzi is on the outskirts of the grove of Arwáth.","'See the cuts and scrapes on this weapon? This soldier of Ordâkh has been involved in many battles, perhaps even in Iridír itself! He may have fled from my mother and her warriors, even as he fled from me and from Surdûsha today. But no longer. He landed no blow upon me when he turned to fight; see how dry is the blood upon the blade?\
\
'This sigil is a token of Barkhûsh, the Dark Lord who is no more. It is one more sign that the Ordâkhai have no honour, and without the fell magic of their dread master they have no future either... at least not in Ambarûl.\
\
'We should search the wooded grove to the north and ensure no others of the Ordâkhai hide within.'","Talk to Shanthar at Arwáth","'While Rahâzi and I fought the soldiers here, some of the men broke away from the rest of the group and fled to the north. Rahâzi chased them, but we should hurry after her and ensure she has not fallen victim to a trap set by the cunning Ordâkhai!'","Rahâzi is eager to hunt down and defeat the Ordâkhai who remain in Ambarûl to threaten her people.","'The three of us must go to the Ordâkhai encampment Surdûsha discovered north-east of Iridír and put them all to the sword! This is a task for Dumûri warriors... and for those who claim to be their allies.'","As you approach, you see that Rahâzi defeated the warriors she pursued","You hear the rustling of leaves and feel a light breeze on your skin, but that is all","'When my mother burned the temple at Iridír and drove the Ordâkhai from the village, some of them must have remained hidden in the wild. Now they seek to return and take back Ambarûl, but we will not allow that to happen!\
\
'The three of us must go to the Ordâkhai encampment Surdûsha discovered north-east of Iridír and put them all to the sword! This is a task for Dumûri warriors... and for those who claim to be their allies.'","The weapon bears sign of use in many battles, but the blood on the blade is dry","Find Rahâzi to the north of Omboha","Talk to Rahâzi outside the grove of Arwáth","'I heard sounds of fighting without.'","'Could you feel the presence of my people that dwell here in Arwáth, though their bodies have long since faded?'\
\
You admit to Shanthar that you did not, and he smiles with understanding.\
\
'Even I do not always feel them near, friend, but it is a comfort to know they remain in this Middle-earth. To depart from these lands seems to me, and to others of the Kintai, frightening and unnatural: a terrible and unknowable afterlife. That road is closed to us, and we are glad of it.\
\
'If you would give to the warrior who remains outside Arwáth the thanks of warden Shanthar and the faded Kintai who dwell here, I would be grateful. I am not without my defences, but I have not been required to make use of them for some years.'","Outside the grove of Arwáth, Rahâzi asked you to search her foes for signs of their purpose in Ambarûl.","'I am fine. These men were no match for me!'","Rahâzi believes you should venture within the grove of Arwáth and ensure that no Ordâkhai hide within.","Defeated Ordâkhai warriors throughout Ambarûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ordâkhai remnants gather at a war-camp to the north-east of Iridír, in Ambarûl.","'I am fine. These men were no match for me!\
\
'We should search their bodies and take their weapons. They may have items among their belongings that help us prevent further attacks upon my people. A map to other of their encampments would be the most welcome of all!'","Find the camp of the Ordâkhai to the north-east of Iridír","'If you would give to the warrior who remains outside Arwáth the thanks of warden Shanthar and the faded Kintai who dwell here, I would be grateful. I am not without my defences, but I have not been required to make use of them for some years.'","Rahâzi is interested to examine the items you collected from the body of her foe.","<rgb=#00FF00>Listen</rgb> for the faded Kintai in the grove of Arwáth","'We should search their bodies and take their weapons. They may have items among their belongings that help us prevent further attacks upon my people. A map to other of their encampments would be the most welcome of all!'","Surdûsha keeps a watchful eye on Omboha.","Rahâzi pursued the Ordâkhai to the outskirts of the grove of Arwáth.","'The Kintai have no interest in departing the circles of the world, as I have heard other Elves may. When my people reach old age, they become... untethered... in spirit. They begin to fade, and in time they belong to the natural world. Some even now remain in this grove, and if you <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> beneath the scarlet leaves of the Sarláshi trees you might hear them.'","'The grove is inhabited by an Elf-warden? How interesting. It is quite rare to encounter one of the Kintai, for they concern themselves mainly with their groves and do not venture from them without great need. If the Ordâkhai located the Elf within Arwáth, they would have slain him easily. He is fortunate we came here.'\
\
Rahâzi surveys the grove and then turns to face in the direction of Iridír.\
\
'You have proven yourself a help to me, stranger. Perhaps it is time you tell me your name.'","Venture within the grove of Arwáth to the north","Search the body of the slain Ordâkhai warrior outside Arwáth","Stand in the grove of Arwáth beside one of the trees with red leaves","Defeat Ordâkhai warriors throughout Ambarûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ordâkhai remnants gather at Omboha, north-east of Iridír","Present the items you found to Rahâzi outside the grove of Arwáth"},
[2871]={"'Deserters from the raids in the north have camps here in Fordirith. Deprive them of the blood-marks with which they seek to reward the deaths of my people! Recover too the weapons of my fallen kinsmen. It would be an insult for the weapons of the Uch-lûth to be used against them.'","'Wadu at least seems pleased with you, ${PLAYER}. If his family ruled the Uch-lûth, perhaps our road south would be easier. Sadly, it appears that his father Suvulch, though respected by the brenin of the Uch-lûth, is not one of his brehur.\
\
'Still, respect earned is not respect wasted. Perhaps Wadu's respect for you will help us as we must deal more closely with the Uch-lûth.'","Wadu is at Echad Dagoras, the camp of the Grey Company in Fordirith, Enedwaith.\
\
You have collected blood-marks and weapons from fallen Uch-lûth and should bring them to Wadu as he requested.","Recovered weapons from fallen Uch-lûth clansmen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wadu has expressed his displeasure at the slaying of his kin by other Dunlending clans and wants you to fight on his behalf.","'It brings me no joy to see these marks, nor to receive these weapons, for they are reminders of the Uch-lûth that have fallen and of the greed of these people that were once my kin. But no more! These other lûth are no longer of my stock. They are cowards, slaves to gold, and are no longer Men. They are like Orcs now, and the brave Uch-lûth will treat them like Orcs.\
\
'You will continue to do so? Good. You are not one of us, but you will be a friend to my family. Perhaps we will compare the tallies of the slain when all of Dunland is unified again and under the strong rule of the Uch-lûth! I look forward to that time.\
\
'Tell your duvodiad friends what you have done for Wadu. I am not certain about them, but about you I have made up my mind. Your strength of will is like to mine, and you are made of similar stuff, strong as the stones of Dunland.'","'You have not yet done what you said you would do for Wadu.'","Collected blood-marks from Dunlendings in Fordirith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Uch-lûth will tolerate your presence, but other Dunlending lûth will be openly hostile. They have been given gold and have forgotten their true allegiances. Many of them travelled north into the land of the holly, but they have returned. They are cowards on their own, and they are cowards on behalf of their new master!\
\
'But these lûth that fight for gold have no loyalty to their former brothers. They fight even the Uch-lûth! For every one of my people they slay, they put a mark in blood on a chip of wood. They believe their new master will pay them for every one of their kinsmen they slay. It is an abomination.\
\
'They have already killed some of my people. Travel to the deserters' camps north of here and deprive them of the blood-marks they have already collected. Recover, too, the weapons of my fallen brothers. I do not want them taken by their foes.'","Talk to Lothrandir at Echad Dagoras","Collect blood-marks from Dunlendings in Fordirith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring blood-marks and Dunlending weapons to Wadu at Echad Dagoras","Chapter 10: Blood-marks","Lothrandir is at Echad Dagoras, in Fordirith, northern Enedwaith.\
\
You have pleased Wadu with your heroics on his behalf among the Dunlending deserters and should tell Lothrandir of your successes.","'Tell your duvodiad friends what you have done for Wadu. They were wise to bring you, for your will is strong, like one of the Uch-lûth! They speak in riddles and seem always on the verge of despair. I do not wonder that they are not welcome in Dunland.'","Deserters can be found north of Echad Dagoras, in Fordirith.\
\
Wadu has asked you to recover blood-marks from the Dunlending deserters in Fordirith and to recover the weapons of his fallen kinsmen.","Recover weapons from fallen Uch-lûth clansmen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2874]={"Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin.\
\
Rósar, el Maestro de la Forja, ha identificado tu arma, y ahora deberías mostrársela a Wafi.","'Has recorrido un largo camino para llegar hasta aquí, ${PLAYER}. ¿Qué asunto podría traer a alguien tan valiente como tú desde Acebeda hasta la Mansión de Thorin?'\
\
Wafi mira el arma y silba de asombro.\
\
'¡Sin duda, esta es una reliquia de los Días Antiguos! Me temo que no puedo identificar para ti el linaje y las fortalezas de esta arma; es demasiado antigua para mi saber, por mucho que haya estudiado estas materias.\
\
'Sin embargo, mi pariente Rósar, el Maestro de la Forja, sin duda tendrá más que decir que yo, pues su conocimiento es vasto y supera al mío. Muéstrale el arma y te dará una valoración de su fuerza y su potencial.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Los objetos legendarios deben ser identificados por un Maestro de la Forja antes de poder usarse. Este proceso revela ciertas fortalezas que el arma puede tener.</rgb>","'Las armas de esta factura pueden tener una historia larga y legendaria, ${PLAYER}. Su historia crece con cada enemigo malvado que derriba: cuantos más siervos del mal abata esta arma, más letal se vuelve.\
\
'Solo unas pocas personas con gran pericia pueden leer la historia de un arma a partir de su artesanía. Te envío con alguien que puede ayudarte más: el enano Wafi, en la Mansión de Thorin, en la lejana tierra de Ered Luin.\
\
'Busca a Wafi junto a los grandes fuegos de la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin. Puede ayudarte a encontrar a alguien con habilidad para interpretar el linaje y el poder de un arma como esta.'","Habla con Wafi","Rósar, el Maestro de la Forja, está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin. Tiene la habilidad necesaria para identificar el arma misteriosa que has adquirido.\
\
Wafi te ha indicado que Rósar, el Maestro de la Forja, identifique tu arma para que puedas comprender su fuerza y su potencial.","Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin.\
\
Wafi te ha pedido que encajes una de las reliquias en tu arma para personalizar aún más sus capacidades.","El Maestro de la Forja ha identificado el arma, revelando sus fortalezas ocultas.","Encaja una reliquia de montura en tu arma","'Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin. Está lejos de aquí, pero hay muy poca gente capaz de reconocer las fortalezas de un arma por su forja, y Wafi es una de ellas.'","Capítulo 10: Linaje olvidado","Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin.\
\
Wafi te ha pedido que encajes en tu arma una de las reliquias que tienes para personalizar aún más sus capacidades, y ahora está esperando para hablar contigo.","Has encajado una reliquia de montura en tu arma","'¡Increíble, ${PLAYER}! Esta arma es realmente poderosa, y has tenido la fortuna de hacerte con algo así. Sin embargo, no es lo bastante fuerte para enfrentarse a la criatura de la que hablas. ¡Mil maldiciones sobre su pellejo inmundo por mantener a los enanos lejos de Moria!\
\
'Veo que tienes varias reliquias. Deberías aplicar una a tu arma para personalizar aún más sus capacidades. Cuando lo hayas hecho, vuelve a hablar conmigo.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Hay cuatro tipos distintos de reliquias que puedes encajar desde el panel de objetos legendarios: monturas, gemas, runas y elaboradas. Un arma puede tener una de cada tipo a la vez.</rgb>","'Buena elección, ${PLAYER}. Obtendrás más reliquias en tus aventuras, y puedes personalizar tu arma con la reliquia adecuada para cada situación.\
\
'Esta arma aún no es lo bastante fuerte para derrotar al Guardián del Agua, camarada ${CLASS}, pero podría llegar a serlo. Te diré cómo lograrlo.'","Equipa tu nueva arma","Lleva el arma al Maestro de la Forja para que la identifique","'Deberías encajar una de las reliquias que tienes en tu arma, ${PLAYER}. Encajar reliquias te permite personalizar aún más las capacidades y fortalezas de tu arma.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Hay cuatro tipos distintos de reliquias que puedes encajar desde el panel de objetos legendarios: monturas, gemas, runas y elaboradas. Un arma puede tener una de cada tipo a la vez.</rgb>","'Debes equiparte con tu nueva arma si quieres ver cómo aumenta su valor.'","'Mi pariente Rósar, el Maestro de la Forja, puede identificar armas de este tipo que adquieras durante tus viajes, revelando sus fortalezas secretas y su potencial de crecimiento.'","Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin.\
\
Hundi te ha dicho que le muestres tu nueva arma a Wafi en la Mansión de Thorin. Wafi podrá ayudarte a determinar las características intrínsecas del arma.","Ahora que tu arma ha sido identificada, debes equiparla si quieres aumentar su valor.","Has recibido un arma de los Días Antiguos, descubierta por los enanos en un escondrijo oculto, y ahora debes desentrañar sus secretos."},
[2875]={"Dithalion está junto a las forjas de Rivendel.\
\
Hundi te pidió que le muestres tu nueva arma a Dithalion, un elfo de Rivendel que podrá ayudarte a sacar partido de tu arma.","Has recibido un arma de los Días Antiguos que los enanos descubrieron en un escondrijo oculto, y ahora debes desentrañar sus secretos.","'Veo que te han dado algunas tracerías. Deberías aplicar una a tu arma para personalizar aún más sus capacidades. Cuando lo hayas hecho, vuelve a hablar conmigo.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>- Hay una gran variedad de tracerías que pueden añadirse a tu objeto legendario.\
\
- Entre ellas están las heráldicas, las Palabras de poder, las Palabras de maestría y las Palabras de artesanía.\
\
- Se encajan en tus objetos de forma muy similar a las Esencias.</rgb>","Habla con Dithalion junto a las forjas de Rivendel","Dithalion está en las Forjas de Rivendel.","Dithalion está en las Forjas de Rivendel.\
\
Has inscrito una tracería en tu arma y ahora deberías hablar con Dithalion.","'Buena elección, ${PLAYER}. Inscribir tracerías en tu arma mejorará tus habilidades y a menudo ayudará a cambiar el curso de la batalla.\
\
'Esta arma aún no es lo bastante fuerte para derrotar al Guardián del Agua, camarada ${CLASS}, pero podría llegar a serlo. Te diré cómo puede llegar ese momento.'","'Las armas de esta factura pueden tener una historia larga y legendaria, ${PLAYER}. Su historia crece con cada enemigo malvado que derriba: cuantos más siervos del mal abata esta arma, más letal se vuelve.\
\
'Solo unas pocas personas con gran pericia pueden leer la historia de un arma a partir de su artesanía. Te remito a alguien que puede ayudarte más: el elfo Dithalion, junto a las forjas de Rivendel. Es sabio y erudito en muchos asuntos, incluido el estudio de las armas antiguas.\
\
'Si Dithalion no puede ayudarte, sin duda conocerá a alguien que pueda discernir el linaje y los poderes de un arma de esta hechura.'","'Dithalion estará junto a las forjas de Rivendel, ${PLAYER}. Está lejos, pero puede que logre extraer de tu nueva arma algún conocimiento que nos sea útil.'","'Has recorrido un largo camino para llegar hasta aquí, ${PLAYER}. ¿Qué asunto podría traer a alguien tan valiente como tú aquí, a las Forjas de Rivendel?'\
\
Dithalion mira el arma y se queda inmóvil, con los ojos abiertos por el asombro.\
\
'¡Esta es una reliquia de los Días Antiguos, camarada! Un arma así tiene un potencial sin igual para crecer en poder, y su leyenda crece junto con la tuya.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>- Los objetos legendarios pueden mejorarse de varias formas mientras recorres la Tierra Media:\
\
- Sus estadísticas básicas aumentarán junto con las tuyas a medida que subes de nivel.\
\
- Se les puede encajar una amplia variedad de tracerías, y esas tracerías pueden mejorarse aún más con runas.\
\
- En tus aventuras encontrarás tracerías y runas por todo el mundo. También puedes obtenerlas gastando Escritura Antigua en el Word-hoard de Gobetham, situado en la Última Morada.</rgb>","Capítulo 10: Linaje olvidado"},
[2876]={"Capítulo 10: El Intercambio","Laeglang, Lamwen y Súlthel están en algún lugar de Gathbúrz, al este de Ost Galadh y fuera de los muros de Dol Guldur.\
\
Gruingalas te ha pedido que llames de vuelta a los exploradores que vigilan la fortaleza de Dol Guldur en Gathbúrz.","Habla con Súlthel en Gathbúrz","Habla con Gruingalas en Ost Galadh","Gruingalas está fuera de la entrada de Gadorgar, en Ost Galadh.\
\
Has llamado de vuelta a los exploradores de Gathbúrz y deberías regresar con Gruingalas con las noticias que reunieron en el territorio salvaje.","'Me has encontrado en mi camino de regreso desde las fronteras del sur entre los Pasajes de Ceniza. La tierra allí está devastada y muerta, y el hedor del mal está en todas partes.\
\
'Parece que Gorothúl ha entrenado a Hombres malvados en las artes que aprendió de su propio maestro; están buscando atar espíritus malignos a su servicio en los confines de los Pasajes de Ceniza.\
\
'Regresaré a Ost Galadh con mi informe sobre ese lugar.'","'Achardor me dio un mensaje para ti, . Tu amigo, el enano Bróin... no se puede encontrar. Ha estado desaparecido desde que te fuiste a llamar a los exploradores. Achardor no quiere esperarlo; dice que quiere deshacerse de Mazog de inmediato y completar la misión.\
\
'Habla conmigo cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}, y te llevaré a la Guardia Oculta para que puedas discutir el asunto con ellos.'","Habla con Lamwen en Gathbúrz","'Ibas a regresar con Gruingalas en Ost Galadh y contarle lo que he visto en los Pasajes de Ceniza, ¿no es así? Estaré allí tan pronto como pueda, pero seguramente llegarás antes que yo.\
\
'Por favor, date prisa, ${PLAYER}. Podría ser importante.'","'Dile a Gruingalas que estaré allí pronto. Él está en Ost Galadh, ¿no es así?'","'Informa a Gruingalas con las noticias que te he dado. Volveré pronto y le daré más detalles sobre la presencia de los Orcos en Gathbúrz.\
\
'Está en Ost Galadh, ¿no es así?'","Habla con Gruingalas y reúne con la Guardia Oculta","'¿No hablarás con Achardor? Sé que Bróin querrá formar parte de esta etapa final de la misión, y Achardor no debe dejar que su ira lo ciegue ante los peligros de la prisa.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no se puede completar con una comunidad.</rgb>","Gruingalas está en Ost Galadh, esperando para hablar contigo.\
\
La misión de la Guardia Oculta está llegando a su fin: ha llegado el momento de intercambiar a Mazog por los prisioneros enanos.","'La Guardia Oculta ha fracasado, ${PLAYER}. Achardor ha sido asesinado, Mazog ha sido capturado y Bori sigue en cautiverio.\
\
'Sigileth está de luto con Issuriel dentro de Gadorgar. Ha pedido no ser molestada.'","Habla con Laeglang en Gathbúrz","'Lamwen, Súlthel y Laeglang están en algún lugar de Gathbúrz, al este de aquí y fuera de los largos muros de Dol Guldur. Averigua lo que han descubierto durante su tiempo explorando las tierras salvajes entre aquí y Dol Guldur y diles que regresen aquí para prepararse para el intercambio de Mazog.\
\
'Debemos saber todo lo que hay que saber sobre los peligros en Gathbúrz antes de que la Guardia Oculta haga su movimiento.'","La misión de la Guardia Oculta continúa: es hora de llamar de vuelta a los exploradores de la Hueste Dorada y llevar a Mazog a las puertas de Dol Guldur a cambio de los prisioneros.","Gruingalas está fuera de la entrada de Gadorgar, en Ost Galadh.\
\
El intercambio no salió según lo planeado, y la misión de la Guardia Oculta ha terminado en fracaso: Achardor está muerto, Mazog ha sido capturado y Bori sigue en cautiverio","'Según mi exploración, parece probable que Gathbúrz servirá como área de preparación para los ejércitos de Dol Guldur cuando se muevan para atacar Lothlórien. Hay varios campamentos aquí, pero afortunadamente los Orcos aún no se están reuniendo en gran número.\
\
'Regresaré a Ost Galadh y compartiré lo que he aprendido.'","'No ha habido mucha actividad más allá de los muros de Dol Guldur, ${PLAYER}. Para ahora seguramente ya están al tanto de la existencia de la Hueste Dorada; me pregunto si sospechan alguna de sus verdaderas intenciones. Es una gran ofensiva, es cierto; pero ¿sospechan que no buscamos la victoria? ¿Que estamos atrayendo su atención hacia un punto que nosotros elegimos, en lugar del que ellos elijan?\
\
'Volveré a Ost Galadh de inmediato. Esperemos que no hayamos alarmado demasiado al Enemigo, y los tomaremos por sorpresa en todos los aspectos.'","'Los Malledhrim enviaron a varios exploradores para espiar el terreno frente a la fortaleza de Dol Guldur; querremos saber lo que han aprendido y hacer que regresen aquí antes de llevar a Mazog el resto del camino hasta las puertas de la fortaleza.\
\
'Busca a los exploradores Lamwen, Súlthel y Laeglang en las tierras salvajes de Gathbúrz, al este de aquí y antes de los muros de Dol Guldur. Diles que regresen y que se emprenderá la última etapa de la misión de la Guardia Oculta.\
\
'Con la información de estos exploradores, estaremos mejor preparados para efectuar el intercambio de Mazog por los enanos prisioneros.'"},
[2877]={"'That may help him, if he is not already beyond saving. How did he come to be so far from the road? What happened to him after he left the tomb of Nirgambâr, where we lost his trail? He would not have purposefully left his satchel in that tomb if he planned to spend days alone in the heat, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Silirtas, would your people give their aid to a man this near to death?'","This man is not dead! His breathing is shallow, but he lives... for now","Chapter 11.10: A Dead Man In The Desert","Some of the water passes parched lips, but more of it spills onto the sand","Tharashil is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.","Talk to Silirtas by the dying man","'What is... who are...'\
\
Balakhâd's voice is dry and raspy. He stares wildly around himself and you are put in mind of an animal caught in a trap. He sees the Elves gathered nearby and his cracked lip curls up in a sneer.\
\
'You are... going to kill me...?'\
\
You tell him that the Elves of the Oasis have agreed to try and heal his various hurts, and may have already saved his life. You ask him how he came to be by himself in the desert, and say too that you know the water-bearer Sadûkh helped him escape from the Kindred of the Coins. Despite the sun damage and his scorched skin, the expression of confusion on his face is readily apparent.\
\
'How do you know all this?' he asks.","'It is perhaps a meaningless choice, for Silirtas has already gone to tell Tharashil what we have found. To return now without him would be... difficult to explain. Let us go to the Oasis at Shonith and learn if the healing arts of the Kintai will resolve this philosophical difficulty for us, or raise further such questions.'","Sigileth is in southern Khûd Zagin.","'Give him some of that water... but slowly, or you might harm more than heal.'","'I think this man might have been Balakhâd. I think this was the son of Balakhôr, and he was the last of the Heirs of Castamir.'","Tharashil nods as you approach, but her expression is guarded","Silirtas hurries away.","Sigileth hands you her water bladder","Talk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith","Balakhâd eyes you warily","Find Balakhâd behind the pavilions north of the water in Shonith","'He lives still?\
\
'He will not live for long without water. He may already have gone too long without it. Here, give him some of this... but slowly, or you might harm more than heal.'","You have done what you can for the dying man, and should give Sigileth's water bladder back to her.","Sigileth believes the dying man can be saved, but if he is to recover at Shonith you will need Tharashil's permission.","Talk to Sigileth in southern Khûd Zagin","Sigileth and Silirtas have found something in the dry reaches of Khûd Zagin.","Return her water bladder to Sigileth","'No, I do not think this dead man is Sadûkh after all.\
\
'I think this man might have been Balakhâd, ${PLAYER}. I think this was the son of Balakhôr, and he was the last of the Heirs of Castamir.'","Balakhâd is behind the pavilions north of the water in Shonith.","Balakhâd is behind the pavilions to the north of the water in Shonith.","Examine the dead man by Sigileth and Silirtis in Khûd Zagin","Silirtas stands in southern Khûd Zagin by the dying man.","Sigileth stands by the dying man in southern Khûd Zagin.","Talk to Balakhâd in Shonith","Wait for Silirtas to depart","'It is not customary for the Kintai to welcome Men such as he to our groves. He is here at your request, and Sigileth's. The two of you must be responsible for him.\
\
'You will find him behind the pavilions to the north of the water here in Shonith.'","'I have a question for you, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'As the son of Balakhôr and the last of the Heirs of Castamir, Balakhâd is undeniably an enemy of not only the Kingdom of Gondor but of my people specifically; the hatred of the Heirsworn for Elves is well-known. It is in our power to help him. If our paths had not crossed his, he likely would have died without our knowledge. And yet here we stand. What is the right course?'\
\
You give Sigileth your opinion, and she nods.\
\
'It is a difficult question, but this is my answer: if the healing arts of the Kintai are sufficient to coax him back to health, he may tell us what Azagath and Nakási are planning, or where they have gone. Whatever he knows may be of crucial importance to us.\
\
'It is perhaps a meaningless choice, ${PLAYER}, for Silirtas has already gone to tell Tharashil what we have found. To return now without him would be... difficult to explain. Let us go to the Oasis at Shonith and learn if the healing arts of the Kintai will resolve this philosophical difficulty for us, or raise further such questions.'","Return to Tharashil in south-western Shonith","Offer water to the dying man in southern Khûd Zagin","'Silirtas, would your people give their aid to a man this near to death?'","Sigileth has asked you to examine the dead man to discover what spelled his end.","'The Kintai do not willingly refuse their aid, when they have the ability to give it.\
\
'I will return with haste to Shonith and tell Tharashil there is need for her healing arts.'","The man is barely alive, but a gift of water may help bring him back from death's brink.","'Silirtas has told me of your dead man, and a place has been made for him. The healers who dwell here at Shonith will see what can be done for his injuries, but he spent too long exposed to the harsh environment of the desert to recover quickly, or completely. A single day and night without cover would be too many, and he suffered several.\
\
'It is not customary for the Kintai to welcome Men such as he to our groves. He is here at your request, and Sigileth's. The two of you must be responsible for him.\
\
'You will find him behind the pavilions to the north of the water here in Shonith.'"},
[2879]={"'I will go with you in friendship to Tol Send, but I urge you and Gandalf to treat carefully with the shade, and to guard against sweet-seeming words. He is not what he once was, and I fear Gandalf may let the pursuit of knowledge blind him to that fact.'","Gandalf, Elrond, and Glorfindel have come to Tol Send, where they await an audience with the shade of Isildur.","'I expected these words, ${PLAYER}, for when I learned the shade of Isildur remained bound to this place, I knew it would not be long before Gandalf desired to press him for knowledge of the Disaster that befell him after the war.'\
\
You tell Elrond that the Wizard also thinks Isildur might know something about Magoldir the Elf, whose name appears frequently in the Black Book.\
\
'Magoldir? I too fought at the Siege of Barad-dûr, but I do not remember an Elf by that name. He cannot have been high in the counsels of Gil-galad, ${PLAYER}, or I would surely remember him. No, that is unfair. Many were the heroes who fought alongside the Last Alliance, of every kind: Elves, Men, Durin's folk, and even some of the hól-budlan rose up to oppose the threat of Sauron. I do not claim to know each of these heroes personally; Magoldir may have accomplished some great feat without attribution. Even if he did not, to perform one's duty without the expectation of glory is still worthy of praise and remembrance.\
\
'The War of the Last Alliance and the Siege of Barad-dûr that concluded it ended in victory, ${PLAYER}, but there was sorrow too. The cost was high. Even if his memory returns, the shade of Isildur may not wish to speak of it to us. Let Gandalf gird himself against disappointment if that be so.\
\
'You should ask Glorfindel if he wishes to accompany us to Tol Send. He also fought at the Siege of Barad-dûr, and will no doubt be interested in anything the shade of Isildur might say to us.'","'I propose we return to Tol Send to speak with Isildur, but not alone. No, let us bring some others who also fought at the Siege, and who might help Isildur recover his memories. I speak of two Elf-lords who have come to the Beorninghús at this most fortuitous time: Elrond and Glorfindel, both of Rivendell. Bring them word of my intent and let us all meet on the Isle of Flowers in the Gladden Fields, where we will speak with the shade.'","A chill breeze disturbs the petals on the Isle of the Flowers","'We find ourselves in a curious position, ${PLAYER}. The shade of Isildur was bound to the land where he fell, much as was the shade of Arvedui, in Forochel. But here, Isildur's shade was kept hidden from searching eyes by the arts of Gultháva, the Maiden of the Gladden. Her sorceries made him forget, but as they fall away I believe his memories will return. He could tell us much of what befell him during the opening years of the Third Age, when he perished in the Gladden Fields and the Ring was lost. I and others of the Wise have pieced together some of the story, but here we have an occasion to learn the true account, and I would not miss it!\
\
'But this is not merely an academic interest, ${PLAYER}, as important as that may be. No, the shade of Isildur may shed some light on another matter that concerns us most directly. I trust you have not forgotten the Black Book of Mordor and the dread Gúrzyul who seeks it? I have not yet deciphered all of its pages, but my study did reveal frequent appearances of the name \\qMagoldir\\q within its covers. Now, the records show an Elf named Magoldir served in the company of High King Gil-galad during the Siege of Barad-dûr at the close of the Second Age. Can this be the same Magoldir? I think it may be, and the shade of Isildur could help us learn more of him.\
\
'I propose we return to Tol Send to speak with Isildur, but not alone. No, let us bring some others who also fought at the Siege, and who might help Isildur recover his memories. I speak of two Elf-lords who have come to the Beorninghús at this most fortuitous time: Elrond and Glorfindel, both of Rivendell. Bring them word of my intent and let us all meet on the Isle of Flowers in the Gladden Fields, where we will speak with the shade.'","'Magoldir? The name is familiar, but not for any particular deed or duty. He was a warrior in Gil-galad's train, I believe, but one of many. I think I set him to scouting the reaches of Mordor on a number of occasions, but I do not know much else of him. Gandalf thinks the shade of Isildur may know more? Perhaps, ${PLAYER}, perhaps, but something gives me pause.\
\
'It is Gandalf's desire for knowledge that compels him to pursue this course. He wishes to oppose the will of Karazgar, and he believes that uncovering the secrets of the Black Book of Mordor will prove crucial to that aim... but I do not know that I agree. Sometimes knowledge is buried for a reason, and bringing it out into the light of day only serves to reopen wounds once-healed, to renew grief once-accepted.\
\
'Three thousand years have passed since the War of the Last Alliance and the Siege of Barad-dûr, but for my people it seems still near. I remember the grief of those years, and the hurts we suffered. What can be gained by dwelling upon that sad tale? Sauron was defeated, but at great cost, and not forever.\
\
'I fear what the shade might say, ${PLAYER}. He was once the son of Elendil, High King of the Númenóreans, but that was long ago; he has spent the centuries since then in darkness. It must have left its mark upon him. I will go with you in friendship to Tol Send, but I urge you and Gandalf to treat carefully with the shade, and to guard against sweet-seeming words. He is not what he once was, and I fear Gandalf may let the pursuit of knowledge blind him to that fact.'","Talk to the shade of Isildur on Tol Send","The shade of Isildur is on Tol Send, in the Gladden Fields.","Talk to Elrond outside the Beorninghús","Gandalf, Elrond, and Glorfindel wish to meet you on Tol Send, the Isle of the Flowers in the Gladden Fields.","'You should ask Glorfindel if he wishes to accompany us to Tol Send. He also fought at the Siege of Barad-dûr, and will no doubt be interested in anything the shade of Isildur might say to us.'","Meet up with Gandalf, Elrond, and Glorfindel on Tol Send in the Gladden Fields","Talk to Glorfindel outside the Beorninghús","'We are here, and must now learn what we can from this shade. Let courtesy guide your words, ${PLAYER}, for such windows on the past are rare and must be carefully opened, lest they close for good!'","Chapter 11.1: A Window On the Past","Glorfindel is outside the Beorninghús.\
\
Gandalf and Elrond wish for you to ask Glorfindel to go with you to Tol Send, there to speak with the shade of Isildur about several matters of import.","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send","'Greetings to you and your companions, ${PLAYER}. The bonds of sleep in which I was held have loosened, and many of them have already fallen away. My memory has begun to return to me, but slowly; there are still gaps in my recollection.\
\
'But know this: if you aid me, I will do what I can to help you in return. I ask for only one thing. I ask for vengeance. Nay, not truly, for the target of my vengeance must be long-vanished. I ask for peace, for a settled mind.\
\
'I cannot yet remember the ambush that brought me low and ended the lives of my sons, but I know it was not the work of Orcs alone. I was betrayed, though I cannot see the face of my betrayer. I ask that you help me learn the identity of this traitor. The passage of time has brought him beyond my reach, but I will not rest until I know the reason for his treachery. In that I will take some comfort, and find rest. What say you, friend?'\
\
You tell the shade you will do what you can to help him.\
\
'Then my memory is yours, ${PLAYER}, and may the empty spaces in my recollection heal and provide some knowledge that will be of use to you.'","The shade of Isildur may be able to tell you much about events long shrouded in mystery, but only if he can cast off the remaining vestiges of the Maiden's enchanted slumber.","'Now we must learn what we can from this shade. Let courtesy guide your words, ${PLAYER}, for such windows on the past are rare and must be carefully opened, lest they close for good!'","Elrond is outside the Beorninghús.\
\
Gandalf asked you to bring Elrond word of his intent to speak with the shade of Isildur, and his desire that Elrond and Glorfindel accompany the two of you to Tol Send."},
[2880]={"Belondor stands beside the road that runs from Ambarûl into Khûd Zagin.","The time has come for your travelling party to take the road south into Khûd Zagin.","Defeated jackals or servals in Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The food and water Girhâzi has provided for your travelling party can be found at the entrance of the village.","Belondor also has something to say to you.","'While we walked, Rahâzi spoke to me of the creatures we can expect to encounter in this land: birds on the wing, jackals or servals among the sands, and snakes or lizards baking among the rocks. I would like to test some of the arrows I was gifted by the people of Iridír. Shall we hunt some of these creatures and learn the lay of the land?'","'Girhâzi has supplied us with food and water with which we can restock for the journey ahead, ${PLAYER}. Make sure you have enough of each. In the days of my shipboard service to Gondor, few things were as necessary as stocking the larder of your ship with water and food. After all, you might not set foot upon land for days or weeks!\
\
'We travel afoot now and not by ship, but what the Ambarûli say of the land to the south reminds me of my past voyages. There may be little opportunity in the days ahead to restock our supplies, so ensure you have what you will need from Girhâzi's provisions.'","Chapter 11.1: Girhâzi's Price","Talk to Belondor by the road that runs from Ambarûl into Khûd Zagin","'We travel afoot now and not by ship, but what the Ambarûli say of the land to the south reminds me of my past voyages. There may be little opportunity in the days ahead to restock our supplies, so ensure you have what you will need from Girhâzi's provisions.'","Wait for the new arrival","Talk to Khôltekh at the village entrance of Iridír","'My mother insists, and I agree, that I must be allowed to combat the Ordâkhai as we encounter them on this journey. I must be permitted to diminish their ability to threaten Ambarûl if such opportunities present themselves.'","Either Rothog or Húrshauk rumbles appreciatively. It is difficult to say which it was","Girhâzi has given you assistance and supplies to help you on the road into and through Khûd Zagin... but not without a price.","Defeated lizards or snakes in Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You supply yourself with the food Girhâzi provided, and suggest your companions do the same","Rahâzi has arrived at the entrance of her village.","Defeat jackals or servals in Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Corudan stands beside the road leading south into Khûd Zagin.","'My mother has commanded that I join your travelling company, ${PLAYER}. I will serve as your guide within the lands through which you travel, and my knowledge of the Shagâni people will be of help to you. In this way my mother also hopes to secure the bonds of friendship between the Ambarûli and the people of Umbar, unless any of the Kindred here object?'\
\
Belondor, Rothog, and Khôltekh remain silent, but the dwarf stares at you meaningfully.\
\
'There is one thing more,' Rahâzi continues. 'My mother insists, and I agree, that I must be allowed to combat the Ordâkhai as we encounter them on this journey. I must be permitted to diminish their ability to threaten Ambarûl if such opportunities present themselves.'","'At last you two return! The others told me to wait here for you.\
\
'Something happened while you were away.'","Rahâzi arrives on the run","Take the road south into Khûd Zagin from Ambarûl","Rothog has something to say.","'Girhâzi has done much for us, and to provide her own daughter as a guide on the road is more than I might have expected. I hope her requirement that she be permitted to fight the Ordâkhai will not prove an inconvenience.\
\
'But we should set out, for the road ahead will be a long one. We will worry about the price Girhâzi has called for us to pay another time.\
\
'Let us depart, and travel to the southern reaches of Ambarûl, where the road runs into Khûd Zagin. Once there, we will plan our further course.'","Talk to Corudan along the road into Khûd Zagin","'Let us depart, and travel to the southern reaches of Ambarûl, where the road runs into Khûd Zagin. Once there, we will plan our further course.'","Defeat hunting birds in Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah. The cost reveals itself.'","Corudan calls a halt to your southward travel","'I approve of this warrior! What is the name of her order? The Dumûri?\
\
'I too desire to combat the Ordâkhai whenever such becomes possible, and Húrshauk feels the same. We welcome this warrior woman to our band.'","Defeated hunting birds in Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Rahâzi at the village entrance of Iridír","'Let us stop here for now.'","You supply yourself with the water Girhâzi provided, and suggest your companions do the same","'I too desire to combat the Ordâkhai whenever such becomes possible, and Húrshauk feels the same. We welcome this warrior woman to our band.'","'Let us stop here for now. I suggest that the two of us move ahead into Khûd Zagin and scout the terrain that awaits us. While we walked, Rahâzi spoke to me of the creatures we can expect to encounter in this land: birds on the wing, jackals and servals among the sands, and lizards or snakes baking among the rocks.\
\
'I would like to test some of the arrows I was gifted by the people of Iridír. Shall we hunt some of these creatures and learn the lay of the land?'","Defeat lizards or snakes in Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Khôltekh is at the village entrance of Iridír.","Restock your supplies using Girhâzi's provided water","Restock your supplies using Girhâzi's provided foodstuffs","Someone approaches at a run.","'What does the leader of these folk ask from us, ${PLAYER}? No one provides something of value without gaining something in return, and Belondor said this Girhâzi mentioned a price of some kind to him. Not only that, but some among our company have accepted gifts from the Ambarûli! The Elf Corudan admired some new arrows he was gifted, and one of the craftswomen here mended the old Gondorian's boots with clean stitching and fresh patches.\
\
'What is Girhâzi's price for these supplies and these gifts from her people? More importantly, now that they have been accepted, how will we refuse the cost she asks?'","Talk to Belondor at the village entrance of Iridír","Talk to Rothog at the village entrance of Iridír","Corudan has suggested that you defeat the birds, jackals or servals, and lizards or snakes that threaten your southward journey into Khûd Zagin."},
[2881]={"Wait for Durin to come to a decision","Talk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb","Mótsog nods solemnly at Durin.\
\
'I swear to fight for you, my friend of old, my king, for as long as I am able. I will deliver to you control of the kingdom I once stole, and if the last rays of the sun vanish behind the mountain before I seize your victory, I will perish with sorrow in my heart, and none before or since will know such grief as I know in my failure.'","Mótsog stands silently, and says nothing more.","Mótsog addresses you once again.\
\
'I deem you are his close advisor. Advise him then of this: I will walk in the world for only one more day before my long life is spent. When the sun sets on this day, my breath will be stilled and I will disappear from this place, never to return. In that time I have but one desire. I wish to do whatever my friend commands, for the vigil of so many years has given me this knowledge: Durin is the rightful king of the dwarves.\
\
'He was my first friend, my dear companion, and having made him an enemy I mourned the brother I lost. Now in the span of the single day I have remaining to me I will do what I can to deliver him his kingdom.'","'I am conflicted, ${PLAYER}. I am grateful to know now without doubt that I am he who I wished to be... but Mótsog's part in this discovery does not erase his treachery, nor will it cause me to forgive his misdeeds.\
\
'I must think upon what is to be done.'","Mótsog waits quietly for Durin's decision, and says nothing.","Talk to Mótsog and learn if he will accept Durin's decision","'Well, ${PLAYER}, it seems the conquest of Gundabad will succeed or fail by nightfall. Let us hope we will celebrate the victory before the sun sets on this day!\
\
'I know what I must now do.'","Durin waits for Mótsog's answer.","Durin stands in Mótsog's Tomb far below Gundabad.","Durin stands in Mótsog's Tomb far below Gundabad, trying to decide what is to be done.","Durin stands in Mótsog's Tomb.","Mótsog has told you that he will walk in the world for only one more day before his long life is spent, and he wants to do what he can for the friend he once betrayed.","'I have decided, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Were I not to be king when my father leaves the throne, I could say to Mótsog, \\qBe gone. Let the sun set upon you, and trouble no longer the dwarves.\\q That would even be just, for the wrongs of the Greymaul Rebellion did not abate when the Sunder-battle ended. No, the injuries left by that conflict remain with us. Do Zhélruka and Longbeard not bristle at the perceived slights of the other, and ponder if something of the Greymaul spirit lives on behind their rival's clenched teeth? Do they not look upon the Stout-axe with distrust, brooding upon his long habitation in Mordor? The lesson of Mótsog was taught to the dwarves early, and did not diminish with the years.\
\
'Were I not to be king when my father releases the crown, I could climb the secret stair to the known levels of Gundabad, leaving Mótsog and what I learned here behind. But I cannot, for I will have the concerns of a king, as I did six times before. Mótsog is a tool to be used, ${PLAYER}, and I will wield this tool against our foes. I will use him to wrest control of the Mountain-home from both Orc and Dragon.\
\
'Surely Hrímil Frost-heart will remember the Greymaul leader who injured her during the Sunder-battle, and without the power of the dragon behind him, the Gabil'akkâ will be able to deal with Gorgar.'\
\
Durin once again addresses the impassive figure in the hidden chamber.\
\
'What say you, Mótsog? Will you spend your last day fighting for the dwarves you once betrayed? I do not command you; I only ask it of you.'","'What says Mótsog to this?'","Chapter 11.1: Soon To Wake"},
[2882]={"Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.","'I did not think we would encounter the Khûdi so quickly, but they had eyes upon our group from the moment we passed beyond the Ikorbân River. They must be desperate for wealth with which to conduct their rebellion against the Ordâkhai. Why else should they attack a group such as ours, with so many evident warriors and our own deadly weapons near at hand?\
\
'There is a cavern in the heights on the eastern side of Ghalbûru, and more of the Khûdi dwell within. The dwarf Khôltekh asked to see it.'","Talk to Rothog in Ghalbûru","Khôltekh is in the caves of Ghalbûru.","Find Khôltekh inside the caves of Ghalbûru","Ghalbûru's apothecary Babarín is located outside in the village, beneath her canopy on the island in the middle of the pool.","'We were waylaid by a number of Shagâni highwaymen who mistook us for vulnerable travellers; Rothog and his khopeshes cured them of that misconception very quickly. After Rahâzi made clear to them that we share an enemy in the Ordâkhai, they invited us to their hideout in the rocks to the south-east, a place called Ghalbûru.\
\
'I stayed behind to tell you where everyone has gone. Let us now join them at Ghalbûru.'","It will take some time for Babarín to prepare the soothing poultice. You can wait for it to be ready, or you can speak to your companions throughout Ghalbûru.","'Who is this man Khôltekh has tasked you with healing, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You quietly describe what you were told concerning Sadûkh and how the Kindred of the Coins believes Azagath's former servant might have spirited Balakhâd from Umbar and into the wild. Corudan purses his lips in thought.\
\
'Something is not right here. I know not what, but this puzzling mosaic seems to be missing some pieces. Keep your eyes open.'","'The making of the poultice will take some time. Such things cannot be rushed. You must hope your friend can survive until it is ready.\
\
'I recommend you keep yourself busy. Perhaps then you will not notice the time passing.'","'Sadûkh's condition has worsened. I care not if he dies, but I would rather he first told us of Balakhâd's fate.\
\
'I would know if we must be concerned about the Heirs of Castamir. As long as Balakhâd might remain somewhere alive in the wild, the Heirs will remain a threat to Umbar and to the Kindred.'","Rothog is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Babarín is beneath her canopy on the island in the middle of the pool.","'The highwaymen of Ghalbûru tell me they found this man dying beside the road outside Jirush, left for dead by the Ordâkhai. They brought him back here to interrogate him about the caravan with which he travelled, and if any of its treasure might have been overlooked by the Ordâkhai. It seems he was too badly injured to speak to them, so they have abandoned the effort. He has been left for dead twice now, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Khôltekh lowers his voice and speaks to you in hushed tones.\
\
'Did you take note of the clothing he wears? He is dressed in the Umbari fashion, and matches the description I was given for the water-bearer that aided in Balakhâd's escape from the Citadel of Winds. Sadûkh he was named, yes? I deem he travelled with no caravan, but in the company of a single disguised man. The whereabouts of that disguised man are of great interest to me, and to the Kindred of the Coins, as you are well aware.\
\
'The highwaymen have abandoned their efforts to restore him to health, but we need him to tell us what has happened to Balakhâd. Speak to the apothecary outside in Ghalbûru proper and learn what we will need to save this man's life. I care not if he dies, but he must not die before he tells us what he knows.'","Collect riverside reeds in Ghalbûru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The poultice is prepared. I hope it provides some comfort for your friend, and will help to heal his hurts. He will have a long road ahead of him, for the swords of the Ordâkhai brought him very near to death, but the use of this poultice should help him to recover.'","'Is it true that Khôltekh identified the dying Umbari man the highwaymen brought to Ghalbûru to be Azagath's water-bearer Sadûkh? That is most surprising! The dwarf must have an eye for faces to have so readily identified him so far from the city.\
\
'What do you think Sadûkh might tell us of Balakhôr's son Balakhâd? If he still lives, the dreams of the Heirs of Castamir remain alive, and may cause problems for Gondor in the future.'","'Is it true the injured man you seek to heal is Azagath's former water-bearer Sadûkh? If he might be made to tell us what happened to Balakhâd, we might count one of our objectives satisfied... and so early on our journey!'","Bring the healing poultice to Sadûkh in the caves of Ghalbûru","'These highwaymen thought to rob us of coin, so I showed to them the medallion that marks me as one of the Kindred of the Coins; they recognized it not. The city of Umbar is a good distance away from this arid land, and word travels slowly.\
\
'Then I showed to them my khopeshes, and that was a language they understood. The language of death travels quickly in every land, ${PLAYER}! Ha! Ha! Ha!'","Babarín's healing poultice must surely now be ready","'I hope that poultice provides some comfort for your friend, and will help to heal his hurts.'","Chapter 11.2: An Incident On The Road","The hideout of Ghalbûru is among the rocks south-east of the road through Khûd Zagin.","'I am reminded of our stay in the Shield Isles, ${PLAYER}. The freebooters there share something in common with these rebels, I think, though neither knows it. You should have seen how rapidly they lowered their weapons when Rothog raised his own! Both these rebels and the freebooters of the Shield Isles can make rapid calculations when they must!'","'Wh-wh-' he struggles to speak as you administer the poultice. After a moment, he closes his eyes.\
\
'I... thank you...' he says weakly. His eyes flutter open once again and he manages to turn his head to look past you. A look of terror crosses his face as he sees Khôltekh standing nearby.\
\
'He... he is here! He... seeks to punish me!'","Your travelling party encountered some difficulty with highwaymen on the road into Khûd Zagin and followed them back to their hideout.","'You have returned with the ingredients? I confess I did not think you would.\
\
'I will make the poultice for which you have asked. It will take some time. Such things cannot be rushed. You must hope your friend can survive until it is ready.\
\
'I recommend you keep yourself busy. Perhaps then you will not notice the time passing.'","Ingredients needed by Babarín can be found throughout Ghalbûru: hardy plant leaves and riverside reeds.","'The people who live here frequently quarrel among themselves, finding it difficult to agree on a single course of action. That is not a problem we have in Umbar Baharbêl, for the Kindred of the Coins is a strong body, made up of strong voices.\
\
'That is not to say the rebels of Ghalbûru lack wisdom. They seem quite frightened of both me and Húrshauk... and is that not both knowledgeable and wise?'","Khôltekh has found an injured man resting in the caves of Ghalbûru.","'Before we left Iridír for Khûd Zagin I said we might speak in private of the dreams that troubled our rest. Do you wish to speak of them now? Of what did you dream, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Sigileth that the details of your dream faded with the dawn, but you remember that her brother Corudan spent some portion of it in despair, seeking for Sigileth but unable to find her. You also remember one of the Nazgûl leading a band of Orcs in search of something in an unknown land, and the words \\qbeyond living memory,\\q but their significance has faded with the night. Sigileth nods thoughtfully.\
\
'I dreamt of a long corridor leading into darkness, ${PLAYER}. I sought something, though I cannot remember what, but I knew it lay at the end of the corridor. I think Cruel Dancer was beside me, but when I turned my head to look at her she was gone. I am reminded now of the Room of Voices beneath Dol Guldur, but the feeling of this corridor was... different, somehow.\
\
'I awoke disturbed. It may have been only a dream, but my people know such dreams often foretell the future, or shed light upon the past, and should not be ignored.'","Talk to Sirgon in Ghalbûru","'We need this man to tell us what has happened to Balakhâd. Speak to the apothecary here in Ghalbûru and learn what we will need to save this man's life. I care not if he dies, but he must not die before he tells us what he knows.'","Babarín gives you the healing poultice she prepared","Collect hardy plant leaves in Ghalbûru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Babarín, the apothecary in Ghalbûru","Talk to Babarín in Ghalbûru","Find the entrance to Ghalbûru in Khûd Zagin","'You need a remedy for the dying man that was lately brought to Ghalbûru? I will not say he is beyond saving, but he lost a great deal of blood to the blades of the Ordâkhai stationed in Jirush. They would not have purposefully left him alive; they believed he was dead already.\
\
'I can make a poultice that may help him, but I have exhausted my supply of ingredients. You must bring me the hardy plant leaves and riverside reeds I will need to fashion this remedy. You can find them around Ghalbûru if you truly must see this man healed.'","'I can make a poultice that may help him, but I have exhausted my supply of ingredients. You must bring me the hardy plant leaves and riverside reeds I will need to fashion this remedy. You can find them around Ghalbûru if you truly must see this man healed.'","Examine the injured man lying on the bed in the caves of Ghalbûru","Collected riverside reeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the ingredients you collected to Babarín in Ghalbûru","Collected hardy plant leaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I stayed behind to tell you where everyone has gone. Let us now join them at Ghalbûru to the south-east.'","Sadûkh is resting in the caves of Ghalbûru. The entrance to the caves is located in the heights on the eastern side of Ghalbûru.","Khôltekh nods in the direction of the injured man lying on the bed","The man is seriously injured. He is dressed in the Umbari style","Sirgon is at the north-western entrance of Ghalbûru.","'I see Belondor found you, my friend.'","'The Khûdi who dwell here at Ghalbûru are brigands and highwaymen, ${PLAYER}, disorganized and given to quarrelling among themselves instead of uniting effectively against the Ordâkhai. If they were responsible for driving the Ordâkhai out of Ambarûl, instead of my mother Girhâzi, Iridír would still be occupied by soldiers of the Empire!\
\
'With only five or six Dumûri to fight alongside me I might make things different in Khûd Zagin, but it is not so.'","Khôltekh is inside the caves of Ghalbûru. The entrance to the caves is in the heights on the eastern side of Ghalbûru.","Talk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru","'I see Belondor found you, my friend.\
\
'The folk who dwell here name this place Ghalbûru, which they told me means \\qThieves' Cut.\\q I do not think they gave it that name, but they have embraced it. These caves must have been home for brigands and highwaymen throughout the years, but now that the Ordâkhai have tightened their grip on Khûd Zagin, Ghalbûru has become a hideout for those who resist that empire.\
\
'I am reminded of our stay in the Shield Isles, ${PLAYER}. The freebooters there share something in common with these rebels, I think, though neither knows it. You should have seen how rapidly they lowered their weapons when Rothog raised his own! Both these rebels and the freebooters of the Shield Isles can make rapid calculations when they must!'","'The language of death travels quickly in every land! Ha! Ha! Ha!'","The rest of your travelling companions have come to Ghalbûru","Talk to Khôltekh in the caves of Ghalbûru","Wait for the poultice to be prepared or speak to your travelling companions throughout Ghalbûru","'The Khûdi must be desperate for wealth with which to conduct their rebellion against the Ordâkhai.\
\
'There is a cavern in the heights on the eastern side of Ghalbûru, and more of the Khûdi dwell within. The dwarf Khôltekh asked to see it.'"},
[2883]={"Chapter 11.2: Dwarrowmoot","'I will call for Dwarrowmoot once again, ${PLAYER}. There I will explain the final steps we must take to drive Hrímil Frost-heart and her thrall Gorgar from Gundabad. Only then will the Mountain-home will be ours again.\
\
'Climb the secret stair back to Zul-mazal, ${PLAYER}. Then I ask you to seek out a leader of the Iron Garrison such as Bósi or his kin, Glóin of the Longbeards, Prince Ingór of the Zhélruka, and Imák the Stout-axe, and tell them to bring their companies of dwarves to the Thing-fold for Dwarrowmoot.'","'Dwarrowmoot is almost upon us. I will meet you at the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts.'","Durin fears that the foes prowling the Welkin-lofts may have hindered the arrival of his dwarves, and wants you to make the high passes as safe as possible.","Talk to Bósi, Bróin, or Bori in Zul-mazal","Climb the secret stair out of the depths and return to Zul-mazal","Talk to Imák on the western shore of the lake in Gloomingtarn","Meet up with the dwarves on the south-eastern side of the Thing-fold for Dwarrowmoot","Durin is at the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts for Dwarrowmoot, but is disappointed that more dwarves have not already arrived.","Talk to Durin at the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts","Talk to Prince Ingór at Maergrind in Máttugard","Defeat Orc-kind in the Welkin-lofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'That was all we needed, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you for your efforts on behalf of the Gabil'akkâ. More dwarves have arrived!\
\
'It is time for Dwarrowmoot.'","Talk to Glóin at the Steepset in Máttugard","'Thin the numbers of Orcs and Angmarim in the Welkin-lofts and diminish the potential distractions for dwarves coming to the Fold, ${PLAYER}!'","Many dwarves have arrived for Dwarrowmoot... but not enough","Your friends greet you with enthusiasm and with worry","'${PLAYER}! What did you discover beyond those secret stairs? How fares the prince? Has he need of us? We are ready!'\
\
You tell Bróin that Durin does have need of him, and indeed the prince calls for the rest of his kin to answer his call.\
\
'Dwarrowmoot? Can it be? I will send word to the others, and at once! We shall assemble at the Thing-fold and there await Prince Durin!'","Durin has decided to call for Dwarrowmoot, a meeting of all the dwarves, where it will be decided what should be done to secure Gundabad.","'Dwarrowmoot? Is that what it sounds like?\
\
'Well, you must forgive me, but I was not present at the last one! The Stout-axes had other things on their minds, as you might imagine! But I will attend this one. My people should be represented, for this Moot may determine the success of the conquest. There are few of my people here, but they will answer Durin's call.\
\
'Durin can count on my attendance, and on my axe, if it comes to that.'","'Some dwarves have arrived, but not enough... not nearly enough!\
\
'What is taking them so long, ${PLAYER}? Mótsog has less than a day remaining to him, and I am relying upon him to strike fear into the dragon's heart. If the Greymaul is unable to stand with us...\
\
'Perhaps the dwarves are stopping to fight Orcs and Angmarim on the way? Thin their numbers in the Welkin-lofts and diminish the potential distractions for dwarves coming to the Fold, ${PLAYER}!'","Defeat Angmarim in the Welkin-lofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Your efforts have enabled more dwarves to arrive for the Dwarrowmoot. Durin is eager to begin.","'The time has come for me to call for Dwarrowmoot, a meeting of all the dwarves here in the Mountain-home. It was held at the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts whenever dwarves had grave matters to discuss or a need that could not be addressed without a consensus of many dwarf-lords. It was a ritual for the martialing of war or the making of peace, and was common at one time. When Gundabad was briefly reclaimed at the outset of the Sixth War, the first Dwarrowmoot in four thousand years was called at the Fold, and the course of that conflict was decided.\
\
'I will call for Dwarrowmoot once again, ${PLAYER}. There I will explain the final steps we must take to drive Hrímil Frost-heart and her thrall Gorgar from Gundabad. Only then will the Mountain-home be ours again.\
\
'Climb the secret stair back to Zul-mazal. Seek out a leader of the Iron Garrison such as Bósi or his kin, Glóin of the Longbeards, Prince Ingór of the Zhélruka, and Imák the Stout-axe, and tell them to bring their companies of dwarves to the Thing-fold for Dwarrowmoot.'","'I will call for Dwarrowmoot once again, ${PLAYER}. There I will explain the final steps we must take to drive Hrímil Frost-heart and her thrall Gorgar from Gundabad. Only then will the Mountain-home be ours again.\
\
'Climb the secret stair back to Zul-mazal, ${PLAYER}. Then I ask you to seek out a leader of the Iron Garrison such as Bósi or his kin, Glóin of the Longbeards, Prince Ingór of the Zhélruka, and Imák the Stout-axe, and tell them to bring their companies of dwarves to the Thing-fold for Dwarrowmoot.'","'Dwarrowmoot, eh? So we come to it at last. Good! The Zhélruka will hear what the Longbeard prince has to say, and we will await our reward when the fighting is done.\
\
'Aye, there will be fighting, make no mistake of that. Durin calls for the dwarves to assemble at the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts, after all. Has he not considered how exposed that hillside is to the air? We will be meeting in full view of the peak, from which Hrímil watches over the lands all about.\
\
'One thing is clear to me, ${PLAYER}. Dwarrowmoot will decide the fate of Gundabad, and of us all... one way or another.'","Durin has asked you to climb from the depths and return to Zul-mazal, where you can begin gathering the dwarves for Dwarrowmoot.","'Dwarrowmoot! To think I should live to see another! I remember the glory of the last, though I was just a lad. Thráin led a great attack upon the Fold, recovering it from the Orcs for the first time in thousands of years. He called for the lords to determine where the hammer stroke of our war should fall; we left Gundabad when it was decided, and only a small garrison remained. Much might have been different had the Moot chosen otherwise.'\
\
Glóin shakes his head.\
\
'But that was long ago, and now our concerns are with the Mountain-home and not at Khazad-dûm; we need not have our attention divided. I will gather the Longbeards, ${PLAYER}. My prince will have his Moot!'","Defeated Orc-kind in the Welkin-lofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Angmarim in the Welkin-lofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Durin at the Thing-fold","Durin has called for Dwarrowmoot on the south-eastern side of the Thing-fold, in the Welkin-lofts.","Durin asked you to bring word to a number of dwarves about the upcoming Dwarrowmoot:\
\
Bósi, Bróin, or Bori at Zul-mazal.\
Prince Ingór at Maergrind in Máttugard.\
Glóin at the Steepset in Máttugard.\
Imák on the western shore of the lake in Gloomingtarn.\
\
These dwarves will select others of their kind to attend the Dwarrowmoot. Time is short!"},
[2884]={"'What is it you wish to know?'\
\
You ask the shade about an Elf named Magoldir who fought for the Last Alliance at the end of the Second Age.\
\
'Was it the last?' he responds with a grim laugh. 'We called it the Great Alliance. It took years to assemble enough soldiers, from many different lands, and yet more years spent in fighting. We thought it was the end of the world; it seemed the war would last forever.'\
\
He falls silent for a time, considering your question.\
\
'I knew an Elf named Magoldir. He befriended my sons, if I remember aright, and fought alongside them during the Siege of Barad-dûr. And there was another, too: a , the same as you, who adventured with my sons during the last days of the war. Yes. Let me tell you what I remember of this , and through those words you may learn something of use concerning Magoldir the Elf. But before I tell you this tale, you will first need to recover something. The Orcs spent countless years delving in the muck of the Gladden Fields, and they brought the things they found to their various camps in the area. Go to the encampment south-west of here and retrieve a weather-stained coffer from within the camp. Its contents will refresh some of my memory, and then I will speak to you of the  who befriended my sons, and was allied with Magoldir the Elf.'","'I told you there was a  who befriended my sons, and who fought with the Great Alliance at the Siege of Barad-dûr. This box contained all of ${PLAYER:her[f]|his} possessions. After the war, ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} came north with us on that doomed road, and died there.\
\
'But I could say much of ${PLAYER:her[f]|his} story before its ending, and you may learn something worth knowing of Magoldir. As I speak to you of times long past, you are welcome to take as reward whatever items you will; ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} was a , the same as you, and ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} would be pleased for ${PLAYER:her[f]|his} possessions to be once again of service in the fight against evil.\
\
'Take a close look at these Memories of the Great Alliance, and I will speak to you of the Siege of Barad-dûr.'","Retrieve weather-stained coffer from Sharkey's Slough","'Yes, that is the coffer I expected. Set it down among the flowers.'","'These things no doubt possessed some meaning for their owner,' Elrond continues, 'but to the half-orcs they would have seemed of little worth. The chest must have remained in the mud of the Gladden Fields, forgotten and ignored, for many years.'","You set the weather-stained coffer down among the flowers","'As I speak to you of times long past, you are welcome to take as reward whatever items you will; ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} was at home in the wild, the same as you, and ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} would be pleased for ${PLAYER:her[f]|his} possessions to be once again of service in the fight against evil.\
\
'Take a close look at these Memories of the Great Alliance, and I will speak to you of the Siege of Barad-dûr.'","Ontamo is in Díngarth, chief fortification of the Great Alliance in Mordor Besieged.","Elrond is on Tol Send, the Isle of the Flowers in the Gladden Fields.\
\
Elrond examines the weather-stained coffer with some interest.","Talk to Ontamo in Díngarth, Mordor Besieged","'But victory would not come swiftly. The siege would last for seven long years.'","Talk to the shade of Isildur","Chapter 11.2: The Same As You","The Memories of the Great Alliance will allow you to experience the Siege of Barad-dûr at the end of the Second Age, as relayed to you by the shade of Isildur.","The shade of Isildur has agreed to tell you what he remembers of the Elf named Magoldir and the Siege of Barad-dûr that concluded the Second Age.","The dented coffer is caked in mud, ravaged by the passage of years","The shade of Isildur is waiting for you to bring the weather-stained coffer to Tol Send.","'This is very interesting, ${PLAYER}. The half-orcs must have pulled this chest from the mud as they scoured the Gladden Fields for treasure.'\
\
Elrond opens the lid of the coffer and examines the items within: old pieces of equipment, small trinkets, and time-worn artifacts of unknown value.\
\
'These things no doubt possessed some meaning for their owner,' Elrond continues, 'but to the half-orcs they would have seemed of little worth. The chest must have remained in the mud of the Gladden Fields, forgotten and ignored, for many years.'","Talk to Elrond on Tol Send","Bring the weather-stained coffer to Tol Send","'As I speak to you of times long past, you are welcome to take as reward whatever items you will; ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} was a , the same as you, and ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} would be pleased for ${PLAYER:her[f]|his} possessions to be once again of service in the fight against evil.\
\
'Take a close look at these Memories of the Great Alliance, and I will speak to you of the Siege of Barad-dûr.'","The shade of Isildur is pleased that you found the weather-stained coffer and brought it to Tol Send, and now wishes to tell you the tale he promised.","'Before I tell you what I remember of this ${CLASS} and Magoldir the Elf, you should recover something from the encampment to the south-west. I speak of a weather-stained coffer that lies within the camp. Its contents will refresh some of my memory, and then I will tell you of the ${CLASS} who befriended my sons, and was allied with Magoldir the Elf.'","'After Dagorlad, the Great Alliance threw down the Black Gate and marched into Mordor.'","Use the Memories of the Great Alliance and be transported to Mordor Besieged (Second Age)","'You there! ${CLASS}! Listen well to me, for this is urgent, and cannot wait!'","The shade of Isildur asked you to retrieve a weather-stained coffer from the encampment of Sharkey's Slough, south-west of Tol Send."},
[2885]={"Talk to Magoldir among the bodies of the slain Orcs","'You improved the defences here at Díngarth? Good, good, and just in time! I have received word that a patrol of Orcs has been spotted to the south, leaving the encampment of Mokh Shapat. If we don't do something about them, and at once, King Isildur will be most aggrieved!\
\
'Your work here is not yet done! Hurry to the south and slay the Orc band before the king comes to Díngarth!'","'You heard Orc-voices far to the south of Díngarth? You need to investigate, and at once! The king might be here any moment!'","Ontamo asked you to collect wood and stone for patching up the fortifications at Díngarth and to keep resting soldiers from giving Isildur the impression of laziness when he comes to inspect the defences.","Repair the fortifications at Díngarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected wood for patching (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ontamo awaits your return in Díngarth.","Ontamo is at Díngarth, awaiting word of your success against the Orcs.","'The fortifications of Díngarth need to be repaired before King Isildur conducts his inspection! Use the wood and the stone you collected to improve the weaknesses in our defences!'","'Mae govannen, friend. I am sorry, but you have come too late to join in the festivities!'","Defeated Orcs south of Díngarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am afraid you have come too late to join the festivities, friend. These Orcs thought to do some mischief to the Alliance, but they were neither stealthy nor clever enough to escape my notice. They felt the bite of my blade and did not like it!\
\
'I am called Magoldir, and my sword is Orthadel, the Rising Star. I wield it at the command of Gil-galad, and it has proven the undoing of Orcs and evil Men for the long years of this siege. My errand today was to scout the southern reaches and report discovery of anything suspicious, but if I suspect anything now it is that these Orcs should have known better than to come this far west! Even after these long years of siege, they still test the encampments of both Men and Elves, probing for weaknesses. If they think we will relax our guard, they are mistaken, and we will prove it ever so.\
\
'It was a pleasure to meet you, friend. Return now to Díngarth and relay word of this Orc raiding-party to whichever leader there has the command. These Orcs have come to the end of their raiding days, and will trouble us no further.'","Collect wood for patching the defences of Díngarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You came today from Díngarth? Return there now and relay word of this Orc raiding-party to whichever leader there has the command. These Orcs have come to the end of their raiding days, and will trouble us no further.'","An Elf stands among the bodies of a slain Orc raiding party","Talk to Ontamo at Díngarth","You have stumbled upon an Elf surrounded by the bodies of a slain Orc raiding party.","'I have received word that a patrol of Orcs has been spotted to the south, leaving the encampment of Mokh Shapat. If we don't do something about them, and at once, King Isildur will be most aggrieved! Hurry to the south and slay the Orc band before the king comes to Díngarth!'","The guttural voices of Orcs can be heard among the rocks far to the south of Díngarth.","Ontamo has asked you to improve the fortifications at spots in need of repair in and around Díngarth.","'I have been informed that King Isildur of Gondor plans to return to Díngarth in order to inspect the defences! As the master of fortifications, the responsibility falls to me to ensure that the king is satisfied by the state of them. But that is no easy task, for Díngarth was the first encampment we constructed after the Alliance pushed through the ruins of the Gate, seven years gone. It has been repeatedly assailed by the forces of Sauron, and rebuilt anew following the worst of the assaults.\
\
'Isildur rules Gondor with his brother Anárion, at the behest of their father, the High King, and there is no end to the worries upon which they must dwell as the siege drags on. King Isildur would not trouble to return to Díngarth if he thought our business here unimportant. He must know, as I do, that if the forward positions of the Alliance are pushed back, Díngarth will become our only foothold in the Black Land. To face defeat after such cost of lives and years would be impossible to bear!\
\
'So I ask you to gather wood and stone from around Díngarth and patch up the fortifications. You will impress King Isildur with the sweat of your brow and I shall impress him with my foresight and my leadership. Look too for resting soldiers and get them moving. To see such sluggards lazing about would surely offend the king's eyes. Go then, and see these tasks done!'","Get resting soldiers at Díngarth moving again (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Orc raiding parties remained a threat, even years after the siege began.'","Disturbed resting soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Chapter 11.3: A Day at Díngarth","Ontamo is worried about the imminent inspection of the fortifications of Díngarth by Isildur, King of Gondor, and has requested your aid in their improvement.","Investigate the sound of Orc voices far to the south of Díngarth","'Not every subject of Gondor was willing to put the kingdom first. I was not blind to it.'","Collected stone for patching (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What can you say of the Orcs? Dead? Good, but it does not matter.'\
\
Ontamo scowls and clenches his fist.\
\
'Isildur has chosen not to come to Díngarth! This was my opportunity to impress the King of Gondor with my maintenance of the defences, and now it has come to naught! I spoke of Díngarth's importance to the Great Alliance, but it seems Isildur does not agree after all! Instead of a personal visit, he has sent his sons to assess the defences! His sons only! They can bestow neither land nor title, not while their father lives! Bah!'","'So I ask you to gather wood and stone from around Díngarth and patch up the fortifications. You will impress King Isildur with the sweat of your brow and I shall impress him with my foresight and my leadership. Look too for resting soldiers and get them moving. To see such sluggards lazing about would surely offend the king's eyes. Go then, and see these tasks done!'","An Orc raiding party was seen patrolling south of the encampment of Díngarth, and Ontamo asked you to take care of it before King Isildur arrived for his inspection of the defences. Orcs can be found leaving their encampment of Mokh Shapat, far to the south of Díngarth.","Defeat Orcs south of Díngarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect stone for patching the defences of Díngarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2886]={"Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Corudan asked you to go to the south-western entrance to Ghalbûru and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for some sign of Sadûkh.","Sadûkh is no longer here. Where did he go?","Khôltekh is in the caves of Ghalbûru.","'You have brought to me the jackal teeth I requested? They will become the centrepiece of my next work of craft, the sale of which will put food upon my table when next a caravan passes through Jirush. You have earned the information I have to tell you, my new friend.'\
\
Erinesh looks over his shoulder to ensure the guards are out of earshot.\
\
'The greatest part of the garrison of Ordâkh marched north beneath the banner of the Black Serpent to fight in Barkhûsh's war against Gondor, and most of them died there. Defeated stragglers returned from that campaign over the months that followed, and most of them came to gather in the only place they believed to be safe: that is why the black serpent flies still over Jirush. The garrison has been made strong again, and the Ordâkhai rule over the Khûd, if nowhere else. They waylay travellers along the Road of Riches and exact harsh tolls from them, competing with brigands and highwaymen for the same coin.\
\
'The soldiers demanded a toll from the man you sought, but he resisted. They slew his companion and dragged him into the fortress above Jirush. I do not know why they kept him alive. I have not seen him emerge from the fortress, so the number of his days may be few, or already spent.'","Talk to Corudan outside the entrance to the caves of Ghalbûru","Talk to Urugal at the south-western entrance to Ghalbûru","Rahâzi suggested that you return to Sadûkh to tell him what you learned of Balakhad's location before you help her infiltrate the fortress above Jirush. Sadûkh is recovering from his injuries in the caves of Ghalbûru.","Corudan is outside the entrance to the caves of Ghalbûru, located in the heights on the eastern side of the village.","'How could Sadûkh go anywhere beneath anyone's notice with such injuries as he possessed? Go to the north-eastern and south-western entrances to Ghalbûru and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for any sign of him. He surely cannot have gone far.'","There is no sign of Sadûkh at the north-eastern entrance to Ghalbûru","Talk to residents of Jirush who can tell you about Balakhad's location (${CURRENT}/3)","In the caves of Ghalbûru, Sadûkh seeks assurances that you will protect him from his enemies.","Sadûkh sees enemies all around him, believing there to be knives everywhere... even within Ghalbûru.","'The Ambarûli warrior Rahâzi will be interested to learn that one of the men we seek may now be held by her hated foe. See what she has to say about this, ${PLAYER}. I will remain here and keep an eye upon Sadûkh.'","Go to the south-western entrance to Ghalbûru and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for some sign of Sadûkh","'The man you seek was brought alive into the fortress above Jirush? We cannot know if he lives still... but there is one way to learn of it for certain.'\
\
Rahâzi's eyes sparkle as she continues.\
\
'It is time for me to call upon the promise you made to me, ${PLAYER}. I ask that you help me infiltrate the fortress. I will slay the Ordâkhai within, and you can search for the man they hold captive. Before we do this, you should inform the injured man back in the caves of Ghalbûru that we may be able to rescue his companion.'","Silence hangs over the town of Jirush, as if the entire town holds its breath","Rahâzi has suggested that you go to the town of Jirush in the desert to the west and see if any of the townsfolk there know Balakhad's location.","Talk to residents of Jirush who can tell you about Balakhad's location (2/3)","Sadûkh eyes you warily, and you ask him what happened to Balakhâd","'If Balakhâd had fallen in battle with the Ordâkhai, his body would have been found when the highwaymen of Ghalbûru encountered Sadûkh. I think it is more likely the soldiers brought him back to Jirush.\
\
'The Ambarûli warrior Rahâzi will be interested to learn that one of the men we seek may now be held by her hated foe. See what she has to say about this, ${PLAYER}. I will remain here and keep an eye upon Sadûkh.'","'No one wishes to speak with you about the man the soldiers apprehended outside the city several days ago? I am not surprised. My neighbours do not wish to draw the eyes of their occupiers upon them again, for to do so might brand them rebels against the empire. They have not my courage.\
\
'No, I am not afraid of the soldiers who live in the fortress, but if I am to answer your questions I need some assurance it will be worth my while.\
\
'I am a craftsman of fine things, but with fewer caravans passing along the Road of Riches, I need to price my individual wares more highly than before. If you bring me the sharp jackal teeth I need for a necklace I am making, I will tell you what I know about this man you seek. Jackals can be found outside the city and throughout the sands of Khûd Zagin. Now remember: only the sharpest of their teeth will suffice for my purpose, and earn you the answers you desire.'","Collected sharp jackal teeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Go to the north-eastern entrance of Ghalbûru and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for some sign of Sadûkh","Assure Sadûkh that you will protect him","Talk to Sadûkh in the caves of Ghalbûru","'It is time for me to call upon the promise you made to me, ${PLAYER}. I ask that you help me infiltrate the fortress. I will slay the Ordâkhai within, and you can search for the man they hold captive. Before we do this, you should inform the injured man back in Ghalbûru that we may be able to rescue his companion.'","Talk to Rahâzi in Jirush","'Let us learn the truth of it! First we will ask questions... and then we will draw blood, if such becomes necessary. Jirush lies to the west.'","'What? Sadûkh is missing?\
\
'I thought his injuries were such that he could not move well or quickly. How could he go anywhere beneath anyone's notice?\
\
'Go to the north-eastern and south-western entrances to Ghalbûru and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for any sign of him. He surely cannot have gone far.'","Townsfolk of Jirush can be found throughout the city.","Bring the sharp jackal teeth to Erinesh in Jirush","Corudan asked you to go to the north-eastern entrance of Ghalbûru and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for some sign of Sadûkh.","Chapter 11.3: Knives Everywhere","'It is a mystery, but the solving of it must wait. If we are to locate Balakhâd and fulfil our promise to Rahâzi, we will need to tread with care. We have not the time to search for Sadûkh. I do not understand where he could have gone. Perhaps he will turn up when we return.'","There is no sign of Sadûkh at the south-western entrance, but a guard beckons to you","'If you bring me the sharp jackal teeth I need for a necklace I am making, I will tell you what I know about this man you seek. Jackals can be found outside the city and throughout the sands of Khûd Zagin. Now remember: only the sharpest of their teeth will suffice for my purpose, and earn you the answers you desire.'","Erinesh stands in the centre of Jirush.","Erinesh may know something about Balakhad's location, but he wants you to collect jackal teeth for him before he tells you anything. Jackals can be found throughout Khûd Zagin.","'What are you seeking, stranger?'\
\
You ask Urugal if he saw the injured Umbari man pass this way out of Ghalbûru, and he shakes his head.\
\
'No, I have not, and I am the most vigilant of my brothers. If your injured man came this way I would have seen him. Not only this, but if he left Ghalbûru he would not last very long among the rocks and stones of the Khûd. Animals hardy enough to survive there would make a quick meal of a man as injured as he, and that is to speak not of otherworldly evils even more frightening than the creatures of the land.\
\
'Yes! If the beasts do not feast upon him, he may become the prey of Ishími, the Anguished Wind that haunts the deserts of Shagâna! Ever since the fall of Barkhûsh, the whispering and wailing of Ishími has driven to madness strong men caught in the barren wastes. I do not mean this in an insulting fashion, but the man you have lost did not appear very strong to me. If he left Ghalbûru that Umbari man is surely dead.'","'I am sorry. I know nothing.\
\
'Please leave me be. I do not wish to speak with you.'","'If only... if only I had done as... as the letters directed. Instead we fled from the city, surviving in the wild lands... for weeks... but always we felt the jaws of discovery pressing on our heels. In this land we were discovered by an Ordâkhai patrol outside... outside their hilltop fortress! My lord Balakhâd fought bravely... but... to no avail!'","Corudan is outside the entrance to the caves of Ghalbûru, in the heights on the eastern side of the village.","'There are knives everywhere! Everywhere!'\
\
Sadûkh's eyes dart from your face to Khôltekh and back again.\
\
'Promise me... promise me you will protect me...' he gasps through the pain.","Collect sharp teeth from jackals in Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Rahâzi is in the centre of Jirush.","Urugal has beckoned for you to speak with him.","'If your injured man left Ghalbûru he would not last very long among the rocks and stones of the Khûd.'","Sadûkh is resting in the caves of Ghalbûru.","'It is of no use, then...' he murmurs sadly. 'The Kindred... the Kindred will never let me live... knowing I helped their prisoner escape their clutches. They did not know I prayed for... for the return of the Heirs of Castamir. I received word from Saklaphêl that... if I aided her son in his escape, she would attack the city and overthrow... the usurping Kindred!'\
\
Puzzled, you ask how the widow Saklaphêl was able to send a message to Sadûkh from her exile in the Shield Isles. He coughs wetly, and tries to dab away the blood.\
\
'Every morning... I collected the jar set aside for me and filled it with water from the bay. It was the task of water-bearers... to fill the fountains within the Citadel for Azagath. On several mornings... there were letters for me hidden beneath my jar. They told me to bring Balakhâd to a safe location beneath the city, in Umbar-môkh. Saklaphêl and the Heirs would then attack and restore our rightful ruler!'\
\
You ask why Sadûkh left the city instead of hiding Balakhâd in Umbar-môkh, as the letters directed, and tears suddenly stream from his face.\
\
'I thought that would be too near the Kindred, and they would find him easily! If only... if only I had done as... as the letters directed. Instead we fled from the city, surviving in the wild lands... for weeks... but always we felt the jaws of discovery pressing on our heels. In this land we were discovered by an Ordâkhai patrol outside... outside their hilltop fortress! My lord Balakhâd fought bravely... but... to no avail!'","'Did the injured man give you the information you sought?'\
\
You tell Rahâzi that one of the men sought by your travelling companions may have been brought to the town of Jirush in Khûd Zagin by a patrol of Ordâkhai soldiers. She nods thoughtfully and grips her weapon more tightly.\
\
'Then let us learn the truth of it, ${PLAYER}! First we will ask questions... and then we will draw blood, if such becomes necessary. Jirush lies to the west.'","Talk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru","Talk to Khôltekh in the caves of Ghalbûru","'I have nothing to say to you. Please move along, and do not disturb me! We have troubles enough without such as you drawing the attention of soldiers from the fortress!'","Travel to the entrance of Jirush, located in the desert to the west"},
[2888]={"Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Khôltekh is at the north-west entrance to Ghalbûru, east of Jirush.","'Now tell the Dumûri warrior we are ready to satisfy the obligation we promised. I saw she waits just to the north.'","'Are you ready to go? The fortress awaits us. It will not prevent us from slaying many Ordâkhai, or from freeing the captive you seek!'","Talk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru and infiltrate the fortress above Jirush","'I foresee one potential problem with this adventure of Rahâzi's: what will we do if we are unable to locate Balakhâd before she attracts too much notice with her attack upon the Ordâkhai?\
\
'Will you ask my sister to come with us as we infiltrate the fortress of Jirush? I would feel better if she accompanied us!'","'I will come with you. You will need someone who can search the fortress quickly and quietly, for we may not have long before Rahâzi causes the Ordâkhai to sound the alarm.'\
\
Sigileth cocks an eyebrow at you, and you tell her that Corudan said much the same thing.\
\
'We are siblings, after all, ${PLAYER}. It is nice to hear that some of my way of thinking has become his own. It was not always so!\
\
'Now tell the Dumûri warrior we are ready to satisfy the obligation we promised. I saw she waits just to the north.'","Sigileth is in the centre of Jirush.","Chapter 11.4: Shadows In Jirush","Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru, waiting to go with you to the fortress above Jirush.","Talk to Khôltekh at the north-west entrance to Ghalbûru","Talk to Sigileth in the centre of Jirush","Return to the north-west entrance of Ghalbûru, east of Jirush","Talk to Sigileth on the western side of Ghalbûru","'I overheard something within the fortress that may help us locate Balakhâd, but...'\
\
Sigileth frowns and studies your face closely.\
\
'He is alive, ${PLAYER}, but I think you should return to Ghalbûru and tell the others that he was slain by his Ordâkhai captors. When you deliver these tidings, keep a close eye upon Khôltekh and Rothog in particular. My brother told me about Sadûkh's disappearance, and something in the manner of it fills me with suspicion. I distrust those two; was not Khôltekh among the last to see Sadûkh alive?\
\
'Perhaps the two of them will betray their thoughts if they believe Balakhâd is dead.'","Khôltekh greets you as you approach. 'Well?' he prompts you","Sigileth is on the western side of Ghalbûru.","Sigileth suggested you return to Ghalbûru, but that you keep the information you learned about Balakhad to yourself.","'What is this I hear? The son of Balakhôr the Scourge was slain by his Ordâkhai captors? Pity. It seems the Heirs of Castamir have at last succumbed to the fate that pursued them, and none will mourn their passing. I find it fitting that Balakhâd was ended at last by the folk with whom he thought to ally. So ends one foe of the Kindred of the Coins, if not the worst of them!\
\
'I would raise a mug in toast if this place had anything worth drinking. But even that cannot dampen my spirits.'","'Will you ask my sister to come with us as we infiltrate the fortress of Jirush? I would feel better if she accompanied us!'","Rahâzi is prepared for the two of you to assault the fortress above Jirush, but Corudan and Sigileth want to accompany you, hoping to find Balakhad before the Dumûri warrior alerts the Ordâkhai.","'Let us go, then, and without delay!'","Talk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru","'Balakhâd is alive, but I think you should return to Ghalbûru and tell the others that he was slain by his Ordâkhai captors. When you deliver these tidings, keep a close eye upon Khôltekh and Rothog in particular. My brother told me about Sadûkh's disappearance, and something in the manner of it fills me with suspicion. I distrust those two; was not Khôltekh among the last to see Sadûkh alive?\
\
'Perhaps the two of them will betray their thoughts if they believe Balakhâd is dead.'"},
[2889]={"The cheers seem to shake the mountain itself: 'Gundabad is ours!'","Gorgar has been defeated and Hrímil Frost-heart has fled on injured wings, abandoning the high places to Durin's army. You have achieved victory!","'The Dragon's cowardly escape has broken the spirit of her armies! They flee and scatter, seeking for Gorgar to lead them; they know not that he is dead, but the rumour will spread.\
\
'Injured as she is, Hrímil will not prevent us from reclaiming the Mountain-home! Gundabad is ours!'","Durin has entrusted you with accompanying Mótsog to the peak, there to face Hrímil Frost-heart. The prince and all of the Gabil'akkâ will create a path through the enemy forces so you can achieve your mission!","Talk to Durin on the mountain-side","At the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts, Durin prepares for the battle to come.","Chapter 11.4: The Last Greymaul","'Mótsog must reach the peak, ${PLAYER}. I need you to get him near enough that he can strike the killing blow upon the Dragon. Can you do this?'\
\
You assure Durin that you will see it done.\
 \
'I entrust no one else with this, my friend. All now depends upon you and the last of the Greymauls. If we do not see each other again, know that it has been an honour to fight alongside you, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
He clasps your hand briefly and raises the Red Axe in quick salute.\
\
'Are you ready?'","'Go then, and hurry! Our time is running short!\
\
'The Gabil'akkâ will clear a path for you.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Durin and accompany Mótsog to the peak... and to Hrímil Frost-heart"},
[2890]={"King Isildur of Gondor shakes his head disapprovingly, and calls you to him","Ontamo believes that he has been personally insulted by Isildur's decision to send his sons to inspect the defences at Díngarth, rather than come himself, and he has decided that you should meet with them instead.","Isildur is at the Gondorian encampment of Adambel.","Vëamacil is waiting to speak to you, now that Tárandil has given you no suggestions for his birthday present.","'As much as I would enjoy reporting the defences insufficient, if only to see Ontamo squirm, I cannot. Díngarth is as prepared as it needs to be. I presume that is your doing? Of course it is!\
\
'I have taken a liking to you, friend! What say you to returning to Adambel with us? You will find the company much more pleasing than here at Díngarth, and I know my brothers will not object. There is one thing, however. You should think of a birthday present to give to Tárandil, and bring it with you when you come to Adambel. Ask him what he wants!'","Collect trophies from wargs in Arandor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vëamacil is at Díngarth, waiting to take a meal with you before he conducts the inspection of the encampment's defences.","'Like every good plan, this will take some doing. Go slay some Orcs and some wargs, and collect trophies from them. We can deliver them to Tárandil at the encampment of Adambel, and tell him they are just the first part of his birthday present. He will love it, friend, trust me.'","Tárandil is at Díngarth.\
\
Vëamacil has decided that you should come with them to Adambel, but that you should first ask his foster-brother Tárandil what he wants as a present for his birthday.","'I told you I wanted for nothing, friend, or at least nothing in your power to give! Why should Tárandil ask for aught when the war shows no sign of stopping? Give me an end to the siege, and I will measure it my finest birthday since the war began! But even that would bring little comfort to my heart. These years have been hard, and one good day cannot balance out the rest.\
\
'Vëamacil thought I would want these trophies for a present? They smell terribly, but I tell you true that my brother usually smells much worse! Be not offended if I cast them into a fire and rid the soldiers here of their stench. It is a pity that Vëamacil's odour cannot be cleansed so easily!'","Collected trophies from wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to King Isildur at Adambel","'Youngest of my sons in Mordor, prone to jesting. Laughter came easily to him.'","Find Tárandil at the encampment of Adambel","Tárandil nods in greeting as you approach","Give the trophies to Tárandil as a birthday present","'My foster-father Isildur does not approve of Vëamacil's jests. It is a trait we share!'","Tárandil has gone to the primary Gondorian encampment of Adambel.\
\
Vëamacil asked you to slay Orcs and wargs and bring trophies of your victories to his foster-brother Tárandil as a birthday present.","'I don't want anything. Really.\
\
'Actually, if you can get Vëamacil to remain silent for even five minutes, I would consider that the worthiest of birthday presents!'","'Yes? Ah, thank you for the welcome, but I must ask you not to use that name. At our uncle's request, my brothers and I have agreed to take on false names in order to hide that we are kindred with the kings. You may call me Vëamacil, and if I do not respond to it, keep trying until I do! One day I will no doubt be used to the name... and when that day comes the war will be over and there will be no further need to take these precautions!'\
\
Vëamacil laughs and nods in the direction of Ontamo, who is poorly attempting to hide his scowls.\
\
'When the siege was still young, a few years back, one of my brothers met with Ontamo. The description he conveyed of him was... not kind. \\qHe is a fawning, little man, more concerned with his own elevation than with the good of the kingdom,\\q he told us. From that day forth, it has amused me to ensure he never gets the ear of my father or my uncle. See how he stews! This siege seems endless, and jests are in short supply; we must find them where we can.\
\
'I like you, my new friend. Let us take a meal first, and then my brothers and I will conduct our inspection. Honestly, there is little need for it. If the Alliance is pushed back from its forward encampments, we will have more problems than a well-defended Díngarth could solve!\
\
'Let me know when you are ready to take a meal and sit with my brothers, friend.'","Orcs and wargs can be found throughout Arandor in Mordor Besieged.\
\
Vëamacil asked you to collect trophies from Orcs and wargs to give to Tárandil for a birthday present.","The sons of Isildur have conducted their inspection, and now Vëamacil wishes to speak with you.","Tárandil is in the primary Gondorian encampment of Adambel.","'This disrespect cannot stand. If the king chooses not to meet with me himself, well, I shall extend him the same discourtesy by not meeting with the sons he sent in his stead! You meet with them, ${CLASS}. I find myself otherwise engaged and cannot spare the time to meet with three unproven striplings, sons of the king though they be.\
\
'One of them stands yonder, do you see him? He is to the north-east, dressed in green. See what he wants, and why his father could not deign to visit us himself!'","Ontamo feels insulted by Isildur's decision to send his sons to conduct the inspection of Díngarth's defences, and has asked you to speak with them instead.","Collected trophies from Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to one of Isildur's sons at Díngarth","Talk to Vëamacil and complete 'Instance: The Sons of Isildur'","Collect trophies from Orcs in Arandor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Are you ready? Then let us find my brothers and sit for a time before we conduct the inspection. The siege has gone on for years, and it can wait for the span of one meal, can it not? At any rate, I say we will fight better with full bellies!'","'What is the meaning of this foolishness? I pray you do not encourage my sons in this behaviour, ${CLASS}, or you will risk my anger. I have taught them the importance of an even temperament and a steady hand, for my sons are of a king's lineage and a ruler has no time for jest. If you are a friend to them, and to me, you will remind them of this from time to time.\
\
'Tárandil is mine to foster, and while he is not in the line of kings, he is still dear to me. I deal with him as I deal with my sons, and it is my hope he will prove a good example to them, and guide them on their path, wherever it leads.'","Talk to Vëamacil at Díngarth","Talk to Tárandil at Díngarth","'I bid you welcome, ${CLASS}.'","'One of Isildur's sons stands yonder, do you see him? He is to the north-east, dressed in green. See what he wants, and why his father could not deign to visit us himself!'","'I don't want anything. Actually, if you can get Vëamacil to remain silent for even five minutes, I would consider that the worthiest of birthday presents!'","Chapter 11.4: The Sons of Isildur","'You should think of a birthday present to give to Tárandil, and bring it with you when you come to Adambel. Ask him what he wants!'","'Ah, he's always like this. Tárandil never wants anything. Well, I won't allow him to get away with it this time! He is my foster-brother, and he is going to have the finest of birthdays, with the very best presents. What do you think, my new friend? Give me your hand on this, and we will see it done!'\
\
Vëamacil stands up straight and gives a shout, which causes nearby soldiers to look up in alarm.\
\
'I've got it! We're going to give my foster-brother the only thing he truly wants: we're going to give him an end to the war! Let us do what we can to bring an end to this endless siege of Mordor. That will make for the very best present, will it not?\
\
'Like every good plan, this will take some doing. Go slay some Orcs and some wargs, and collect trophies from them. We can deliver them to Tárandil at the encampment of Adambel, and tell him they are just the first part of his birthday present. He will love it, friend, trust me.'"},
[2891]={"Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Sigileth is by the north-western entrance to Ghalbûru.","'I want to thank you for honouring your promise to me, ${PLAYER}. I will not say my mother wished to test your loyalty and that of your companions, but neither will I deny it! But you have proven a friend to me and an enemy of Ordâkh, and that means you are a friend to the Ambarûli.\
\
'Take care in the Khûd, friend ${PLAYER}. The Kintai are rarely seen, and it is said they abhor visitors. You should be safe with Sigileth, but keep my words in your mind. I will see you when you rejoin the company!'","Khôltekh is by the north-western entrance of Ghalbûru.","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru","Having received tidings of Balakhad's death, Khôltekh is ready to leave Khûd Zagin behind, taking most of the travelling company with him.","'¿Todo está bien?'","'The Elf woman has something to say?'","'Your farewells are made? Then let us make for the road south-east of Jirush. I understand that will bring us near to the Oasis of Shonith, where dwell a band of the Kintai.'","'This is as far as we go.'","'¿Si?'","'If Balakhâd is dead, we have no reason to delay further in Khûd Zagin. Most of the map Azagath saw fit to take from the Mâkhda Khorbo consisted of lands further to the east. Whatever Azagath and Nakási seek to find must lie somewhere east of here, deeper into Shagâna.\
\
'Hmm? What is it?'","Sigileth stands by the road south-east of Jirush in Khûd Zagin.","'You should bid farewell to the rest of the company, ${PLAYER}. When you have satisfied the Elf woman's curiosity about the Elves dwelling in Khûd Zagin, you can look for the rest of us at the city of Kûr Anzar, in Imhûlar to the east. Perhaps we will have captured Azagath and Nakási by the time you rejoin us. On this day all things seem possible!'","Sigileth planned to meet with you along the road south-east of Jirush.","Talk to Belondor in Ghalbûru","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Corudan in Ghalbûru","Sigileth is by the north-western entrance of Ghalbûru.","Chapter 11.5: Deception and Departure","'Let us make for the road south-east of Jirush. I understand that will bring us near to the Oasis of Shonith, where dwell a band of the Kintai.'","Talk to Corudan in Ghalbûru","You should <rgb=#00FF00>wave</rgb> to your departing companions, and say your farewells to them. Sirgon is by the north-western entrance to Ghalbûru.","Talk to Sirgon in Ghalbûru","Meet with Sigileth along the road south-east of Jirush, in Khûd Zagin","Talk to Sigileth by the road south-east of Jirush","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Sirgon in Ghalbûru","'I agree that most of the company should continue onward in pursuit of Azagath and Nakási, but I would ask a boon of you, Khôltekh.'\
\
The Temámir shrugs in noncommittal fashion, and Sigileth continues.\
\
'Ever since  returned from the grove of Arwáth with word of the Kinta people, I have desired to learn more about the Elves that remain apart from my own people. I understand there is an oasis here in Khûd Zagin where some of that folk remain, and I would like to meet with them.\
\
'When the company departs, I ask that  stay behind with me, and together ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} and I will go to find the Kintai of the oasis.'","You should <rgb=#00FF00>wave</rgb> to your departing companions, and say your farewells to them. Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Corudan is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Talk to Khôltekh in Ghalbûru","Sirgon and Belondor are by the north-western entrance to Ghalbûru.","Talk to Sigileth in Ghalbûru","'Sigileth told me you are staying behind when the rest of us continue eastward, ${PLAYER}. I hope the two of you find what my sister hopes to find.'\
\
Corudan holds your gaze for a moment, and then smiles.\
\
'To our next meeting, my friend! Each of us must remain on guard, of course.'","'Good-bye, ${PLAYER}. Be safe in Khûd Zagin, and avoid trouble with the Ordâkhai if you can! What am I saying? I have known both you and Sigileth the Elf for long enough now to know that the two of you are deadly enough to resolve any trouble which finds you!\
\
'Rejoin us as soon as you are able, my friend.'","'When the company departs, I ask that  stay behind with me, and together ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} and I will go to find the Kintai of the oasis.'","'Take care in the Khûd, my friend.'","Rahâzi watches you silently.","You should <rgb=#00FF00>wave</rgb> to your departing companions, and say your farewells to them. Corudan is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Sigileth nods at your approach","'That sounds like a waste of time to me... but your business is your own. If an Elf wishes to go in search of other Elves, who is Khôltekh to quash that fanciful errand? The company will travel more swiftly without the two of you.\
\
'You should bid farewell to the rest of the company, ${PLAYER}. When you have satisfied the Elf woman's curiosity about the Elves dwelling in Khûd Zagin, you can look for the rest of us at the city of Kûr Anzar, in Imhûlar to the east. Perhaps we will have captured Azagath and Nakási by the time you rejoin us. On this day all things seem possible!'","Talk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru","'To our next meeting, my friend! Each of us must remain on guard, of course.'","'Stop, ${PLAYER}. This is as far as we need go.\
\
'The Oasis of Shonith is not our destination.'","'Farewell to you, ${PLAYER}. I hope you will not remain with the Elves of the Oasis for too long, for we may have need of you and Sigileth the Elf when we catch up to Azagath and Nakási.\
\
'But Shagâna is a vast land, and the two of them might hide within any number of secret hiding-places. It may take us much searching to find them.'"},
[2892]={"Talk to Prince Ingór","Habla con Bróin","The Gabil'akkâ celebrates its victory in Gundabad.","Mótsog gazes at the western horizon","Habla con Bori","'This was a great victory for the Longbeards, and for Prince Durin! You know what that means: there will be a tremendous call for me to make statues of everyone involved, heroes in mighty pose with their weapons aloft! I will be kept busy for years, and will need to hollow out the mountain entire to have stone enough! Perhaps I should accelerate the training of my apprentice after all....\
\
'But one thing still confuses me, ${PLAYER}. I am perplexed by the identity of the mysterious dwarf you accompanied to the peak. Do you know who he was?'\
\
You stare at Stáli in disbelief, for surely the sculptor has spent hours working on mosaics depicting the likeness of Mótsog.\
\
'You don't know either, I suppose,' Stáli continues. 'He did seem a regal and powerful figure. I wonder if he knows anything about the Zabad'ibîn?'","The dwarves have achieved victory in Gundabad, and the Gabil'akkâ celebrates on the mountainside.","Talk to Stáli the Hewer","'Are all such Dwarrowmoots so eventful, ${PLAYER}? You should have told me you planned to invite Hrímil Frost-heart and her armies!\
\
'But the day belongs to us, and the Dragon has escaped to nurse her wounds. If Durin and the Zhélruka prince know what they are doing they will dispatch courageous warriors to put an end to the threat of her, and fast! Still, this is a great victory, and I intend to celebrate it. I advise you do the same!'","Mótsog gazes toward the western horizon.","Chapter 11.5: Gundabad Is Ours!","Talk to Imák","'You should have seen it, ${PLAYER}! The Orcs pressed in around us and I thought for sure it was the end. But then Fastrith and Bróin came rushing by, and they swung their axes so swiftly and in such concert they seemed to be one dwarf and not two! I have never seen anything like it!\
\
'Their battle-dance was really something. You don't suppose Fastrith has a sister she hasn't mentioned? I never cared much for wooing before, but the sight of their spirited scuffle has made me want to find a deadly dwarf-woman with which to share such joyful combat, and let our enemies beware!\
\
'You let me know if you find one, ${PLAYER}, and I shall tidy my beard and sharpen my axe-blade, the better to impress her!'","'My day is nearly up, friend of my friend. The sun is setting.\
\
'I will rest well with the knowledge that Durin is once again at home in Gundabad, as he should have been. And when he is king, he will lead all the dwarves into a new age of peace and prosperity, as was always his desire.'\
\
Mótsog stands quietly for a moment. When next he speaks, his voice is low, as if he addresses someone you cannot see.\
\
'In all the long years of my sleep, through which I watched all the trials of the dwarves, I have seen the end of countless days. But I have never seen a sunset so beautiful as this.'\
\
Lost in his thoughts, he has forgotten you stand near. You decide to leave him in peace.","'We have the victory, ${PLAYER}! Gundabad is ours.'\
\
Bósi nods with satisfaction despite his own injury.\
\
'Brogur would be pleased at our success, but if I know my cousin he would be disappointed that he missed all the fighting. And yet, his son Bróin fought well when the Dwarrowmoot was interrupted, so perhaps fatherly pride would prove a balm for Brogur's heart.'\
\
Bósi peers at you closely.\
\
'Do you know something, my friend? During the battle, while you made your way to the peak, I thought I saw my cousin fighting alongside you. It must have been only a trick of the light, but for a moment I would have sworn it was Brogur. Well, it is a day for battle-shouts and tales of glory, and those were always my cousin's favourite days. Perhaps he could not resist one more.'","Talk to Fastrith","'We have done it, ${PLAYER}! Prince Durin has achieved what he swore to do, and the Mountain-home has been reclaimed!\
\
'Aye, there remains a dragon to manage, but I saw her flight as she flew away, wounded, and I deem more than her pride was injured here. And without Gorgar to command, her grip over Orc-kind will surely be loosened.\
\
'Enjoy the victory, but prepare for the next! It is a Longbeard saying, but all of the Gabil'akkâ would do well to keep it in mind!'","Durin is up the slope to the east, celebrating the victory of the dwarves.","Find Mótsog down the slope to the west","'When first I came to Elderslade, I asked you to keep a secret for me, ${PLAYER}. Do you remember? I feared I did not have the courage to fight another war like the one that claimed my father Brogur's life, in dark Khazad-dûm. And I did not. When the Dragon appeared above the Dwarrowmoot, it was as if I was back in the depths of that drowned treasury, scared and alone, but this time there was no Zigilburk near at hand, no hope of survival. I despaired, ${PLAYER}, and I thought to run.'\
\
Bróin stares at his feet. When he looks up at you again, a fire blazes in his eyes.\
\
'But then I saw Fastrith standing near, and a great courage rushed through me, a courage I never thought I could have again. I raised my axe, and without a word the two of us set upon the approaching Orcs, and our battle-dance was like nothing I had ever experienced. I would not have thought it possible! But so it was, and now Gundabad is ours!'","Talk to Venko","Talk to Durin high above Gundabad","Talk to Mótsog high above Gundabad","Habla con Glóin","Mótsog has stepped away, unnoticed, from the celebrating throng.","'I must thank you again, my friend, for all your help. We could not have retaken the Mountain-home without you!'","'When we set out for the Wells of Langflood from Skarháld, did you think this is where our journey would lead? I tell you now that I did, for the Zhélruka are noted optimists!'\
\
Venko laughs long and loudly.\
\
'Perhaps not, my friend. But both Durin and Prince Ingór have reached an understanding, and their agreement should end years of tension and conflict. A place will be made for my people in Gundabad, and we will work together with the Longbeards to defend it from any who would seek to take it from us, whether they be Orc or Dragon or any other fearsome foe!\
\
'I will yet have a hearth above which to hang my brothers' swords, and I know both Lékhun and Dúsek would be pleased.'","'Hrímil Frost-heart is wounded, and we will need to deal with her, but for now let us enjoy the victory!\
\
'What say my dwarves? What say my courageous allies?\
\
'Let all take up the cheer: Gundabad is ours!'","'It is done, ${PLAYER}. Durin has agreed that the Zhélruka will have a place in Gundabad, and I am satisfied. Let the old rivalries wash away in the torrent of our shared hardships, and let new bonds be forged by the blood we spilled together.\
\
'There will still be work to do to make a home for my people in Gundabad, but I welcome it. If you help us the work will be easier! What say you to this, ${PLAYER}? Good, good. The Zhélruka welcome your assistance!'","Mótsog stands on the slope, watching the setting sun.","Habla con Bósi.","'You made it, ${PLAYER}! We did not have a good view of the peak, so I could not tell exactly what befell you once you departed up the slope, but Bróin assured me that you knew what you were doing.\
\
'As for us, it turns out that Bróin and I complement each other in battle fairly well! I knew what his axe would do even before he did, and he knew the same for mine! I would prefer not to boast, but I daresay the Orcs will not choose to tangle with the two of us for some time! And if they do: beware!\
\
'Once my master Stáli begins to teach me the art of sculpting, I should like to immortalize this battle in stone! Picture this, ${PLAYER}: me and dear Bróin back to back, axes at the ready, while a whirlwind of Orcs and hobgoblins encircle us. Our foes are carved from a single sweep of the rock, with no telling where one enemy ends and another begins! And for a name? Hmmm... perhaps I will call it \\qThe Courtship!'\
\
Fastrith blushes suddenly.\
\
'Well, perhaps. We will see! Names are very difficult, aren't they?'"},
[2893]={"'Even my grandsire should not neglect his own weapon, should he? If we need sharpen our blades every morn, I say that even High King Elendil should benefit from his son's advice. Bring a whetstone and my father's warning to my grandsire King Elendil, friend. You will find him somewhere around Adambel, I warrant, and spare not the lecture!'","'Alas! It is with the benefit of looking back that I know now what I did not know then. Sauron did not hide from us out of fear, and he did not think to outlast us with time alone. Nay, it was with purpose that he waited in Barad-dûr, biding his time. He knew what we did not: the Ghâzab Bôron had won a decisive battle against the armies that had gone to face it. Even now, the Storm of Wrath moved in the direction of Mordor, chasing the defeated Thíuda and Longbeards before it.\
\
'Sauron needed do nothing but wait for the Rhúnhoth hordes to arrive, and wait he did, secure in his tower and confident his victory would arrive with the Storm. We knew not what approached, and we let the long years of the siege lull us into complacency. We would learn our mistake before long, but that is further ahead in my tale.'","Delivered a whetstone and a warning (${CURRENT}/6)","'It is the command of the High King? Let us begin, and without delay!'","'Forgive the interruption. I return now to my tale.'","'My blade is as sharp as it was both yesterday, last week, and a month past, but all the same I will not spurn the gift. I do not call for the servants of Sauron to attack, but neither do I enjoy the tedium of this endless calm. I will spend some of today sharpening my sword. Pointless shall be neither the exercise nor the blade, my new friend!'","Vëamacil is at Adambel.\
\
Now that you have trained with the soldiers, High King Elendil expects you to convey his reprimand to his grandson Vëamacil.","'He has a sword. Why not give him a whetstone and remind him that we are at war?'","A crate of whetstones can be found by the camp-fires to the north in Adambel, the primary Gondorian encampment in Mordor Besieged.","King Isildur of Gondor is at the encampment of Adambel.","Deliver whetstones to idle soldiers and the sons of Isildur (5/6)","'Thank you for the whetstone and for father's warning, though I really needed neither. Every day seems much like the one before, and the Orcs have not dared tangle with our warriors for some time!\
\
'Still, there may be some wisdom in it. Aye, I think it may be worthwhile to ensure that everyone who bears a weapon has what he needs to keep it in pristine shape. Yes, my friend, everyone, from the lowest soldier to the very highest!\
\
'Indeed, even my grandsire should not neglect his own weapon. If we need sharpen our blades every morn, I say that even High King Elendil should benefit from his son's advice. Bring a whetstone and my father's warning to my grandsire King Elendil, friend. You will find him somewhere around Adambel, I warrant, and spare not the lecture!'","Collected the crate of whetstones","'Find some soldiers with which to train as a reminder not to let down their guard. Afterwards, convey the words I spoke to my grandson, as well as my displeasure. He has the blood of kings, and should act such.'","'It was only a bit of fun, my friend. Do not let my grandfather's words sour your day. But look! Did you not say you met this Elf earlier, among the corpses of our enemies and his? He has come now to Adambel on some errand, and will be pleased to speak with you.\
\
'Give him a whetstone!'","Magoldir is at Adambel, the primary Gondorian encampment in Mordor Besieged.","Elendil stares at you sternly","Engaged in a spirited bout of training at Adambel (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'I am ready for you! Hold nothing back, for I will not either!'","'Hello again. I will take one of these whetstones, and gladly, for my own sword could use the sharpening. Let it not be said that I took poor care of Orthadel, the Rising Star, for in return he might take poor care of me!\
\
'Elf-soldiers, like those of other races, must keep their weapons and their wits as sharp as they can. That has always been my experience, and I wonder if it has been yours?'","'My muscles ache already, but if this is the High King's command I will not cry off. Let us begin!'","King Isildur of Gondor worries that his sons have allowed the length of the siege to dull their wits and their weapons, and wants them each made sharp again.","'It must have taken no small measure of courage to lecture my father thus. Or foolishness!'","Magoldir nods at you pleasantly","High King Elendil has commanded that you train with soldiers at the encampment of Adambel and remind them not to relax their guard despite the length of the siege.","'Find a crate of whetstones somewhere here at Adambel and deliver its contents to idle soldiers throughout the encampment. Remind them of the need for weapons clean and sharp, and see that they heed my warning! Do not forget to give whetstones to my sons, as well; they may need the reminder most of all. False names will only protect them for so long.'","'I would not need three guesses to know which of my grandsons sent you to me thus, ${CLASS}. He has spent too long in idleness, and forgotten the danger. The tedium of the hours is a dangerous foe for an army at rest, but a forgotten enemy long-accepted is even more of a threat!\
\
'I will take this whetstone, and thank you for it, but know this: my blade Narsil needs sharpening but rarely, and I am not lax with its keeping. Let my grandson take these words to heart: a soldier needs sharpening just as a weapon does, and if one is neglected neither can carry out its work. He should treat the business of war more seriously, and leave the jesting for tavern-keepers and stable-boys.\
\
'Find some soldiers with which to train, as a reminder not to let down their guard. Afterwards, convey the words I spoke to my grandson, as well as my displeasure. He has the blood of kings, and should act such.'","Idle soldiers can be found throughout Adambel.\
\
Isildur asked you to deliver whetstones to idle soldiers of the Alliance, as well as to his sons.","Train with soldiers at Adambel (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The shade of Isildur has interrupted the telling of his tale with a brief aside.","'It has been some time since Sauron sent his Orcs against us, but they may return at any moment. We must be ready, with sharp blades and sturdy armour prepared to turn aside their attacks. Find a crate of whetstones somewhere here at Adambel, by the camp-fires to the north, and deliver its contents to idle soldiers throughout the encampment. Remind them of the need for weapons clean and sharp, and see that they heed my warning! Do not forget to give whetstones to my sons, as well; they may need the reminder most of all. False names will only protect them for so long, and in the end they must rely upon their weapons. That is the way of war.\
\
'I must now attend my brother Anárion, but I will leave you with these tasks and my thanks for their successful completion.'","Talk to Isildur at Adambel","Chapter 11.5: The Storm in the East","Give Magoldir a whetstone at Adambel","Delivered a whetstone and a warning (5/6)","Talk to the shade of Isildur at Adambel","'Ah, I cannot blame them for relaxing their guard. When first we pushed through the ruins of the Black Gate with the vanguard, it seemed victory was near, and Sauron must surely abandon the fight. Yet it was not so. He hid within his tower, sealing the door against us, and he has not been seen again. Days turned to weeks, weeks turned to months, and then at last we measured the time in years. The siege seems without end. Sauron is trapped in his tower, and though his servants test us from time to time, the Dark Lord seems content to outlast us, or at least to make the attempt. I would rather he face us in battle, and put an end to this endless waiting!\
\
'Is it any wonder that the idleness causes my sons to chafe, sharpening their tongues and not their weapons? It is difficult to remain alert when combat with the enemy is merely a memory; our swords untested, our shields unbattered. Perhaps Sauron makes us wait in the hope that we will grow tired and abandon the cause. If that be so, he is more fool than we thought! We will wait as long as is necessary!'","Deliver a whetstone and a warning to High King Elendil at Adambel","High King Elendil can be found somewhere within Adambel, the primary Gondorian encampment in Mordor Besieged.","Find a crate of whetstones in Adambel","Deliver whetstones to idle soldiers and the sons of Isildur (${CURRENT}/6)","Talk to Vëamacil at Adambel","'Thank you, friend. I will make use of this whetstone, and take heed of the warning, as well.'"},
[2894]={"Defeat foes of the Great Alliance in Parth Daenath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Glorfindel at Echad-in-Edhil","Talk to Magoldir on the northern slope of Amon Amarth","Find the location east of Adambel that Magoldir wishes to scout","Magoldir wishes to report to Glorfindel of the Bright Company at the encampment of Echad-in-Edhil, north-west of Adambel in Mordor Besieged.","Magoldir surveys the surrounding terrain from the slope of Amon Amarth","'We have arrived. Are you ready to go with me to deliver my report? I do wish we had something of substance to tell Glorfindel, but no scout can decide what it is he finds.\
\
'Let me know when you are ready to meet with the leader of the Bright Company.'","'Now let us see what we might spy from the height.'\
\
Magoldir peers into the distance, looking west, north, and east from the slope of Amon Amarth.\
\
'I do not know if this information will aid the Bright Company after all, for all is quiet, and there is little movement upon the plain. Is there some fell reason for this calm, or does Sauron tire of his war as we do? I do not like this uncertainty, friend. See you there the great fortress across the plain? That is Amon Fuin, the Gloom-hill, and it is a den of evil. I do not like it, but I tell you true that I like the quiet of Parth Daenath even less, if that were possible!\
\
'If you are willing, I would ask you to come with me to Echad-in-Edhil, where we can report of this to Glorfindel. It may be he will know what to make of this unpleasant stillness.'","Glorfindel, leader of the Bright Company, is waiting to speak with you in the Elf-camp of Echad-in-Edhil.","'It is no accident that brought me hither, friend. No indeed! I came here seeking you, for I have been given an errand for which you might be well-suited. These two eyes have the keen sight of my people, but the eyes of one such as you might pick up something I miss, and your skills turn aside the danger of whatever we find!\
\
'I was sent to scout the southern reaches at the behest of Glorfindel, leader of the Glánnothrim, the Bright Company. They have devoted themselves to combating the evils of old that linger still in Middle-earth. Oh, do not mistake me! I do not belong to that esteemed group, but I tell you true: if an Elf of the Bright Company asks you to do something, only a fool or a coward would refuse, and I deem myself neither. It is my belief that Glorfindel plans their next step, and the information I return to him could prove crucial! Will you aid me in this?'\
\
Magoldir smiles and raises Orthadel in salute.\
\
'It shall be a fine hunt, my friend. Let us patrol to the east of this encampment, skirting the northern face of Amon Amarth, and slay whatever foes mischance to cross our path. There is a location I would have us scout, and once I am satisfied we have not missed anything, I will make my report to Glorfindel.'","Chapter 11.6: Tales of the Bright Company","Talk to Magoldir and complete 'Instance: Tales of the Bright Company'","Defeated foes of the Great Alliance (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I welcome any assistance you can provide, ${CLASS}, not just to the Bright Company but to the Great Alliance as well. We must not let Sauron's inaction lull us to sleep. Indeed, let us renew our attention and maintain our guard, and perhaps we will catch unawares the Dark Lord himself!\
\
'His is a singular evil, for every command comes from Barad-dûr: when to attack, when to retreat, and when to mask his intention. Against this stands our Alliance, and its strength comes from the unity of our separate peoples. It is Gil-galad's belief that Sauron will try to sever those bonds, and in so doing he will reveal our greatest weakness, and strike at our vulnerability.\
\
'But instead he has pulled back his hand, abandoning all pretense of engaging us in serious combat. It puzzles me that the Dark Lord has drawn his forces back in this fashion. What is he planning?'","'This way, my friend. May Glorfindel know what to make of this unpleasant stillness.'","Magoldir stands at the entrance of Echad-in-Edhil, waiting for your readiness to report to Glorfindel, leader of the Bright Company.","Magoldir has come to Adambel on behalf of the Bright Company, and seeks your help.","Find the entrance to Echad-in-Edhil","'It was the primary encampment of the Elves in Mordor for the long years of siege.'","Talk to Magoldir at the entrance to Echad-in-Edhil","Magoldir desires to scout a location to the east of Adambel for Glorfindel of the Bright Company.","'Let us patrol to the east of this encampment, skirting the northern face of Amon Amarth, and slay whatever foes mischance to cross our path. There is a location I would have us scout, and once I am satisfied we have not missed anything, I will make my report to Glorfindel.'"},
[2896]={"'You say you bring a message from King Anárion? Deliver it, friend, for I am his to command!'\
\
You tell Martore that Anárion believes Sauron nears the end of his resolve, and a renewed assault on the part of the Great Alliance may bring an end to the war.\
\
'It is my heart's wish that the king guesses aright, but this is not the first day I have heard this hope given voice. I think it more likely that Sauron prepares some new weapon to unleash upon us. Still, I will not abandon my duty. I will fight on!\
\
'For Anárion and for Isildur! For Gondor!'","'It is a mystery to me, and to Gil-galad, and to Lendelen my closest advisor. Rare is the puzzle we three cannot solve, ${CLASS}, and that by itself is worrisome.\
\
'Magoldir is not the only scout who has reported stillness on the plateau of Gorgoroth. I possess a number of such reports now, and each tells a similar tale: fewer enemy patrols than before, and a reduction in the number of foes assaulting the encampments of Men or Elves. I will inform Gil-galad of these reports, but I ask that you bring word to the leaders of Gondor. I understand Elendil is in council, and I would not have him disturbed, but if you bring these reports to one of his sons they will deliver word to him when he is free.\
\
'Seek out Isildur or Anárion at Adambel. I am troubled by these reports, but cannot say precisely why. Perhaps the sons of Elendil can pinpoint the reason behind my worry, and speak such words as will abate it.'","'Let us go to Díngarth at once to meet with Vëamacil, and you will hear what he told me. It may be that together we can solve this mystery, and if we act quickly we may save some lives as well!'","Anárion asked you to bring his message to soldiers in the field east of Adambel, nearer to the Dark Tower. He also charged you with defeating servants of Sauron and the beasts that stalk among the crags of Mordor.","Vëamacil is at Díngarth.\
\
Tárandil told you that his brothers may have found some clue to the mystery of the missing soldiers.","'Welcome back, my friend! I trust Tárandil told you we might be near to solving the mystery of our vanished soldiers? It is true. How can I say these were no mere deserters?'\
\
Vëamacil raises an eyebrow, barely able to mask a grin.\
\
'We have an onlooker, ${CLASS}, someone who could spy upon the latest disappearance without being seen. Someone who was beneath notice: one of the Hól-budlan. She saw everything.'","Anárion has been summoned to an urgent council and is unavailable. Isildur's foster-son Tárandil has called you over and wishes to speak with you.","Talk to Tárandil at Adambel","'Blame not my brother for his eagerness. All of us, to a man, desired an end to the war.'","'There are soldiers in the field of battle east of Adambel, nearer to the Dark Tower. Find them and relay to them this message: \\qSauron nears the end of his resolve, and a renewed assault may break the morale of his defenders!\\q I ask also that you slay whatever servants of Sauron and vile beasts you find on your way. Let every success sing the tale of the victory that surely approaches! It will not be long now, friend!'","Defeat beasts and servants of Sauron in Mordor Besieged (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You came too late to deliver Anárion's hopeful message, for Astondor has been slain.","'Yes? How came a ${RACE} of Gondor to be in possession of reports from Glorfindel of the Elves? Have you not your own duties to perform, your own captain to follow?'\
\
Anárion's stern visage suddenly melts away, and his expression becomes merry.\
\
'Nay, friend, I mean rather that you might serve as an example to some who might forget: only together can we defeat the will of Sauron. I see frustration in the faces of my men; how could I not, after seven years of siege? But your coming today is a reminder that, unlike Sauron, we are not alone. We stand together against him: Men, Elves, dwarves. Aye, all the peoples of Middle-earth have joined hands to oppose his evil. This endless waiting cannot last, no matter how certain it seems it must. Tell me, ${CLASS}, what word you bring from Glorfindel of the Elves.'\
\
You relay the reports of Glorfindel's scouts, and Anárion listens to your words with increasing excitement.\
\
'I too have noticed fewer attacks of late, but I thought little of it. Now I wonder. Can it be that Sauron's resolve has been tested by the long years of siege? His allies are not allies at all, but servants only! His domination of their spirit can be no substitute for the bonds of friendship formed in battle, like those we formed with the Elves and the others of our Alliance. I draw hope from these reports, and see in them a sign that our victory must soon be at hand!\
\
'There are soldiers in the field of battle east of Adambel, nearer to the Dark Tower. Find them and relay to them this message: \\qSauron nears the end of his resolve, and a renewed assault may break the morale of his defenders!\\q I ask also that you slay whatever servants of Sauron and vile beasts you find on your way. Let every success sing the tale of the victory that surely approaches! It will not be long now, friend!'","'My foster-father and King Anárion have been summoned to an urgent council, and they would not tell me the reason. It may be nothing, or it may not. But that is not the matter that brought me here. I came here to find you, and bring you back with me!\
\
'Do you remember what my brothers and I discussed with you when we met at Díngarth? A curious number of soldiers had vanished from their posts in recent weeks, not simply while on patrol but also from within the safety of our own encampments. Deserters, Ornaher thought, but the rest of us were not so sure. Well, now we have discovered evidence that these vanished soldiers might not have succumbed to cowardice at all!\
\
'Let us go to Díngarth at once to meet with Vëamacil, and you will hear what he told me. It may be that together we can solve this mystery, and if we act quickly we may save some lives as well!'","Bring Anárion's message to Tumbomehtar","'What message brings you to this blasted plain, friend? Good tidings or ill?'\
\
You tell Tumbomehtar that Anárion believes the war may soon be ended if the soldiers of the Alliance remain steadfast. He grimaces.\
\
'So neither good nor ill, then, for I hear nothing new in the king's words. He has my love and my respect, for my loyalty is to both of Elendil's sons and the kingdom they made on these shores, but I have seen no sign the end of the siege is any nearer now than it was these past few years. King Anárion is a good man, but I see in him the desire of all soldiers to welcome the onset of peace at the slimmest of portents. It fell to him to defend the borders of Gondor while his brother travelled north to gather the Great Alliance; Anárion has been fighting this war longer than many of us, and he must feel the weariness of it as keenly as any soldier of Gondor.\
\
'I hope he is right that it will soon be ended, but I will lay no wager upon it.'","Return to Anárion at Adambel","'Seek out Isildur or Anárion at Adambel. I am troubled by these reports, but cannot say precisely why. Perhaps the sons of Elendil can pinpoint the reason behind my worry, and speak such words as will abate it.'","Bring Anárion's message to Martore","'My brother Anárion and I had been called away, summoned to an urgent council.'","Glorfindel of the Bright Company has collected a number of scouting reports from his Elves in the field, and wishes for you to investigate what they might signify.","'Even were the war to end tomorrow, it would not matter to the dead.'","Bring Anárion's message to Astondor","Chapter 11.7: Anárion's Guess","Talk to Vëamacil at Díngarth","Defeated beasts and Sauron's servants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have done as Anárion asked, and should return to him at Adambel.","Bring the scouting reports to either Isildur or Anárion at Adambel","Glorfindel asked you to deliver the scouting reports to either Isildur or Anárion at the Gondorian encampment of Adambel."},
[2897]={"Talk to Sigileth at Shonith","Collect sand-sifter meat in Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Thank you for helping provide some meat and feathers for us, friends. Each of them will sustain the Kintai who tend the grove here in their own way: the meat for food, and the feathers as fletching for our arrows.\
\
'Sometimes we lose sight of the need for such tasks as these, with our eyes always upon the importance of our overall charge.'","'Now you see the difficulty of our charge, friends. The Kintai fight to preserve what we can among the wastes, even as the circle of our influence grows ever smaller; even the greenery that used to thrive now withers and dies, and the desert creeps ever closer. Much of this land was covered with a great forest in ages past, the Emerald Wood of Nisigím. The very oldest of my people cursed the name of the Great Enemy, Morgoth, whose servants hewed the trees and devastated the land, turning large tracts of the Emerald Wood into desert.\
\
'But that was long ago, and those elders of my people faded even before my birth. The work of the Kintai helped to restore some measure of the Emerald Wood, coaxing life from the barren stones and ensuring it could live before they moved on. The Kintai became a wandering people, moving from place to place, tending to the groves throughout Shagâna, but still they named the Emerald Wood of Nisigím their home.\
\
'Stories of Nisigím's beauty seem now an impossible dream. When the Empire of Ordâkh dried the rivers and came north, their invasion parched the land and caused a great drought that withered cropland and forest alike. A terrible blight befell the trees of Nisigím, turning them as hard as stone. The forest has now become Adagím, the Corpseholt, and we of the Kintai now name ourselves Avabár-kintai, the Elves Without A Home.\
\
'That has not changed our mission, friends, but like others who dwell in these lands we accept whatever help may be offered. If you will bring us sand-sifter meat and bird feathers from the creatures of Khûd Zagin, you will help the Kintai with their efforts. There is a coffer among the pavilions north of the water in which you may leave the items you gather for us.'","Sigileth is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.","Tharashil is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.","Collected chunks of sand-sifter meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Chapter 11.7: The Oasis at Shonith","Sigileth has sought out the leader of the Kintai who dwell at Shonith","Sigileth is on the leader's rise in the south-western reaches of Shonith.","'Tharashil is the leader of the Kintai who dwell here at the Oasis of Shonith and tend its grove. She has welcomed the two of us here, so long as we disturb not her people.'","Talk to Tharashil at Shonith","'Sometimes we lose sight of the need for such tasks as these, with our eyes always upon the importance of our overall charge.'","Talk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith","Meet up with Sigileth far to the south-east at the Oasis of Shonith","Walk closer to the edge of the overlook and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over Shonith","Tharashil asked you to leave the meat and feathers you collected in the coffer north of the water in Shonith.","'I ask that you walk north, closer to the edge of this rise, and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over Shonith. Perhaps then you will know why we of the Kintai feel so strongly about this work to which we are called.'","'This is Tharashil, ${PLAYER}, and she is the leader of the Kintai who dwell here at the Oasis of Shonith and tend its grove. She has welcomed the two of us here, so long as we disturb not her people.\
\
'I told her you met with Shanthar, warden of a grove in northern Ambarûl, and she is interested to hear how he fares.'","'The trail has gone cold, for now. If our quarry sought to avoid further encounter with the Ordâkhai, they may have ventured far to the south of Jirush, which might bring them within view of the Kintai. We should seek out the Elves said to live beside the desert sands.\
\
'No, my desire to meet with the Elves of the Oasis was not just a pretense, and it was not only in service of our deception. I do wish to speak with the Kintai, and even if they have not seen our prey, should Khôltekh ask questions of our stay in Khûd Zagin it will be good to have answers.\
\
'Let us continue on to Shonith before we rejoin the company at Kûr Anzar.'","Collect bird feathers in Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Like others who dwell in these lands we accept whatever help may be offered. If you will bring us sand-sifter meat and bird feathers from the creatures of Khûd Zagin, you will help the Kintai with their efforts. There is a coffer among the pavilions north of the water in which you may leave the items you gather for us.'","Collected bird feathers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sand-sifters and birds can be found throughout the desert regions of Khûd Zagin.","Shonith is green and thriving, in stark contrast to the desert beyond the encircling rocks","'Let us continue on to Shonith before we rejoin the company at Kûr Anzar.'","'I have something to ask of Tharashil, but I fear it may be considered impolite.'","Shonith is an oasis far away in south-eastern Khûd Zagin.","'I am called Tharashil, and it is true that I lead the Adúrhid clan of the Kintai. There were many more of us in years past, but now we move from grove to grove, seeking to forestall the encroaching decay and death that threatens them all. With our ministrations here I hope to maintain Shonith against the spread of the Dust Sea that we of the Kintai name Lithashár.\
\
'It is good to hear that Shanthar remains at the grove he tends, for he was a dear friend to me in years now gone, before the Ordâkhai dried the river and spoiled the lands hereabout.\
\
'To understand our people, as your Eldar friend claims to desire, you must understand our work. I ask that you walk north, closer to the edge of this rise, and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over Shonith. Perhaps then you will know why we of the Kintai feel so strongly about this work to which we are called.'","Leave the meat and feathers in the coffer north of the water in Shonith","Talk to Sigileth in south-western Shonith","Although your investigation at Nirgambâr did not find what Sigileth expected, she believes you should continue on to Shonith as you told your travelling companions you intended.","'This is a place of beauty.'","You leave the sand-sifter meat and bird feathers in the coffer","Tharashil asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over Shonith and consider the work of the Kintai."},
[2898]={"Wait for Aitárshun to turn his attention to you","The Kinta Elf Aitárshun sways slightly within the bole of his red-leafed Sarlásh","'Be not afraid, friends. The process is a natural one.'\
\
Aitárshun breathes deeply, seemingly unconcerned with the tree-limbs that surround him. You tell him that Tharashil wanted him to tell you about something called a Veróth.\
\
'This is mine, my friend. You might call a Veróth a tree-tomb. My people weave the red-leaved Sarlásh trees around the body of a Kinta who has begun to fade, and from then on the two grow together. When the Kinta has at last become dust, the Veróth remembers the shape of the body and serves as a memorial to the faded one. The ritual preparation of the Veróth binds the Kinta to the grove in which it grows, and his spirit can then watch over the place he so loved.'\
\
Concerned, you ask Aitárshun if you have hindered his process of fading with your questions. He smiles.\
\
'Trouble yourselves not, my friends. I am not afraid to fade, as some among my kind may be, but I find myself appreciating even short conversations as this as my time approaches. They become less frequent as every day passes.'","Tharashil falls silent and gathers her thoughts","'Who are you? What are you doing here? This is not a place of safety.'\
\
You introduce yourself and tell her that Tharashil asked for you to speak with Aitárshun and Silirtas to learn more about their people. Silirtas stares at you coldly.\
\
'Tharashil is well-meaning, but she is also misguided. She thinks to hasten the process, but I know such a thing cannot be sped along without cost. Aitárshun spoke to you of the fading of the Kintai, I assume? He welcomes it. He eagerly awaits the loss of his awareness, the onset of the Tróthul trance, the cold embrace of the Sarláshi to grow around him, the prison of his Veróth. I know it is expected of me to do the same, but I cannot. I am frightened of these things.\
\
'Know you why I come so often to Er-atûr? It is because when a Kinta resists fading, and is instead slain in battle, their spirit is loosed upon the world. They become wandering, restless spirits, increasingly wrathful and hostile. I come here to see what awaits me if I do not fade, seeking to convince myself to undergo the process. I have not yet succeeded.'","Tharashil is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.","Talk to Silirtas at Er-atûr","'Did Aitárshun speak to you?'\
\
You tell Tharashil that he did, and that he seems very content to fade in the manner of his people. Tharashil sighs.\
\
'Aitárshun and I have given you an incomplete picture of the Kintai, friends, and for that I apologize. It is only right that I remedy that oversight. If you would learn more of my people, you should seek out Silirtas. At this time of day she is often to be found at Er-atûr, where many wrathful spirits linger. Er-atûr is to the north-west of Shonith.'","'Your friend's question is not impolite. The ways of the Kintai may seem unusual to others, as the ways of the Eldar seem to us.'\
\
Tharashil rests a finger upon her cheek, considering how best to explain this practice of her people.\
\
'My people awoke as did other Elves, but we did not follow Taknûn the Hunter when he led the others on the long road west. The Kintai chose to stay in these lands, for they were filled with natural beauty and Taknûn's destination seemed unknown and frightening to us; we were unwilling to follow him there, and for that the Eldar gave us an insulting name. I will not speak it here. Instead, the Kintai name ourselves Tárthai: Those Who Remained.\
\
'We dwelt in the Emerald Wood of Nisigím, as I have told you, and despite the harm caused there by Morgoth's servants and finished more recently by the Empire of Ordâkh, we never felt the Eldar's desire to travel the westward road. That place your friend names Valinor is not open to us, and we want it not.'","Talk to Tharashil at Shonith","Aitárshun is on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith.","Talk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith","Er-atûr is to the north-west of Shonith.","'If you would learn more of my people, you should seek out Silirtas. At this time of day she is often to be found at Er-atûr, where many wrathful spirits linger. Er-atûr is to the north-west of Shonith.'","At last Aitárshun speaks to you","You and Sigileth have found Silirtas, the Kinta of whom Tharashil spoke","Tharashil wants you to learn about her people, the Kintai of Ikorbân.","You introduce yourself to Aitárshun and await his response.","The attention of Aitárshun has moved away from you, and it may be some time before it returns.","Tharashil has much to tell you about her people, the Kintai.","'Because my people are not drawn to Valinor, the eldest among them were very old during the later years of the Second Age. Their weariness of the world was so great that some of these Kintai began to \\qfade,\\q falling into trances while their bodies passed away to dust. This was not the end, though their material bodies were gone: their spirits were free to wander as wraiths, which we of the Kintai name Väiri.\
\
'Some of the Väiri wander invisibly throughout the lands in which they once walked, whispering on the wind but unable to make clear their wishes. Others who feel a strong bond with a particular location have been known to become guardians of the oases and groves throughout Shagâna. If a Kinta feels such a strong connexion during their lifetime, he or she may prepare to undergo the fading process at one of these beloved locations. The trance-like state of Tróthul that precedes fading may take only a short time, or it may take much longer; some of the Kintai you see here at Shonith have been preparing themselves to fade for years.\
\
'When one of the Kintai finally enters Tróthul at one of our groves, it is our custom to fashon a Veróth around them. The Veróthi may be difficult for you to understand. Perhaps you would like to speak to Aitárshun about this aspect of the fading process? He will appreciate the company. Look for him on the easternmost island in the water. You may reach it by use of the bridges.'","Meet with Aitárshun on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith","'When one of the Kintai finally enters Tróthul at one of our groves, it is our custom to fashon a Veróth around them. The Veróthi may be difficult for you to understand. Perhaps you would like to speak to Aitárshun about this aspect of the fading process? He will appreciate the company. Look for him on the easternmost island in the water. You may reach it by use of the bridges.'","Silirtas is at Er-atûr, north-west of Shonith.","'This must be Silirtas, the Kinta of whom Tharashil spoke.'","Talk to Sigileth at Er-atûr","'I have seen a number of Elves sitting or standing at various locations around the grove, their eyes open but unaware of their surroundings. Is this a manner of restful sleep among the Kintai?'","Find Silirtas at Er-atûr, north-west of Shonith","Aitárshun is on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith, reachable by the bridges.","Sigileth is at Er-atûr, north-west of Shonith.","Talk to Aitárshun in Shonith","Chapter 11.8: The Fading of the Kintai"},
[2899]={"Isildur's son Vëamacil can be found at Díngarth.","'Keep this in confidence, and tell Tárandil none of this. But return to Vëamacil with Tûka's wisdom, and my own. We must rescue these soldiers of Gondor, but if the Mordorrim are involved, we should not involve my foster-brother in this adventure.'","Talk to Tûka, leader of the Hól-budlan, on the outskirts of Díngarth","Tûka, matriarch of the Hól-budlan, has made a discovery concerning the missing soldiers, and the sons of Isildur want your help to track down a solution to the mystery.","Talk to Vëamacil at Díngarth","'Find Tûka in Díngarth and hear her story complete!'","'I have told you what I know. But Amon Fuin is well-defended, and even the sons of Isildur should beware of that place!'","'You are friend to the sons of Isildur? I will tell you what I told them, and may the information be of some use to you!\
\
'My people are often underestimated by the Big Folk, and for that reason we can go where they might not, and remain below the notice of unobservant eyes. It is a useful skill, and one we have put to use in the fight against Sauron and his armies. Let no one say the Hól-budlan have not lived up to their word, or carried their share of the war's burden!\
\
'I was walking in the night air, looking forward to the comfort of sleep, when I heard the voice of a man of Gondor. His words were low and indistinct; it took me some time to find the speaker. He was stretched out upon his bedroll, like many other soldiers sleeping nearby, but unlike these others he muttered in his sleep. He sat up all of a sudden, giving me quite a fright, and I greeted him but he saw me not.\
\
'Judging from his speech, he thought he heard a woman's voice he recognized: that of a sweetheart from home, seemingly. He walked out of the camp, stepping over the bodies of his sleeping fellows. By now my curiosity was well and truly wakened, and I followed him at a safe distance. Outside the camp, far from the guards or the light of the torches, he was attacked and subdued by a pair of Mordorrim! They were well-armed with dangerous-looking knives; I dared not risk making myself known, so I could not rescue him, but I did follow them for a time. They got too near to Amon Fuin and I had to give up the pursuit, but I knew I needed to tell someone what I saw. These Mordorrim used some trickery to lure him from the safety of the camp; who can say what evils awaited him within Amon Fuin?\
\
'That is all I know. But Amon Fuin is well-defended, and even the sons of Isildur should beware of that place!'","Chapter 11.8: Tûka's Wisdom","'Well do I remember the words of Abrazâni. Even now they move me to pity, and to grief.'","'Tûka's words make it clear: the missing soldiers are not cowardly deserters. Nay, they were ensorcelled by the cultists of Sauron we call the Mordorrim, and brought to Amon Fuin, the Gloom-hill, for some fell purpose. They may still be alive! My father is in council, and there is no one else to attempt a rescue! You must help me and my brothers save these missing men!'\
\
Ornaher pauses, his expression conflicted.\
\
'I must tell you something, friend, and I beg you to keep it in confidence. It is this: we should not ask my foster-brother Tárandil to accompany us on this errand. Like my older brother Meldaran and my cousin Meneldil, Tárandil was born in Númenor, where he was given the birth-name Adûnzagar. His father... his real father, mind you... was a cruel man named Ûrizagar, the Sword of the Sun. He was a captain-general of the fleet, and he worshipped at Sauron's altar. He wished for his son Adûnzagar to follow him on his evil path, but his wife wanted only happiness for her son; Abrazâni she was called, and she was a friend in childhood to Isildur and Anárion. She pleaded for them to take her son with them on the ships, and escape that doom. But Abrazâni was betrayed by the servants of Ûrizagar, and when the great wave sank Númenor beneath the Sea, Abrazâni perished.\
\
'But in this, at least, let the wife of cruel Ûrizagar find happiness. For her son Adûnzagar escaped on the ships to Middle-earth, and when they arrived safely on these shores, my father took him as his ward. To protect the boy from the suspicions of good folk and Sauron's servants alike, he set aside Adûnzagar's birth-name. Henceforth he was called Tárandil, foster-son to the king, and for all my life I knew him as an older brother. He has my love, and always will.'\
\
Ornaher looks away, sorrow etched upon his face. He drags his booted toe in the dirt. When he faces you again his expression has hardened.\
\
'He is my brother in all things, friend, save blood. It is not Isildur's blood that runs through his veins, but that of Ûrizagar. His father worshipped at the altar of Sauron. What if that weakness lies within Tárandil, even today? These Mordorrim are cultists of Sauron, and I fear my foster-brother might succumb to their whispers, their temptations, where the rest of us would not.\
\
'Keep this in confidence, and tell Tárandil none of this. But return to Vëamacil with Tûka's wisdom, and my own. We must rescue these soldiers of Gondor, but if the Mordorrim are involved, we should not involve my foster-brother in this adventure.'","Isildur's son Ornaher can be found in Díngarth with the Hól-budlan matriarch Tûka.","Tûka, leader of the Hól-budlan, may have some clue as to what befell the missing soldiers. She can be found in Díngarth.","'You see? It is as I thought all along! Soldiers of Gondor have been ensorcelled by the Mordorrim, and it is up to us to save them, if we can. You and I will do this, with Ornaher at our side. We will leave Tárandil behind; there is no need to wake him, not so near to his birthday.\
\
'What's that? Tûka thinks it would be foolhardy for us to brave Amon Fuin? Well, I thank her for her stealth, but her wisdom she can keep. You need not fear to go with us! Ornaher and I are of Isildur's blood-line, friend, and we will protect you.'","Talk to Ornaher at Díngarth","'Who is this secret onlooker? Her name is Tûka, and she is the matriarch of the Hól-budlan. Her folk are known for their skill at the art of stealth, and in this case she has seen something of great interest to us and to the Alliance! Find her here in Díngarth and hear her story complete. She told me but a portion of it, and I tell you it was enough for me to know we need hear it all!'"},
[2900]={"Talk to Vëamacil and complete 'Instance: All Is Quiet'","Isildur's foster-son Tárandil is at Ram Raedas.","'Where have you been? I have been looking everywhere for you! It is quite unlike my brothers to disappear without saying a word to me... I feared some evil had come for them!'\
\
Tárandil shakes his head.\
\
'I should choose my words more carefully. The evil comes not just for them, but for all of us. My eldest brother has ridden from the gates of Mordor with fell tidings. To protect his kinship with the kings during the war, he has taken the name Meldaran, but I fear the safety that has given him might be soon exhausted. Find him at Ram Raedas and learn what has happened.\
\
'Did we hope the war would soon be ended? What fools we were! I think the end does come, but not in the form we wished. Alas for the Great Alliance!'","Chapter 11.9: All Is Quiet","'You are friend to my brothers? You are friend then to me, though we have no time to spend in greeting. I rode hard from the gate, but my errand is not yet finished. Need drives me, and will not let me rest, for I must bring my report to my father the king.\
\
'This is my message: the Longbeards and the Thíuda of the north that stood against the Rhúnhoth have suffered a crushing defeat. The Easterling horde was greater by far than we thought; our allies have been utterly defeated. They were to be our shield against this second army, but now the shield has fallen, and we lie exposed to the Storm of Wrath. The Ghâzab Bôron is on its way.'","Talk to Meldaran at Ram Raedas","'My eldest brother Meldaran has ridden from the gates of Mordor with fell tidings. Find him at Ram Raedas and learn what has happened, if you have the heart for it.'","'You are ready, as I am? Then let us be off, and quietly. We can be as loud as we like when we return victorious, but for departure silence is our ally.'","Isildur's son Meldaran has come to Ram Raedas with worrying tidings.","'Make your preparations and tell me when you are ready to depart. Outside of Barad-dûr, the Gloom-hill of Amon Fuin is one of the last places still held by Sauron. We must not fear it, but we should be prepared for anything!'","Isildur's son Vëamacil is at Díngarth.","Stirred to action by the discovery that the missing soldiers were abducted by Mordorrim cultists, Vëamacil and Ornaher are eager to attempt a dangerous rescue in the heart of Amon Fuin.","Talk to Tárandil at Ram Raedas"},
[2901]={"Silirtas stands in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed.","'Look at this.'","Defeat lizards or avanc in south-western Khûd Zagin (3/4)","The sand falls through your fingers","'I have found the body of a dead man, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Think you this might be Sadûkh, who disappeared from Ghalbûru?'","'I intended to slay lizards to the south-west before I returned to Shonith. Let us together defeat them. I appreciate the company, and the two of you are fine listeners.'","Silirtas has agreed to tell you about her people and what they have learned about the lands of Khûd Zagin.","Silirtas falls silent in the middle of her thought","Silirtas asked you to investigate the river-bed where once the River Usâl ran through Khûd Zagin. To the north-west you see some water remains in the channel.","'What can be done, ${PLAYER}? What should be done?\
\
'We cannot leave her here, but neither can we carry her back to Shonith!'","Continue further to the north-west and examine some of the sand among the tumbled rocks","Lizards and avanc can be found in the south-western corner of Khûd Zagin.","Sigileth has found something among the southern sands of Khûd Zagin.","Talk to Silirtas in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed","Silirtas stares blankly forward, seemingly unaware of your presence.","Sigileth calls for you to join her among the southern sands","This is one of the few places where water still collects where the River Usâl once flowed","Silirtas turns her head to you, apparently aware of you and Sigileth once again","Sigileth has found something in southern Khûd Zagin.","Sigileth has found the body of a dead man","Examine sand in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed","Silirtas asked you to investigate the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once ran through Khûd Zagin. To the north-west a tumble of stones fills the channel.","Sigileth waits politely for Silirtas to resume her story, but the Kinta remains silent.\
\
'What happened following the invasion of the Ordâkhai after the Great Dearth?' Sigileth prompts her.\
\
'Silirtas?'","Silirtas stands in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed, but she says nothing.","Chapter 11.9: Silirtas and the Great Dearth","'What? I must apologize. I hope I did not worry you.'\
\
Silirtas shakes her head and looks around at the dry river-bed in which the three of you stand.\
\
'I told you I fight the fading experienced by my people? On occasion I become untethered from my surroundings, losing my grip upon the material world; it can take the form of a loss of awareness. Think not that I welcome such moments! I fight against them always, keeping my hands and my mind busy with whatever tasks the Kintai of Shonith need completed, but it is painful. It would be easy for any other to succumb, to sit down within one of our groves and fade as have so many of my people... but not Silirtas.\
\
'Why did I bring you to the River Usâl?'\
\
You remind Silirtas that she wanted to show you something of her reasons for resisting the fading of the Kintai, and that the dry river-bed was somehow a part of it. She nods with understanding.\
\
'Yes, I remember now. When a Kinta enters the trance of Tróthul and is entombed within the Sarláshi trees that compose a Veróth, they become bonded to their grove. They remain there through the years, ever watchful but unable to affect the world outside. Can you imagine the frustration of remaining a prisoner for untold centuries while the land you love rots and dies all around you? Can you imagine the sorrow of watching as the River Usâl dries up and the Great Dearth withers the beauty you remember into a dead or dying shadow, with you unable to prevent or reverse it?\
\
'So I choose not to fade, and if that means I must remain ever-vigilant and constantly active, then that is what I shall be. I intended to slay lizards or avanc to the south-west before I returned to Shonith. Let us together defeat them. I appreciate the company, and the two of you are fine listeners.'","'Why do I fight the fading of my people? I will show you. The River Usâl once flowed through this land, but now only its dry bed remains. Walk within that empty channel and examine the sand within it. You will come to better understand me.'","Talk to Sigileth in southern Khûd Zagin","'Silirtas, are you well?'","Examine sand further to the north-west, alongside the little water that remains in the channel of the River Usâl","Silirtas asked you to investigate the dry river-bed where once the River Usâl ran through Khûd Zagin, to the west.","Silirtas watches the sand fall from your fingers onto the dry ground","'Silirtas? Are you feeling well?'","Defeat lizards or avanc in south-western Khûd Zagin (${CURRENT}/4)","Join Sigileth and Silirtas in the desert of southern Khûd Zagin","Talk to Sigileth in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed","Defeated lizards or avanc (${CURRENT}/4)","Sigileth is in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed.","Silirtas is in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed. She again seems aware of both you and Sigileth.","'More than a hundred and twenty years ago, these lands were green and bountiful. The banks of the River Usâl were alive with a riot of beautiful vegetation. I understand the folk who dwelt beside it named it \\qthe Abundant Kingdom\\q in their language, and I can think of no name more appropriate for the thriving land of my memory!\
\
'But then Ordâkh came. With terrible magic the sorcerers of that Empire caused the drying of the River Usâl and its most important tributaries. Marshes shrank away to nothing, and the river-lands withered and burned. None of my people know for certain, but I believe the blight that wasted the Emerald Wood came north with the Ordâkhai when they caused this Great Dearth. And that is why -'","'And so I continue to fight the fading to which my people succumb. It is painful, but I have not yet given in to it. Unless my heart is greatly changed, I cannot imagine myself becoming content enough to fade in the manner of Aitárshun or others among the Kintai.\
\
'Why do I fight it so? I will show you.\
\
'The River Usâl once flowed through this land, but now only its dry bed remains. Walk within that empty channel west of here and examine the sand within it. You will come to better understand me.'"},
[2902]={"Snár, el Maestro de la Forja, puede encontrarse junto a las Forjas de Rivendel.\
\
Tu arma posee un potencial oculto que puede desbloquearse reforjándola con un Maestro de la Forja. Este proceso aumenta el daño del arma y revela su potencial.","Dithalion está junto a las Forjas de Rivendel.\
\
Ahora que has reforjado el arma, deberías volver con Dithalion para demostrar su progreso.","'Esta antigua arma puede ser reforjada por un Maestro de la Forja, permitiendo que su poder aumente hasta igualar la habilidad de quien la empuña.\
\
'Una vez reforjada, puede que posea la fuerza necesaria para enfrentarse a la criatura que acecha en el Lago Negro, ${PLAYER}. Deberías llevarla al Maestro de la Forja para reforjarla, y tal vez tu hoja renovada logre por fin vencer la carne del cruel Guardián.\
\
'Lleva esta arma a Snár y la reforjará de nuevo, y entonces quizá veremos su verdadero potencial.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>- A medida que aumenta el nivel de tu personaje, tu arma puede llevarse a un Maestro de la Forja para reforjarla. \
\
- Reforjar tu arma aumenta su poder y puede desbloquear ranuras de tracería adicionales.</rgb>","'Te doy la bienvenida de nuevo, ${PLAYER}. ¿Ese arma de los Días Antiguos demostró su valor, o fue una búsqueda en vano?'\
\
Los ojos de Ráthwald se abren de sorpresa.\
\
'¡Esta arma se ha vuelto aún más poderosa en tus manos, ${PLAYER}! ¡Ahora sí tenemos fuerza para plantarnos ante el horror de ese lago fétido!'","'¡Vaya arma la que has encontrado! Si quieres reforjarla y aumentar su potencial, vuelve a hablar conmigo y me aseguraré de que se haga.\
\
'Pero ten presente esto, camarada: la verdadera fuerza de esta arma vendrá de quien la empuñe. Creo que ahora ya tienes lo necesario para superar a los enemigos que se alzan contra ti.'","'¿Ahora comprendes el potencial de tu arma? Sí, ahora puede portar heráldica.\
\
'Debes regresar de inmediato a Acebeda y mostrarle a Ráthwald, el enano del arco en ruinas cerca de Echad Dúnann, que empuñas una gran arma. Seguro que dará nueva esperanza a los enanos de su compañía.\
\
'Ve de inmediato, camarada. Considero que esa arma ha surgido del mismísimo tejido de la leyenda para este propósito.'","Capítulo 11: Forjada de nuevo","'Lleva tu arma al Maestro de la Forja para reforjarla, ${PLAYER}. Solo así sabremos si ahora será lo bastante resistente para vencer a la criatura del Lago Negro.'","'Ve de inmediato al campamento de Echad Dúnann, en Eregion, y habla con Ráthwald. Debe ver el arma que empuñas ahora y el poder que puede tener contra la criatura del Lago Negro.'","Ráthwald está en el arco en ruinas cerca del campamento de Echad Dúnann, en Eregion.\
\
Tu arma se ha vuelto realmente poderosa, quizá lo bastante como para usarla en combate contra el Guardián ante las Puertas de Durin.","Habla con Snár, el Maestro de la Forja, en las Forjas de Rivendel","Diathalon desea ver tu arma reforjada de nuevo."},
[2903]={"Chapter 11: Grief and Insight","'I cannot believe this! The traitor Saruman has been influencing our errand without our knowledge, and we have played right into his hands!\
\
'This stage of our journey, this investigation into the mystery posed by Nár, is over. Halbarad is right: the next stage of our journey will take us south into Dunland, likely towards war and danger, right beneath the shadow of our enemy, but it does not matter. What matters is that we journey. For good or ill, the Grey Company will continue on its road.\
\
'This detour means our enemy knows we are coming. We must hope he does not know why, but if he does, perhaps that knowledge will cause him to make a mistake, to make some error he will regret.\
\
'Our friends have perished. Our hope for the future must not die with them. The Grey Company will ride again, and soon. You will come with us, if you still wish to. I would not blame you for changing your mind, for the road will be hard.'","'Hurry! You must ask Nár these questions before the effects of the brew fade! I want to know why this had to happen! I will not leave here without answers!'","The distant expression that Nár usually wears has been replaced with a shrewd glare. He is still under the effect of the strange-smelling brew, but that clarity may not last long.","'I must follow Halbarad's orders, but I will not leave until I have some answers! After the disaster of the Forsaken Road, I strode through the Coomb and collected the ingredients for the strange-smelling brew: Kibil-luwz, Nijam-mujdu, and Hulwul-hurz. Frithgeir did not want to, but at the end I gave him no choice, and he has brewed the drink and given it to Nár.\
\
'Hurry! Go now to Nár and ask him, once again, how he knows of the Oath-breakers! Ask him how he knows the words of Elrond concerning the Paths of the Dead! Ask him why my friends are dead!\
\
'Go, ${PLAYER}! We will leave Zudrugund, but first I want to know why all of this had to happen!'","Talk to Nár at Zudrugund","Devastated by the losses suffered by the Grey Company on the Forsaken Road, Halbarad wants you to tell Corunir it is time to leave.","'I have given Nár the brew once again. Your Ranger friend had a strange fire in his eyes, and I did not feel I could refuse. You should hurry, for the effects will not last.'","'Tell Corunir to return to Lhanuch. We are done with Zudrugund and done with Nár.'","Corunir is at Zudrugund.\
\
Halbarad wants you to tell Corunir to come back to Lhanuch.","Corunir is at Zudrugund.\
\
You have spoken with Nár about a number of topics of interest to Corunir and should tell the Ranger what you have learned.","Talk to Corunir at Zudrugund","Talk to Corunir in Zudrugund","'I want Corunir to come back from Zudrugund. It is time we made ready to leave once again, and I want every Ranger ready to depart. We have lost too many of our number to foolish detours! Enough!\
\
'Go to Zudrugund and tell Corunir that it is done. We ride at first light. I do not care what Nár may know, or of what Ergothorn was afraid. I thought we could attain some secret, some new wisdom that would be of use to Aragorn when we come at last to him in Rohan, but I was wrong.\
\
'There is no secret weapon, no easy victory. Go to Corunir and tell him we are done with Zudrugund and done with Nár.'","Nár is in Zudrugund.\
\
Corunir, angered by the loss of his friends along the Forsaken Road, has forced Frithgeir to give Nár the strange-smelling brew once again, in order for dwarf to give clear answers about his knowledge.","'I am sorry for what has happened to your friends because of this. I did not think this could happen.'"},
[2904]={"Habla con Ningloril en Thangúlhad","'¿Estás aquí para ofrecer tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}? Nos encontramos en tiempos de guerra, aunque sea una guerra para la que no se pueda esperar una victoria duradera. Celeborn ha dado la orden a la Hueste Dorada de comenzar su marcha no para ganar el día, sino como una acción de retraso.\
\
'Incluso un fracaso aquí tendrá algún valor, porque el verdadero objetivo de la Hueste Dorada es mantener la atención del enemigo, y eso lo tenemos por seguro. Espero que vivamos lo suficiente para que eso tenga consecuencias.'","'Quizás fue una tontería pensar que tratar con el enemigo era posible, ${PLAYER}, pero había algo que ganar y parecía que valía la pena intentarlo. Ahora ha fracasado, pero las fuerzas de Dol Guldur verán el efecto de traicionarnos bajo una bandera de paz.\
\
'La sección principal de la Hueste Dorada ha acampado en Thangúlhad, un campamento al este de aquí, en Gathbúrz. Preséntate a Ningloril allí, porque ella tendrá algo que un ${CLASS} como tú podría hacer para el beneficio de la Hueste Dorada en la próxima etapa de esta campaña. Una advertencia: Ningloril es severa y no se da a bromas ociosas. No pruebes su paciencia o te irá mal.'","Capítulo 11: El Enfoque hacia Dol Guldur","'Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, un campamento de la Hueste Dorada ubicado en Gathbúrz, al este de aquí. Tendrá mucho trabajo para un ${CLASS} como tú.\
\
'Recuerda mi advertencia: Ningloril es severa y no se da a bromas ociosas. No pruebes su paciencia.'","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, al este de Ost Galadh, en Gathbúrz.\
\
Gruingalas te ha enviado para ofrecer tu ayuda a Ningloril, ahora que la misión de la Guardia Oculta ha fracasado.","La misión de la Guardia Oculta ha fracasado, y ahora las esperanzas restantes de Celeborn y Galadriel dependen únicamente del brazo principal de la Hueste Dorada."},
[2905]={"'Things are not right in Enedwaith, ${PLAYER}. As we have come further south, it becomes more clear to me that the plans of the Wizard Saruman, told to us by Elrond, are more advanced than even the Elf-lord believed.'\
\
You tell Saeradan of your encounter with Wadu of the Uch-lûth, and he nods grimly.\
\
'We have few friends here, ${PLAYER}, and I fear they are becoming fewer. Wadu may speak for us, but I am not convinced that his clan will listen. Already there are more clans in Enedwaith than just the Uch-lûth, and they are hostile to us. Travel a short way to the north and see what has become of the road. I fear it has been blockaded at the command of Saruman.'","'You have brought me nothing?'","'Saeradan has gone on ahead, ${PLAYER}, and established a camp in the Windfells. He planned to investigate the state of the road that runs through Enedwaith and Dunland, for he worried that it had been blocked by hostile Dunlending clans.\
\
'Go now to his camp far to the south-west of here, on a hilltop in the Windfells. Help him with his investigation. I know he will be happy to have your help.'","Saeradan is at his camp, Echad Saeradan, in the Windfells, in Enedwaith. His camp can be found on a hilltop in the Windfells, south-west of Echad Dagoras.\
\
Lothrandir has sent you into the Windfells to assist Saeradan.","'Saeradan's camp is located in the Windfells, on a hill-top far to the south-west of here.'","Bring the report and the ancient sword to Saeradan","'For what purpose have our enemies blockaded the road north?'","Chapter 11: The Blockade","Talk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan","Inside the coffer you find a report and a sword with ancient markings","'Investigate the road north of here and determine if it has been blockaded. I fear that it has.'","Saeradan takes the report from you and reads it with growing concern. He then marvels at the sword.\
\
'This confirms what I feared, ${PLAYER}. One of the Dunlending clans has been ordered, likely by Saruman, to blockade the road north and to slay any who seek to pass that way. This sword is of ancient make; see the markings here in the shape of horses? This is a sword of the Rohirrim.'","The road that runs north through Dunland and Enedwaith has been troubled by hostile Dunlending clans, and the Grey Company is worried by these reports.","'It is not right for the road to be blockaded.'","Investigate the road north of Echad Saeradan for evidence of a blockade","Saeradan is at his camp south of the blockaded road in Fordirith.\
\
You found a report and a sword with ancient markings in the coffer at the blockaded road and should bring them to Saeradan.","The road north of Echad Saeradan may have been blockaded by forces of Saruman.\
\
Saeradan has asked you to investigate the road north for signs of blockade."},
[2906]={"Capítulo 11: Valor inconmensurable","'¡Lo has hecho muy bien, ${PLAYER}! ¡Tu arma ha avanzado a un nivel realmente impresionante!'","'Las armas de tal valor mejoran a medida que se usan, ${PLAYER}. Solo cuando se blanden en combate pueden alcanzar la verdadera medida de su grandeza.\
\
'Equipa el arma y úsala contra enemigos dignos, y mejorará a medida que tú también progresas. Cuando haya alcanzado un alto grado de valor, tráemela a mí o al erudito Dithalion, en Rivendel, y uno de nosotros te aconsejará sobre lo que debes hacer después.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Los objetos legendarios ganan experiencia cuando luchas con ellos contra enemigos que otorgan experiencia. Cuando un arma así recibe suficiente experiencia, sube de nivel.</rgb>","Lleva tu nueva arma a Wafi o a Dithalion","'Las armas de tal valor mejoran a medida que se usan, ${PLAYER}. Solo cuando se blanden en combate pueden alcanzar la verdadera medida de su grandeza.\
\
'Úsala contra enemigos dignos, y mejorará a medida que progresen tus propias habilidades. Cuando haya alcanzado un alto grado de valor, tráemela a mí o al erudito Wafi, en la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin, y uno de nosotros te aconsejará sobre lo que debes hacer después.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Los objetos legendarios ganan experiencia cuando luchas con ellos contra enemigos que otorgan experiencia. Cuando un arma así recibe suficiente experiencia, sube de nivel.</rgb>","Tu nueva arma tiene un potencial de valor inconmensurable, pero aún debes blandirla en combate.","Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin, y Dithalion está junto a las Forjas de Rivendel.\
\
Ahora que has combatido a muchos enemigos con tu nueva arma, deberías volver con Wafi o con Dithalion para demostrar tu progreso."},
[2907]={"'Go now, my friend, and speak of Narsil and of Aiglos to the frightened Men and Elves who have forgotten the vows they made when they joined the Great Alliance. Will they join their own tales to those of proud Elendil and noble Gil-galad? Will they wield their own weapons alongside Narsil, sharp and deadly, and alongside Aiglos, bright and cold? Tell them! This may be the end, but let it be an end that shall be worthy of song!'","'I have learned there is to be a council of the kings, at which they will discuss what can be done about the Ghâzab Bôron. My brothers will likely be permitted to attend, but I will not.\
\
'You asked what I wanted for my birthday, and I told you I wanted nothing. But now I know what I want for my birthday present. I want this. I want to attend the council.'","Words are no more use to the despairing soldiers of the Great Alliance. Better now to collect the weapons they cast aside with the hope that they will still be of use to those who remain to fight.","The Longbeard and Thíuda armies that engaged with the Ghâzab Bôron, the Rhúnhoth Storm of Wrath, have been utterly defeated, and now nothing stands between the flank of the Great Alliance and the onrushing horde.","'I will see these weapons go to those who remain. Those soldiers with the heart to fight may still make use of them.\
\
'But wait, friend. As I look upon these weapons, I am filled with newfound courage. These swords have seen battle, even during the long, slow years of our siege. Their tale is one of standing strong, though today their owners do not. But there are weapons in our Alliance of whom the minstrels sing: Narsil, the blade of my grandfather Elendil, and Aiglos, the spear of Gil-galad. The tale of these weapons is long, and will be longer still! They will not be cast aside. Nay, they will be wielded to the last, and if their song is to end in battle with the Ghâzab Bôron, is that not a glorious end?\
\
'Go now, ${CLASS}, and speak of Narsil and of Aiglos to the frightened Men and Elves who have forgotten the vows they made when they joined the Great Alliance. Will they join their own tales to those of proud Elendil and noble Gil-galad? Will they wield their own weapons alongside Narsil, sharp and deadly, and alongside Aiglos, bright and cold? Tell them, my friend. This may be the end, but let it be an end that shall be worthy of song!'","'Word of the approaching horde began to spread throughout the camps of the Alliance.'","'It is no use. Words will no longer avail us! Better to collect the weapons they have cast aside, for those at least may still be of some use to those soldiers who remain to fight!'","Chapter 12.1: The Approaching Storm","Speak inspiring words to fearful soldiers at Ram Raedas (0/8)","'We cannot despair. We must not. Already I see men casting down their weapons! We must stop them. Quickly, tell the men it is not over! Tell them we must still fight!'","'Sauron has bested us! This endless waiting did not signify a beaten enemy at all! He waited for the Ghâzab Bôron to swell to such size as it could not be opposed, and now we will be crushed between the Rhúnhoth and the Dark Tower!\
\
'We cannot despair. We must not. Already I see men casting down their weapons! We must stop them. Quickly, tell the men it is not over! Tell them we must still fight!'","Collect abandoned weapons at Díngarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected abandoned weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Ornaher at Díngarth","Remind Elves of the Alliance about Aiglos, the spear of Gil-galad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Frightened Men and Elves can be found at Díngarth.\
\
Ornaher believes tales of Elendil's sword Narsil and Gil-galad's spear Aiglos may inspire the frightened Men and Elves to stand against the Ghâzab Bôron.","Spoke inspiring words about Aiglos, the spear of Gil-galad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Fearful soldiers can be found at Díngarth, despairing at the news of the approaching Rhúnhoth horde.","'I was at the Morannon when the wounded began to arrive: weary Men and dwarves, bloody and battered, the tale of their defeat writ large upon mournful faces. I saw King Durin from afar, but even from such a distance I could see his face was ashen, and the fire of battle had gone out of him. I spoke with Huneric Hundred-slayer, lord of the Thíuda, and my heart wept to hear his account of the battle on the field of Khôn-khaigu.\
\
'\\qWe had so many victories!\\q he said to me, \\qBut it was a deception. We were drawn forward by the promise of those successes, and only when we thought the end was near did Sauron's commanders reveal the true size of the Easterling horde. We fought valiantly, Man and dwarf alike... but we could not fight for long against so many. Any who survived the massacre fled, and I fled with them. Those who could not were captured, cut to pieces or burned on altars to Sauron. A few score can move faster than a horde, and we outpaced the Rhúnhoth, but still they come. They will be here before long.\\q\
\
'So said Huneric to me, and I must bring word to my father. Tell my brothers I will see them after I deliver my message.'","Remind Men of the Alliance about Narsil, the sword of Elendil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deliver abandoned weapons to Ornaher at Díngarth","Tárandil is at Díngarth, and he desires to speak with you.","'But men were now without hope. They cast aside their weapons and despaired.'","Talk to Tárandil at Díngarth","You have gathered many weapons cast aside by despairing soldiers at Díngarth, and should bring them to Ornaher for distribution to those who may still wield them.","Spoke inspiring words about Narsil, the sword of Elendil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I must bring word of the Ghâzab Bôron to my father. Tell my brothers I will see them after I deliver my message.'","Isildur's son Ornaher is at Díngarth."},
[2908]={"Dampen the cloth and fill the jar with water from the deepest part of the oasis","Talk to Idhraid by the northern pavilion","'You bring the items we sought from Idhraid? Very good.'","'Azagath and Nakási must not find the stockpile they seek. They will set the world aflame.'","Silirtas is waiting for you to return to her with the damp cloth and water jar she requested of you.","'If Silirtas is to join us, as she has suggested to me, we will need to seek permission from Tharashil.'","'I would not agree with the Heirs of Castamir about very many things, ${PLAYER}. We have found the single exception.\
\
'We must catch up to our travelling companions and tell them we have learned what our quarry seeks. If Silirtas is to join us, as she has suggested to me, we will need to seek permission from Tharashil.'","Talk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith","Silirtas suggested that you speak with Idhraid about what it will take to heal Balakhâd of his injuries, and also that you fill a jar with water from the deepest part of the oasis. Jars for this purpose can be found at the front of the pavilion in northern Shonith.","You inform Tharashil of Balakhâd's condition and his vow to depart from Shonith as soon as he is able to walk. You also ask for her permission to allow Silirtas to accompany you and Sigileth on your journey eastward.\
\
'I am the warden of this grove, but I have not the power to keep Silirtas from doing as she wishes. Had I that power, she might have already entered Tróthul and begun to safely fade within a Veróth of her own! But I do not, and she insists upon fighting the process.\
\
'If she truly wishes to go with you, I hope you will keep her safe. She fights the fading, but I understand the fight is painful, and even one so strong-willed as Silirtas cannot achieve victory in every battle. It is the lot of her people to fade, though she wishes otherwise.'","Sigileth is at the northern pavilion in Shonith.","Help Balakhâd drink from the jar of water","You help Balakhâd hold the jar you filled with clean water from the oasis, and he manages to drink. After a few moments, he looks up at you with a guarded expression.\
\
'We are... not friends. These Elves are alien to me, and I do not trust them. As soon as I am... well enough to walk... I will leave this place, and never return.\
\
'But you and these Elves are... you are right about something. If the Kindred finds the hidden cache of Narghâk they seek...'\
\
Balakhâd falls silent, mopping his forehead with the damp cloth you brought from Idhraid.\
\
'In Gondor they named it \\qUmbari Fire,\\q for they knew not of its long use in these lands, and only learned of it when it was used against them. But my father knew. He dreamed of harnessing it against his enemies, but even with all the men at his command he could find no stores of it. He believed it gone from the world.\
\
'It should be gone. Azagath and Nakási must not find... the hidden stockpile they seek. They will set the world aflame.'","Talk to Sigileth at the northern pavilion in Shonith","'We must show this man we will harm him not, unless he inflict some injury upon the Kinta people or our grove. His hurts are severe, but if our healers are permitted to tend them, he may recover.\
\
'Collect a jar from the front of this pavilion to fill with water from the deepest area of the pool. Speak also to Idhraid nearby, for she is lately arrived from Vartúlin and brings with her great knowledge of the healing arts. She may have some advice of use to us.'","Silirtas believes that Balakhâd knows more about Narghâk, the Hungry Fire, than he is letting on. He may speak further on the subject if his hurts are healed.","You should dampen the cloth given to you by Idhraid and fill the jar you collected with water from the deepest reaches of the oasis in Shonith.","Idhraid gives you a cloth to dampen in the water","Silirtas has begun trying to ease Balakhâd's hurts with the damp cloth.","Balakhâd is at the northern pavilion in Shonith.","Bring the damp cloth and water jar to Silirtas at the northern pavilion in Shonith","Wait for Silirtas to soothe Balakhâd's burning skin with the damp cloth","You dampen the cloth and fill your jar with water from the deepest part of the oasis","'I gave you a cloth to dampen in the pool, so the pains of the dying man may be eased. Perhaps in gratitude he will leave the Kintai be, and never return?'","Chapter 12.1: The Hungry Fire","'Collect a jar from the front of the pavilion to fill with water from the deepest reaches of the pool. Speak also to Idhraid, for she is lately arrived from Vartúlin and brings with her great knowledge of the healing arts. She may have some advice of use to us.'","'I observed the two of you as you brought that dying man to Shonith. He trusts not my people? Perhaps we share that feeling. I dwelled in the Emerald Wood of Nisigím before the blight killed the trees, and it was Men that unleashed it.\
\
'No, it was not his doing; I know the lives of Men are short, and he could not have been born when Nisigím withered. But I know also his kind.\
\
'I am a healer. I will give you a cloth to dampen in the pool, so his pains may be eased. Perhaps in gratitude he will leave the Kintai be, and never return? Be sure to collect water from the deepest part of the pond! Water from the shallower reaches will not be as effective.'","You pick up the jar","Tharashil is in south-western Shonith.","Collect a jar front the northern pavilion to fill with water for Balakhâd"},
[2909]={"Collected a Mordorrim badge of rank","Bring the patrol badges to Tárandil at Adambel","Vëamacil is at Adambel, dismayed by the result of the council of the kings.","Chapter 12.2: The Council of Kings","Talk to Tárandil and complete 'Instance: The Council of Kings'","Tárandil is at Adambel, hoping to attend the council of the kings.","'Go to my grandfather, then. I have nothing more to say to you.'","'I see the weariness in you, though you seek to hide it. Let us speak about the task to come, and why you were selected to join with the Bright Company on this mission, and my grandsons were not.'","Talk to Elendil at Adambel","'Isildur generally treats me the same as he treats my foster-brothers, but there are limits to his even-handedness. I fear this will be one such case, for there are still many who consider me no true son to the king. I too... there are times I am reminded that he is not truly my own father, and I wish he would listen to my words, pay heed to the advice I give... but he does not.\
\
'Do not misunderstand me! I consider Isildur my true father, for he raised me as his own and I would have it no other way. There is a reason I count my years from the day I was fostered by the king and not from the day of my birth! But there is a sadness about my early years and you will understand if I do not wish to speak of it to you.'\
\
Tárandil falls silent, pondering solutions.\
\
'Yes, I think I have it! Perhaps we can prove we both deserve to attend this council, my friend. There are those in the Dark Lord's service hopeful of attaining glory, and they seek the honour of leading their own patrols. Mordorrim hopefuls gather west of the entrance to Amon Fuin, and hopeful Orcs can be found in and around Mokh Darga. Look for Easterling hopefuls south of the road halfway between Mokh Darga and Barthost. Let us each find some of these hopeful leaders and seize their badges of rank. If we present these trophies we may prove ourselves deserving of attendance at the council!'","'Perhaps we can prove we both deserve to attend this council, my friend. There are those in the Dark Lord's service hopeful of attaining glory, and they seek the honour of leading their own patrols. Mordorrim hopefuls gather west of the entrance to Amon Fuin, and hopeful Orcs can be found in and around Mokh Darga. Look for Easterling hopefuls south of the road halfway between Mokh Darga and Barthost. Let us each find some of these hopeful leaders and seize their badges of rank. If we present these trophies we may prove ourselves deserving of attendance at the council!'","Collect a badge from an Easterling hopeful","'I hope this works. It must!'","Tárandil wants to attend the council of the kings, but he fears it will not be permitted without some evidence that he is deserving.","Collected an Orkish badge of rank","Collect a badge from a Mordorrim hopeful","Collected an Easterling badge of rank","'I cannot believe you get to go on the daring mission and I do not! You are just a ${CLASS}, and I am the son of a king!\
\
'I am sorry, I did not mean that. But you must see that it is unjust! My brothers and I are not afraid! All of us save Tárandil volunteered to accompany the Bright Company, and yet we must remain behind with him, as if his cowardice was our own! If we are going to die when the Ghâzab Bôron arrives, I would much rather die fighting on the offensive within the Dark Tower than back on my heels on this blasted plain!\
\
'If it is a jest, it is a poor one! I cannot believe my father would treat us so. It is not your fault, friend, it is his. I apologize for my words, but my blood is hot. My grandfather wishes to speak with you. Perhaps when you go to him you will ask him to reverse my father's decision and allow my brothers and I to join with the Bright Company on this mission?'","Collect a badge from a hopeful Orc patrol-leader","High King Elendil is at Adambel, and has asked to speak with you.","Patrol leaders, and others who intend to lead such excursions, can be found throughout Parth Daenath. Mordorrim hopefuls gather west of the entrance to Amon Fuin, and hopeful Orcs can be found in and around Mokh Darga. Look for Easterling hopefuls south of the road halfway between Mokh Darga and Barthost.\
\
Tárandil believes that proof of your value to the Great Alliance will gain the two of you entrance to the council of the kings, and he wants you to collect badges of rank belonging to hopeful patrol leaders as proof of that value.","'I am impressed! You managed to acquire three badges? I only obtained one! Will you allow us to combine our trove? Four is better than both three or one, friend. And it is my birthday, after all.\
\
'Let me know if you are ready, and we will see if we can attend the council.'","Talk to Vëamacil at Adambel"},
[2910]={"Thórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin is in southern Imhûlar.","'Thórvilon is the guardian of the grove of Vartúlin, in southern Imhûlar.'","'Ah, Silirtas. Still she fights the fate of her people.'","Tharashil has suggested that when you depart from Shonith, you visit the grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar before meeting up with the rest of your travelling company.","Collected diseased boar-hooves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What can Silirtas tell us of Imhûlar?'","Diseased boars, servals, and deer can be found throughout Imhûlar.","Silirtas is just inside the entrance to Imhûlar.","'¿Si?'","Sigileth calls a halt at the entrance to Imhûlar","'This must be Imhûlar. Our travelling companions planned to make for the city of Kûr Anzar, but I understand Tharashil wished for us to first visit the grove of Vartúlin?\
\
'I am not opposed to this plan, but I suggest that we do not linger overlong at that grove. I am concerned for the safety of my brother in the company of the Kindred. I cannot say for certain that Khôltekh or Rothog were responsible for the disappearance of Sadûkh, but neither can I deny it completely.\
\
'What can Silirtas tell us of Imhûlar?'","Collected diseased serval-fangs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Thórvilon in Vartúlin","'The Kinta warden of Vartúlin is Thórvilon; for decades he has sought to find some means of reversing the blight. I suggest that you speak with him as you walk in Imhûlar. Perhaps speaking with him will help Silirtas accept that she must fade? I do not really believe it will, but it is in my nature to remain hopeful.'","Talk to Silirtas by the road into Imhûlar","Find Thórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin, in southern Imhûlar","Talk to Sigileth by the road into Imhûlar","Cross the River Barûg into Imhûlar from Khûd Zagin, north of Shonith","Silirtas stares blankly forward, her awareness once again untethered.","Sigileth stands just within the entrance to Imhûlar.","The leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin is named Thórvilon, and can be found in southern Imhûlar.","Collected diseased deer-hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The lands to the east are named Imhûlar by the Shagâni people, and for the Kintai they are full of memories. Some of those are painful, for we remember when the northern reaches of the Emerald Wood grew there, before it withered and died as a result of the blight brought by the Ordâkhai. But others of those memories are joyful: the spirits of my own parents remain at the grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar; they faded long ago, but whenever I walk beside their trees I feel their presence.\
\
'The Kinta warden of Vartúlin is Thórvilon; for decades he has sought to find some means of reversing the blight. I suggest that you speak with him as you walk in Imhûlar. Perhaps speaking with him will help Silirtas accept that she must fade? I do not really believe it will, but it is in my nature to remain hopeful.'","'The Emerald Wood of Nisigím has been blighted by the Ordâkhai, and it is no longer a place of green beauty. Now it is Adagím, the Corpseholt, and Thórvilon and others of my people seek to slow the spread of the disease that claims it. When last I walked in Vartúlin, the grove remained healthy, but the circle of hale trees had already diminished from its original size.\
\
'North-east of Vartúlin, the city of Kûr Anzar was the birthplace of the Shagâni kingdom of Hamât early in the Third Age. For nearly three thousand years, the Hamâti fought against Gondor and other rival kingdoms, until it was eventually absorbed into the Empire of Ordâkh. I do not know the state of it today.\
\
'On our way to Vartúlin we should hunt some of the diseased animals that walk among the dead trees. Thórvilon oft desires to study the blighted creatures for some clue to curing the pestilence in Adagím.'","Chapter 12.2: The Dead Forest","Thórvilon glances at Silirtas with understanding","Collect diseased boar-hooves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I see that Silirtas still fights our people's fate. I am saddened to see it, but not surprised; she and I have spoken about it before, and her decision then was clear. I see it has not changed.\
\
'How can it be so easy to accept in others, and yet so difficult to accept when it affects those dear to us? Alas, I see this difficulty most clearly within my own family, and the contradiction is visible to me! But it is not my decision to make for Silirtas, and my words on this subject will sway her neither for nor against.'\
\
Thórvilon accepts the satchel containing the diseased hooves, fangs, and hides from the pestilential creatures of the dead forest, and sadly looks them over.\
\
'If there is aught to learn from these, we will learn it. I dare not hope the blight can be reversed, but perhaps we can fight it, as Silirtas fights the fading.'","The road into Imhûlar crosses the River Barûg north of Shonith.","'You have come to aid the Kintai of Vartúlin with our work? I welcome it, though I fear the blight that has transformed these woods resists our efforts, and has so far proven impossible to reverse. The best for which we can hope is to slow its spread. You and Silirtas have my thanks.'","Silirtas stands by Thórvilon in Vartúlin.","Collect diseased deer-hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Give the hooves, fangs, and hides to Thórvilon","'On our way to Vartúlin we should hunt some of the diseased animals that walk among the dead trees. Thórvilon oft desires to study the blighted creatures for some clue to curing the pestilence in Adagím.'","Talk to Silirtas in Vartúlin","You have found Thórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin","Thórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin, is in southern Imhûlar.","'This must be Imhûlar.'","Collect diseased serval-fangs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2911]={"Glorfindel catches your attention, a sorrowful look on his face","'Glorfindel of the Elves desires to speak? If he wishes to continue the tale he may do so, though he seems ill at ease.'","Tûka is outside the tunnel of Halroth, which the Bright Company hopes to use to infiltrate Barad-dûr.","Glorfindel is on Tol Send.\
\
Glorfindel has interrupted the shade of Isildur in his telling of the tale, and wishes to speak with you.","'Very well. I will conclude the tale, despite my misgivings.'","Talk to Vëamacil and complete 'Instance: A Bad Birthday'","Tûka is outside the entrance of Halroth, a tunnel carved in the rocks of Mordor.","'There is nothing else you need help me with at Halroth. You may as well return to Adambel, and relay the news that the tunnel entrance is less-watched than it might have been.'","'They never told me the precise number, but in the end Tûka must have been satisfied.'","The shade of Isildur is on Tol Send, waiting to tell you more of the tale of the Great Alliance.","'I say Glorfindel should speak on, and delay no further.'","Talk to the shade of Isildur on Tol Send","'Over here... as quiet as you can!\
\
'This is the tunnel about which I spoke at the council. Some of my people followed it a goodly way, and it seemed to them that it did curve in the direction of the Dark Tower. We all agree that it must empty into the dungeons, and if the Elves are as powerful as they say they will be able to make it at least as far as the tower. Beyond that, well...'\
\
Tûka shudders.\
\
'There are a lot of eyes out here. We should thin out some of the foes this near to Halroth, but not so many as to be suspicious. You had better get to it!'","Talk to Tûka outside the entrance to Halroth","Talk to Glorfindel on Tol Send","Lendelen of the Bright Company has suggested a dangerous mission to overcome Sauron's domination of the Ghâzab Bôron, and a number of preparations must be made before it can be attempted.","'The sun dawned sickly on the day the mission of the Bright Company was to take place. They gathered at Echad-in-Edhil and prepared to depart for the secret way of Halroth.'","'Our Alliance is composed of the mightiest heroes of the age, ${CLASS}, and together we have achieved many victories. But here, after seven years of siege, our triumphs are mere memory. Sauron has outmaneuvered us. If we cannot overcome his domination of the Ghâzab Bôron, it will not matter how many great heroes stand with us. Our defeat will be certain, and it will be forever.\
\
'If Lendelen is trustworthy, as I am told he is, there are few only who can break the spells enwreathing the Oath-stone. They must reach the chamber in which it lies, though it be kept within Barad-dûr itself. Their purpose must be hidden from Sauron, for if he learns what they seek to do he will turn his every thought upon preventing it. If he sees a ${CLASS} among the most powerful High Elves that walk in Middle-earth, he may hesitate. \\qWhat purpose do you serve?\\q he may wonder, and in that briefest of delays the mission of the Bright Company might be accomplished. It is a hard thing to ask, ${CLASS}, but we must seek every advantage we can. It is likely you will not return.\
\
'But there are still preparations to be made before the Bright Company departs. You should find the Hól-budlan matriarch Tûka, somewhere to the east of our encampments, for she intended to scout the entrance to the tunnel discovered by her people.'","'I am glad you have returned, for I... I wish to apologize to you for my words earlier. I repented of them not long after you left, and would have them unsaid. Alas, that is beyond my power. Still, I beg you will forgive me. The war must soon end, one way or another, and I would not have us part with such a cloud of ill feeling between us.\
\
'My brothers and I plan to take a last meal together at Díngarth, for it seems clear the mission of the Bright Company is the final hope of the Great Alliance, and we may not have another opportunity. I hope that you will join us, my friend. Let me know if you will.'","Chapter 12.3: A Bad Birthday","'I hoped it would not be necessary to recall that dark day, but I see now it cannot be avoided.'","'Thank you, my friend. Let us go together to Díngarth. It is Tárandil's birthday today, and we are celebrating as best we can.'","'It is my turn to take up the tale, ${PLAYER}. Well do I remember the glory of the Bright Company, but if there was valour so too was there tragedy. I hoped it would not be necessary to recall that dark day, but I see now it cannot be avoided.'\
\
Glorfindel turns to address Gandalf, sorrow etched on his face and regret in his voice.\
\
'I beg your forgiveness, Olórin, Mithrandir, Gandalf. I wished it were not necessary to speak of it, but speak of it I will, if there is no other way.'","Find Tûka outside the entrance to the tunnel of Halroth","'I do not understand Glorfindel's reluctance, ${PLAYER}. I have studied the records of the Siege of Barad-dûr and understand well the price of victory over Sauron. I know too that the victory did not last, and it would be many thousands of years before Sauron's ultimate defeat.\
\
'There is nothing Glorfindel need keep from me, and his belief that I will be disturbed by this tale of the Bright Company is most puzzling to me. I say he should speak on, and delay no further.'","'Well done! You defeated just the right number, I would say: not too many nor too few. The passage of the Bright Company should be unremarked upon, which is better than we might have hoped!\
\
'There is nothing else you need help me with at Halroth. You may as well return to Adambel, and relay the news that the tunnel entrance is less-watched than it might have been.'","'I think you've almost got it! But not quite!'","Vëamacil is at Adambel, and he wishes to speak with you.","'There are a lot of eyes out here. We should thin out some of the foes this near to Halroth, but not so many as to be suspicious. You had better get to it!'","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send","'\\qNot too many, nor too few,\\q Tûka had said, and that was all.'","Glorfindel closes his eyes, and nods with reluctant agreement","'But there are still preparations to be made before the Bright Company departs. You should find the Hól-budlan matriarch Tûka, somewhere to the east of our encampments, for she intended to scout the entrance to the tunnel upon which our hope rests.'","Defeat enemies in the vicinity of the entrance to the tunnel of Halroth, in Emyn Duir.\
\
Tûka thinks you should defeat watchful eyes near the entrance to Halroth, not too many and not too few.","'This way... and be as quiet as you can.'","Defeat just the right number of enemies outside Halroth, in Emyn Duir","'The Hól-budlan could move about unseen, and Tûka was the most skilled of them all.'","Gandalf is on Tol Send. He has listened with interest to the tale told by the shade of Isildur, but does not understand the need for Glorfindel's interruption.","Glorfindel is on Tol Send, and he has volunteered to complete the tale begun by the shade of Isildur, despite his misgivings.","Talk to Vëamacil at Adambel"},
[2912]={"'Kûr Anzar is occupied by soldiers of Ordâkh and cultists of the Church of the All-seeing?\
\
'Our companions cannot have gone there, ${PLAYER}.'","Place a boundary stone on the slope to the southern pavilion in Vartúlin","Travel toward Kûr Anzar, to the north of Vartúlin","'I am embarrassed, ${PLAYER}. At least Thórvilon is a friend, and understands the difficulties I have faced in these past few years. They have become more frequent as Tróthul seeks to claim me, but I will not allow it.\
\
'I am eager to meet the others of your company, for speaking with new folk and having new experiences will help me to stave off Tróthul. It has ever been so, and this adventure seems to me no different.'","Sigileth is outside Adakûr in Imhûlar.","You pick up a number of stones from the pile","Having satisfied Thórvilon's request, you should return to the centre of Vartúlin and check on Silirtas.","'The protective arts with which we ward our groves have become less effective over time, but it is the hope of the Kintai that they will forestall the encroaching darkness long enough for us to discover a lasting solution. We have inscribed runes of guarding and renewal upon boundary stones that must be placed along the perimeter of Vartúlin.\
\
'Will you retrieve some of the boundary stones from the pile across the bridge and set them along the borders of the grove? I will remain with Silirtas until she returns to herself.'","Placed boundary stone","Sigileth calls for a halt and says you should defeat the wights near Adakûr","You arrive at an ideal location for scouting Kûr Anzar","'Go to the north-east and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> toward the city of Kûr Anzar. We must know what awaits us within.'","Pick up boundary stones from the pile across the bridge in Vartúlin","Chapter 12.3: The Encroaching Darkness","That should be enough stones to fulfil Thórvilon's request.","Sigileth is in Vartúlin.","'I am eager to meet the others of your company, for speaking with new folk and having new experiences will help me to stave off Tróthul. It has ever been so, and this adventure seems to me no different.'","'These wights were disturbed by something nearby, ${PLAYER}, and I fear the hand of the Church of the All-seeing in this.\
\
'Go to the north-east and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> toward the city of Kûr Anzar. We must know what awaits us within.'","Sigileth wants to rejoin the rest of your travelling company at Kûr Anzar, to the north of Vartúlin.","'We should defeat some of the wights near Adakûr.'","Kûr Anzar is filled with soldiers and cultists. Your companions cannot have gone there","Thórvilon has enlisted your help to protect Vartúlin and the Kintai from the encroaching darkness that threatens Imhûlar.","Talk to Silirtas in the centre of Vartúlin","Sigileth wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at Kûr Anzar from a location to the north-east and determine the situation inside the city.","'Yes. We have lent some aid to Thórvilon, now we should continue on to the north-east to rejoin the company. My brother Corudan will be very pleased to meet Silirtas and to learn of her people, as was I.\
\
'I have said our farewells to Thórvilon. Now we should travel to the north, from where we can assess the situation in Kûr Anzar. Silirtas said the Kingdom of Hamât was absorbed by Ordâkh, and the city may not be friendly to us or to the representatives of Umbar we seek to rejoin.'","A pile of the boundary stones can be found across the bridge in Vartúlin.","Place a boundary stone at the western entrance to Vartúlin","Defeat wights near Adakûr in Imhûlar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should defeat some of the Dead that lurk at Adakûr before they threaten the folk that live in Imhûlar.","Place a boundary stone at the north-eastern entrance to Vartúlin","'Will you retrieve some of the boundary stones from the pile across the bridge and set them along the borders of the grove? I will remain with Silirtas until she returns to herself.'","Talk to Sigileth in Vartúlin","Defeated wights near Adakûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at Kûr Anzar from here","Find the location to the north-east from which to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at Kûr Anzar","'Let us travel northward, from where we can assess the situation in Kûr Anzar without venturing within the city. Silirtas said the Kingdom of Hamât was absorbed by Ordâkh, and the city may not be friendly to us or to the representatives of Umbar we seek to rejoin.'","Talk to Sigileth outside Adakûr","Place a boundary stone north of Thórvilon","Thórvilon has asked you to place boundary stones around the edges of Vartúlin."},
[2913]={"Your companions within Urmâkh eagerly await the tale of your adventures.","Corudan, Sirgon, and Rahâzi eagerly wait to hear the tale of your adventures","Corudan, Sirgon, and Rahâzi are within Urmâkh.","Spoke to residents of Urmâkh about Gondor (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Sirgon is within the city of Urmâkh.","'Nowhere in any of these lands would hide such a gathering as that from outside attention, Sigileth!' cries Silirtas.\
\
'But if they came to Imhûlar and planned to stop at Kûr Anzar, they might have turned from that course and stayed for a time at Urmâkh.\
\
'If we go to the north-west and search within the city of Urmâkh, we may find your friends.'","Sigileth waits for Silirtas to answer.","Your companions consider the tale you have woven","'I am pleased you and Sigileth have returned to us, ${PLAYER}. We have had little in the way of success since you left us.'\
\
Sirgon's demeanour is downcast, and you ask him what troubles him. He sighs and kicks a stone in the grass.\
\
'I have been engaged in an argument with the warrior-woman Rahâzi, and it has enshrouded me in a storm-cloud of ill feeling. She speaks of beloved Kings of Gondor as if they were tyrants, and says King Elessar will be no different than they! The title \\qHyarmendacil\\q is a noble one in Gondor, and memory of the Kings who wear it brings to mind many triumphs throughout history! But Rahâzi treats these victors as if they were monstrous regents and bloodthirsty warmongers! How are the rulers of her land remembered in Gondor, I ask you? How might she defend such as they?\
\
'King Elessar is a man of noble heart and bearing. How can I convince Rahâzi of what I know to be the truth?'","Silirtas is outside Adakûr in Imhûlar.","'I am worried about this substance sought by Azagath and Nakási. If this is truly as destructive as it sounds, we must prevent them from finding it at any cost. The others of our group have gone in search of their trail. The occupation of Kûr Anzar has made that more difficult than it might have been.'","'They are wrong, ${PLAYER}! King Elessar is a good man, and he will live up to his promise, for both Gondor and for Shagâna. The kings of old that took the title of Hyarmendacil were neither as wise nor as just as King Elessar. He will not become as they were.'","Talk to Silirtas outside Adakûr in Imhûlar","Rahâzi challenged you to speak with residents of Urmâkh and learn their opinions of Gondor.","Talk to Sirgon within Urmâkh","'¡Por fin!'","'Shagâna has always suffered at the hands of Gondor. When the Black Númenórean Castamiri departed from that kingdom and established the union of the Khôrthan League, it was to Shagâna that the Gondorian king Vinyarion pursued them, bringing war and death. He stopped not there, but continued deeper into lands that held no enemies for him. He burned the great city of Shâraban in a tremendous conflagration, and its charred bones still smolder today.\
\
'This was the man who took the title of Hyarmendacil II. We name him Ugdûmu, the Butcher. They say he had a change of heart in his elder years, and repented of the evil he wrought. I believe it not.'","Corudan, Sirgon, and Rahâzi are within the city of Urmâkh.","With Kûr Anzar occupied by soldiers and cultists of the Church of the All-seeing, your travelling companions must have gone somewhere else.","'This man of Gondor thinks to lecture the daughter of Girhâzi about the history of her own people? Do you know the meaning of the title \\qHyarmendacil\\q worn by his beloved kings, ${PLAYER}? He told me the meaning of it is \\qSouth-victor.\\q\
\
'The Shagâni have given titles of our own to one of those kings. The ruler known in Gondor as Hyarmendacil the First is known in Ambarûl as Lûgula, \\qthe Despot of the North.\\q The second Gondorian king to claim the title of Hyarmendacil has a different title among the people whose ancestors he slaughtered. He is called Ugdûmu: \\qthe Butcher.\\q\
\
'Speak to the folk who dwell in this village and you will see that your Gondorian friend knows not of what he speaks.'","Speak to residents of Urmâkh about Gondor (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Tell your companions what befell you while you were apart","'You speak to my friends about Kings of Gondor? You are bold to speak so, stranger. Hyarmendacil means \\qSouth-victor,\\q and all who claimed this title wear evil reputations in Shagâna. Others have sought to achieve that title through conquest and bloodshed, and failed.\
\
'A king named Minardil sought to become Hyarmendacil III, but he was slain by the Heirs of Castamir before he could adopt it properly. The Heirsworn of today are no friends of mine... but to cease the glory-seeking of a third Hyarmendacil seems to me fine work indeed.\
\
'That title remains unclaimed to this day, but who can say whether the new King of Gondor will think to increase his own glory and the size of his kingdom by adopting the title of Hyarmendacil III, though it lie long dormant? The histories of this land teach us unpleasant lessons, stranger; perhaps you should heed them.'","Find your travelling companions somewhere in Imhûlar, perhaps in the city of Urmâkh","Talk to Corudan within Urmâkh","'King Elessar is a man of noble heart and bearing. How can I convince Rahâzi of what I know to be the truth?'","'When my sister told me she wanted to meet with the Elves of the Oasis, I did not think she would bring one back with her! It is a pleasure to meet you, Silirtas, and I am eager to learn more about you and your people. If there is anything you would hear from me concerning the Land of Lothlórien or the other places I have seen on my travels, you have only to ask.'\
\
Corudan turns to you, his welcoming expression replaced with one of great concern.\
\
'I am worried about this substance sought by Azagath and Nakási. If it is truly as destructive as it sounds, we must prevent them from finding it at any cost. The others of our group went in search of their trail while we spoke with the people here in Urmâkh. The occupation of Kûr Anzar has made locating our prey more difficult than it might have otherwise been.'","Find your travelling companions in the village of Urmâkh, north-west of Adakûr.","'If your friends came to Imhûlar and planned to stop at Kûr Anzar, they might have turned from that course and stayed for a time at Urmâkh. Let us go to the north-west and search within Urmâkh for your companions.'","Talk to Rahâzi within Urmâkh","'Speak to the folk who dwell in this village and you will see that your Gondorian friend knows not of what he speaks.'","Chapter 12.4: A Change of Plans","'Stories of the Gondorian kings who named themselves Hyarmendacil are well-known to my people, for they are brutal tales of conquest and despair; they are also lessons to us. The first of these, Ciryaher Hyarmendacil, he we name \\qLûgula,\\q conquered the coasts and held them with the sword, that he might affirm his kingdom's control of the seas; the lands in the interior were made border-marches of Gondor. He installed puppet-kings in these cities of Shagâna, and took their children to live in Gondor as hostages.\
\
'Thus was their good behaviour ensured, but he returned every seven years to reaffirm the loyalties of the kings. When he finally died, the Ambarûli celebrated so enthusiastically that a unit of Gondorian soldiers was sent to restore order, and dozens perished.\
\
'One hundred years after his death, another sought to attain glory in our lands, but through great force of will and show of arms, the Shagâni dealt him defeat after defeat. He retreated, and from the safety of his northern home he felt he could not claim the title of Hyarmendacil. That spared him not from becoming known in Shagâna as \\qLûgula-min,\\q the Second Despot.'","'Where might our companions have gone instead? Silirtas, is there a settlement somewhere within Imhûlar where folk of Gondor, Umbar, and Shagâna might gather together without drawing notice? The group includes a dwarf, an Elf, and a half-troll as well. Also, the half-troll's lion, should that affect your answer.'\
\
If you did not know the Elf-warrior so well, you might think Sigileth was jesting. She catches your eye and holds it with her own while she waits for Silirtas to answer."},
[2914]={"Chapter 12.4: The Glory of the Bright Company","'Listen now to the last glory of the Bright Company, and may it prove worth the sorrow I foresee in its telling.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'Forgive me, Olórin, Mithrandir, Gandalf. Forgive me, Lendelen.'","'Do not trouble yourself, Glorfindel, on my account. All that was kept from me has been restored, and I do not begrudge you for keeping secret that which the Valar hid from me. Indeed, in this knowledge I find reassurance, for I see now that my reluctance to oppose Sauron directly was borne from Lendelen's sad fate. And is it not true that Frodo's quest proved successful, and the Ring and the Dark Lord both defeated at one stroke? Indirect opposition found success where direct opposition could not, and in that I may say the Bright Company came at last to have its greatest triumph.\
\
'But I remember now that which I did not before. I know the end of the tale.'","Talk to Glorfindel on Tol Send and complete 'Instance: The Glory of the Bright Company'","Talk to Glorfindel on Tol Send","Glorfindel is on Tol Send. He has agreed to finish the tale begun by the shade of Isildur, despite his misgivings.","Glorfindel has volunteered to finish the tale begun by the shade of Isildur, for he fought alongside the Bright Company and remembers both the triumph and the sorrow they encountered within the Dark Tower.","Glorfindel is on Tol Send.","'And so it is done, ${PLAYER}. When I beheld Olórin in a new guise in this Third Age, I knew him to be Lendelen come again. And yet he knew nothing of his former life, and remembered nothing of the trials he endured within Barad-dûr.\
\
'I could think of one reason only for that: the Valar had kept the memory of that experience from him as a mercy and a kindness. For if he remembered the cruel tortures he suffered at the hands of Sauron, how could he oppose the Dark Lord upon his return, knowing the extent of Sauron's malice?\
\
'And so we chose not to speak of Lendelen or his sad fate within the Dark Tower during the final days of the Second Age. I did not wish to inflict this harm upon Olórin, Mithrandir, or Gandalf... and for that I beg his forgiveness. Lendelen was my closest advisor, my dearest friend, and I failed him. I thought it best to leave his memory behind, for if that was the purpose of the Valar I would not wish to do otherwise.'","'Will you hear me, then?'","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send","Gandalf is on Tol Send."},
[2915]={"'One of the residents here, Sharûkh, spoke of a need for various animal parts that might be put to a number of different uses: legs from toads, bristles from something called a zizanu, and the stingers from deadly scorpions. No enemy of these folk would gather such items as these for them, would they? I would really appreciate your gathering these items for Sharûkh, ${PLAYER}, and so would the King!'","Rahâzi wants you to defeat cultists throughout Imhûlar, especially in the occupied city of Kûr Anzar.","Collected scorpion stingers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect toad legs in Imhûlar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected zizanu bristles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You should speak to Irnamar about the work you have done combatting the Barkhûshim.'","Defeated cultists in Imhûlar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You fought cultists of Barkhûsh?\
\
'You have done some good here today, stranger. I am not one to turn away help when it is offered; neither am I one to withhold my gratitude when a good deed is done on my behalf. So you have the thanks of Irnamar for fighting against these foes of my people.\
\
'That is all you will have. I hope you expected nothing more.'","Sirgon has spoken with the people of Urmâkh and wants you to bring them, on behalf of Gondor, some of the ingredients for which they have asked.","'You have the thanks of Irnamar for fighting against the cultists of Barkhûsh.'","Chapter 12.5: Not An Enemy, If Not A Friend","Bring the ingredients to Sharûkh within Urmâkh","'I want to prove that Gondor is not an enemy to the people here, ${PLAYER}, and that King Elessar is different than the rulers of the past whose names the Shagâni curse.\
\
'One of the residents here, Sharûkh, spoke of a need for various animal parts that might be put to a number of different uses: legs from toads, bristles from something called a zizanu, and the stingers from deadly scorpions. No enemy of these folk would gather such items as these for them, would they?\
\
'I would really appreciate your gathering these items for Sharûkh, ${PLAYER}, and so would the King!'","'I am glad we have done what we could on behalf of King Elessar and Gondor, as little as it might have been. It is my hope that our words and deeds will be here remembered in the days ahead, and such will serve the cause of peace between these lands. We may not yet be friends, but I would have us first not be enemies.\
\
'I am glad we did what we could for the folk of Urmâkh, but it is time for us to be on our way. Belondor has sent word to us that they have located the trail of Azagath.'","Collect scorpion stingers in Imhûlar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Sirgon within Urmâkh","'Sirgon is eager to prove the worth of his king and his kingdom? Then let his friends prove his trust is not misplaced!\
\
'There are cultists of Barkhûsh throughout Imhûlar and in the city of Kûr Anzar, ${PLAYER}. Deal them a grave injury and perhaps the folk of this village will understand Sirgon's trust in his liege lord. You should then relate the good you have done to the woman Irnamar. I spoke with her earlier and she bemoaned the evils done by the cultists in Kûr Anzar.\
\
'You will not remove centuries of distrust from the hearts of these folk with one deed on their behalf, ${PLAYER}. At least you will make more safe the road we must take, if nothing else.'","Sirgon is within Urmâkh.","Collected toad legs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Irnamar within Urmâkh","Sirgon wants to prove that Gondor is not a threat to the people of Shagâna.","Sharûkh is within Urmâkh, waiting for you to bring the ingredients Sirgon promised.","Irnamar is within Urmâkh.","'There are cultists of Barkhûsh throughout Imhûlar, ${PLAYER}. Deal them a grave injury and perhaps the folk of this village will understand Sirgon's trust in his liege lord. At least you will make more safe the road we must take, if nothing else.'","Rahâzi is within Urmâkh.","'If your Gondorian friend believes we will forget centuries of ill use by his kingdom and his rulers, his head is full of rocks. Still, I appreciate it.'","Collect zizanu bristles in Imhûlar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'This work of yours is a help to me, but if your Gondorian friend believes we will forget centuries of ill use by his kingdom and his rulers, his head is full of rocks.\
\
'Still, I appreciate it. These items contain traces of the disease that plagues these creatures, and our land, but with careful handling they can still be of use to me.'","Talk to Rahâzi within Urmâkh","Defeat cultists in Imhûlar and the city of Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2916]={"His memory restored by the words of Glorfindel, much that was hidden from Gandalf has been returned to him: pain, loss, and suffering, but knowledge also.","Elrond is on Tol Send, and he wishes to pick up the tale where Gandalf has left it.","Talk to Elrond on Tol Send","'While Sauron tormented Lendelen within Barad-dûr, the leaders of the Great Alliance met once more in secret. A trap was decided upon, a trap with which to ensnare Sauron and draw him forth from his tower.\
\
'The Lady Galadriel had remained at Minas Ithil after she and Lord Celeborn drove the Nazgûl from the valley. Now she sent her thought to Lendelen, and she spoke directly through Sauron's prisoner to the Dark Lord. \\qOne broke the gates of Ithil,\\q Lendelen said, his last breaths upon him, and Sauron laughed, for he had the mastery.\
\
'\\qTwo sundered the ramparts of Morannon,\\q Lendelen continued, and doubt began to gnaw at the Dark Lord. He had long feared the Elven-rings, and in his secret heart he dreaded to think they could be used against him.\
\
'\\qBut Three...\\q Lendelen said as the last of his strength departed. \\qThe power of the Three, wielded together, shall cast you down at last.\\q\
\
'And so Lendelen perished, and his final words remained hidden to me for this past Age. But now I know what they wrought, for it was by this message that the Deceiver was himself deceived. Sauron climbed to the pinnacle of Barad-dûr, and looking from that vast height he beheld a shining figure ascending the slopes of Mount Doom. Fear seized him, and he imagined that Gil-galad possessed all three Elven-rings, and would use them together to destroy him. For the Three were hidden from his sight, but he thought he could sense they had been united at last.'","'I remember this day. It is burned upon my memory, and will not fade.'","Chapter 12.5: The End of the Tale","'I was with my king on this day. I know what then befell.\
\
'The Dark Lord opened his gates and emptied Barad-dûr, unleashing the last of his armies in a final bid to destroy those who besieged him. On the slopes of Mount Doom he brandished his black mace Mordagnir, wading through friend and foe alike, until at last he faced the High Kings of the Alliance. The One Ring shone on his finger, and he sent forth his evil thought, seeking to dominate Gil-galad's mind when he donned the Three.\
\
'But he did not see it. Gil-galad threw back his head and laughed at Sauron, and the Dark Lord was filled with rage. \\qThe rings of my people may be together,\\q my liege declared, \\qbut they are far from here. Far from you.\\q And Sauron knew he had been deceived, lured from the safety of his tower, and he knew his peril. But above all else he desired to inflict anguish upon those arrayed before him. He sent his will into the One Ring, and his foes were held fast by its spell. Sauron fell upon them in deadly combat, and great gouts of ash and flame roared from the peak of Mount Doom.\
\
'I stood on the slope, too far to aid my king, but near enough to feel the terrible heat of that battle. Even now I can feel it, and I know the pain of that day anew.'"},
[2917]={"Now abandoned by its former occupants, this camp will suit your purpose","The rest of your travelling company has gone ahead to scout the road into Urash Dâr, and you should help them prepare for the next leg of their pursuit.","Light the camp-fire at the abandoned town in Urash Dâr","Talk to Belondor at the road into Urash Dâr","The fire dances, bringing new life to the abandoned town","Talk to Rothog at the road into Urash Dâr","Talk to Silirtas at your new campsite in Urash Dâr","Wait for your companions to arrive","Meet up with the rest of your travelling party in north-east Imhûlar, on the road into Urash Dâr","'No one seems to know where Nakási has gone. She may have quarrelled with Azagath and taken her leave of him, or he may have sent her somewhere with orders to carry out. All we know for certain is that when Azagath passed into Urash Dâr, he did so alone.\
\
'The scout with whom we spoke told us friendly folk once lived at a small village to the north-west, a short distance from here, but when last he passed that way the town was abandoned. Enough may remain of the town that it would serve us well as a foothold from which we might explore within Urash Dâr.\
\
'Will you go ahead and light the fire at this abandoned campsite? When the entirety of our group has there assembled it will become the foundation of our activities within Urash Dâr, and from there we can more effectively search for Azagath.'","Belondor stands by the road leading into Urash Dâr.","You have been charged with setting up camp at the abandoned town to the north-west in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Khôltekh at the road into Urash Dâr","Belondor stands by the road that runs into Urash Dâr.","'I have an uneasy feeling about this place, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'No, the campsite is fine. There is something wrong about the air of this place. Something is not right. I feel as if some evil slumbered within the canyons of Urash Dâr, but it has awoken... and there is something else.\
\
'It is hungry.'","'It is good to see you again. I trust your journey with Sigileth the Elf went well? Our own search has proved fruitful, for we encountered a Shagâni scout who reported seeing Azagath travel alone into Urash Dâr, the furrow-lands to the north. We questioned the scout at some length, and he was quite certain that Azagath travelled alone. Where Nakási has gone no one seems to know.\
\
'What did you discover on your own journey after you parted with us at Ghalbûru, ${PLAYER}?'","'They wait for us along the road into Urash Dâr, located to the north-east of Imhûlar. We should rejoin them before they capture Azagath and Nakási without us!'","You tell Belondor about your adventures, but make no mention of Balakhad","'¡Aquí!'","Belondor is at the road into Urash Dâr, waiting to hear what befell you and Sigileth after you parted in Ghalbûru.","Find the abandoned town to the north-west in Urash Dâr","You have been charged with setting up camp at the abandoned town in Urash Dâr.","Tell Belondor a careful version of what befell you since you parted in Ghalbûru","Belondor sees you approach and calls out a greeting","Khôltekh and Rothog listened to your story, and they have some thoughts of their own.","Chapter 12.6: Among the Furrows","Your companions arrive and try to make themselves at home","A good location for a camp can be found to the north-west in Urash Dâr, at a town recently abandoned by its former occupants.","'Did you find your visit with the Elves of the Oasis a waste of time, ${PLAYER}, as I said it would be?'\
\
Khôltekh laughs suddenly, interrupting your response.\
\
'I am only jesting. I am certain it was of great value. I understand you have brought one of them with you? How strange it must be for her to leave her grove. The world outside must be more dangerous than that to which she is accustomed.'","'They wait for us along the road into Urash Dâr, located in north-east Imhûlar. We should rejoin them before they capture Azagath and Nakási without us!'","Silirtas is at your new campsite in Urash Dâr.","The rest of your travelling party should be in north-east Imhûlar, on the road into Urash Dâr.","'Some of the people we spoke to described a dreadful presence lurking in the canyons ahead. They say whatever this evil might be, it has only come to haunt the furrow-lands in the past few months.\
\
'I do not want to raise my hopes or those of Húrshauk too high, ${PLAYER}, but I hope this evil presence is of the sort that wields weapons. There has been too much walking and not enough fighting on this journey for my taste, and that is true for Húrshauk as well, who feels as I do!'","'Will you go ahead and light the fire at this abandoned campsite? When the entirety of our group has there assembled it will become the foundation of our activities within Urash Dâr, and from there we can more effectively search for Azagath.'"},
[2918]={"'I do not wish to shame Silirtas, ${PLAYER}, but do you think it is wise for her to accompany you beyond the walls of Maurûsh? Should she grow distant at an inopportune moment, she would endanger both your life and her own.\
\
'Perhaps I should go in her stead.'","Silirtas senses that something evil dwells within Urash Dâr, and she is troubled by its presence.","Talk to Mithrandir at your campsite in Urash Dâr","Silirtas wants you to creep closer and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for what might be happening within Maurûsh.","Silirtas is at your campsite in Urash Dâr, preparing to go with you to Maurûsh.","'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. The sensation is unpleasant, but there is something more: it is familiar, somehow. I cannot understand it. The Kintai never dwelled among these canyons, and to my knowledge neither did the Temámir. Men and hill-folk may have fled here from other kingdoms elsewhere in Shagâna, but this has always been an overlooked place. If it was ever otherwise it is beyond my memory, and beyond that of my people.\
\
'But something evil dwells within Urash Dâr now, that much is certain. I cannot determine where exactly it dwells unless we search among the canyons.\
\
'The Ordâkhai built a stone keep, Maurûsh, from which they might oversee the approach from Imhûlar. It should be located across the river to the west. If you scout the approach to Maurûsh you may learn the identity of the sleeping evil within Urash Dâr.'","Talk to Silirtas at your new campsite in Urash Dâr","'You are fortunate I arrived at this moment, ${PLAYER}, for you could not stand against these foes without my help!'","'Perhaps I should go in her stead.'","Silirtas is at your campsite in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Silirtas at your campsite in Urash Dâr","Mithrandir has come to your campsite in Urash Dâr.","Silirtas wears a hurt expression. When she speaks again, her voice is barely above a whisper.\
\
'I believed we had an understanding, ${PLAYER}. I see now that I was deceived! Sigileth is welcome to accompany us, but I will not be left behind. I want to help you investigate Maurûsh, and I am insulted that you think to cast me aside so readily!\
\
'For what purpose do I fight against Tróthul if my allies will not permit me to aid them? Why do I resist the... ailment... inflicting my people if my friends abandon me at the first sign of danger? You weave a Veróth around me even without Sarláshi trees; the prison is made of your own words!\
\
'All of my senses scream that there is evil in Urash Dâr. I want to face it. Speak to me when you are ready to search for it, or I will go by myself to Maurûsh, and you will be the one abandoned!'","Sigileth coughs apologetically and draws you aside","'I want to go with you to investigate Maurûsh. I must see the situation within those walls with my own eyes.'","The sound of Orkish voices, not of the Ordâkhai, drifts from Maurûsh","All seems still within Maurûsh","Silirtas does not speak again, but it is clear she has been deeply hurt. Sigileth begins to say something, but then decides against it.\
\
The three of you prepare to depart for Maurûsh.","Talk to Sigileth at your campsite in Urash Dâr","Silirtas wants you to cross the river to the west and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the stone keep of Maurûsh.","Sigileth is at your campsite in Urash Dâr.","Cross the river to the west and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> in the direction of Maurûsh","'The Ordâkhai built a stone keep, Maurûsh, from which they might oversee the approach from Imhûlar. It should be located across the river to the west. If you scout the approach to Maurûsh you may learn the identity of the sleeping evil within Urash Dâr.'","Creep closer and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for sounds from Maurûsh","Silirtas is at your new campsite in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Silirtas and go with her into Maurûsh","Chapter 12.7: Something Has Awoken","'You say there are Orcs within Maurûsh? That is very unusual, for that keep was built by the Ordâkhai. Without the ruling grip of the Dark Lord I would not expect those two groups to work together, however unhappily.\
\
'I want to go with you to investigate Maurûsh. I must see the situation within those walls with my own eyes.'"},
[2919]={"Talk to Mithrandir at your campsite in Urash Dâr","Talk to Elrohir in Urash Dâr","Find Legolas and Gimli to the north-west of your campsite","Whether by chance or plan, friends have come from afar to lend you their aid. Now they must be brought together to face this new danger.","Talk to Gimli in Urash Dâr","Find Glorfindel to the east of your campsite","'Did you know Mithrandir has journeyed in these lands before now? He spoke of his travels to us as we came south through Harondor. When he walked here long ago, the people who dwelt in this land named him \\qInkanûsh.\\q'\
\
'He spoke too of the Kintai, the Elves of the Oasis who tend to beautiful groves throughout the region.'\
\
You tell Elrohir that one of the Kintai has come with you to Urash Dâr.\
\
'I will be most pleased to speak with her!' he exclaims.","Talk to Glorfindel in Urash Dâr","'The companions that came with me from the north have all returned to camp? Good. Then it is time for me to tell you what I have learned, and what must be done to face it.'\
\
Mithrandir scans the distant horizon and leans upon his staff, gathering his thoughts. When he speaks again, his voice is cold.\
\
'A great evil sleeps in Urash Dâr, undisturbed for thousands of years. It has only now begun to awaken, for the enchantment that kept it from stirring would last until all knowledge of it passed beyond living memory.\
\
'The last to know of this evil used many names, ${PLAYER}. In these lands he was called Barkhûsh. Folk in the north knew him as Sauron. In every land he was the Dark Lord, but he served another in ages past; his master was Morgoth, the great enemy of the world. With the destruction of the One Ring and the death of Sauron, this enchantment, the Geas of Morgoth, has been lifted.\
\
'Morgoth can no longer trouble the circles of the world, but this evil he set in the roots of the earth has outlived even his greatest servant.'","Legolas and Gimli greet you warmly","Talk to Legolas in Urash Dâr","Find Elladan and Elrohir to the north-east of your campsite","'When we left you in Umbar Baharbêl, I thought it would be much longer before we saw you again, ${PLAYER}! But no sooner had we delivered Nimrodel to the shores of Gondor than Mithrandir sent urgent word that he had need of us.\
\
'The journeys Gimli and I planned to take must wait. After all, it is not wise to refuse a Wizard's call.'","Mithrandir has sent you to recall the scouts he sent to the north-west and north-east of Urash Dâr.","'We must find and return the folk I sent in search of you, for we will need them all if we are to face this threat. Seek for Legolas, Gimli, the sons of Elrond, and Glorfindel among the canyons of Urash Dâr. When you have returned with them I will tell you what I know of the great evil that stirs in this land, and how we must stand against it.'","Glorfindel greets you cordially, but his expression remains solemn","'We meet now in unhappier circumstances than a wedding at midsummer, ${PLAYER}, but still it is good to see you. When Mithrandir called for my aid upon arriving at Minas Tirith, I could not refuse it. Never would I refuse such a call.\
\
'If only the Bright Company could have been assembled. Alas, that noble group belongs to another age, and many of those worthies have already departed for the West. I fear even the full complement of the Bright Company might not be enough to face this evil.\
\
'When you learn from Mithrandir what it is we must oppose you will understand. I will see you back at the camp after you have spoken to the others.'","Talk to Elladan in Urash Dâr","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. The merchant vessel that delivered us and the Lady Nimrodel back to Gondor benefitted from full sails, and the seas were calm. The voyage north was much more enjoyable than the one that bore us to Umbar by way of the Shield Isles, with not so much as a cloud in the sky!\
\
'But Gandalf had need of us, and this dwarf would not refuse him... especially not once we met up with him and he said we would travel south on land, through Harondor, and not by ship again so soon!'","Elladan and Elrohir look around curiously, intrigued by the rocks of Urash Dâr","Chapter 12.8: Friends From the North","Mithrandir is at your campsite in Urash Dâr.","'After my brother and I completed our work, we returned to Minas Tirith. While there, we received word from Mithrandir that he had urgent need of us to face some hidden threat.\
\
'Elessar would have come himself, but Mithrandir refused him. With such as we to protect him I know not why, but the Wizard was most clear that Elessar should remain in Gondor and not come south with us.'","'Yes, yes, it is good to see you again. But there is no time to waste now, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'When I at last understood the danger that stirred in these lands, I came from the North in great haste with a number of companions. Not knowing how best to find you, I sent them to search in several different directions. You are fortunate I chose the same path on which you and the Elves were bound, for if I had not found you at that moment...'\
\
Mithrandir falls silent, and taps his staff on the rocky ground.\
\
'Enough of that. But we must find and return the folk I sent in search of you, for we will need them all if we are to face this threat. Seek for Legolas, Gimli, the sons of Elrond, and Glorfindel among the canyons of Urash Dâr. When you have returned with them I will tell you what I know of the great evil that stirs in this land, and how we must stand against it.'"},
[2920]={"Hear what Mithrandir has to say about the Elder Orcs","Hear what Mithrandir has to say about the Grim Southron","Mithrandir is at your campsite in Urash Dâr.","Mithrandir has much to say about a number of different subjects.","Mithrandir wishes to tell you what he has learned about the Geas of Morgoth, and what it could mean for Middle-earth.","Talk to Mithrandir at your campsite in Urash Dâr","'If only I had learned this before now. The deathly spirits of Thuringwath knew of Sauron's rivalry with his banished master, and of his search for the unknown powers Morgoth left behind, but they were slow to reveal these things to me. From their speech and from evil runes carved into the very foundations of Mordor I have pieced together this tale, but the learning came slowly.\
\
'Too slowly, ${PLAYER}. When I understood the magnitude of this threat, I returned to Minas Tirith with all of the haste Shadowfax had to give. I sent word to our trusted allies and our lean band hurried south through Harondor with utmost speed.\
\
'We must fight, ${PLAYER}. We must fight this legacy of Morgoth, or the Sere Ones will restore the Dominion of Zíkar and bring about a new age of darkness in Middle-earth.'","'Memory of the Utûgi and the Thardúth dimmed. In time, only the very eldest of the Kintai surviving in Shagâna remembered these servants of Morgoth. As they began to fade in the manner of their people, those memories vanished with them.\
\
'But Sauron remembered. In the ages that followed, he sent his servants to seek the hidden vaults of the Thardúth, hungering for their power and the secret of breeding anew the mighty Utûgi. The Nazgûl searched for the Sere Ones, but they searched in vain; the geas of Morgoth remained effective. Sauron despaired of ever locating the lost vaults, and turned his attention and his cunning to other matters.'","Hear what Mithrandir has to say about the Kintai","Hear what Mithrandir has to say about the Dark Lord Sauron","Chapter 12.9: Legacy of Morgoth","Hear what Mithrandir has to say about the Thardúth","'In Elder Days the world was greatly changed from its present form; Morgoth coveted it all. His fortress at Thangorodrim served as the seat of his power, but his servants went forth and established the control of their master in lands far distant. One such dominion subjugated for centuries the territory that is today called Shagâna, or Near Harad by the Gondorians. The tyrants of this dominion served Morgoth in all things; their empire was called Zíkar, and trustworthy accounts of it have disappeared. What remains of its history is hard to decipher by any but the most learned among the Wise.\
\
'But to understand the rise of Zíkar you must learn first of the Kintai, the Elves who did not join the Valar in the West. They once knew a great deal about Zíkar, but in the centuries since that empire disappeared they have tried to forget.'","'The eldest of the Kintai were twisted and corrupted into these Sere Ones by rites too vile to contemplate; the Thardúth rose in importance and power until they had become the deadliest rulers of Zíkar. Morgoth charged them with maintaining a tyrannical hold over the lands of the east and south, breeding as many Elder Orcs as they could for his war. When the call came at last, Orcs and wicked men departed for the north in vast numbers, swelling Morgoth's hordes in distant Beleriand.\
\
'But Morgoth's might did not prevail against the combined forces of the Elves and the Valar, and when Beleriand sank beneath the sea the Utûgi sent by the Thardúth were drowned and forgotten. Following the defeat of their dark master, the Thardúth that remained in Zíkar feared uprisings by the emboldened Men of Shagâna, but so too they feared the reprisal of Sauron, who they blamed in part for Morgoth's defeat. Using all of their sorcerous powers they set a geas upon their vaults, sealing them shut and deeming that their location should never be found so long as any lived in Middle-earth who remembered them.\
\
'They took what remained of their Utûgi deep into their sealed vaults and with witchcraft caused them to sleep, never again to wake while their halls remained shut. Last they did the same to themselves, lying down in the dark depths to await the hoped-for day when they could return to the living world above.'","'I believe now that Sauron could never break the geas of Morgoth, for so long as he remembered the Thardúth the enchantment of the Sere Ones could not be undone.\
\
'But then the most unlikely of events transpired: Frodo Baggins accepted the Quest of the Ring. Sauron's Ring was destroyed. Morgoth's greatest servant perished. The Thardúth passed beyond the memory of any who lived in the world, and the seal upon their hidden vaults was broken.\
\
'Sauron was gone, but the Sere Ones, servants of Morgoth his dark master, were loosed once again upon the world.'","'These were the Elder Orcs, fashioned in the pits beneath Zíkar by foul craft of Morgoth. Memory of them faded over the passage of centuries; even the name that was given to them, \\qUtûgi,\\q brought to mind only dimly-remembered images, unfamiliar and indistinct demons of the ancient world.\
\
'The Utûgi possessed a size, strength, and cunning that Sauron coveted but could not replicate; the Orcs he bred in later years could not match those that belonged to his master, and that deficiency rankled. But the Utûgi were not the worst of the evils loosed upon the world by the Dominion of Zíkar, though they passed beyond all living memory in the years since. These were the Thardúth, the Sere Ones, and they served Morgoth in all things.'","'During the early years of the First Age, various kingdoms of Men began to arise throughout Shagâna. The Kinta Elves gave them a wide berth, withdrawing into the Emerald Wood that once covered vast portions of the region; the young kingdoms of Men did not miss the Kintai, but focused instead upon commerce with the Temámir dwarves they encountered. But the Kinta clans and the tribes of Men shared more in common than they believed, for they were each the hated foes of Morgoth, and he wanted them destroyed.\
\
'His servants reserved particular torments for the Kintai, luring them through guile and deceit into hidden caverns beneath the eastern hills, where they were subjected to terrible desecrations. These imprisoned Kintai were twisted into the progenitors of a terrible breed of Orc, the like of which has not been seen since the Dominion of Zíkar ended.'"},
[2921]={"'Ve a las regiones del norte de Gathbúrz, a Búrzkala, Kúfuzg y Hongoi, los grandes campamentos donde se están organizando los ejércitos orcos, y mata a tantos de esa tropa como puedas. Mata también a sus comandantes, para hacer que su próximo asalto sea menos efectivo, y busca en los campamentos planes de batalla para que podamos saber cuándo llegará el ataque.\
\
'Un ataque es inevitable, ${PLAYER}. Podemos ayudarnos mejor aprendiendo cuándo llegará, en lugar de engañarnos con la negación.'","Lleva los planes de batalla a Ningloril","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, el campamento más cercano de la Hueste Dorada a Dol Guldur.\
\
Has derrotado a los comandantes uruk en Búrzkala, Kúfuzg y Hongoi y has recuperado algunos de sus planes de batalla. Ningloril está esperando tu regreso.","Búrzkala, Kúfuzg y Hongoi son campamentos orcos en las regiones del norte de Gathbúrz.\
\
Ningloril te ha pedido que mates a los comandantes uruk de los grandes campamentos del norte de Gathbúrz y que busques en los campamentos planes de batalla.","Has derrotado a un comandante uruk en Hongoi","Derrota a un comandante uruk en Kúfuzg","'¿No has regresado con algo de interés para mí?'","Derrota a un comandante uruk en Búrzkala","Derrota a un comandante uruk en Hongoi","Los ejércitos orcos de Dol Guldur se están reuniendo en grandes campamentos en las regiones del norte de Gathbúrz.","Has derrotado a un comandante uruk en Kúfuzg","Capítulo 12: Los ejércitos de Gathbúrz","Has derrotado a un comandante uruk en Búrzkala","'Los Orcos de Dol Guldur se están convirtiendo en una fuerza de combate peligrosa, ${PLAYER}, bajo el liderazgo de feroces comandantes uruk. Una gran cantidad de estas criaturas se están organizando en tropas en varios grandes campamentos orcos en las regiones del norte de Gathbúrz.\
\
'Lleva la lucha a estos campamentos: Búrzkala, Kúfuzg y Hongoi, y derrota a sus comandantes uruk, porque sin ellos los Orcos serán menos efectivos y el próximo asalto será más débil.\
\
'También deberías encontrar cualquier plan de batalla que pueda estar por ahí en estos campamentos. Podemos aprender cuándo esperar su ataque, para que podamos prepararnos contra él.'","Planes de batalla encontrados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Pude escuchar los gritos provenientes de los campamentos orcos desde aquí, ${PLAYER}; ¡has hecho bien en sembrar el desorden en los campamentos de los Orcos!\
\
'Muchos de estos planes son indescifrables para mí, pero reconozco la palabra \\qdush,\\q que significa hechicería, y esta área rodeada solo puede significar una cosa: ¡el peligro para los Elfos se encuentra allí!'","Encuentra los planes de batalla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2922]={"Saeradan is at his camp in the Windfells.\
\
You have found the former bearer of the sword, but he was not one of the Rohirrim at all. It was Wadu of the Uch-lûth, and when you arrived he was already dead. You should bring the news to Saeradan.","Find the fallen Man of Rohan along the road and try to save him","'The former bearer of this sword may still be alive, ${PLAYER}, but injured and near death. There may be a chance that we can save him; perhaps the hostile Dunlendings who stole his blade did not finish him.\
\
'He may have tidings of Rohan, and as that is where we hope to join Aragorn, they could be of use to us as we journey further south.\
\
'Begin at the blockaded gate north of here and follow the road south, ${PLAYER}. You may be able to find this fallen Rohirrim and save him.'","'Our enemies are cruel and have no mercy in their hearts, that is certain.'","Talk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan","Chapter 12: The Bearer of the Sword","'To gain an ally and lose him so quickly....'","Saeradan has asked you to find the unfortunate bearer of the Rohirrim sword you recovered from the blockade of the road in the Windfells.","Saeradan listens to your account, and his confusion is evident.\
\
'I am sorry indeed to hear that Wadu has been slain, but I cannot understand how he came to possess the sword that was taken from him. It is without doubt a sword of the Rohirrim, and the Men of Rohan are no friend to the clans of Dunland. There is a long history of war between the two, and I fear that if Saruman's plans continue to bear fruit there will be war again.\
\
'Why would Wadu have borne such a sword? And what brought him to that road to die? Was he so o'ermatched in number that even such a well-crafted sword could avail him nothing?'","The former bearer of the Rohirrim sword may be close to death somewhere on the road south of the blockade in the Windfells.\
\
Saeradan wants you to search the road, starting at the blockaded north gate and working your way south, looking for the fallen Rohirrim.","'It is a small chance, but we must take it. If this Man of Rohan is still alive, though the chance be small, we must try and save him. Begin at the blockaded gate on the road north of here and work your way south looking for him.'","The bearer of the sword was not one of the Rohirrim after all...it was Wadu, and he is dead"},
[2923]={"Ráthwald se encuentra en el arco en ruinas cerca de Echad Dúnann, en Eregion.\
\
Has ahuyentado al Guardián del Agua y los enanos han entrado en Moria por fin.","'Are you ready? I will bring you to Bósi so that he may be heartened by the mighty weapon that has returned from the depths of time. This may be the advantage we need to wreak vengeance upon the Watcher in the Water for the death of Bróin and the other lives it claimed that day.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Capítulo 12: El Guardián del Agua","'¡Esta arma podría ser lo que necesitamos para ahuyentar al Guardián del Agua, ${PLAYER}, y permitir que los enanos entren en Moria!\
\
'Habla conmigo cuando estés ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]} y te llevaré a Bósi y Brogur. ¡Estarán encantados de ver que por fin hay esperanza de nuevo!'","'El resto de los enanos ha entrado en Moria en busca de fortuna, ${PLAYER}, ¡y te lo tenemos que agradecer a ti!'","Te has vuelto competente con un arma perdida de los Días Antiguos, y los enanos de la expedición de Bósi están seguros de que ahora puedes enfrentarte al Guardián del Agua.","Ráthwald se encuentra en el arco en ruinas cerca de Echad Dúnann, en Eregion.\
\
Ahora que tienes un arma lo suficientemente poderosa para hacer daño al Guardián del Agua, Ráthwald te espera para llevarte a Bósi.","Habla con Ráthwald y viaja para enfrentarte al Guardián"},
[2924]={"'Will you gather the teeth and claws of jackals and crebain within Urash Dâr? By studying them I hope to learn something of use.'","Collect claws from crebain in Urash Dâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I hope you faced little trouble among the canyons as you collected these items, ${PLAYER}. I will begin my study of them and see what affect the waking of the Thardúth might have upon the creatures that dwell here.'","'I heard the sounds of battle from here! I would have joined you, but Belondor asked that I not leave the camp. He expressed some fear that once I began fighting the lesser Orcs and their Utûgi betters, I might not return, but instead continue deeper into the canyons in the grip of a powerful lust for combat!'\
\
Rothog tilts his massive head to one side.\
\
'Once in awhile Belondor makes a good point, ${PLAYER}.'","'The map you drew for me will help ensure safety during my journey to Ashâgir. I need not fear an ambush by Nakási.'","'On the ride south from Gondor, Mithrandir spoke to me of the Thardúth and the Utûgi. I knew them not, ${PLAYER}, for when the Dominion of Zíkar was at its height I was far away, and... otherwise engaged. The size and scope of the danger posed by Morgoth to the world is difficult to convey. When later I learned of the breaking of Thangorodrim and of his defeat in the Great Battle by the Host of Valinor...'\
\
Glorfindel falls silent, lost in distant memory.\
\
'I knew it to be true and still I could not believe it, ${PLAYER}. He is gone and can never return, but the seed he planted in this land seeks to burst through the crust after years of lying dormant. That cannot but affect the creatures here, and perhaps they will tell us something of how to combat this waking evil.\
\
'Will you gather the teeth and claws of jackals and crebain within Urash Dâr? By studying them I hope to learn something of use.'","Defeated Orcs throughout Urash Dâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Wizard of the North weaves a curious tale, but I have seen little evidence of these creatures that have so frightened him. We should keep our attention upon the purpose that brought us here: the pursuit of Azagath and Nakási. The map they stole may have directed them to some location within these canyons. This was once part of the Kingdom of Hamât, before it was conquered by Ordâkh, and they may have searched for the once-mighty fortress of Ashâgir said to remain here.\
\
'While you were visiting the Elves, we spoke with a scout who claimed Azagath alone crossed into Urash Dâr. That may be true, but I caution you to not lower your guard overmuch; we must search the canyons carefully, for Nakási may remain hidden from our sight, waiting for her moment to strike. I do not wish to leave this camp without reason, for she may think to attack her former allies who remain with the Kindred of the Coins. Still, we must search these canyons!'\
\
Khôltekh raises his hand in a gesture of sudden realization that feels quite artificial to you.\
\
'I have it! I will give you a parchment, and when you find the entrance to Ashâgir, you can draw me a map of the location. Then I will be able to go straight there, minimizing the risk of ambush by Nakási! It is a good idea, ${PLAYER}. Ashâgir is said to be somewhere to the north-west.'","Rahâzi is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","From here you should be able to sketch the map for Khôltekh","Talk to Rothog at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'Why speaks the dwarf Khôltekh of the fortress Ashâgir? While you were gone, he spoke of little else, and to anyone who would listen.'\
\
You tell Rahâzi that you understand he wishes to search for Azagath Sea-shadow within that fortress, and she frowns.\
\
'That was the last of the Hamâti strongholds to fall to Ordâkh, and it is said that it was home to the largest stockpile of Narghâk ever crafted by the sages of Hamât. They resisted the besieging Ordâkhai for a year and a day, but in the end the Hûl of Ordâkh sent assassins on a moonless night to climb the cliff; after slaying the guards they threw open the gates and the Ordâkhai army stormed the fortress.\
\
'With no other choice remaining to him, Taldûmu, last king of Hamât, set the stores of Narghâk ablaze. We name him today the Shâr Who Burned. No one within the fortress, defender or attacker, survived, and the fires burned for six days. When they finally went out, only ashes remained, along with the scraps of Taldûmu's crown, melted into a tangle.\
\
'If the dwarf Khôltekh goes to Ashâgir, I suggest you keep a wary eye upon him. The stockpile of Narghâk that once remained within burned long ago, but the fortress is an ill-omened tomb: the pyre of Hamât.'","Rothog asked you to defeat Orcs throughout Urash Dâr.\
Glorfindel asked you to collect jackal teeth and craban claws from creatures throughout Urash Dâr so he can examine them for unusual effects or signs of corruption.\
Khôltekh asked you to draw him a map to the ruins of Ashâgir in north-west Urash Dâr.","Collected craban claws in Urash Dâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The evils that have awoken within Urash Dâr spell an uncertain future for not just the people of Ikorbân, but for all of Middle-earth.","Glorfindel is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Defeat Orcs throughout Urash Dâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The old man that came from the North speaks strangely and uses words unfamiliar to me, but one thing was clear.'\
\
Rothog bares his fangs in a brilliant and blinding smile.\
\
'The Orcs we have seen before now are the merest imitations of a stronger and larger breed: the Utûgi. I am eager to test my combat prowess against these foes!\
\
'If they are similar to the warriors who fight in Dahâl Huliz, they will attract smaller and weaker Orcs to them as servants and thralls. The sheer force of their presence will draw other Orcs to them. Bring the battle to these weaker Orcs, and we may catch the attention of these Utûgi! I hope it will be so!'","Talk to Khôltekh at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'We will not cower before this threat, no matter how deadly the foes arrayed before us. Have we not powerful allies of our own?\
\
'When I walked in this land, many years ago, the folk here called me \\qInkanûsh.\\q Now I call upon my own memory of their language to name this camp: Ilzag Khûl, the Last Barrier Against Evil. From here we will prepare our defence against the Thardúth and the Utûgi they created. It will have to be enough.\
\
'Speak to our allies here at Ilzag Khûl and devise a plan, ${PLAYER}.'","Collected jackal teeth in Urash Dâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You sketch a map to Ashâgir for Khôltekh","You hear Rahâzi calling for you from the vicinity of the camp-fire","Chapter 13.1: Evil In The Canyons","Bring the map you sketched to Khôltekh at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'You have done as I asked, then? Yes, the map you have drawn makes the location of Ashâgir quite clear to me! Very good, my useful friend. This will help ensure safety during my journey to Ashâgir. I need not fear an ambush by Nakási.'","'I am pleased you fought against the Orcs. May the Utûgi provide a greater challenge!'","Talk to Rahâzi at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'I have begun my study of those trophies you brought me, but it has not yet seen results.'","Talk to Glorfindel at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'If these Utûgi are similar to the warriors who fight in Dahâl Huliz, they will attract smaller and weaker Orcs to them as servants and thralls. The sheer force of their presence will draw other Orcs to them. Bring the battle to these weaker Orcs, and we may catch the attention of these Utûgi! I hope it will be so!'","Rothog is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Khôltekh is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","'Speak to our allies here at Ilzag Khûl and devise the plan by which we will stand against the Thardúth and their Utûgi warriors.'","Bring the teeth and claws to Glorfindel at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'When you find the entrance to Ashâgir, you can draw me a map of the location. Then I will be able to go straight there, minimizing the risk of ambush by Nakási! It is a good idea, ${PLAYER}. Ashâgir is said to be somewhere to the north-west.'","Collect teeth from jackals in Urash Dâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Some of your companions at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr have begun to devise plans for combatting the Thardúth and the Elder Orcs that serve them.","Sketch a map to Ashâgir on the parchment Khôltekh gave to you","Find a good place at which to sketch Khôltekh a map to Ashâgir"},
[2925]={"Gandalf is on Tol Send, deep in thought.","'We have been some time away from the Beorning-lands, and Grimbeorn may worry at our absence. We should return to him and assure him we still have need of his hospitality. I desire also to return to my study of the Black Book of Mordor, for I see now that some things I long held to be certain were perhaps not so, and I wonder at some avenues of learning I might have dismissed too readily.'","Talk to the shade of Isildur on Tol Send","'Yes, my friend, I know what chamber Isildur describes. Many pieces fall now into place for me, for as Lendelen I knew many things and saw much. It is as if a room that was sealed to me has been flung open, and while the pain is unwelcome the knowledge is not. I deem it a worthy trade, though Glorfindel regrets the necessity.\
\
'This I believe, ${PLAYER}. It was known to Sauron's servants that Isildur perished in the Gladden Fields. They scoured the swamplands hereabout in search of the Ring, but they found it not. In time, his bones were recovered and borne away to places of great evil, perhaps to the very Houses of Lamentation it is said lie hidden somewhere within Mordor. What unholy rites were performed with his remains? I hazard no guess, but in time perhaps even the servants of Sauron tired of this villainy, and his bones were brought to some chamber where they, in time, were forgotten.\
\
'The white stone Isildur describes must be the Vandassar of Dúath, which stood in Minas Ithil until the forces of Sauron captured that city during the Second Age. It was moved to Barad-dûr at the direction of the Witch-king, hauled on a great waggon pulled by hill-trolls into Gorgoroth. It was in the Dark Tower that the Bright Company broke the spells upon it. After the war, when the Alliance razed Barad-dûr to its foundation, the Vandassar must have been returned to Minas Ithil. So that explains the white stone, but what of the rotating beacon? Indeed, there was a beacon of some note in that city, kept in an upper chamber atop Barad Cúron, the Tower of the Crescent Moon. It seems to me the bones of Isildur came to lie within the tower. If his shade is to find rest, these bones must be recovered.\
\
'But let us not now dwell upon that task. We have been some time away from the Beorning-lands, and Grimbeorn may worry at our absence. We should return to him and assure him we still have need of his hospitality. I desire also to return to my study of the Black Book of Mordor, for I see now that some things I long held to be certain were perhaps not so, and I wonder at some avenues of learning I might have dismissed too readily.'","'In the chamber I see a white stone, and a rotating beacon. But what does this vision signify?'","'You again? And here I hoped you might have gone, and taken Wizard and Elves with you! It was a pleasant thought, but now it is dashed!'","'Sauron was defeated, but at great cost. Elves and Men wept for their lost kings, for the like of Gil-galad and Elendil would never come again. But there was joy too, for the war was ended and none could see the sorrows of the Age to come. The Ring should have been destroyed on that day, but it was not. Isildur took the Ring as payment for the death of his father and the travails of his people, an heirloom of his house and a record of their triumph over evil.\
\
'The several kindreds that composed the Alliance returned to their homelands, nursing their grief and holding dear the memory of their triumph. We believed Sauron was gone forever, and it was not so.'","After the defeat of Sauron, Isildur faced a number of challenges during the two years preceding his death on the Gladden Fields and the loss of the One Ring.","Chapter 13.1: Two Years of Peace","Gandalf strokes his beard and nods. It is the Wizard's way of asking for attention","'My memory is less certain of the years following the defeat of Sauron, ${PLAYER}. Gultháva's enchantment still enwreathes my mind, and I find it difficult to clearly recall the events that transpired. There were two years of peace, that I know, and during those years the kingdom of Gondor was restored to order. Vows were taken before the Oath-stones, and a tomb made for my father at Amon Anwar. It was to be a hallowed place.\
\
'At last it was time for me to take up my father's place on the high throne in the North. My queen and my youngest son waited for me in Rivendell, where they marked the time during the war, so I chose not to sail. With a company of knights, my sons, and the heirlooms of my house, I rode north... to my death and the death of my sons. We were all of us betrayed. You have agreed to help me avenge this treachery, ${PLAYER}, but I do not see the face of my betrayer, and cannot remember what befell. In my mind's eye I see only a chamber with a white stone, beneath a rotating beacon, but all is hazy, as if I look from a great distance.\
\
'I do not know what this vision signifies. Gultháva's enchantment releases its grip upon my mind but slowly, and leaves only mystery in its wake.'","Grimbeorn is at the Beorninghús.\
\
Gandalf thinks you should return to the Beorninghús and speak with Grimbeorn.","The shade of Isildur is on Tol Send.","Talk to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send"},
[2926]={"Has recogido leña (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Search dead Orcs at the Forest Gate (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Firewood can be found near the base of trees in the Beorning-lands, and Orcs and wargs still threaten the peace of the Beornings.","Thindrif is at the Forest Gate.","'Did you find anything that might explain why the Orcs dared attempt the passage of the Forest Gate? Their need must have been great to challenge us, and they paid dearly for it.\
\
'Wait a moment. Did you say you searched the bodies of four Orcs? That is most peculiar, friend. By my bow, I would swear the raiding-party consisted not of four Orcs but five. Can it be that one of these creatures slipped through the Forest Gate while we were distracted by the others?\
\
'Search to the south in the Beorning-lands for our missing Orc! There may be some tracks you can follow to his hiding-place, if you make haste!'","Bring the crumpled note to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Bring the firewood to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","You found the missing Orc's hiding-place. He is dead, but carries a crumpled note","Thindrif invited you to search the corpses of the Orcs for some clue as to why they attempted to pass through the Forest Gate.","'Search to the south in the Beorning-lands for our missing Orc! There may be some tracks you can follow to his hiding-place, if you make haste!'","Defeat Orcs in the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'A raiding party of Orcs sought to leave the forest by way of the Gate, ${PLAYER}. You can see what happened to them. It is curious indeed for Orcs to challenge us on the road. Did they not know our quivers held their doom?\
\
'They did seem driven by some desperate haste. Search the bodies, and you may learn what caused them to dare the Gate, to their sorrow.'","'These Orcs did seem driven by some desperate haste. Search the bodies, and you may learn what caused them to dare the Gate, to their sorrow.'","You search the Orc but find nothing to explain its presence here","Chapter 13.2: Grimbeorn's Interruption","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús.","Defeated Orcs in the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A number of dead Orcs lie near the Forest Gate","Grimbeorn has not forgotten that Gandalf and the Elves are relying upon his hospitality, and he has some chores for you.","This Orc bears the symbol of Ugrukhôr, Captain of the Pit","Defeat wargs in the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Thindrif thinks one of the Orcs might have escaped into the Beorning-lands during the commotion.","'I have not heard from the Elves at the Forest Gate in some time, and I do not like it. I do not desire their company, but they do owe me the courtesy of telling me when there is trouble on the border of my lands!'","'Gather up more firewood and put an end to the Orc and warg raids, and I will allow the Wizard and the Elves to stay a little longer at the Beorninghús.'","You find nothing of interest on the dead Orc","You found a crumpled note clutched in the hand of the Orc that fled through the Forest Gate.","'You found our missing villain? Did he have anything to tell us of his purpose in Eryn Lasgalen?'","This Orc died wielding his sword, but it did not protect him","'The Elves allowed an Orc to cross through the Forest Gate? Bah! I am pleased to hear you tracked him down.\
\
'The Wizard is inside.'","'Oh, you have returned. What is it?'\
\
Gandalf's expression is troubled, and he seems distracted by something.\
\
'Falch Gurth? No, I have never heard of it before. That is not important right now. I need to speak with you, ${PLAYER}.'","Go to the Forest Gate on the edge of Eryn Lasgalen","Talk to Thindrif at the Forest Gate","'As long as they remain, you must continue to perform the chores I ask of you. We have need of firewood, for so near to the mountains the nights can be cold even in summer. And there are still Orcs and wargs about, despite your efforts of the other day! Put an end to their raids, and teach them a lesson about persistence!\
\
'Carry out these chores and I will allow the Wizard and the Elves to stay a little longer.'","'Yes, very good, fine. You have done the chores I asked you to undertake, and earned the Wizard and the Elves a few more days of hospitality.\
\
'There is something else, however. It is not a matter of real concern, but I find I have not heard from the Elves at the Forest Gate in some time, and I wonder if it signals some trouble for my folk? If it does, I would have this problem resolved early rather than late. Go to the Forest Gate and make certain the Elves have things well in hand. If they don't, be sure to tell them so!'","Search the Beorning-lands for the missing Orc's hiding-place","The note speaks of something called 'Falch Gurth' in which Gandalf may be interested","Defeated wargs in the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Grimbeorn is waiting for you at the Beorninghús.","Collect firewood from the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Read the crumpled note you found on the missing Orc","Grimbeorn has not heard from the Elves at the Forest Gate in some time, and despite his reticence to restart trade with the Elves, he worries about the silence."},
[2927]={"'The emissaries have departed? Good.\
\
'I hope they make haste. If they do not they may find only our bodies remain, crushed beneath the heels of the Utûgi and their Thardúth masters!'","'The Shagâni warrior will speak to Girhâzi of Ambarûl, and it is my hope she will return with many fierce warriors of that folk, but we will need as many fighters as we can gather to face the waking Thardúth.\
\
'It is my plan to send the Kinta woman Silirtas to the oasis groves, that she may return with Elf-warriors of that people; after all, their lands are threatened by the evil that stirs within Urash Dâr; it will not be contained without their help.\
\
'I also wish to send one of the leaders of Umbar to return with as many Umbari soldiers as can be marshalled in haste. What is that ruling body named? The Kindred of the Coins? Who of these should go, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You consider the choices available to you, and decide only Belondor can be trusted to return quickly with a sizeable force of Umbari soldiers. Mithrandir nods.\
\
'Very well. If he is as respected in Umbar as you say he is, he will be best-suited for this task. I ask you to tell him to depart at once, for the hour is late indeed. Then you must do the same for the Kinta Silirtas. Return to me when they have departed.'","Sigileth is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Silirtas at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'But that is not why I came to speak to you. The Wizard from the North has asked me to to return to Ambarûl with a message for my mother. He wants her to send as many Dumûri warriors as she can spare to us, to stand against these waking servants of Morgoth.\
\
'You have allied yourself with this Wizard before, ${PLAYER}. Have you known him to overreact to danger at any moment in the past?'\
\
You confess that if Mithrandir believes he needs an army of warriors to face the Thardúth and their Utûgi, he is probably correct. Rahâzi nods slowly.\
\
'That is what I suspected. Farewell to you, my friend. I will see you again as soon as I can, and let us hope my mother sends the warriors requested by your Wizard!'","Sigileth bids you farewell and leaves on her mission","Rahâzi is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","'I am not the person to carry this message. Will you bear it on my behalf, Sigileth?'","'Farewell to you, my friend. I will see you again as soon as I can, and let us hope my mother sends the warriors requested by your Wizard!'","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Silirtas at Ilzag Khûl","Sigileth stares at Silirtas in stunned surprise, knowing how difficult this admission must be for the Kinta Elf. When she recovers, her voice is thick with emotion and she speaks with understanding.\
\
'I will do this, Silirtas, fear not. Spend not a moment more thinking upon it. The Kintai will be told of our need, and I will return with as many as I can muster, and with utmost speed. Farewell, dear friend.\
\
'Good-bye, ${PLAYER}. Take care of my brother, and make sure he does nothing foolish. It is in his nature to act first and think later, if he thinks at all!'","'Good-bye to you. Take care of my friends in the company, and beware of the terrible creatures that lurk within Urash Dâr! I will see you again, as soon as I may.'","Wait for the emissaries to depart","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Rahâzi at Ilzag Khûl","'There is talk around camp that the Wizard seeks volunteers to bring reinforcements to Urash Dâr to face the servants of Morgoth. Is it true?'\
\
You tell Silirtas that Mithrandir wanted you to ask her if she would be willing to return to the oasis groves of the Kintai with this request.\
\
'I will of course do this, ${PLAYER}. First to Vartúlin I will go, then to Shonith, and if the time can be spared I will speak with Shanthar at Arwáth. The Kintai must defend their groves, as they always have.'","Talk to Belondor at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'If Belondor is as respected in Umbar as you say he is, he will be best-suited for this task. I ask you to tell him to depart at once, for the hour is late indeed. Then you must do the same for the Kinta Silirtas. Return to me when they have departed.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Belondor at Ilzag Khûl","'That is what I wish I could say, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'But I cannot. If these Kintai reinforcements are needed with all haste... we can risk no delay. I know the untethered periods to which I succumb. I... do not want to endanger the delivery of this message, or the return of enough Kintai warriors to face their ancient, forgotten foes.\
\
'I am not the person to carry this message. Will you bear it on my behalf, Sigileth?'","Silirtas takes a deep breath, and then heaves a sigh","Belondor raises his hand in farewell","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Sigileth at Ilzag Khûl","'What asks the Wizard of me, ${PLAYER}? You should speak it aloud, though I believe I know already what my task must be.'\
\
You tell Belondor that Mithrandir wants him to return to Umbar Baharbêl as quickly as he can, and to come back with a contingent of Umbari soldiers.\
\
'I knew in my heart I would be called to do this. I cannot promise I will return with the number of soldiers the Wizard wants... but I will return with as many as I can.\
\
'Good-bye to you, ${PLAYER}. Take care of my friends in the company, and beware of the terrible creatures that lurk within Urash Dâr! I will see you again, as soon as I may.'","You choose not to mention that Sigileth shares this quality with her brother","Mithrandir believes facing the threat posed by the Thardúth will need the strong cooperation of many peoples: the Shagâni, the Kintai, and the Umbari.","Belondor is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Chapter 13.2: The Hour Is Late","The emissaries have left on their missions.","Talk to Mithrandir at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Talk to Sigileth at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Silirtas is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Rahâzi nods and bids you farewell, for now","Mithrandir is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr."},
[2928]={"Corudan stands outside Ashâgir, atop the north-west cliffs in Urash Dâr.","Khôltekh stands within the undisturbed chamber deep within Ashâgir.","Talk to Khôltekh in the undisturbed chamber deep within Ashâgir","Meet with Khôltekh outside Ashâgir atop the north-west cliffs in Urash Dâr","'Will you confront Khôltekh about this discovery? We cannot simply stand by and allow the Kindred of the Coins to acquire such a thing!'","'It is as I feared: a stockpile of Narghâk survived the conflagration of Ashâgir. This chamber must have been sealed away sometime during the Hamâti reign. When Taldûmu set the torch to the rest of the Hungry Fire, this chamber escaped the burning.\
\
'The quakes that shook this land following the defeat of Sauron must have opened the way to this sealed chamber, ${PLAYER}.'","Khôltekh grins widely at you, his eyes alight","'It had been my plan to search the old Hamâti fortress of Ashâgir for an overlooked stockpile of Narghâk, but I had planned to search it alone. Now you can join me, and if Corudan the Elf is so concerned about my comings-and-goings, he can join us as well.\
\
'I will meet the two of you outside Ashâgir, to the north-west.'","Talk to Corudan in the undisturbed chamber deep within Ashâgir","Can this be the hidden cache of Narghâk sought by Khôltekh?","Chapter 13.3: Hidden and Never Found","'I spoke with the Elf Corudan while you sent the emissaries upon their urgent errands. From the description he gave to me it appears the man you pursued here, Azagath Sea-shadow, is a Gúrzyul of Sauron. I believe in his search for the Narghâk stockpile of which Corudan spoke, Azagath may find himself ensnared by the Thardúth. The Sere Ones bore no love for Sauron; they suspected him of treachery and disloyalty to Morgoth. How will they treat with one of the Gúrzyul, I wonder?'","Talk to Khôltekh at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'Have you ever seen anything so beautiful as this undisturbed chamber? Behold: the last surviving stockpile of the Hungry Fire, a weapon thought vanished from the world!\
\
'I see the way forward now. The fortunes of my dominion are on the rise!'\
\
A curious light glimmers in Khôltekh's eye, and you are unable to determine if he speaks of the Kindred of the Coins, the Corsairs of Umbar, or the Temámir of the Shoreward Stone.","Somewhere inside the depths of Ashâgir, Khôltekh believes you will find a chamber containing a lost, hidden cache of Narghâk.","Mithrandir worries that the secrets buried within Urash Dâr might spell doom for not just the folk of Shagâna, but for all of Middle-earth as well.","Talk to Khôltekh outside Ashâgir in Urash Dâr","Corudan stands within the undisturbed chamber deep within Ashâgir.","'I will help search the fortress for this stockpile... but I hope we find nothing.'","Khôltekh can be found at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.\
\
Corudan is concerned about Khôltekh's apparent discovery of a cache of Narghâk, the Hungry Fire.","Talk to Corudan outside Ashâgir in Urash Dâr","'Here we are.'","'Perhaps some of the Narghâk remained in sealed chambers belowground. It is my hope that some of that mighty stockpile escaped the conflagration, and you will help me find it. Does Corudan the Elf find this distasteful?'","Khôltekh stands outside Ashâgir, to the north-west in Urash Dâr.","Khôltekh asked to meet you and Corudan outside Ashâgir, to the north-west in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Corudan at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'I do not like this, ${PLAYER}, but if any member of the Kindred of the Coins finds a stockpile of Narghâk I believe we should know of it. That is true of Azagath or Nakási, but it is also true of Khôltekh.\
\
'I will help search the fortress for this stockpile... but I hope we find nothing.'","'I am worried, ${PLAYER}. I overheard Khôltekh speaking to Rothog, and from his words it appeared that he believes he has discovered a lost cache of Narghâk. Do you think it is true?\
\
'Everything my sister told me about this substance fills me with fear. If Khôltekh has found a stockpile of the Hungry Fire...\
\
'Will you confront him about this discovery? We cannot simply stand by and allow the Kindred of the Coins to acquire such a thing!'","'What do you want?'\
\
You ask Khôltekh if Corudan misheard him concerning the dwarf's discovery of a lost stockpile of Narghâk. Khôltekh peers at you curiously.\
\
'I have not discovered it yet, ${PLAYER}... but I am hopeful it will not be much longer now. It had been my plan to search the old Hamâti fortress of Ashâgir for just such a stockpile, but I had planned to search it alone. Now you can join me, and if Corudan the Elf is so concerned about my comings-and-goings, he can join us as well.\
\
'I will meet the two of you outside Ashâgir, to the north-west. Your map was most clear to me, and I will have no difficulty finding the place. I trust you will have no problems joining me there?'","'The quakes that shook this land following the defeat of Sauron must have opened the way to this sealed chamber.'","Search the depths of Ashâgir for a hidden chamber containing the cache of Narghâk","'It may not come to that! The Thardúth have not woken in thousands of years, and the world is much changed since their Dominion of Zíkar threatened these lands. They may expect little in the way of opposition.\
\
'I spoke with the Elf Corudan while you sent the emissaries upon their urgent errands. From the description he gave to me it appears the man you pursued here, Azagath Sea-shadow, is a Gúrzyul of Sauron. I believe in his search for the Narghâk stockpile of which Corudan spoke, Azagath may find himself ensnared by the Thardúth.\
\
'Judging from the words of Megorlam of Thuringwath, the Sere Ones bore no love for Sauron; they suspected him of treachery and disloyalty to Morgoth. How will they treat with one of the Gúrzyul, I wonder?'","Corudan is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","'Here we are.'\
\
Khôltekh surveys the fortress of Ashâgir.\
\
'Ashâgir once held the largest stockpile of Narghâk ever collected in one place. Rather than surrender it to his enemies, the last Shâr of Hamât set fire to it, consuming fortress, Shâr, and stockpile.\
\
'But perhaps some of the Narghâk remained in sealed chambers belowground. It is my hope that some of that mighty stockpile escaped the conflagration, and you will help me find it. Does Corudan the Elf find this distasteful?'"},
[2929]={"Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","'Give me your attention, and do not let it wander; you must know what I have learned. I have made a worrisome discovery.'","Chapter 13.3: The Picture Painted","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, waiting to divulge what he has learned from his study of the Black Book of Mordor.","'Gothmog has been responsible for much sorrow in each of his guises, ${PLAYER}. It seems too that his fate is interwoven with yours, for even the tale of Vóin is not free of his corruptive touch, though it be written almost a thousand years ago. Gothmog has been a long-simmering font of evil; he can no longer remain unchallenged. It is time at last to put an end to him.\
\
'These past few years revealed to us that which we did not know: King Eärnur was not slain when he rode to Minas Morgul to confront the Witch-king; he was instead transformed into Mordirith, a thrall of the Lord of the Nazgûl. It was by Mordirith's hand that the shadow fell upon Angmar, but he was opposed by Golodir the Ranger and Narmeleth of Lindon, to say nothing of a certain ${CLASS} of my acquaintance. Mordirith's designs were broken, but his spirit persevered and he was given a new guise, and a new task. He would command Sauron's armies in war, second only to his old master, the Witch-king of Angmar.\
\
'But the Witch-king was slain at Pelennor, as few only might have dared hope, and Gothmog's confidence in his own invulnerability was shaken. He fled the field, escaping to Imlad Morgul and sealing the roads in or out of that vale. While Sauron thrived, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth had worries enough to occupy their attention, and Gothmog could be set aside. But now a new fear presents itself to me. Gothmog has had time now to lick his wounds and search the valley for artifacts that might reverse his fortunes. What terrible sorceries might he have discovered?'","'I suspected there was something I missed in the Black Book... and I was right. I could not place my finger upon it, but something stirred within the recesses of my mind, and I found a new avenue of study worth following.\
\
'Will you hear me, ${PLAYER}? Things are not as we believed.'","Talk to Gandalf and complete 'Instance: The Picture Painted'","Gandalf has continued his study of the Black Book of Mordor, and he has much to tell you.","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, shaken by what he has learned from the Black Book of Mordor."},
[2930]={"Talk to Mithrandir during the Dagor Carlanthir","'Few dwell here, but Legolas and Gimli have spoken with a small number of huntsmen and trappers among the canyons. They report an increase of dangerous creatures beside the river flowing from the north-eastern reaches of Urash Dâr.\
\
'That is the direction from which the Utûgi come, ${PLAYER}. Their masters must remain within a hidden place somewhere near the source of the river. It is time for us to confront the Sere Ones.\
\
'The walk will be a long one, but we must remain alert to threats as we proceed. The journey will become more dangerous as we near the hiding-place of the Thardúth.'","Talk to Legolas to the north within the channel of the River Mûshid","Khôltekh admits, with regret, that the shipping of the Narghâk out of Urash Dâr will have to wait until the threat of the Thardúth has passed, and that will require something he does not relish: a confrontation.","'We must be ready for anything.'","'We will together approach Utug-bûr. Let us hope the great courage possessed by our small number will give us safety as we pass beyond the falls.'","'Is it true that the foes we must face were once of my people? Are they truly beyond saving now, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'This must be the cruelest of Morgoth's hurts, a wound deep enough to persist so many thousands of years after his defeat.'","Legolas is to the north within the channel of the River Mûshid that runs through Urash Dâr.\
\
Mithrandir has sent much of your travelling company along the river to the north-east, where he believes the Thardúth dwell. He asked you to speak with them during the approach.","'We are being watched, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I cannot see those who watch us, but I feel their eyes upon us. Can you feel them too?'","Talk to Glorfindel within the channel of the River Mûshid","Talk to Corudan outside Utug-bûr","'¿Si?'","Meet with Glorfindel to the north-east within the channel of the River Mûshid","'Yes, I see now. I understand how the Thardúth remained hidden for so long. When they sealed the doors of their sanctuary, the Sere Ones changed the course of the river, hiding the face of the temple with the new cascade. They then pulled down the cliff-face to completely mask their location, and it remained hidden for the ages to follow.\
\
'The quakes that followed the fall of Sauron shook the earth, changing the cliffs and revealing the entrance to Utug-bûr.'","'The walk will be a long one, but we must remain alert to threats as we proceed. The journey will become more dangerous as we near the hiding-place of the Thardúth.'","Corudan is outside Utug-bûr, in north-east Urash Dâr.","Most of your travelling party has arrived at the approach to Utug-bûr, to the distant north-east in Urash Dâr.","Mithrandir commands your allied forces during the Dagor Carlanthir, the Battle of the Red Waterfall.","'Hemos llegado.'","'The creatures that prowl outside the river channel grow in danger and ferocity; it was wise of Mithrandir to direct us to follow the river as we approach the secret dwelling of the Thardúth.\
\
'We must be prepared for anything; neither I nor Gandalf have been tested by the Sere Ones, neither in this nor any age of the world.'","'We will return to Ilzag Khûl and see what the Wizard from the North has decided to do about these servants of Morgoth.'","Talk to Mithrandir outside Utug-bûr","Silirtas is outside Utug-bûr, in north-east Urash Dâr.","Chapter 13.4: A Greater Power","'The quakes that followed the fall of Sauron shook the earth, changing the cliffs and revealing the entrance to Utug-bûr.'","'But I must not get ahead of myself. This Narghâk cannot be transported anywhere until something can be done about the ancient evil that wakens in Urash Dâr. That will require something of which I am not particularly fond: a confrontation.\
\
'We will return to Ilzag Khûl and see what the Wizard from the North has decided to do about these servants of Morgoth.'","Talk to Mithrandir at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Glorfindel is to the north-east within the channel of the River Mûshid that runs through Urash Dâr.\
\
Mithrandir has sent much of your travelling company along the river to the north-east, where he believes the Thardúth dwell. He asked you to speak with them during the approach.","'We must be prepared for anything; neither I nor Gandalf have been tested by the Sere Ones, neither in this nor any age of the world.'","'With fell sorcery the Thardúth make the falls run as red as blood, and by that name will this battle be known: Dagor Carlanthir, the Battle of the Red Waterfall!\
\
'We could not avoid this battle! We are now all that stands between these servants of Morgoth and the rest of Middle-earth!'","'Neither I nor Gimli know what awaits us at the end of this journey, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps if we had some idea of how the Thardúth remained hidden for so long, but alas!\
\
'We must be ready for anything.'","'This must be the cruelest of Morgoth's hurts, a wound deep enough to persist so many thousands of years after his defeat.'","Talk to Silirtas outside Utug-bûr","Legolas is to the north within the channel of the River Mûshid that runs through Urash Dâr.\
\
Mithrandir has sent much of your travelling company along the river to the north, where he believes the Thardúth dwell. He asked you to speak with them during the approach.","Meet up with the rest of your travelling party to the distant north-east outside Utug-bûr","Mithrandir is outside Utug-bûr, in the north-eastern reaches of Urash Dâr.","Mithrandir is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Corudan outside Utug-bûr and stand against Azagath","Meet with Legolas to the north within the channel of the River Mûshid"},
[2931]={"Soldiers of Ithilien are hard-pressed at Fennas Gost, the Dread Door","Find the bridge of Gúliant over the Morgulduin, west along the road","The walls of the Dead City tower above you, monumental and menacing","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at Minas Morgul when you emerge from the trees along the road, by the stone pillar","Defeat foes throughout Rath Dúath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Be careful, friend! We are hard-pressed here!'","Beregond asked you to defeat foes throughout Rath Dúath, and to scout the terrain by <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb>ing at several important landmarks within Imlad Morgul.","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. I will not say this is a pleasant place, but I know that once it was. This was Imlad Ithil, and nowhere else in Gondor could rival its beauty when the Ithilduin river sparkled in the moonlight like a vein of silver threaded between dark cliffs. When Isildur came to these shores with his father and brother, he was so taken by the beauty of this valley that he built a citadel beneath the slopes of Achathras, tallest peak of the Ephel Dúath. Minas Ithil he called it, and Barad Cúron, the Tower of the Crescent Moon, rose from its topmost level.\
\
'But that was long ago, and the Lord of the Nazgûl coveted the valley and the citadel sheltered within. Twice the Witch-king seized the city. The first time, he possessed it only until the Last Alliance of Men and Elves came south and fought the war that ended the Second Age. Minas Ithil remained under the control of Gondor for centuries, and although it would never again attain the heights it had known under Isildur, it drew the imaginations of poets, artists, and minstrels from all over the kingdom.\
\
'That all came to a sad end with the second of the Witch-king's assaults upon the city. When the Nazgûl captured Minas Ithil for the second time, that name could no longer describe the citadel. It became Minas Morgul, the Tower of Sorcery, and so it would stay.'","Faramir, Prince of Ithilien, can be found near the Bridge of Gúliant in Imlad Morgul.","'My prince has not found it easy to shake his roots as a Ranger; even now he walks somewhere in the valley, despite our warnings. I ask you to find several places from which to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at Minas Morgul and at the Bridge of Gúliant, and also to defeat our foes along the Rath Dúath. Take the road west until you emerge from the trees; there is a short stone pillar by the side of the track from which you can study the walls of the city. Faramir intended to survey Gúliant, and you may find him there when you have accomplished these tasks.'","Fennas Gost, the Dread Door on the outskirts of Gorgoroth, provides access to Imlad Morgul.","Talk to Beregond at Echad Uial","'Welcome, my friend.'","Follow the road west of Echad Uial, until you emerge from the trees near a stone pillar","Find Echad Uial in Imlad Morgul","An injured Ranger at Fennas Gost has called to you, hoping to prevent you from suffering as he has.","Beregond is at Echad Uial in Imlad Morgul.","Beregond hails you warmly, welcoming you to Echad Uial","The dark waters of the Morgulduin rush beneath the stones of Gúliant","Chapter 13.4: The Road to the Moon-lands","Talk to Faramir at the Bridge of Gúliant","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the environs from the bridge of Gúliant","This is one of the locations Beregond described","'It is good to see you. This was once the Bridge of Ithiliant, but no longer. Now it is called by another name: Gúliant.'","Echad Uial is west of Fennas Gost, in Imlad Morgul.","'We established a camp to the west, and you may find the Prince there. Do what you can to help us, for we have need of strong allies and do not dare turn anyone away!'","'I bid you welcome to Imlad Morgul. Ha! Do I say \\qwelcome?\\q This is not a welcoming place, and indeed it must be the least-such I have ever seen!\
\
'Even so, it is my honour and my joy to serve here at the command of King Elessar, for it was his mercy alone that allows me to still draw breath. My crime could not be forgiven: I spilled the blood of my fellows and for that a Guard of the Citadel deserves death. Because I acted to save the life of my lord Faramir, the king named me an exile, and charged me with the further protection of Faramir's life. I do not gainsay the king's wisdom, nor would I, but neither am I blameless. I bear my guilt with me, and strive every day to serve King Elessar and Prince Faramir.\
\
'It is the king's command that Minas Morgul be utterly destroyed and the valley cleansed. I do not know how this might be accomplished, but I will do whatever I can to make it so! Thus do I welcome you to Imlad Morgul, ${PLAYER}, strange though it seem!\
\
'My prince has not found it easy to shake his roots as a Ranger; even now he walks somewhere in the valley, despite our warnings. I ask you to find several places from which to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at Minas Morgul and at the Bridge of Gúliant, and also to defeat our foes along the Rath Dúath. Take the road west until you emerge from the trees; there is a short stone pillar by the side of the track from which you can study the walls of the city. Faramir intended to survey Gúliant, and you may find him there when you have accomplished these tasks.'","Defeated foes throughout Rath Dúath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Be careful, friend! We are hard-pressed here, and attacks can come at any time, without warning!\
\
'It was at Prince Faramir's command that we forced open the Dread Door, and we paid dearly for it. Many of my brethren did not survive the initial attack, but now we hold it against whatever evils try to retake it; we will not risk dishonouring the memory of our fallen by giving it back!\
\
'We established a camp to the west, and you may find the Prince there. Do what you can to help us, for we have need of strong allies and do not dare turn anyone away!'","According to Gandalf, the problem posed by Gothmog has become too serious to bear. Your road leads now to Imlad Morgul, where the creature that was once King Eärnur now lurks.","<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Fennas Gost on the outskirts of Imlad Morgul when you accept this quest.</rgb>\
\
'King Elessar has charged Faramir, Prince of Ithilien, with cleansing the evils from Imlad Morgul. Find his men at Fennas Gost, the Dread Door on the western bounds of Gorgoroth, and aid them with their mission. They will not be able to stand alone against Gothmog, but your help may tip the balance in their favour.\
\
'Remember, my friend: Minas Morgul was once the tower of Minas Ithil, a jewel of Gondorian art and culture, but it has spent long centuries corrupted by the Nazgûl and Sauron's other terrible servants. None can say what dangers you will find within, but I trust that if any ${RACE} has the courage to face them, you do.'","Travel to Fennas Gost on the outskirts of Imlad Morgul","Talk to the injured Ranger at Fennas Gost"},
[2932]={"Belondor stands near Mithrandir during the Dagor Carlanthir.","'An evil will tests my defences! I cannot pinpoint from where this sorcery comes, but I know it must lie within Utug-bûr. One of the Thardúth seeks to know who defies his people, and he challenges my resolve.\
\
'Worry not for me! My defences hold, for the time being. Return to where the fighting is thickest, and lend your aid to your friends once again!'","'Mithrandir is in trouble, ${PLAYER}! Is there nothing we can do to help him? If the Thardúth emerge from within the temple...'\
\
Corudan stares at you with a dawning realization.\
\
'We have to prevent the Thardúth from leaving Utug-bûr! I know what we have to do!'","'It is good to see you are well, ${PLAYER}. When I set out for Umbar Baharbêl I believed your Wizard might wait to begin fighting the battle until I returned with my army, but it turns out that was not in his plan!\
\
'But we are here now, and there is no shortage of Orcs to fight! But where are the ancient creatures of which he spoke? Where are these corrupted Elves?'","'Press forward and lend your assistance where you may! The battle rages all about us, and your friends have need of you!'","'We are lucky indeed that the Shagâni warrior arrived with her mother's fighters, for without them we could not long stand against such numbers. The Dumûri fight fiercely, but Azagath has not yet returned to the field, and I fear when he does he will not be alone. The Thardúth wait to see the strength of our opposition.\
\
'Press forward and lend your assistance where you may, ${PLAYER}! The battle rages all about us, and your friends have need of you!'","Mithrandir struggles against a distant, invisible foe, and says nothing further to you.","'You... you have come back... but the fighting persists...'\
\
Mithrandir's voice is weary with strain, his face haggard and drawn.\
\
'The Thardúth remain... within their temple, ${PLAYER}. We must count that... a blessing...'\
\
Mithrandir falls silent, his attention focused upon a distant, invisible foe.","Mithrandir commands the allied forces during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Corudan stands near Mithrandir during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Talk to Corudan during the Dagor Carlanthir and help him seal Utug-bûr","Complete 'Desperate Battle' quests during the Dagor Carlanthir (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The Dagor Carlanthir rages in Urash Dâr as the servants of the waking Thardúth bring war against the people of Ikorbân and their allies.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>To return to the Dagor Carlanthir in the event you leave it, you can use a banner at your campsite of Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr to return to the fighting.</rgb>","Mithrandir struggles against a distant opponent during the Dagor Carlanthir.","'Did you see the arrival of Belondor? He returned at the head of an army of Umbari soldiers, and they have joined the battle!'","Mithrandir commands the allied forces on the south-western bank of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.","'We need to seal the entrance of Utug-bûr before the Thardúth emerge to finish us!\
\
'We need to retrieve the Hungry Fire from Ashâgir! I will tell Rothog... we have need of his strength!'","The Dagor Carlanthir rages in Urash Dâr.","'There you are! To where did you disappear, ${PLAYER}? No, it matters not!\
\
'Did you see the arrival of Belondor? He returned at the head of an army of Umbari soldiers, and they have joined the battle!\
\
'My own battle with my unseen Thardúth opponent is at a low ebb; he has relaxed his onslaught for the moment, perhaps to change to a more successful tactic. It may be the tide is near to turning.'","Chapter 13.5: The Dagor Carlanthir","Talk to Belondor during the Dagor Carlanthir","'Worry not for me! My defences hold, for the time being. Return to where the fighting is thickest, and lend your aid to your friends once again!'","Talk to Corudan during the Dagor Carlanthir","Talk to Mithrandir during the Dagor Carlanthir"},
[2933]={"'So we are not the only ones taking an interest in Minas Morgul. From your report, it sounds as if Ugrukhôr and Lhaereth have both sent their forces to the city, and Gothmog still commands a significant portion of the Orcs within. Furthermore, this Morgul cultist spoke of one called Dolguzigir, about whom I have heard little. These interests may not align with each other, for now, but we cannot take the risk that they might set aside their differences. Any of these foes will slay us without a second thought.\
\
'The Valley of the Secret Shadow? I do not like the sound of that. Perhaps Mithrandir will know something of this place.'","Faramir has returned, and another familiar face has also come to Echad Uial","'Hmm... the Valley of the Secret Shadow? That is Thuringwath, but its location is unknown to me, and to any good folk, I should expect. Do you remember the Orcs that challenged the Forest Gate on the edge of Eryn Lasgalen? The note you found mentioned a hidden pass named Falch Gurth and a secret enchantment. It is possible these spells masked the way to Thuringwath.\
\
'But I have come here for another reason. I have uncovered developments most interesting from my study of the Black Book of Mordor.'","'Well, did you learn anything that might be of use to us?'","Many foes lie in wait beyond the entrance to the Dead City","'When I was just a boy, my brother Boromir and I had the finest teachers in all of Gondor. They told us tales of noble Elendil, wise Isildur, and bold Anárion, and our days were spent reenacting their most heroic deeds. But of all these tales, it was the fall of Minas Ithil to the Lord of the Nazgûl that most moved my brother's heart. I can still hear his voice recounting it to me on a stormy afternoon, ${PLAYER}, and though the tale is a sad one the recollection is welcome to me.\
\
'\\qAn army of Orcs came to the gates,\\q I can hear him say, \\qbut they were met by a hail of stones. The lord of the city, a great captain named Egalmoth, sent out sorties to sow confusion upon the Orcs and delay their plans. The Witch-king himself sought to breach the gates, but could not; years before and at the request of the King of Gondor, the wizard Curunír placed powerful enchantments upon them, and they held against the Witch-king's evil sorceries. But Egalmoth knew his men could not outlast the forces arrayed against them. At dawn of the appointed day, he sounded his war-horn and led his men on their mounts through the gates, forming a wedge to drive the enemies to either side or trample them underfoot. They rode to the bridge; see the light on their faces as they approach, knowing freedom is near! But it was not to be so, for as they neared the Ithiliant, the bridge sundered, its pieces falling into the river. Egalmoth could go no further, but he despaired not. He commanded his men to turn their backs to the raging river, and they charged once again... straight toward the Orc armies and their fell commanders. So died Egalmoth, but the tale of Egalmoth's Onslaught fills our hearts with joy even today, for we know that he died in service of Gondor, and so we remember him.\\q'\
\
Faramir smiles, remembering his brother's love for this tale. Then he sighs wistfully, and scuffs the stones with the toe of his boot.\
\
'The Nazgûl had weakened the supports of the bridge, so ensuring Egalmoth could not escape that way. Boromir was always quick to point out that it was a strategy they had learned from Isildur, for the son of Elendil had used that very tactic against them when he first escaped Minas Ithil. Theirs was not a mindless evil, ${PLAYER}. Let us be glad they are gone.\
\
'Yes, the Nazgûl are slain with Sauron, but others might still work his evil within the Dead City. South of here, the road climbs up to Minas Morgul. Go there and learn what you can of the situation inside. Defeat whatever foes you find there in memory of the hero Egalmoth, and in memory of my brother too.'","'Perhaps Mithrandir knows something of this Valley of the Secret Shadow.'","Faramir, Prince of Ithilien, has been kept busy maintaining the watch on Minas Morgul.","Mithrandir has made the journey to Echad Uial.","'Scout the ramp between the second and third tier of Minas Morgul, north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë, and learn what dangers lurk within the Dead City.'","The entrance to Minas Morgul is located at the end of the road south of the Bridge of Gúliant.\
\
Faramir asked you to do battle with the foes you find in the Dead City.","Climb the ramp between the second and third tiers of Minas Morgul, north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë","'If you've come to plunder Minas Morgul, you've arrived too late! The coward Gothmog sealed himself away in the tower, but he has minions roving the city, searching for whatever treasures might have been left behind. A doomed search! In the Valley of the Secret Shadow he might have found a useful weapon, but his Orcs cannot find the way.'\
\
The cultist laughs, despite the pain of her wounds, and the blood staining her garb grows a deeper shade of red.\
\
'My master Dolguzigir knows the path, but he will not tell Gothmog. Let the coward waste away in the tower... if he lives that long! More than one enemy desires his blood, and I have seen servants of at least two already. They say the Captain of the Pit will not rest until he has taken Gothmog's head, but he will have a rival for it; I heard Lhaereth the Stained hates Gothmog even worse than she hates your kind or mine, and that is no small amount! Look what... her merrevail did to me!\
\
'Well, I have had my last jest, and I am ready to die. Let them kill each other. They deserve...'","Faramir is at Echad Uial, waiting for you to report on what you encountered in the Dead City.","Talk to Nâlunitir on the ramp between the second and third tiers of the city, north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë","Defeat foes within Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Mithrandir at Echad Uial","Talk to Faramir at Echad Uial","Defeated foes within Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You found a mortally-wounded Morgul cultist on the ramp between the second and third tiers of Minas Morgul, north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë.","Return to Echad Uial and find Faramir","'Other servants of Sauron might still work his evil within the Dead City. South of here, the road climbs up to Minas Morgul. Go there and learn what you can of the situation inside. Defeat whatever foes you find there in memory of the hero Egalmoth, and in memory of my brother too.'","Nâlunitir succumbs to her wounds, a smile on her lips","Passage between the second and third tiers of Minas Morgul can be found north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë.","Find the main entrance to the city of Minas Morgul","Chapter 13.5: The Watch on the Dead City","Suffering from mortal wounds, a Morgul cultist spits curses at you","Faramir intended to return to Echad Uial. You should find him there and tell him what you learned from the dying Morgul cultist."},
[2934]={"Sirgon has sustained a grievous wound, but his allies still fight to defend him","Corudan stands outside Utug-bûr during the Dagor Carlanthir.","'Let us push forward! My blade hungers for the blood of betrayers! Let us fight alongside the soldiers that marched with me to battle! Lead on, ${PLAYER}!'","Belondor has returned at the head of a small army of Umbari reinforcements, but even that may not be enough to turn the tide of the battle.","Sirgon has been grievously injured during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Elladan stands his ground against the encircling foes, but says nothing else.","Hoping against hope, you check the Kinta Elf for some sign of life, but there are none to be found. Silirtas is dead.","'What can we do? We are out of time, ${PLAYER}!'","'This will be our only chance! We have to collapse the entrance before the Thardúth emerge!'","Talk to Sirgon during the Dagor Carlanthir","Over the sound of fighting you hear Corudan calling for you to the east","'I cannot see your face, ${PLAYER}... are you... are you all right?\
\
'The battle is not yet over... is it? I can hear the fighting...\
\
'How... are we doing...?'","Talk to Corudan outside Utug-bûr during the Dagor Carlanthir","Talk to Elladan during the Dagor Carlanthir","Go to the front line of the Dagor Carlanthir, to the north-east","Belondor wants to send some of his soldiers to fight alongside Sirgon at the front line to the north-east.","Talk to Corudan and help him place the caches of Narghâk outside Utug-bûr","Silirtas is dead.","Talk to Corudan in the middle of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir","The Dagor Carlanthir rages all around you","'Is Azagath here? I have business with the Sea-shadow!\
\
'Let us push forward! My blade hungers for the blood of betrayers! Let us fight alongside the soldiers that marched with me to battle!\
\
'Lead on, ${PLAYER}!'","Chapter 13.6: The Madness In His Eyes","Corudan stands in the middle of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.","'It is bad, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Sirgon stood his ground against one of the great Utûgi as it bore down upon us, but he saw not the smaller creature that followed in the wake of the huge Orc: a small and spindly goblin-thing. It stuck him a dozen times with its knife before we noticed.'\
\
Elladan lowers his voice until you can only just hear him over the sound of the fighting.\
\
'He will not survive this battle, ${PLAYER}. We have done all we could.'","Examine Silirtas during the Dagor Carlanthir","The Dagor Carlanthir rages all around you.","'We are not yet finished! We have to place the Narghâk around the entrance, or it will be too late!\
\
'If the Thardúth emerge from Utug-bûr it is all over! ${PLAYER}! Can you hear me?'","Elladan fights by Sirgon's side during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Silirtas lies outside Utug-bûr during the Dagor Carlanthir."},
[2935]={"Talk to Faramir at Echad Uial","'That is quite a tale! One day you will need to tell me where you found this curious tome, ${PLAYER}. The sigil on its face cannot be mistaken for anything save the Eye of Sauron, which marks it as an artifact of evil. How then came it to tell the tale of King Eärnur? Nay, not even so, for he was not yet king. But still, little is recorded of the years before he followed his father Eärnil to the throne. To find such an account in a book bearing the mark of Mordor is troubling to me.\
\
'But Eärnur's doomed adventure into the citadel now called Durthang has brought to mind a recent conversation. Beregond spoke to me of someone with an interest in that place. Speak to my captain and ask him what happened to the man with the shield. A Man of Ithilien he was, but I confess I do not know his name. He was here at the camp, but I have not seen him since I returned.'","Chapter 13.6: The Sword and the Stonemaiden","'Let us not delay. I will tell both you and Prince Faramir what I have learned, if you and he have the time and the interest to listen.'","'Faramir, I must ask that you not pepper me with questions while I tell you both the tale, or it will take much longer! Trust that ${PLAYER} will explain to you anything you do not understand. A Wizard's time is valuable and I cannot spend all day relating my discoveries to you.\
\
'Are you both ready to listen? Very good.'","Talk to Mithrandir in Echad Uial and complete 'Instance: The Sword and the Stonemaiden'","Beregond is at Echad Uial.","Unwilling to remain behind in the Vales of Anduin, Mithrandir has come to Echad Uial with the Black Book of Mordor.","'That is the latest of my discoveries from the Black Book. What else lies between these leather covers, I wonder?'","Faramir is at Echad Uial.","Mithrandir is at Echad Uial, waiting to discuss what else he has learned from the Black Book of Mordor.","Talk to Beregond at Echad Uial","'The man with the shield? Aye, I remember him. I did not much like the look of him, though.'","'Eärnur's doomed adventure into the citadel now called Durthang has brought to mind a recent conversation. Beregond spoke to me of someone with an interest in that place. Speak to my captain and ask him what happened to the man with the shield. He was here at the camp, but I have not seen him since I returned.'"},
[2936]={"Annoth may have climbed the stairs leading to Cirith Ungol. But when did he pass this way, and did he survive?","Beregond charged the soldier Annoth with some tasks around Echad Uial, but Annoth has set his own plan in motion.","Annoth is among the rocky crags within sight of the bottom of the Winding Stair.","'It is good to see you, my friend, for it means the Khundolar you brought out of Gorgoroth has not yet sunk his dagger into your back! I urge you now as I urged you then: keep Ayorzén the Wily at arm's length, for he cannot be trusted!'\
\
You ask Annoth why he failed to complete the inventory with which Dagoras entrusted him, and the Ranger grimaces.\
\
'You make your point sharply, and it wounds me! I do feel badly about shirking that duty, but I had little choice in the matter. I overheard from some of the scouts that Ugrukhôr himself had been seen west of Cirith Ungol, and that he made for Minas Morgul! I have not given up my quest to avenge the Thandrim, ${PLAYER}. I will make the Captain of the Pit pay for his crimes against them, though they be a thousand years distant. Let Ugrukhôr fear the descendant of Halannon the Survivor! I will let no other task hinder me in my vengeance.\
\
'But it seems the reports were false. He has not come himself, so far as I have seen, though his Orcs stalk among the crags. Will you search for some sign of him up the path to the north-east? Then I will return to my duties.'","'The man with the broken shield seemed very interested in the map on the table over there.'","Search for some sign of Ugrukhôr among the crags to the north-east of Annoth","'What did he name himself? Annoth, I think he was called. He carried a broken shield around with him, and it seemed to me he repaired it as best he could with leather straps. The thing was barely holding together, and looked as if it would fall apart at the first blow of an enemy's weapon. Irresponsible.\
\
'I set him to conducting an inventory of the rations and water for the camp, but he has not reported back to me. Go find him, will you? He should be somewhere by the tent to the north-west, among the crates.'","Bring the report to Annoth not far from the base of the Winding Stair","Talk to Annoth among the crags not far from the base of the Winding Stair","Look for Annoth further along the rocky path","The location Annoth marked on the map is north-west of Minas Morgul, up in the mountains. That may be where he has gone.","Bring the report to Mithrandir at Echad Uial","Annoth's dagger is embedded in the map, marking a location north-west of Minas Morgul","Annoth waves a greeting. He does not seem surprised to see you","You found a crumpled parchment in the hand of Ugrukhôr's captain. What secrets lie within?\
\
The soldier Annoth will be interested to see the report you found.","'It seems the reports were false. He has not come himself, so far as I have seen, though his Orcs stalk among the crags near the tower. Will you search for some sign of him among the crags to the north-east? Then I will return to my duties.'","Travel to the location Annoth marked on the map, north-west of Minas Morgul, up in the mountains","Examine the map on the table to the west in Echad Uial","This dead Orc bears Ugrukhôr's symbol, and carries a report for his master","'He marked a location on the map with a dagger? Well, if I were seeking this man I would check that location first!\
\
'But you do not need my advice, ${PLAYER}. You have adventures in the wild to spare, and nearly as many as me!'","Dagoras catches your eye and calls you over","Beregond charged Annoth with a number of duties to perform by the tent surrounded with crates in Echad Uial, to the north-west of his position.","'I set him to conducting an inventory of the rations and water for the camp, but he has not reported back to me. Go find him, will you? He should be over by the tent surrounded with crates, to the north-west.'","Talk to Dagoras at Echad Uial","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! Our work is never done, is it? Ah, I would not have it any other way, my friend, and I suspect neither would you.\
\
'But you are here seeking the Ithilien Ranger with the broken shield? I wondered why he carried it around with him, but I did not ask. He seemed particularly interested in the map on the table over there, just to the west.'","You found a crumpled parchment in the hand of Ugrukhôr's captain. What secrets lie within?\
\
Gandalf will be interested to see the report you found. Return to the Wizard at Echad Uial.","'Hail, friend! It has been many days since last we saw each other. I trust you are well?'","Booted footprints lead to the south-east. Did Annoth come this way?","Dagoras saw Annoth studying the map in Echad Uial, to the west.","Look for Annoth by the tent north-west of Beregond in Echad Uial","Annoth asked you to search for signs of Ugrukhôr up the path to the north-east, among the crags.","'What does Ugrukhôr's captain have to say to his master?'\
\
Annoth studies the crumpled note.\
\
'These words are full of fear, ${PLAYER}. It seems the Masters of Mordor have more worries than King Elessar or Prince Faramir alone, or indeed the two of us; they fear the treachery of their allies. Listen: \\qIf Gothmog has found a weapon to use against the spider-folk and their mistress, he keeps it to himself in his tower.\\q\
\
'The promise of such a weapon will surely draw Ugrukhôr to Minas Morgul! Let us be grateful that the Ungoledain did not slay every member of this Orc raiding-party, for word of this should still reach the Captain of the Pit through the survivors of that band. He will come for Gothmog and for this weapon, and I will be ready. The Thandrim will be avenged!\
\
'You should bring this report back to the camp. Tell them what we have learned, and that Ugrukhôr knows Fennas Gost is closed to him. Instead he sends small raiding parties into Imlad Morgul by way of Torech Ungol, as I suspected!'","Dagoras is in Echad Uial.","Chapter 13.7: Searching for Something","'Annoth shirks one duty and seeks to avoid punishment by providing useful tidings? I have seen it before, but I am not his commander and it is not my place to levy judgment. But I would caution him against pursuing vengeance with such single-minded purpose. He would not be the first to make such a mistake, nor I fear the last.\
\
'But this report does help me piece together some of what I believe Gothmog has been up to while we were occupied with other matters.'"},
[2937]={"Talk to Mithrandir at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Corudan has begged you to rescue Sigileth from within Utug-bûr before it is too late.","'We must seal the entrance... but my sister is still inside! What do we do?\
\
'I beg you, ${PLAYER}! We have to rescue Sigileth before the entrance is sealed!'","'We will not have much time to bring Sigileth back out of the darkness, ${PLAYER}! If the Narghâk explodes while we are still inside...'\
\
Corudan shakes his head firmly.\
\
'We will be quick! We have to be! Hurry now, my friend! There is no time to waste!'","Corudan stands outside Utug-bûr during the Dagor Carlanthir.","'And so the battle ends in victory for the united forces of Shagâna, Umbar, and Gondor. I can still feel the presence of the Thardúth with whom I strove; his hatred and his anger burns still in the darkness of Utug-bûr like a beacon. But his rage is unfocused, and it will be some time before he or his kind can emerge to trouble Middle-earth again.\
\
'The threat of the Thardúth has been reduced, but it is not eliminated. Other vaults of like kind to Utug-bûr may lie just beneath the surface; the breaking of the Geas of Morgoth means the occupants of these other hidden strongholds now stir restlessly, their long slumber nearing its end. I believe the Dominion of Zíkar stretched across much of Shagâna, after all, if the deathly spirit that told me of its existence can be believed. What cause would it have to lie to me, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
The Wizard sighs and you see the faintest hint of a smile beneath his beard.\
\
'It seems I have made a habit of giving you bad tidings, my friend. I was named \\qLáthspell\\q once, in a distant land, \\qIll-news,\\q and if I keep going at this rate you will begin calling me that too!\
\
'So here are some good tidings: by your deeds and those of your friends and allies, a great evil has been opposed. The Thardúth will not rise again for some time, at least.'","Talk to Corudan and go with him into the darkness of Utug-bûr","Chapter 13.7: Sigileth In The Darkness","Mithrandir is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr."},
[2938]={"Faramir is at his camp of Echad Uial.","Defeat Orcs in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The spirit in the stone will only allow Gúrzyul to pass? Are you certain we cannot force our way inside? Ah, that is not likely. Watching-stones possess a strange power, and physical force will not generally overcome it. Perhaps Mithrandir can work some Wizard-magic to get us past this barrier?\
\
'Unless you know of a Gúrzyul that might be willing to accompany us past the Watching-stone, ${PLAYER}, I can think of no other way.'","Talk to Mithrendan in the centre of the tier troubled by merrevail, in Minas Morgul","'Unless you know of a Gúrzyul that might be willing to accompany you past the Watching-stone, ${PLAYER}, I can think of no other way.'","'I believe Gothmog searched the dungeons and hidden chambers of Minas Morgul for some weapon that might reverse his fortunes. I have learned enough of the Valley of the Secret Shadow to know that the entrance was blocked by enchantments fashioned by the Lord of the Nazgûl, such that the very passage was hidden to the eyes of all but the Nine and Sauron himself. But they are all gone, and now Falch Gurth lies open once again. Did Gothmog delve within, and did he find the weapon he sought inside Thuringwath? Now he hides within Barad Cúron, the Tower of the Crescent Moon. You must gain access to the tower, ${PLAYER}. Speak to Prince Faramir and he may know how this may be accomplished.'","Defeat the Dead in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A watchful presence stands guard at the entrance to the tower, barring your passage","Mithrandir is waiting for you to return to Echad Uial with word of what guards the entrance to Barad Cúron.","'Defeat foes as you climb from level to level in the Dead City, and speak with such of my scouts as still remain within: Mithrendan in the centre of the merrevail-haunted tier, and Culang, who intended to scout the uppermost tier of the city. They may have learned something of the tower's guardians.\
\
'Good fortune to you, my friend. Our net closes upon Gothmog... I can feel it. Just a little more and we will be done with him, and Middle-earth need fear his evil no longer.'","'We always meet in foul places, ${PLAYER}. Just for once I would welcome a meeting in a field of flowers beneath a lovely blue sky. Someday, perhaps. Ah, even then I should not trust it, and would suspect the flowers of hiding some creeping danger, and the sky of turning stormy without warning.'\
\
Culang smiles grimly, and asks you about the errand that brings you to the uppermost tier of the city.\
\
'You seek to gain entrance to the tower? If you must go that way, go with caution, for I tell you it is not undefended. Some watchful presence guards the gate. More than that I cannot say, for I turned away upon sensing its presence.'","'None but Gúrzyul and their servants may pass,' the spirit whispers in your mind.","Defeated merrevail in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated the Dead in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Return to the North? No, that was not for me, nor for Culang. We and some others decided to remain in Gondor, aiding Elessar as we aided Aragorn. It was the king's wish that we help Prince Faramir make safe his lands, and so here we are.\
\
'I was charged with scouting the old libraries of the city, a sad errand. It was Valardis, Isildur's queen, who assembled here a great library of Númenórean lore. But the books of Númenor were burned with the coming of the Nazgûl, and when Queen Valardis learned of Isildur's death on the Gladden Fields, she never again came south. What few records escaped the torch were brought to other archives in Gondor and Arnor; the libraries of Minas Ithil never again thrived as they once had, and when the Nazgûl once again claimed the city, they filled the ashen shelves with tomes of evil and scrolls of foul ritual.\
\
'I entered those dark archives and found them accursed. They are touched by a sickness, ${PLAYER}. I do not mean a pestilence such as that which befouls the swamps of Agarnaith in Gorgoroth. It is no plague. Nay, it is a sickness of the mind. I walked those aisles and beheld dear friends of mine, now departed, as if they lived still. Celairant...'\
\
Mithrendan shakes his head.\
\
'No, it was not he. It can have been nothing more than a trick, but it was cruel, and I could not stand such torture for long. I heard whispering in the darkness, and dared search no further.\
\
'Something in that archive brings to mind our past experiences and seeks to turn them against us. Beware if you go that way, ${PLAYER}. Each of us has sorrow enough behind us that such a weapon could be used against us with great precision, and prove deadly.'","Foes sworn to many different masters stalk the various levels of Minas Morgul.\
\
Faramir asked you to defeat enemies throughout the Dead City and to meet up with the Rangers Mithrendan and Culang on the upper levels.","The entrance to Barad Cúron is guarded by a watchful presence. Culang warned you to be careful, but if you are to gain access to Gothmog's lair inside the tower you will need to dare the guardians.","The watchful presence is unmoved by your need, and bars your passage","The watchful presence regards you coldly, its malice coalescing before you, a solid wall of impassability. You are reminded of the spirit in the watching-stone outside the cavern of Nargroth, but this presence has a different feeling than Zaghárog. There was a mischievous bent to Zaghárog's evil; here there is order, a reverence for rules and commands that the other spirit of your acquaintance did not possess.\
\
'None but Gúrzyul and their servants may pass,' the spirit whispers in your mind, and you see an image of Gothmog standing before the tower, making known his pronouncement before the watching-stone. The spirit in the stone serves Gothmog, and will carry out his command.","Talk to Mithrandir at Echad Uial","Culang will be interested to hear what guards the entrance to Barad Cúron.","Talk to Faramir at Echad Uial","A watchful presence stands guard at the entrance to Barad Cúron.","'The tower is sure to be well-protected, ${PLAYER}, and gaining entry will be difficult. Would that swords alone might suffice! But I think it will not be so. Minas Morgul is a place of fell enchantment and terrible sorcery, and I suspect our weapons alone will not overcome whatever guards the tower.\
\
'Defeat foes as you climb from level to level in the Dead City, and speak with such of my scouts as still remain within: Mithrendan in the centre of the merrevail-haunted tier, and Culang, who intended to scout the uppermost tier of the city. They may have learned something of the tower's guardians.\
\
'Good fortune to you, my friend. Our net closes upon Gothmog... I can feel it. Just a little more and we will be done with him, and Middle-earth need fear his evil no longer.'","Investigate the entrance to Barad Cúron, the Tower of the Crescent Moon, south of Culang's position","Talk to the watchful presence that bars entrance to Barad Cúron","Defeated Orcs in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat merrevail in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Following his retreat from the Battle of the Pelennor, Gothmog fled to Imlad Morgul and the safety of the Dead City. Did he attempt to weaken the bridge west of Minas Morgul, as both Isildur and the Lord of the Nazgûl had once done? I cannot say for certain. I destroyed that bridge to protect us from further assault, but it occurs to me now that there was another result of my action: so too did I protect Gothmog from further assault by us. The western approach was blocked, and he needed fear no attack from that direction. He then sealed Fennas Gost, not to protect himself from us, for we had not yet entered Mordor and he had little reason to think we could, but to protect himself from Sauron, and from Sauron's servants.\
\
'Why would they wish him ill? That is easy to see, ${PLAYER}. He commanded the loyalty of his own thralls, but there were other forces in Mordor that would deem him a failure, perhaps even a traitor to Sauron. Had he not suffered defeat after defeat in his guise of Mordirith, failing to achieve victory in the North? As Gothmog, had he not then suffered defeat on the field of battle before the walls of Minas Tirith? Yes, there are many in the Black Land who might question his loyalty, and none so greater than Sauron himself. Had the Quest of the Ring not succeeded, had the Dark Lord not fallen, who is to say what Sauron might have done to punish Gothmog? But Frodo did succeed, and Gothmog was given a reprieve, brief though it was.\
\
'I believe he searched the dungeons and hidden chambers of Minas Morgul for some weapon that might reverse his fortunes. I have learned enough of the Valley of the Secret Shadow to know that the entrance was blocked by enchantments fashioned by the Lord of the Nazgûl, such that the very passage was hidden to the eyes of all but the Nine and Sauron himself. But they are all gone, and now Falch Gurth lies open once again. Did Gothmog delve within, and did he find the weapon he sought inside Thuringwath? Now he hides within Barad Cúron, the Tower of the Crescent Moon. You must gain access to the tower, ${PLAYER}. Speak to Prince Faramir and he may know how this may be accomplished.'","Talk to Culang on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul","Chapter 13.8: Guardians of the Tower","'You seek to gain entrance to the tower? If you must go that way, go with caution, for I tell you it is not undefended. Some watchful presence guards the gate. More than that I cannot say, for I turned away upon sensing its presence.'","'The Watching-stone outside Barad Cúron will only allow Gúrzyul to pass? That may be a problem, my friend. The Ranger Annoth did tell us that Ugrukhôr seeks to gain access to the tower, but he seems unlikely to cooperate with us, ${PLAYER}, and as it stands we do not know for certain where the Captain of the Pit may be found. There is also the matter that if we did learn Ugrukhôr's location, Annoth would not allow us to join hands with his hated foe, no matter the purpose or duration of the peace. No, Ugrukhôr will not help us gain access to the tower.'\
\
Gandalf leans on his staff, deep in thought. When he stands up straight once again, there is a twinkling in his eye.\
\
'We have no Gúrzyul close at hand, ${PLAYER}... but perhaps we can make one of our own.'","Mithrandir wants you to adventure once again in Minas Morgul and investigate the enchantments that must bar the path to the Tower of the Crescent Moon."},
[2939]={"'We have known each other for less than a year, but it seems I have been indebted to you countless times. You have my thanks once again, ${PLAYER}, and those of my sister. You did not have to follow me into the darkness of Utug-bûr, risking entombment with our terrible foes, but you came with me anyway.'\
\
Corudan grasps your forearm tightly.\
\
'I will never forget that, my friend.'\
\
He releases your arm and your gaze. If you did not know better, you would think his expression might be one of embarrassment. It passes quickly and he is once again his usual practical self.\
\
'Could we have sealed the entrance to Utug-bûr without making use of the Narghâk, ${PLAYER}? Now it matters not, for the deed is done. The collapse required very little of the Hungry Fire, and much of that substance remains in the hidden stockpile deep within Ashâgir. We must set a guard upon it, night and day, to ensure that none think to use it for their own purposes.\
\
'You know of whom I speak, but I would not trust the Hungry Fire in the hands of any who seek it.'","The Dagor Carlanthir has ended, but the cost of victory was high and left its mark upon those who were there.","'This is... important, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Sirgon winces with the effort of speaking, but he refuses to be silent.\
\
'My wife... and my children... tell them I love... I love them. Tell them too... that I was a fool to leave... but that at the end... I was... at peace.\
\
'And I want you to... tell Gwallang... that I captained a boat... of my own. I set out upon... my final voyage... and I look forward to... to seeing him again... on a distant shore. Tell him not... that I died like... like this.'\
\
Sirgon closes his eyes and it seems he is gone, but with a great effort he opens them one last time.\
\
'Elessar... must not be... the foe of the... Shagâni people.... He must not be... the third... the third... Hyarmendacil...\
\
'Will you... help him... help him... live up to...?'","'But the cost of this victory was high. Those who survived the battle will need words of healing and of support now, ${PLAYER}. You must give them what you are able, for they will look to you for guidance: Shagâni, Umbari, and Gondorian alike.'","Sigileth is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","'Húrshauk now likes you very much. There is nothing like a shared victory to knit bonds of friendship, is there? Go ahead and give him a pat, ${PLAYER}. You and he have both earned it! Ha! Ha! Ha!'","'I received word as you approached the city, ${PLAYER}. I understand you faced a great evil on behalf of the Kindred of the Coins, and for that you have my thanks, and those of all Umbari. I look forward to a more detailed account of your adventure. Ask anything of the Kindred and it will be yours, if it is in our power to grant.'\
\
You tell Hármelak that without Belondor's arrival at Utug-bûr with his contingent of Umbari soldiers, the battle might have been lost. All you ask is the continued aid and support of Umbar Baharbêl against the servants of Morgoth that now threaten Middle-earth.\
\
'My city will be honoured to assist in this fight, ${PLAYER}. Is there aught else?'\
\
You tell Hármelak that the Wizard Inkanûsh will call upon the Kindred sometime in the days ahead, and he will have advice and guidance to provide. The Golden Queen stares at you thoughtfully.\
\
'I see. Speak to the guard outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja and tell him to expect this visitor. When the Wizard arrives he is to be allowed before us without delay.'","Jaith stands guard outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja.","'I was in darkness even before I passed the threshold into Utug-bûr, ${PLAYER}. As Azagath approached Silirtas with murder in his eye, I was overcome by a rage I have never felt before, and never will again. I pursued him into the temple, but I saw nothing of my surroundings; the steps were a red haze, the fog that surrounded me pulsed in time with the pounding of my blood. I would slay him, and I would die with him, and Silirtas would be avenged.'\
\
Sigileth stares at you with haunted eyes.\
\
'What did Silirtas say happens to a Kinta that is slain in battle? \\qThey become wandering, restless spirits, wrathful and hostile,\\q she said. For that to be her fate filled me with tremendous anger and sorrow, and still does. No amount of death and vengeance can repay Azagath or his masters for the cruel, endless un-life they have forced upon Silirtas.\
\
'Back in Umbar I spoke to Nauriel of the Green Hills about the futility of vengeance, and I meant it. Was that not the lesson of Cruel Dancer? I thought I had learned the lesson well, but it was not until I heard your voice in the darkness of Utug-bûr that I truly learned what it means to rise above the cycle of death. For Silirtas I gave it up. If she is to wander, I too will wander. If she is to be restless, I will try to give her rest. And if she is wrathful, I will seek to give her peace.\
\
'Baugliltir has done its work. I will leave it before Utug-bûr in memory of Silirtas, and of Cruel Dancer, and of Sigileth.'","Húrshauk rumbles at you appreciatively","Talk to Rothog at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'This triumph is bittersweet, ${PLAYER}. I am sorry for the losses you have suffered. I too weep for lost friends: dear Surdûsha, with whom I joined the ranks of the Dumûri only a few years ago, perished during the battle.\
\
'She would not wish me to dwell upon it, and as a trained warrior I know to do so is a weakness. But her loss cuts deeply.\
\
'I know this battle had to be fought eventually, ${PLAYER}, and if it was not waged in Urash Dâr it would one day have to be fought in Ambarûl, perhaps within Iridír itself. Surdûsha would not have wanted that, and neither would I.'","'I have made Sirgon as comfortable as I can, ${PLAYER}, but there is nothing else that can be done.\
\
'His final moments approach.'","'The stories of our past glories and our mighty heroes spread from fighter to fighter during the battle, inspiring each of my warriors to attain ever greater heights of skill and ferocity. In days to come, the tale of the Sabûdamar, the red-rush battle, will join those revered accounts!\
\
'When Rahâzi came to Iridír with your need, I considered sending only a small number of Dumûri in my stead; I am glad now I did not, for the battle was glorious and I would weep to miss it! Let the Ordâkhai tremble before our demonstrated might against foes older and more terrible than they, and know that to the Ambarûli they are nothing!'","Talk to Girhâzi at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Talk to Belondor at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'There are none in this land better than I at spy-craft. It was not always so... but it is now. Bear that in mind should you think to oppose my interests.'","'For now the Thardúth are defeated, but we must not lower our guard. I must learn more about these servants of Morgoth if we are to counter them, and I must learn it quickly. The Dominion of Zíkar passed beyond living memory, but record of its terrible rule in that distant age may remain hidden elsewhere in Shagâna. I will seek for this lost history, and if it is to be found anywhere I will find it. It seems I am to be Inkanûsh again! It has been many years since that name was used of me, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'But first I should speak with the rulers of Umbar. I understand one of their number remained behind in the city? The Lady Hármelak, you say? Go there and tell her a Wizard has advice and guidance to share, if she has the wisdom to heed it.'","'I am sorry, did you say I am to allow a Wizard inside the Meeting-hall? Imagine that! A real, live Wizard! I will of course allow him to pass.\
\
'Did he give you any indication of when he will arrive, ${PLAYER}? Are Wizards known to be punctual?'\
\
You assure Jaith that Inkanûsh the Wizard will arrive whenever he arrives, and not a moment sooner or later. He thanks you, a puzzled expression on his face, and says in that case he will wait for as long as he must.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>The story continues in future updates!</rgb>","Sirgon embarks upon his final voyage, and speaks no more","Girhâzi and Rahâzi are at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Khôltekh at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'Speak to the guard outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja and tell him to expect this visitor. When the Wizard arrives he is to be allowed before us without delay.'","'Húrshauk is a good judge of character... nearly as skilled at reading people as Rothog!'","Chapter 13.8: Last Words","Sigileth says nothing further.","Rothog's lion Húrshauk is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","'His final moments approach.'","'I know this battle had to be fought eventually, ${PLAYER}, and if it was not waged in Urash Dâr it would one day have to be fought in Ambarûl, perhaps within Iridír itself. Surdûsha would not have wanted that, and neither would I.'","Return to Hármelak in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, in Umbar Baharbêl","'But first I should speak with the rulers of Umbar. I understand one of their number remained behind in the city? The Lady Hármelak, you say? Go there and tell her a Wizard has advice and guidance to share, if she has the wisdom to heed it.'","Húrshauk waits for you to <rgb=#00FF00>pat</rgb> him","Corudan is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Rahâzi at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'I heard something very interesting, ${PLAYER}. I heard that not only is the son of Balakhôr alive, but he was seen fighting on the edge of the battle. I wonder: how could this be true when you assured me that Balakhâd was dead?'\
\
Instead of answering the question, you pose one of your own, asking what Khôltekh knows about the disappearance of the water-bearer Sadûkh from Ghalbûru. The dwarf eyes you appraisingly.\
\
'I must apologize, ${PLAYER}, for I underestimated you. It will not happen again.\
\
'But know this: there are none in this land better than I at spy-craft. It was not always so... but it is now. Bear that in mind should you think to oppose my interests.'","'My hunger for battle is sated... for now! My khopeshes are in need of sharpening once again, and is that not the mark of a successful journey?\
\
'I enjoyed fighting alongside Tatháta, but she seems to have disappeared again. In the brief time that I have known her she has never enjoyed large gatherings... unless those large gatherings involve a great number of combatants!\
\
'Few can understand the leonine language of Húrshauk as I can, but I will tell you that he now likes you very much. There is nothing like a shared victory to knit bonds of friendship, is there? Go ahead and give him a pat, ${PLAYER}. You and he have both earned it! Ha! Ha! Ha!'","Hármelak is in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","Rothog's lion Húrshauk looks at you pointedly","Belondor is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Jaith outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","Talk to Corudan at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","'We must set a guard upon Ashâgir, night and day, to ensure that none think to use the Hungry Fire for their own purposes.'","'Let the Ordâkhai tremble before our demonstrated might against foes older and more terrible than they, and know that to the Ambarûli they are nothing!'","Rothog is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","'The cost of this victory was high. Those who survived the battle will need words of healing and of support now, ${PLAYER}. You must give them what you are able, for they will look to you for guidance: Shagâni, Umbari, and Gondorian alike.'","Talk to Mithrandir at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Khôltekh is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Hármelak in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","'This is... important, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Sirgon winces with the effort of speaking, but he refuses to be silent.\
\
'My wife... and my children... tell them I love... I love them. Tell them too... that I was a fool to leave... but that at the end... I was... at peace.'\
\
Sirgon closes his eyes and it seems he is gone, but with a great effort he opens them one last time.\
\
'Elessar... must not be... the foe of the... Shagâni people.... He must not be... the third... the third... Hyarmendacil...\
\
'Will you... help him... help him... live up to...?'","Talk to Sigileth at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Sirgon is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Hármelak watches as you approach her dais","Talk to Sirgon at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Mithrandir is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr."},
[2940]={"Talk to Mithrandir at the Eagle and Star","A familiar figure nods in greeting","'That is the tale, as it is known to the Wise and to those of Isildur's line. But I would have you remember this, ${PLAYER}: whatever Eärnur may have been, that man is no more. Do not let the knowledge of who he once was stay the punishment that is due. He is now wholly evil, and all of Middle-earth has suffered at his hands and those of his masters.'","Mithrandir has come to the Eagle and Star.","Investigate the mysterious figure in the darkened corner of the tavern","Aragorn is at the Eagle and Star, and he wishes to tell you the story of Eärnur's last days.","'So you are still alive, ${PLAYER}? Good for you. When last I saw you, you planned a foolish raid upon some stronghold in Mordor, thinking a disguise might keep you safe. It seems the advice I gave you proved helpful, for you live still! Are you here to thank me for your survival? Know that I am Ayorzén the Unrewarded, and will gracefully accept whatever coin or treasure you balance against your life!'\
\
Ayorzén's eyes narrow when no reward is forthcoming, and they narrow further when you tell him you need his help gaining access to the tower atop Minas Morgul.\
\
'You only come to me when you need something, ${PLAYER}. Am I to dress up as one of the Nurnhoth, as you did before? For I will not. I led the Khundolar into battle! Men followed me to war, even to death, and if my star has fallen low it will rise again. I wear these garments now, but in time I will again don my shining armour, and lead Men to victory! Keep your base disguise. Ayorzén the Proud will have none of it.'","Aragorn is at the Eagle and Star.","'What has your friend Ayorzén gotten up to of late, ${PLAYER}? Is he still as Wily as he ever was? Go to Minas Tirith and speak with the gossipmonger Meldir, just inside the entrance to the city. He will know where the Easterlings who came out of Gorgoroth have gone.'","The door of the tavern swings open and Mithrandir enters","Ayorzén watches you guardedly, and with suspicion","Ayorzén says nothing, his eyes still fixed upon the mask of Karazgar.","'I will never again wear the clothes of a prisoner. Indeed, the garment I wear now seems too near to that for comfort!'","'If you seek Easterlings, you may find them at the Eagle and Star, to the south-west.'","Ayorzén does not know the disguise you had in mind","Talk to Aragorn at the Eagle and Star","Talk to Ayorzén at the Eagle and Star","Talk to Aragorn and complete 'Instance: The Warrior Remade'","Find Ayorzén at the Eagle and Star, in Minas Tirith","Ayorzén's eyes widen in surprise","Mithrandir has a plan for you to deceive the guardians of Barad Cúron, but it will require some outside help.","Meldir told you that Ayorzén might be found at the Eagle and Star, a tavern south-west of the entrance to Minas Tirith.","Talk to Meldir just inside the entrance to Minas Tirith","'Did you kill him, then? There is only one mask such as this in all the world, ${PLAYER}, and the Weeping Warrior would never part with it. Long did he stalk the lands of my people, bringing death without mercy to all. For all my years, the mention of his name drained the courage of even the bravest soldier, and set to weeping mothers and fathers both, remembering children slain by his blades for no reason at all. The sight of his mask commanded...'\
\
Ayorzén falls silent.","Place the mask of Karazgar on the table in front of Ayorzén","'Old habits do not always vanish easily, my friend. It remains a wonder to me how much a difference one's garb can make in the eyes of the people. What would Barliman have to say if he saw me in my king's raiment? No, I should prefer to wear this to the Pony. That is Strider's place, not Elessar's.\
\
'Mithrandir has told me some of what he has learned from that tome you discovered in Járnfast, and he entreated me to tell you what I know of King Eärnur's last days. Some of this you may have heard already, but the true story was never intended for the ears of the common folk, and some of it was passed down only by the Wise and to those of Isildur's line, kept secret in the wilderness.\
\
'I will tell you what I know of it, if that is your wish.'","'I will tell you the tale of Eärnur's last days, as it was told to me.'","Ayorzén is at the Eagle and Star in Minas Tirith.","You should place the mask of Karazgar on the table in front of Ayorzén, and enlist him to help you.","Ayorzén the Wily is at the Eagle and Star in Minas Tirith.","'He is further inside, in the corner. Speak to him while Ayorzén considers our proposal.'","'Nay, my friend, do not look at me with such horror! I do not speak of performing Sauron's dread ritual! The act of bleeding the men and women that became the Gúrzyul required more than just Sauron's morgul-knife Gulthauk. It needed also a will of evil, and be glad that is not a thing we possess. But we do have in hand something else.'\
\
The Wizard opens his satchel of possessions and removes an unpleasant artifact: the Mask of Karazgar.\
\
'The Weeping Warrior dogged our steps in the North, ${PLAYER}, and he inflicted much pain and sorrow upon dwarves and Men. But he does possess two useful traits: his reputation, and his absence. Of all the Gúrzyul, he may be the most feared: a Black Númenórean who moved with stealth, appearing out of nowhere to slay and torment before vanishing, leaving only the memory of a frightening visage, a masked evil. He captured dragons and brought them to Sauron, but it is long since he was seen in Mordor. Rumour of his cruelties in far-off Rhûn will have spread even here.\
\
'I think the spirit of this Watching-stone will know of the Weeping Warrior and his exploits in the East and in the North, and I think too that it will not have seen him in long centuries, if at all. Were you to wear the mask, the spirit would no doubt see through our deception. But if another were to wear it, perhaps one of the Khundolar who rarely come to the Vale, who is to say what the spirit might think? And if Karazgar were to bring a powerful prisoner to Gothmog, the very ${RACE} who has proven so troublesome to Gothmog's schemes, would the spirit not allow both of them access to the inner sanctum?\
\
'What has your friend Ayorzén gotten up to of late, ${PLAYER}? Is he still as Wily as he ever was? Go to Minas Tirith and speak with the gossipmonger Meldir just inside the entrance of the city. He will know where the Easterlings who came out of Gorgoroth have gone.'","Talk to Ayorzén the Wily at the Eagle and Star","Mithrandir has directed your attention to a darkened corner in the room furthest from the entrance.","Aragorn has come to the Eagle and Star to meet with you, wearing a disguise that hides his identity.","'You are looking for Easterlings? Aye, King Elessar has called for them to be given places to stay in Gondor, and the kingdom will follow his command. But he cannot bid every man or woman of Gondor to open their hearts to these newcomers, and were he to try he would likely face his first failure as king. Many here lost loved ones to Khundolar swords within view of these walls, and they can neither forget nor forgive it.\
\
'But if you seek Easterlings, you may find them at the Eagle and Star, to the south-west. The barkeep there has welcomed their coin, at least.'","Chapter 13.9: The Warrior Remade","The gossipmonger Meldir is just inside the entrance to Minas Tirith.\
\
Mithrandir has sent you to Minas Tirith seeking the assistance of Ayorzén, but first you need to find him.","'Has he agreed to our scheme, ${PLAYER}? Ah, I see he considers it. May he hasten his decision! How much time does he think we have?\
\
'But there is another here with whom I would have you speak. Did you not notice him enter? I see his ascension has not diminished his former skill at moving without being seen, nor his desire to make use of it!\
\
'Unless I miss my guess he will be in the furthest room, ${PLAYER}, in a darkened corner.'","'If you seek Easterlings, you may find them at the Eagle and Star, to the south-west. The barkeep there accepts their coin, at least.'"},
[2941]={"'Tulk está esperando para hablar contigo justo al otro lado de las Puertas de Durin. Lo recuerdas, ¿verdad? Está complacido de que hayas sido de tanta ayuda para la expedición y le encantará volver a hablar contigo.'","Tulk está justo al otro lado de las Puertas de Durin, junto al lago inmóvil donde luchaste contra el Guardián del Agua.\
\
Te han dicho que hables con Tulk sobre los enanos que han entrado en Moria.","Capítulo 13: ¡Khazad-dûm al fin!","'¡Hola, ${PLAYER}! ¡Por fin estamos dentro de Khazad-dûm! Hay muchísimo trabajo por hacer en los distintos campamentos que estamos levantando aquí, y puedes ayudarnos a tener éxito en la enorme tarea que tenemos por delante.\
\
'Bósi me pidió que te recompensara por tu liderazgo ante las Puertas. Toma esto con su agradecimiento y el de toda la Guarnición de Hierro.'","'Tulk está justo al otro lado de las Puertas de Durin, esperando para hablar contigo.\
\
'El Lago Negro está vacío ahora y parece seguro, aunque sigue siendo fétido. Tulk te dirá cómo puedes seguir ayudando a la Guarnición de Hierro cuando llegues al interior de Moria.'","Los enanos por fin han entrado en Moria, pero su labor no ha hecho más que empezar. Tendrás que ayudarles en su lucha si quieren lograr algún éxito en las salas olvidadas de Khazad-dûm."},
[2942]={"Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, en Gathbúrz.\
\
Has derrotado a los espíritus crueles en los Pasajes de Cenizas y has recuperado los libros de hechizos utilizados por los estudiantes de Gorothúl para atarlos a su servicio.","'Según estos planes de batalla, los hechiceros bajo la tutela de Gorothúl buscan invocar espíritus crueles al servicio de los ejércitos de Dol Guldur. No es la primera vez que escuchamos esto, pero apoya las palabras de Súlthel, un explorador Malledhrim que pasó por aquí al regresar a Ost Galadh.\
\
'No se puede permitir esta vil artesanía del Enemigo. Viaja hacia el sureste a los Pasajes de Cenizas y busca a Sâd Doldúr. Derrota a cualquiera de los espíritus crueles que los hechiceros allí ya han atado a su servicio. Derrota también a los estudiantes de Gorothúl y apodérate de los libros de hechizos con los que trabajan su maldad.\
\
'Ninguno de estos hechiceros tendrá la habilidad de Gorothúl, pero aún así serán enemigos peligrosos. No subestimes ninguna de las fuerzas del Enemigo.'","'Has hecho bien en traerme estos libros y en derrotar a los espíritus crueles que encontraste en Sâd Doldúr antes de que pudieran ser usados contra nosotros. Me aseguraré de que los libros sean destruidos.\
\
'Hay poco tiempo que perder, ${PLAYER}. Los exploradores informan que los ejércitos de Gathbúrz pueden estar en marcha.'","Recoge los libros de hechizos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los espíritus crueles y los hechiceros que los invocan se encuentran en Sâd Doldúr y en los Pasajes de Cenizas. Derrota a estos estudiantes de Gorothúl y prívate de los libros de hechizos con los que trabajan su maldad.'","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","Ningloril ha estudiado los planes que recuperaste y ha aprendido que los hechiceros bajo la tutela de Gorothúl están invocando espíritus crueles en los Pasajes de Cenizas.","Espíritus crueles derrotados en los Pasajes de Cenizas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva los libros de hechizos a Ningloril para que sean destruidos","Los espíritus crueles y los hechiceros que los invocan se encuentran en Sâd Doldúr y en los Pasajes de Cenizas.\
\
Ningloril te ha pedido que derrotes a los espíritus crueles que están siendo atados al servicio de los estudiantes de Gorothúl en los Pasajes de Cenizas y que prives a los hechiceros de sus libros de hechizos.","Libros de hechizos recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Capítulo 13: Los estudiantes de Gorothúl","Derrota a los espíritus crueles en los Pasajes de Cenizas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2943]={"'You must find Wadu's father. He will likely be at the Uch-lûth village of Lhanuch, and must be given both the unhappy news and the sword that was taken from his son.'","Find Wadu's sister Nona at Lhanuch and give her the ancient sword","Chapter 13: The Sword Returned","Find Wadu's father at Lhanuch and give him the ancient sword","'If you must speak of Wadu, you waste your time! I will not hear of him! Bring your words of him to his sister Nona, if you must, but waste my time no further!'","Wadu's father Suvulch can be found somewhere within the Uch-lûth village of Lhanuch.\
\
You need to find the father of Wadu and bring him the sad news of his son's death. Additionally, he should be given the ancient sword of the Rohirrim that was taken from Wadu when he was slain.","Wadu's sister Nona can be found somewhere within Lhanuch, the village of the Uch-lûth, in Nan Laeglin.\
\
Suvulch has coldly dismissed the death of his son Wadu, calling him a coward. You should bring the news of Wadu's death and the ancient Rohirrim sword to his sister Nona instead.","'It is no use dwelling upon such mysteries, for we may never know the answers to them. He spoke of his family to you, did he not? They must be told of his death, and the sword returned to them.\
\
'You will likely find them at Lhanuch, the village of the Uch-lûth, in Nan Laeglin. You should ask the people there until you find his father and bring him both the unhappy news and the sword.\
\
'It may seem cold, but perhaps the death of his son at the hands of another Dunlending clan will soften the father's heart to the Dúnedain. Wadu may still help us in our errand, though he be slain.'","The sword that was taken from Wadu should be returned to his family at the village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin.","'Speak not to me of Wadu! He is a coward, and no son of mine!'\
\
The silence following this proclamation stretches awkwardly for too long a time. Suvulch reads your expression.\
\
'He is dead? Then his chance for courage is ended, and I mourn only that. No, I will hear no more of it! If you have words of Wadu, tell them to his sister. If the powers were just, Nona would have been the son and he the daughter, for she is like iron and could make her father proud! With the clans all around the Uch-lûth preparing for war and closing in upon us, the only good thing Wadu ever did for us is rid us of his cowering presence!'","'You have nothing for me? Begone.'","Nona listens sorrowfully as you recount your discovery of her brother's death. There is the briefest trembling within her deep eyes, then it is gone. The emotion mastered, Nona stares at you sternly.\
\
'Wadu was not the fighter our father Suvulch wanted him to be, and when he spoke to him, which was rarely, Suvulch was cruel. I tried to give Wadu the lessons he needed, lessons in the sword and the axe and the ways of fire, but I could not teach him the courage he needed. My words to him were harsh. If they drove him to his death I would have them back!'"},
[2944]={"Glorfindel is in Sul Madásh.","'I do not understand your meaning, Cúridwan! Can you not speak more clearly, in remembrance of the friendship we once shared?\
\
'What does the choice of the Kintai so many years ago have to do with poor slain Baharúd?'","'This is my purpose for coming to this place, ${PLAYER}. I know it. I must bring these tidings to Silirtas, no matter how difficult or dangerous that task may be.'","Cúridwan is in Sul Madásh.","'On this subject my lips are sealed, ${PLAYER}. Ulishár and Baharúd lived their lives among the Kintai, and I will not speak against the traditions of their people.\
\
'And yet in my heart I feel it is wrong to say \\qtheir\\q people. Perhaps they are truly \\qmy\\q people after all, though long divided by time and tradition.'","'Our visit to Sul Madásh has been an eventful one, but our work here is not yet done. Some of the Utûgi fled back into Adagím. We must track them down before we continue south to join with Mizâdi's army.'","'Could one of the Kintai be welcomed in that distant place that lies beyond death?'","Chapter 14.10: One People","'That was their choice, but none commanded the choice must be forever.'","Talk to Sigileth in Sul Madásh","'Can you not speak more clearly, in remembrance of the friendship we once shared?'","'This is what I have been seeking, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Sigileth turns to face you, and you see tears in her eyes. The Elf-warrior seems not to notice them.\
\
'I must find the Väiri that was once Silirtas. I must tell her that the westward way to the Undying Lands is open to her. She is not doomed to the endless unlife of a wandering, rageful spirit, but can choose to accept the fate of the Eldar and pass into the Blessed Realm!\
\
'This is my purpose for coming to this place, ${PLAYER}. I know it. I must bring these tidings to Silirtas, no matter how difficult or dangerous that task may be.'","'For all of my life I have been told this is the way of my people. I know not what to think.'","Inkanûsh is in Sul Madásh.","A hush has fallen over Sul Madásh.","A hush has fallen over Sul Madásh","'Perhaps I am being foolish, but I spoke to my brother of this choice. I spoke of something I never considered before today, something I do not believe myself. Can such a land of peace and beauty truly exist beyond death? And why would such a place be open to my people, who were unwilling to follow Taknûn the Hunter to it when he sought to bring us there so many centuries before?\
\
'Is it not better to remain in the land with which you are familiar, even if your memories fade and all that remains is the anger and disappointment of the Väiri? For all of my life I have been told this is the way of my people. I do not know what to think, ${PLAYER}.'","In the aftermath of the Utûgi raid on Sul Madásh, Cúridwan has surprising news to share with the Kintai.","Talk to Cúridwan in Sul Madásh","'If the Sorceress in Green here remained, she might already have restored the Emerald Wood! But of her I have received no word.'","'It is natural to fear that which you have not seen, Ulishár. But I believe Cúridwan has spoken true.'","Talk to Ulishár in Sul Madásh","Talk to Inkanûsh in Sul Madásh","'The choice lies with Baharúd.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Sing</rgb> or <rgb=#00FF00>mourn</rgb> in your own way.","Ulishár is in Sul Madásh.","Sigileth is in Sul Madásh.","'It is the memory of our friendship that compels me to ease your heart, dear Ulishár, if it is in my power to do so! But I can speak no more clearly than this.'\
\
Cúridwan extends her arms to encompass all the Elves that stand nearby: Sigileth, Corudan, Glorfindel, and the sorrowful Kintai watchers.\
\
'The Elves were fashioned as one people, not as two. The west road is not closed to the Kintai, though they followed it not when it was offered. Should a Kinta set aside his fear of the unknown, the fate given to all the Elves could be his as well.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Sing</rgb> or <rgb=#00FF00>mourn</rgb> in your own way","'I know not what your brother would choose for himself, Ulishár. None but Baharúd can know if he would choose to remain in this land he loved or if he would accept the fate given to Elvendom at its creation.\
\
'We must all mourn him in our own way, but if you sing or speak of this choice, it may be he will hear you. The long traditions of the Kintai may have hidden this possibility from him, but they could not have taken it from him entirely.'","'Set aside these doubts, Ulishár, if you can. I know such words come more easily to the speaker than to he who hears them! And yet I ask you to heed them all the same, for I have cause to believe what Cúridwan has spoken today.\
\
'Many of the Elven-wise dwell in the Blessed Realm beyond the circles of the world; they return not to Middle-earth. In the Undying Lands all weariness falls away, and there the warmth of the sunrise banishes all earthly concerns: pain, fear, and doubt have no hold upon that place, and those who dwell within.\
\
'It is natural to fear that which you have not seen, Ulishár. But I believe Cúridwan has spoken true: the Eldar and the Kintai were fashioned as a single people, no matter the separate roads down which they walked afterward. Your people are a part of Elvendom, as is Glorfindel and these others. I believe the Kintai could share their fate, if they desired it.'","Talk to Glorfindel in Sul Madásh","'Never before have I sought to interfere with the traditions of the Kintai. What has happened to work this change in me, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'I ask despite knowing the answer. It is the blight that holds Adagím in its grip that causes me to speak these words aloud! Rarely did I speak with Baharúd beyond the exchange of simple greetings and well-wishing, but some years ago his brother Ulishár was dear to me. It grieves me to see Ulishár's sorrow that his brother's spirit must remain trapped within blighted Adagím, when I know it might be otherwise.\
\
'If the Sorceress in Green here remained, she might already have restored the Emerald Wood! But of her I have received no word.'","'Even if that were so...'\
\
Ulishár stares sadly at the body of his brother Baharúd.\
\
'Could one of the Kintai be welcomed in that distant place that lies beyond death? Or would he be considered a stranger and turned aside?\
\
'We have been so long apart. What could this place hold for a Kinta save fear and resentment?'","'Many of the Kintai I have known so loved their lands they sought to remain there beyond death, fading from all but memory; their Veróthi remain to comfort those they leave behind. This has been the tradition of the Tárthai ever since they chose not to follow the one they call Taknûn the Hunter on the great journey westward. They feared what lay at the end of that road, and preferred to remain in the lands they knew and had come to love.\
\
'That was their choice, but none commanded the choice must be forever.'"},
[2945]={"Since you have returned to the grove of Laivárth, you should speak to Shadalith and see if everything is all right.","Examine the corpse of the dead Utûgi warrior","This warrior of the Utûgi died not to blade or arrow, but to something else","Inkanûsh is waiting in Sul Madásh for you to return with news of the raiding-party of Utûgi.","Find the fleeing Utûgi warriors near Laivárth","The creature that slew the Utûgi warriors has come back for you!","Shadalith wanted you to see what happened to her bucket in Laivárth.","Talk to Shadalith in Laivárth","'A party of great brutish Orcs approached the Hill of the Mother not long ago, shouting harsh cries and moving at great speed. I hid behind Amûma for fear they would discover me, but before they espied me they were discovered by something else!'\
\
Irsinith smiles grimly.\
\
'A mass of spiders boiled from the underbrush and fell upon the Orcs. The one you saw perished immediately; the rest of the raiding-party escaped further to the west. It is possible they might encounter Laivárth, but I suspect their preoccupation with the attacking spiders may hide the grove from their discovery.\
\
'It is said that a terrifying spider dwells somewhere within the forest, Badharál the Gorger by name. I never believed I would be glad to see the arrival of Badharál's spawn, but on this day I must confess I was!\
\
'Still, I am glad they did not turn their attention upon me. Perhaps Amûma shielded me from discovery.'","'The bucket fell apart a short time after you left, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps the samples of the blight interacted with the water in a curious way? The combination seems to have undone the sealings between the slats of my bucket... and now I need a new bucket. I may have learned something, but what I have learned remains a mystery to me. Such is the way of wisdom, I suppose.\
\
'You need not worry about my problems, friend. Judging from the sounds of battle I heard before you arrived, I deem that you have plenty of your own! Thank you for visiting Laivárth again and checking in on me! Return to Sul Madásh with my friendship.'","'The surviving Utûgi fled from Sul Madásh in the direction of the Hill of the Mother. Blighted though she be, I fear the damage such creatures might do to the old tree in their wrath.\
\
'Hurry there and ensure they inflict no harm upon her, ${PLAYER}.'","Shadalith is in the grove of Laivárth.","The remaining Utûgi warriors escaped to the north-west, heading for the grove of Laivárth.","Inkanûsh asked you to pursue the Utûgi raiders before they cause further harm to the Kintai of Adagím.","'Hurry to the Hill of the Mother and ensure the fleeing Utûgi inflict no harm upon her!'","Follow the escaping Utûgi north-west to the Hill of the Mother","'Ah, my friend! It is good to see you again! I was hoping you would return to Laivárth so I could tell you what I have learned from my experimentation with the samples of the blight you brought to me.'\
\
Shadalith pauses dramatically.\
\
'The blight hates buckets! See for yourself!'","'Terrible creatures with the mien of Orcs approached the Hill of the Mother not long ago.'","Shadalith's bucket has fallen apart, spilling its water everywhere","Examine Shadalith's bucket in Laivárth","The other Utûgi warriors perished outside the grove of Laivárth.","One of the Utûgi succumbed to its wounds not far from the Hill of the Mother.","Something slew the last of the fleeing Utûgi outside Laivárth","'Thank you for visiting Laivárth again and checking in on me! Return to Sul Madásh with my friendship.'","One of the Utûgi, at least, succumbed to his wounds","Examine the corpse outside Laivárth... and survive","Talk to Inkanûsh in Sul Madásh","Chapter 14.11: The Raiders Pursued","The Utûgi escaped to the north-west. That way lies the Hill of the Mother!","Irsinith may have seen what befell the Utûgi raiding-party as it approached the Hill of the Mother.","'The rest of the raiding-party escaped further to the west, in the direction of Laivárth.'","Talk to Irsinith on the other side of Amûma at the Hill of the Mother","'The blight samples you brought to me have had an adverse effect upon my bucket!'","You survived your encounter with the spawn of Badharál","'You have accounted for all of the fleeing Utûgi raiders? Good, good, good. Then it should be safe for us to continue southward into Kighân without fear that we leave Sul Madásh in peril if they were to return.\
\
'I have enlisted the aid of a guide to show us the way further south into Mûr Ghala. You have already met him, ${PLAYER}. His name is Ulishár.'"},
[2946]={"Talk to Beregond in Echad Uial","Defeat Orcs in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ayorzén has agreed to help you gain access to Barad Cúron, but even with the Easterling's aid this mission will not be free of danger.","'I do not like this Easterling. I do not want him troubling Prince Faramir.'","'Go with Ayorzén to speak with the Ranger Culang on the uppermost tier of the city, outside the entrance to the tower, but first investigate each of these threats as you climb up each level of the city. If Gothmog or the other Masters of Mordor have called for this increased activity on the part of their minions, they must be opposed.'","Beregond is at Echad Uial, in Imlad Morgul.","'Let us go to this camp, then. Ayorzén is not afraid.'","'Kill them all, kill every one!'\
\
Beneath the mask of Karazgar, you hear Ayorzén giggling to himself.\
\
'Do you not find me more convincing than the Weeping Warrior himself?'","'I am ready. Are you not?'","Defeat the Dead in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Ayorzén at the Eagle and Star","'I do not like this Easterling, ${PLAYER}. Are you certain we have no other choice?'","'I have never seen the inside of this city before now. It is not as frightening as your people led me to expect, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps they are all cowards after all?'","'Good fortune to you, ${PLAYER}. I think you will need it.'","Talk to Ayorzén on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul","Chapter 14.1: The Closing Net","Ayorzén is on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul.","Talk to Ayorzén at Echad Uial","'Something has been happening in the upper levels of the tower, ${PLAYER}. A short time ago a flight of merrevail descended upon the beacon. I could not see from here what they tried to do, but whatever it was they did not achieve it; there was a great flash and a sound as of thunder, and dozens of them fell in torment.\
\
'It has been quiet since then, but I do not trust the silence. Be careful if you still intend to carry out Mithrandir's plan.'","Defeated the Dead in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It has been quiet ever since the merrevail attacked, but I do not trust the silence. Be careful if you still intend to carry out Mithrandir's plan.'","'Something has happened on the upper levels of the city, ${PLAYER}, but I know not what. Merrevail were seen clinging to the upper reaches of Barad Cúron, illuminated in the light of the tower's beacon, and something has stirred the Orcs in the lower levels to greater activity. Of the risen Dead in the middle tiers there are few reports, but that in itself gives me concern.\
\
'Go with Ayorzén to speak with the Ranger Culang on the uppermost level of the city, outside the entrance to the tower, but first investigate each of these threats as you climb up each tier of the city. If Gothmog or the other Masters of Mordor have called for this increased activity on the part of their minions, they must be opposed.\
\
'Have they enacted the final stages of some scheme, even as we prepare to undertake our own? I hope it is not so, but an air of dread and mystery lies upon Minas Morgul and it makes me wonder.'","Ayorzén has come to Echad Uial, in Imlad Morgul.","Ayorzén is at the Eagle and Star in Minas Tirith.","Mithrandir has returned to Echad Uial, in Imlad Morgul.","You tell Ayorzén how to get to Echad Uial","'The men here do not like me, ${PLAYER}. It brings a smile to my face to hear their whispers, to see the way they look at me with fear in their eyes. Why? Because it means they remember. Even fallen so low, Ayorzén is not forgotten. If the cards had fallen differently, these others might be unwelcome guests in my own war-camp, and they would not be free to whisper then. This man, this Beregond? He is a mere underling. But Ayorzén was no man's underling.\
\
'I remember leading my own band, strong Khundolar warriors who would live or die at my command. Perhaps that time will come again, for I feel my star is once again on the rise! After all, you will soon be indebted to me for this favour, as will many other powerful men. Why, Beregond's own prince will be in my debt, and perhaps then he will speak to me with more respect.\
\
'Call me Ayorzén the Prepared, ${PLAYER}, for I am ready; ready for this plan of yours, and for a hopeful future.'","'I will play the part of Karazgar, ${PLAYER}, but Ayorzén the Helpful has a number of conditions.\
\
'Know this: I will not endanger myself to save you! If this deception appears ready to fail, I will not maintain it. You may be a friend to me in this city, but in the Morgul Vale the only men who still have friends are the dead ones. The living cannot stay living if they hold friendship more dearly than their own skin. Ayorzén must come first. Are we agreed?\
\
'Yes? Very well. I did not escape the end of the war and the dungeons of the Dark Lord to die in the Morgul Vale. If that is understood, then I will help you. Where do we need to go?'","Orcs and other foes remain a danger within Minas Morgul, and you should thin their numbers before setting Mithrandir's plan into motion.","Culang is standing watch near the entrance to Barad Cúron on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul.","Mithrandir calls you to speak with him","Defeated Orcs in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat merrevail in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Culang on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul","Defeated merrevail in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Mithrandir in Echad Uial","'Mithrandir has told me of his plan, and I will not speak against it. But I urge you to remain alert, ${PLAYER}, for many centuries have passed since the Tower of the Crescent Moon last fell into the grasp of evil. Even Mithrandir cannot say what you might find within. Gothmog alone would be threat enough, but while Sauron held our attention Gothmog had time enough to ransack Minas Morgul for its secrets; he may have prepared some defence or trap we cannot anticipate.\
\
'I will give you one further warning. If the Khundolar Ayorzén does agree to help you with this, remain alert for any sign of treachery. I believe he will aid you for as long as his interests align with yours; see that they do and he may be worthy of trust. But if that becomes otherwise...\
\
'Good fortune to you, ${PLAYER}. I think you will need it.'"},
[2947]={"Stand by the small knot of people to the south of Tasâdi and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation","'Rumours are like water, my friend. If you have the ability to keep it contained, you can control who receives it, and its value only increases. But once it is spilled, there is no returning it to the container!\
\
'Whispers about the approaching Wizard have already spread throughout the market, and few are interested in what I have to say about him, for they can hear these tidings everywhere! My trade is in news and information... what now can I do?\
\
'Alas for Tasâdi, once the most accomplished rumourmonger in all of Umbar Baharbêl! She is finished. Fine, then! Go to the south and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to the whispers of my former customers. They know all that I have heard, and more beside!'","Despite the claims of the Umbari that they would know the Wizard when he entered the city, just such a person has already arrived.","'Have you seen him? Has a Wizard come to Umbar Baharbêl?'","Some folk just past the fountain south of Phârex are discussing the effect a Wizard could have on the political situation of Umbar Baharbêl. You should <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation.","Talk to Inkanûsh beside the Fathomwell beyond the archway","Stand by the small group of people to the south past the fountain and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation","Talk to Phârex at the Waterway Market","'This talk is getting out of hand, if you ask me. What use could we have for a Wizard? Folk such as that bring only trouble. They say they can take on many forms, and creep undiscovered into places where they are not wanted! I did not trust the cultists of the All Seeing, and I will not trust a Wizard either... they seem little different to me!'","Ushrin has his own opinions concerning the effect of a Wizard on these lands.","Talk to Ushrin at the Waterway Market","Talk to Tasâdi at the Waterway Market","'I have heard the arrival of a Wizard heralds the onset of good fortune! Wherever he walks, golden coins are said to fall from his pockets, and these are free for the taking by any who chance upon him!\
\
'I have kept my eyes peeled for him, but my wife also expects me to make my purchases at the market and return to her. How am I to shop while there could be a Wizard and his golden coins so near, with me blind to his presence?'","Tasâdi usually holds court at the Waterway Market to the south-east of Dâr Laja.","'Alas for Tasâdi, once the most accomplished rumourmonger in all of Umbar Baharbêl! She is finished. Fine, then! Go to the south and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to the whispers of my former customers. They know all that I have heard, and more beside!'","Phârex has caught your eye.","During a gap in the argument, you hear a familiar chuckle from beyond the archway","'Can it be so? Has the day come at last?'\
\
Jaith looks about furtively before continuing with a hushed, eager tone.\
\
'Rumours abound that the Wizard Inkanûsh now approaches the city! We guardsmen of Umbar Baharbêl trade not in gossip... but Kinsman Belondor's soldiers returned from Ikorbân with news of him, and they say he will perform feats of magic for any who ask him! These are dangerous times, ${PLAYER}, as you well know, and the Kindred of the Coins might have need of such feats if they are to keep their people safe.\
\
'Will you go to the Waterway Market to the south-east and see if anyone has yet seen the Wizard Inkanûsh? The rumourmonger Tasâdi often holds court there at this time of day, and if anyone has heard anything about the Wizard, it will be she!'","'Ah, there you are, my friend. I wondered if you would come to see me here.\
\
'I have overheard one or two fanciful beliefs about me and my Order while I rested here. I shall not test your patience by repeating them.'\
\
You ask the Wizard where he keeps all of his golden coins, and he chuckles to himself.\
\
'I see that you have heard some of them. Did you hear too that I apparently possess the ability to take on forms enough to put Beorn himself to shame? Alas, it is not so. Still, the Umbari were so eager to see this impressive figure they have imagined that they paid me little mind, and I entered the city with little fanfare. I have been quite untroubled today... or perhaps I should say I have not been disturbed by the Umbari. The threat posed by the Thardúth and their Utûgi warriors fills me with unease.'","'Will you go to the Waterway Market to the south-east and see if anyone has yet seen the Wizard Inkanûsh? The rumourmonger Tasâdi often holds court there at this time of day, and if anyone has heard anything about the Wizard, it will be she!'","A small knot of people to the south of Tasâdi seem to be discussing what they have heard. You should <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation.","A small knot of people to the south of Ushrin loudly discuss the rumours concerning a Wizard's powers. You should <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation.","Chapter 14.1: Whispers of Wizardry","Umbar Baharbêl is alive with rumour that a Wizard will soon arrive to speak with the Kindred of the Coins about the many threats facing the city.","'What use could we have for a Wizard? Folk such as that bring only trouble.'","The opinions of these folk are split concerning the value a Wizard might provide","They notice you listening to their talk and quickly fall silent","Stand by the small group of people to the south of Ushrin and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation"},
[2948]={"'I sense the presence of my bones, ${PLAYER}! They are nearby!'","Talk to Ayorzén on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul and complete 'Instance: Gothmog's Rage'","The nearby presence of Isildur's bones has allowed his shade to assume physical form in Barad Cúron.","Talk to the shade of Isildur in Barad Cúron","'I will do my best to get you beyond the guardians of the tower, ${PLAYER}, but I will not die for you.\
\
'We will meet back here if we get separated.'","Chapter 14.2: Gothmog's Rage","Ayorzén is on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul, willing to help you gain access to the Tower of the Crescent Moon.","The time has come to deal with Gothmog. With Ayorzén's help, you hope to gain access to the Tower of the Crescent Moon and your long-time foe hiding within.","'But I am no coward, and I am ready to play my part in this foolhardy scheme. Are you as prepared as Ayorzén the Courageous?'"},
[2949]={"'This is not the first time I have come to Shagâna or to Umbar Baharbêl. When my purpose brought me to these lands, years ago, it was not as Mithrandir. Nor did I wear the name Gandalf when I crossed the Ikorbân River in search of answers among the great cities of the south. I was called \\qInkanûsh\\q by the people who dwelled in these lands, and let it be so again while we here remain. I have been a friend to all the Free Peoples of the North, but the names they gave to me ring harshly against Shagâni ears.'\
\
Inkanûsh puffs on his pipe before continuing, but as he begins to speak again something draws his attention.\
\
'There is a commotion at the gate, ${PLAYER}. If you are agreeable, we will together see what has happened to disturb the peace. Perhaps they have found someone that better fits their expectation of a Wizard?'","Talk to Inkanûsh beside the Fathomwell and go with him to investigate the nearby commotion","The Wizard Inkanûsh wishes to go with you to investigate the nearby commotion. Speak with him beside the Fathomwell on the eastern side of the city.","Chapter 14.2: The Wizard, the Queen, and the Kindred","Inkanûsh stands by the stable-master at the Fleet-gate in south-eastern Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Inkanûsh by the stable-master at the Fleet-gate","The situation in these lands will demand careful handling by all of the affected parties: rulers, Wizards, soldiers, and common people alike.","'Hármelak is wrong. Ordâkh is not powerless, it is true, but the gravest danger facing these lands, and indeed all lands in Middle-earth, belongs to the Thardúth! How can this Umbari woman believe that Utug-bûr might be the only dwelling the Thardúth ever fashioned in all of Shagâna's vast reaches?\
\
'Before I came to the city I dispatched some of our friends to travel north into Harondor. Legolas, Gimli, and the sons of Elrond will ensure the Thardúth and their Utûgi warriors did not go that way to endanger Gondor. If they discover such a threat they will send word to me.\
\
'But our road lies to the south, ${PLAYER}.'","'Let us see what has caused this commotion at the gate, and if we might be of some service in ending it.'"},
[2951]={"Chapter 14.3: Young Soldiers of Old Wars","Inkanûsh has come to the Kinta grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar.","'Even now my soldiers heed this call. Stand by the gate and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for the warriors that come from Kûr Anzar to join me on the southward road into danger.'","Inkanûsh believes your journey south alongside Shâra Mizâdi should begin in Imhûlar with stops at Urmâkh and Vartúlin.","Soldiers weary from battle slowly make their way up the road to Urmâkh","Inkanûsh coughs meaningfully, drawing your attention","Stand by the eastern gate of Urmâkh and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for Mizâdi's returning soldiers","Glorfindel has arrived at Urmâkh, and wishes to speak with you about the next leg of your journey.","'I am almost... home. I have dreamt of living here once again in peace, but...\
\
'For how long can I remain at Urmâkh, knowing that Shâra Mizâdi faces our enemies in distant lands? Her own husband Eshtali perished in recent days, and still she fights.\
\
'But I know not if I am as strong as she.'","'These creatures of Orc-kind of which Thórvilon speaks are almost certainly Utûgi, ${PLAYER}. If you will go search for sign of these invaders outside Vartúlin, I will tell him what we know of them and their Thardúth masters.\
\
'Be careful. The Utûgi must be driven by some evil purpose if they dare approach the groves of the Kintai.'","'It is always the same, ${PLAYER}. In this place I see young soldiers of old wars, fighting and dying in battles they did not cause and whose roots they cannot see. They fight against Ordâkh as I fought against Mordor, and they fight for Mizâdi as I fought for Gil-galad the High King. Do they think this will be the last battle they need fight, as I believed then? Did I call them young soldiers? Perhaps I am one of them after all, despite my years!\
\
'I understand Mizâdi and her army will travel the longer way through Khûd Zagin into Mûr Ghala, avoiding the dangerous forest road, but Inkanûsh wishes otherwise. He would have us speak first with Thórvilon, the Kinta warden of the grove of Vartúlin. It is the Wizard's plan to take the forest road through what remains of the Emerald Wood, ensuring that the Utûgi did not go that way unseen.\
\
'It seems a good idea to me. The creatures we fought at the Dagor Carlanthir were fearsome, and I do not want them to prey upon the Kintai. Our kindreds are long divided, but they remain Elves, and dear to me even from such distance.'","Soldiers that fought for Mizâdi at Kûr Anzar slowly climb the road to Urmâkh.","The Kinta Thórvilon tends the grove of Vartúlin, to the south-east of Urmâkh.","'Mizâdi intended to return to Urmâkh to regroup with her own soldiers before travelling south. Speak with her when you arrive, and give her my thanks. Her ambitions, and the army she commands to accomplish them, will be of great service to us if I am right and the Thardúth lurk within Mûr Ghala.'","Talk to Shâra Mizâdi at the town of Urmâkh in Imhûlar","'I am pleased to have your aid and support, friend, and that of the Wizard Inkanûsh! We reclaimed Kûr Anzar, but it was not enough. Even possessing the Crown of Renewed Hamât is not enough, for Bârshud remains alive to threaten my young kingdom and its people. We will only be safe when Bârshud has been slain and the Empire of Ordâkh knows the courage in our hearts and the strength of our sword-arms.\
\
'Even now my soldiers heed this call. Stand by the gate and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for the warriors that come from Kûr Anzar to join me on the southward road into danger.'","'My folk have noticed strange Orc-like creatures moving among the trees outside Vartúlin. We believed them to be Orcs at first, but these were dressed strangely and seemed a larger breed than the Orcs we have encountered before.'","Shâra Mizâdi intends to rejoin her army near the town of Urmâkh in Imhûlar, and Inkanûsh asked you to speak with her there about her plans.","Talk to Thórvilon at Vartúlin, south-east of Urmâkh","'Inkanûsh wishes for us to speak first with Thórvilon, the Kinta warden of the grove of Vartúlin. It is the Wizard's plan to take the forest road through what remains of the Emerald Wood, ensuring that the Utûgi did not go that way unseen.\
\
'It seems a good idea to me. The creatures we fought at the Dagor Carlanthir were fearsome, and I do not want them to prey upon the Kintai. Our kindreds are long divided, but they remain Elves, and dear to me even from such distance.'","'I know not if I am strong enough to continue this fight.'","Talk to some of Mizâdi's soldiers on the road to Urmâkh (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Glorfindel inside the eastern gate of Urmâkh","'So it is true: the Utûgi leave the lands in which they awoke and begin to threaten others nearby. Our mission grows more serious.\
\
'But we cannot leave Imhûlar just yet. While you were gone, Thórvilon spoke to me of a woman about whom I must learn more. He says she is named Cúridwan, and she has been a friend to the Kintai for as long as he can remember.'\
\
Inkanûsh looks at you closely, one of his eyebrows raised.\
\
'Thórvilon is one of the Kinta Elves, ${PLAYER}, and his memory is long. How can it be that this woman has lived in this place for such a span? This mystery and others have prompted me to ask a number of questions I have not before thought to ask.\
\
'I must speak with this woman. I must speak with Cúridwan.'","Draw forth your foe and defeat him in the dead woods of Imhûlar outside Vartúlin","'What brings you back to Vartúlin, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Thórvilon that you have come with the Elf-lord Glorfindel and the Wizard Inkanûsh to secure the safety of the Emerald Wood on your journey to oppose the Empire of Ordâkh. The warden of the grove strokes his chin.\
\
'My folk have noticed strange Orc-like creatures moving among the trees outside Vartúlin. We believed them to be Orcs at first, but these were dressed strangely and seemed a larger breed than the Orcs we have encountered before.'","Search for some sign of the Utûgi to the north or north-east of Vartúlin","'Give me a moment to rest, if you would. I am not so young in years that I feel not the road, nor the fighting I faced before it.\
\
'Shâra Mizâdi wrested my home of Kûr Anzar from the Barkhûshim and Ordâkhai that held the city, and for that she will have my gratitude and my loyalty. Aye, unto death! Many others of my neighbours and my friends feel the same. We knew not that we might be Hamâti once again, but the coming of the Shâra wakened us to this truth: history is an unbroken chain that links the past to the present, even as it lies forgotten in the dust, or trampled underfoot.'","Inkanûsh fears that the Utûgi have drawn near to the grove of Vartúlin, and he wants you to search the dead woods nearby for some sign of their presence.","'We will not travel alone, ${PLAYER}! Glorfindel has agreed to accompany us on our southward journey, and he waits for us at the town of Urmâkh, in Imhûlar. Once we have reunited with him, I suggest we meet with the Kintai at the grove of Vartúlin. Our road must pass deeper into what was once the Emerald Wood, but now that forest is changed and the Kintai will guide us safely within.\
\
'Mizâdi intended to return to Urmâkh to regroup with her own soldiers before travelling south. Speak with her when you arrive, and give her my thanks. Her ambitions, and the army she commands to accomplish them, will be of great service to us if I am right and the Thardúth lurk within Mûr Ghala.'","Shâra Mizâdi invited you to stand by the eastern gate of Urmâkh and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for her returning soldiers.","'I will follow Shâra Mizâdi even to death.'","Inkanûsh waits for the report of your scouting at the Kinta grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar.","You feel hostile eyes upon you from somewhere close by","The Utûgi falls to the ground, defeated, but your fears are confirmed","Talk to Inkanûsh at the Kinta grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar","Hostile eyes study you from nearby. You need to draw this foe out of hiding!","'As you search for sign of these invaders outside Vartúlin, I will tell Thórvilon what we know of the Utûgi and their Thardúth masters. Be careful. The Utûgi must be driven by some evil purpose if they dare approach the groves of the Kintai.'"},
[2952]={"'I paid the greatest price. Only I am worthy to possess Thuringwath's secrets.'","Talk to Culang in the throne room of Barad Cúron","Culang is in the throne room of Barad Cúron, concerned about the sound of newcomers approaching.","Culang is in the throne room of Barad Cúron.","Gothmog believes he is most deserving of Thuringwath's secrets, but his enemies encircle the tower and wish to challenge him for them.","Talk to Culang in the throne room and complete 'Instance: A Vengeful Heart'","Chapter 14.4: A Vengeful Heart","Gothmog stirs","'My enemies seek access to the gorge of Thuringwath, but they are unworthy of the secrets within. That place was enwreathed with spells, kept from the eyes of all but Sauron's most trusted servants. My Master could claim the right, as could the others of his order, but the Nazgûl are gone to the void and will not return. None but Gothmog now has the right. Have I not paid the greatest price of all?'","'I cannot tell from his words if he found aught of use in that place, ${PLAYER}. His wound looks to be mortal, but he was kept alive by dark arts, and I cannot say for certain if it be so. If he is dying, let him die! The sooner his evil is gone from this world, the better!\
\
'He claims to deserve whatever weapon lies within Thuringwath. Did he find it or no?'\
\
Culang draws a sharp breath.\
\
'Did you hear that?'","'Did you hear that? Someone comes!'","'${PLAYER}, have you escaped serious injury? Annoth was not so fortunate. He has achieved the vengeance he sought, though it arrived not in the manner he sought. Let him rest now, and may the Thandrim for whom he grieved find peace with the death of Ugrukhôr.\
\
'And so the Captain of the Pit is undone by the sword of Annoth, wielded by Gothmog, and now both Ugrukhôr and Gothmog are undone. Is that not the nature of evil? Treacherous even to its own. None shall mourn for either of the slain.'"},
[2953]={"Chapter 14.4: Calling On Cúridwan","'Will you come with me to speak with this woman? Let me know when you are ready to depart.'","Inkanûsh has returned to the Kinta grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar and wishes to speak with you.","'The answers to my questions must wait until we find Cúridwan somewhere within Adagím. I am nothing if I am not patient, ${PLAYER}. I trust you have not heard otherwise!'","Talk to Inkanûsh at Vartúlin","Inkanûsh has many questions to ask of the mysterious woman Cúridwan who dwells near Vartúlin.","Inkanûsh waits at Vartúlin for you and Glorfindel to go with him to speak with Cúridwan.","'Then let us call upon Cúridwan and learn if she has answers to my questions.'","Talk to Inkanûsh at Vartúlin and go with him to speak with Cúridwan"},
[2954]={"'You have returned, presumably in victory? Tell me what transpired in Barad Cúron, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
You briefly relate the events within the tower to Mithrandir, and the Wizard nods with understanding at the death of Annoth.\
\
'That is all too often the result of a vengeful heart, my friend. It did not take a Wizard's sight to see that Annoth might not walk back down that road. But what of Ugrukhôr and Gothmog? And did Ayorzén prove able in the battle? Our Khundolar friend has not entered the tale since you passed beyond the guardians at the entrance of the tower.'\
\
You conclude your story, and tell Mithrandir that Ayorzén did not meet you at the place you arranged.\
\
'Hmm. I have not seen him here either. Perhaps Faramir or his scouts know something.'","Ayorzén is waiting for you on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul.","There is no sign of Ayorzén here either","Gothmog is in the throne room of Barad Cúron, trying to speak despite his wounds.","Talk to the shade of Isildur in the throne room of Barad Cúron","You should leave the tower and meet up with Ayorzén on the uppermost tier of the city","The shade of Isildur has asked you to bring the casket containing the dust of his bones out of Barad Cúron.","Chapter 14.5: A Final Escape","Mithrandir is at Echad Uial.","There is no sign of Ayorzén at the meeting-place. Perhaps he returned to Echad Uial?","Gothmog presses a broken key into your hand, and dies at last","'We should leave the tower and meet up with Ayorzén at the meeting-place. It was north of the tower entrance, on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul, wasn't it?'","'Even with his last breath he raged against Gondor, and shamed his people! He did not repent of his evil misdeeds. He claimed to regret nothing? His words speak falsely to me; it is clear he felt regret only at his failure to fulfil Sauron's commands and achieve the victory of Mordor!\
\
'He should have resisted, ${PLAYER}, and died as Eärnur. My brother Anárion would have fought the torments of the Lord of the Nazgûl, and embraced death rather than succumb to such evil. So too would I. But instead, he became a tool for evil, and he dies as Gothmog. Let him rot where he lies.\
\
'I do not want my bones to remain here any longer. Pick up the casket of dust and bring it from the tower.'","'Ayorzén? My scouts did see him, ${PLAYER}, but they had no good tidings to relate. They last saw him moving eastward at great speed, bearing the mask of Karazgar about his person. He passed into Gorgoroth and has not been seen since.\
\
'I spoke with Beregond. He believes that Ayorzén will use the mask of Karazgar to rally Men of the East to his banner, becoming once again the commander he wished to be. Did he say his star was on the rise? Perhaps so, and perhaps not. I should not envy Ayorzén his position if the true Weeping Warrior should come seeking the pretender!'","'I should not envy Ayorzén his position if the true Weeping Warrior should come seeking the pretender!'","'Mordor should have been... should have been mine. No one endured... what I endured. Not Ugrukhôr... not Dulgabêth... not the pestilential queen of... Agarnaith. A curse on them all... but I levy my worst upon Isildur who could have prevented it and did not! He calls me coward? He knows nothing of the torments that made me! From that crucible of evil I was born anew, the greatest creation of Angmar! I was to usher in a new age!'\
\
The fire in Gothmog's eyes flickers and burns low.\
\
'Why could I not, ${PLAYER}? There were so many chances, but... the Ranger and the Elf-maid...'\
\
Gothmog stares at the floor, his life's essence departing.\
\
'Narmeleth. I think Narmeleth knew the same torments as I. How could she fight... longer than...?'\
\
He falls silent, and it seems as if he will speak no more. As you are about to turn and leave, he reaches out to you, a trinket held in his clenched fist.\
\
'Listen to me, ${PLAYER}. There was a Morgul-slave who knew the secrets of this place. At my Master's command... he forged a key. \\qOnly this weapon cannot be overcome,\\q the dwarf said to me. I spent the time I could... seeking it... but it eluded me. I give it to you, ${PLAYER}. If Mordor cannot be mine... let it be no one's! Find this weapon and use it... against all who seek to master the realm that was denied me!'","You did not find Ayorzén at the meeting-place, and should look for him at Echad Uial.","Talk to Gothmog in the throne room of Barad Cúron","'By the Tree of Gondor! Gothmog clings to life. He tries to speak, ${PLAYER}, and we should listen. Is it not said that dying men rarely speak falsely with their last breath?'","The shade of Isildur is in the throne room of Barad Cúron.","Meet up with Ayorzén outside Barad Cúron, on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul","Death has come to Barad Cúron and claimed two of the masters of Mordor. How many countless others have perished in that cruel throne room over the years?","Talk to Mithrandir at Echad Uial","Talk to Faramir at Echad Uial","'Ayorzén has gone beyond our reach, for now. His deception was not entirely unexpected to me, but I wished he might act otherwise. The price of his aid is clearer now, but I deem his help to be worthwhile, all the same.\
\
'I will take this casket containing the dust of Isildur's bones and arrange with King Elessar for a waggon to bring it north. I believe its arrival at Rivendell will at last fulfil Isildur's oath, and grant him rest.\
\
'I will also examine this broken key. If it truly unlocks the door to \\qa weapon that cannot be overcome\\q we will need to treat it with care. Even at the end, Gothmog sought death and despair for his enemies, and we must not forget that he counted us in that group. This broken key could be one last trap, one final act of vengeance against those who served him his ultimate defeat.\
\
'I have exhausted my study of the Black Book. Vóin has told us what he can, and it is with a measure of sorrow that I close it for good. I will turn my attention now to this broken key and Gothmog's final words, but you should take a moment to rest and recover your strength. Much of the evil within Minas Morgul has been opposed this day, and defeated! For that you should celebrate!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>The Epilogue will become available from Mithrandir at Echad Uial once you have completed Chapters 1-14 of the Black Book of Mordor</rgb>","Prince Faramir is at Echad Uial.","Look for Ayorzén at Echad Uial","Pick up the casket of dust in the throne room","Bring the casket of dust and the broken key to Mithrandir at Echad Uial","'Perhaps Faramir or his scouts know something of Ayorzén.'","'Let Gothmog rot where he lies. He shamed his people.'"},
[2955]={"'Well, then. I know not what it means, but it smells terrible.'","Shadalith is at the grove of Laivárth.","'Your friend Cúridwan may be at the grove of Laivárth, to the north-east. You should look for her there.'","Talk to Athgai at the border with Adagím","Mauthark and Mokh Grazádh can be found among the swamps of Adagím.","Talk to Shadalith in Laivárth","Defeat Orcs from Mauthark or Mokh Grazádh in Adagím (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have returned with the samples of the rot I asked you to collect? Thank you for doing this for me!\
\
'I have placed a bucket of water to the west. Will you add the portions of the blight you collected to the water? I am interested in the effect they may have upon the water.'","'Your friend speaks the truth: it is difficult to watch the blight consume our land, twisting the trees in horrible mockery of their once-healthy forms. Some among my people believe the fungal contagion spews from a single entity: Sívigush, the Earth-terror; others believe the blight is itself alive, and Sívigush is in fact an evil composed of every tendril, mushroom, and spore released into the foetid air of Adagím.\
\
'I know not what I believe. If you are willing to take this trowel and bring back a sample from several locations where the rot has taken hold, perhaps we can learn something that will be of use. I will speak with your friend while you conduct this study on my behalf, and help the two of you as I can.\
\
'The rot is particularly bad to the north-east, north-west, and west of Laivárth.'","Athgai told you to seek the grove of Laivárth, north-east along the path in Adagím.","Collect sample of the rot west of Laivárth","Talk to Glorfindel in Laivárth","Collected a sample of the rot north-east of Laivárth","Defeated Orcs in Adagím (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Chapter 14.5: Rot of the Moulder-wood","'Imagine how it must feel to live in this wood, and watch the corruption advance with the passage of the hours, and of the days!'","'I have placed a bucket of water just over there. Will you add the portions of the blight you collected to the water? I am interested in the effect they may have upon the water.'","Collected a sample of the rot north-west of Laivárth","Thórvilon is at the Kinta grove of Vartúlin, in Imhûlar.","Athgai stands at the border with Adagím.","Shadalith is in Laivárth.","'Perhaps Inkanûsh and Cúridwan together will be able to fight the corruption that has taken root in Imhûlar and Adagím. I hope it is so! Hurry on to speak with Athgai at the border into Adagím, and hasten the meeting of these two wise ones!'","'It is the foolhardy traveller who passes into an unfamiliar land without knowledge; we must not be unprepared. What can Thórvilon tell us of the woods into which we must go?'","Shadalith stands nearby in the grove of Laivárth.","Shadalith asked you to retrieve samples of the rot at locations to the north-east, north-west, and west of Laivárth.","Shadalith placed a bucket of water to the west. She wants you to add the samples of the blight you collected to the water so she can see if there is any effect.","Eager to speak with the mysterious Cúridwan, Inkanûsh wishes to travel with you into Adagím, the Moulder-wood, where a terrible blight has taken hold.","Collect sample of the rot north-west of Laivárth","You add the blight to the water and a noxious fume rises into the air","'Wait a moment, newcomers. Few come this way, save the Orcs, and it is my duty to keep watch for any who stray this far into the wood. What business have you in Adagím?'\
\
You tell the Kinta guard that you are only passing through on your way south, but that you hoped to find Cúridwan somewhere on the way. Athgai nods thoughtfully.\
\
'I stopped and spoke with her briefly a few hours ago, as I have stopped you. She said she possessed a salve that might cure us of the Lâg Dávrit. If only it might be true! She passed north-east in the direction of Laivárth. If you head that way too, might I trouble you to defeat some of the Orcs that lurk beside the path? They seem untroubled by the noisome fumes that now fill the air, and it is our burden to thin their numbers before they become emboldened. They have fashioned two camps near here, Mauthark and Mokh Grazádh, and if you defeat these creatures you will be aiding both the Kintai and your friend Cúridwan.'","'The fungal corruption has begun to work on this grove as well, despite the efforts of its tenders to halt its spread. See the mark of the blight there, and there? My heart is heavy, and I have only just arrived! Imagine how it must feel to live in this wood, and watch the corruption advance with the passage of the hours, and of the days!'","'What can I tell you about Adagím that will not pain me? Very little, my friend. So much of the Emerald Wood has been tainted by blight and corruption that the beautiful forest of my youth seems somehow unreal. When the Ordâkhai came north, something they brought with them damaged the soil. The blight that slew the trees of Imhûlar began first in Adagím, taking the form of a terrible fungal rot. Many groves of my people were abandoned, until only Sul Madásh remained unspoiled.\
\
'The Adagím of today is a nightmarish, boggy wilderness, despite the efforts of the Kintai. Some of us fled westward to Vartúlin, or to Shonith beside the Khûd, but I fear it is only a matter of time before the blight consumes every tree that once grew within the Emerald Wood of Nisigím.\
\
'Perhaps Inkanûsh and Cúridwan together will be able to fight it, ${PLAYER}. I hope it is so! Hurry on to speak with Athgai at the border with Adagím, and hasten the meeting of these two wise ones!'","'Cúridwan passed north-east in the direction of Laivárth. If you head that way too, might I trouble you to defeat some of the Orcs that lurk beside the path? They seem untroubled by the noisome fumes that now fill the air, and it is our burden to thin their numbers before they become emboldened. They have fashioned two camps near here, Mauthark and Mokh Grazádh, and if you defeat these creatures you will be aiding both the Kintai and your friend Cúridwan.'","Collect sample of the rot north-east of Laivárth","A Kinta woman standing nearby murmurs her agreement","Add the blight samples to the water bucket in Laivárth","'Bring back samples from several locations where the rot has taken hold and we may learn something of use. I will speak with your friend while you conduct this study on my behalf, and help the two of you as I can.\
\
'The rot is particularly bad to the north-east, north-west, and west of Laivárth.'","Glorfindel stands in the grove of Laivárth.","Collected a sample of the rot west of Laivárth","Find the grove of Laivárth in Adagím","'If Cúridwan has gone ahead into Adagím, that is where our road must lead. But it is the foolhardy traveller who passes into an unfamiliar land without knowledge; we must not be unprepared.\
\
'What can Thórvilon tell us of the woods into which we must go?'"},
[2956]={"'The road to discovery is often slow and riddled with setbacks. Such is the way of things.\
\
'Your friend Glorfindel spoke to me of your search for Cúridwan. She has likely gone on ahead to Sul Madásh, largest of the Kinta groves within the Emerald Wood. But wait!\
\
'Before you come to Sul Madásh, you should spend a moment at Tûl Ama, the Hill of the Mother. Look for it to the south-east, for it is on your way. The Old Mother, Amûma in my tongue, is unmistakable. You will know her at once, and Cúridwan is like to have stopped there herself.\
\
'Farewell, my new friends.'","'Inkanûsh and I spoke with Irsinith while you were away, ${PLAYER}, and she confirmed what we believed.\
\
'Cúridwan came this way earlier in the day. She proceeded onward to the south-east, and must be making for Sul Madásh, home of the Kintai in Adagím.'","Irsinith is at the Hill of the Mother in Adagím.","Irsinith is at Tûl Ama, the Hill of the Mother.","Talk to Glorfindel at the Hill of the Mother","'Before you come to Sul Madásh, you should spend a moment at Tûl Ama, the Hill of the Mother. Look for it to the south-east, for it is on your way. The Old Mother, Amûma in my tongue, is unmistakable. You will know her at once, and Cúridwan is like to have stopped there herself.'","Talk to Glorfindel at Tûl Ama","'I knew what to expect and still the sorrow cuts me deeply, ${PLAYER}. This great mother-tree of the Emerald Wood stood unharmed for untold years, but now the blight that savages Adagím works its evil even upon her. See the blood-red sap she weeps as she mourns!\
\
'Can the Ordâkhai really have wrought this? The Kintai with whom we have spoken seem to believe this corruption began when that Empire crossed north... but how could they have caused such evil as this? Does it not seem beyond their capability, if not beyond their cruel intent?'","'Can the Ordâkhai really have wrought this? The Kintai with whom we have spoken seem to believe this corruption began when that Empire crossed north... but how could they have caused such evil as this? Does it not seem beyond their capability, if not beyond their cruel intent?'","Talk to Irsinith at the Hill of the Mother","Irsinith asked you to collect venom-sacs, sickly wings, and damaged leaves from creatures located not far from the Hill of the Mother in Adagím.","Collected damaged leaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect venom sacs from spiders in Adagím (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find Tûl Ama to the south-east of Laivárth","Collect damaged leaves from Huorns in Adagím (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'For years I have pondered that question, friends of the Kintai, but no solution has come to me. I cannot conceive of such a thing: who would willingly inflict such harm upon this land, or upon Amûma and her children? I have long been the warden of this grove. Tending to her in this state has left me weak and sorrowful.'\
\
Irsinith sighs heavily, and you are struck by the notion that she seems very much alike to the mother-tree she guards. You ask if there is anything you and Glorfindel might do to lighten her burden.\
\
'The corruption affects both plants and animals, and by observing these signs we can track the spread of the blight through the forest. Will you bring me venom sacs from spiders, sickly wings from nearby flies, and damaged leaves from Huorns in the woods? I would collect these myself, but I am quite exhausted today already. Perhaps I will speak with your sympathetic friends while you are away and learn how I might aid you in return?'","Collect sickly wings from sickle-flies in Adagím (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Fungal rot has already crept up the trunk of Amûma, the Old Mother of Adagím","'The corruption affects both plants and animals, and by observing these signs we can track the spread of the blight through the forest. Will you bring me venom sacs from spiders, sickly wings from nearby flies, and damaged leaves from Huorns in the woods? I would collect these myself, but I am quite exhausted today already. Perhaps I will speak with your sympathetic friends while you are away and learn how I might aid you in return?'","Collected venom sacs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the venom sacs, wings, and leaves to Irsinith at the Hill of the Mother","'Thank you for bringing me these. I will study them later, when I am feeling better. Right now I am simply so tired.'","Glorfindel stands sorrowfully by Amûma, the Old Mother of Adagím.","Tûl Ama, the Hill of the Mother, is to the south-east of Laivárth.","Chapter 14.6: Beside the Weeping Mother","The Kinta woman turns sorrowful eyes upon you","Grateful for the help you provided, Shadalith has suggested that you visit Tûl Ama, the Hill of the Mother, on your way to Sul Madásh.","Collected sickly wings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am just so tired. Please excuse me.'","Glorfindel is at the Hill of the Mother in Adagím."},
[2957]={"Talk to Corudan in Sul Madásh","Corudan stands in the centre of Sul Madásh.","'The path to the south-east will bring us to Sul Madásh. Let us move now with haste, but keep in our hearts the memory of the hurt done to the Old Mother Amûma. Should we be given the opportunity to avenge that hurt, I would have us do it.\
\
'But for now our road leads to Sul Madásh, and Cúridwan.'","Kintai within Sul Madásh told you that the Kinta Ulishár might know of Cúridwan's whereabouts.","Inkanûsh stands at the southern entrance to Sul Madásh.","'The interesting day continues! I welcome you to Sul Madásh as I welcomed the others. So many visitors after days of so few have proven the perfect curative for the hours of tedium I usually face!\
\
'Harm not the grove, and the Kintai will treat you well.'","Find Ulishár to the east","'Harm not the grove, and the Kintai will treat you well.'","The Kinta Ulishár has overheard your conversation and might have some advice for you.","Kintai within the grove of Sul Madásh may know of recent visitors.","Travel to the southern entrance of Sul Madásh","'I have not seen Cúridwan since we came here to Adagím, I am sorry.'","'Let us speak with Kintai throughout Sul Madásh and they will guide us to Cúridwan.'","Talk to Inkanûsh at the southern entrance to Sul Madásh","The Kinta guardsman Baharúd stands at the southern entrance to Sul Madásh.","'Have I heard you aright? You seek Cúridwan?'","Talk to a Kinta of Sul Madásh north-east of the entrance","'I should have known your road would lead this way, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'My sister and I came here to speak with the Kintai; she searches for some means of freeing Silirtas from the cruel fate inflicted upon her by Azagath. In my heart I feel there can be no such release, but Sigileth is so certain...\
\
'She speaks now in conference with one of the elders of Sul Madásh, but if there were a way to free the wrathful Väiri from their fate as wandering spirits, surely the Kintai would know of it.'\
\
You ask your friend if he has seen Cúridwan somewhere within Sul Madásh. He shakes his head.","Talk to Ulishár in Sul Madásh","Talk to Baharúd at the southern entrance to Sul Madásh","Talk to another Kinta of Sul Madásh further into the grove","'The woman Cúridwan? I have not seen her today.'","One of the Kinta coughs politely and holds up a questioning hand","'So many visitors, he says! Now these are promising tidings, ${PLAYER}. Let us speak with Kintai throughout Sul Madásh and they will guide us to Cúridwan.'","The Kinta grove of Sul Madásh remains a bastion of health and beauty among the dead or dying trees of Adagím. Did Cúridwan come this way?","Chapter 14.7: Visitors to Sul Madásh","'Ulishár was a good friend of Cúridwan. You should be able to find him to the east.'","'The path to the south-east will bring us to Sul Madásh.'","You have found a familiar face, if not the one you sought","A Kinta guardsman of the grove calls to you in greeting","'Cúridwan? She has long been a friend of the Kintai, and has worked tirelessly to help us preserve our groves. I have not seen her today, but years ago Ulishár was a good friend of the Golden Maiden, before he...\
\
'Never mind. You should be able to find Ulishár to the east.'","Sul Madásh lies to the south-east of the Hill of the Mother, in Adagím."},
[2958]={"Baharúd gazes away into the distance.","You see no sign of Cúridwan, but many dangers lurk that way","'If Cúridwan came to these woods but avoided Sul Madásh, she must have had some reason. I am no adventurer, and would rather stay within these bounds, but my brother Baharúd would no doubt enjoy the search. Ask him if he will accompany you! You will find him at the entrance to the grove to the south-west.'","Cúridwan is at the Elderwell in Adagím.","Baharúd suggested that you travel west through the swamps to continue your search.","'She is gone? Did she not say she would wait here for us to return? I did not really know Cúridwan as well as my brother Ulishár did, but I was not aware her head was always floating away among the clouds! Have you known anyone else like that, ${PLAYER}? And if you have, how do you put up with it?\
\
'Let us hope she went to Sul Madásh. I am not eager to chase her throughout Adagím any longer!'","This would be a good place to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for Cúridwan","'Ulishár thought I might be interested in accompanying you to search for Cúridwan? My brother is most considerate! While he desires not to leave the grove unless he must, I feel quite the opposite.\
\
'If he is correct that Cúridwan may have skirted Sul Madásh, there is no need for us to look for her within view of the grove. We should travel south-east and see if we can pick up her trail in the further reaches. While we walk you can tell me about your adventures, for I judge that you have had a number of them!'","Collect crocodile teeth north-west of the Elderwell (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Baharúd is at the southern entrance to Sul Madásh.","Talk to Cúridwan at the Elderwell","Talk to Sigileth in Sul Madásh","Travel west through the swamps to continue your search for Cúridwan","'Perhaps Cúridwan returned to Sul Madásh. I am not eager to chase her throughout Adagím any longer!'","Cúridwan came to Adagím, but she never reached Sul Madásh. Where wandered the Golden Maiden?","'Let us make our way through the swamp to the north-west and continue our search.'","Baharúd is in the swamps west of Sul Madásh, in Adagím.","Return to Sul Madásh and look for Cúridwan","Travel south-east of Sul Madásh through the swamp-land","Talk to Baharúd in the swamps south-east of Sul Madásh","'I have done you a disservice, ${PLAYER}. I should not have spoken of my brother if I could not tell you all.\
\
'Ulishár once took great joy in wandering far across the lands of Shagâna, west to the shores of Umbar and south to the fringe of the great desert of Gûl Sakhâsha. He would come back with tales of his adventures, much like the ones I believe you have had!\
\
'Several years ago, he was captured by soldiers of Ordâkh. They imprisoned him in one of their cities, where he was made to labour. The watch on him lapsed as the armies of Ordâkh assembled and marched north to war, and a few months past he escaped and crossed the Mûr. Ever since he returned, he has been unwilling to leave the bounds of Sul Madásh.\
\
'Now I have told you all, and I ask that you please speak not of this to Ulishár. Come, our destination lies to the south-west: the Elderwell. I remember Ulishár used to visit this place with Cúridwan, in happier times.'","'I had hoped my salve could put an end to the Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight, but alas! It is not enough. The corruption birthed beneath Adagím fights against each of the arts I bring to bear against it, and the Pale Blight is a symptom only; so too are the fungal blossoms that spring all about us. I must strengthen my salve, and for that I need to learn more.\
\
'I spied crocodiles to the north-west as I climbed to this place. Collect their teeth and some samples of the blight near which they live, and bring them to me for study. My mind is awhirl with the possibility that this corruption can be beaten and its harm undone.'","Collect samples from blight pustules north-west of the Elderwell (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Baharúd calls for a halt","Talk to Baharúd at the entrance to Sul Madásh","Baharúd is in the swamps south-east of Sul Madásh in Adagím.","Your search for Cúridwan now leads south-west to the Elderwell.","Cúridwan asked you to collect crocodile teeth and samples of the blight north-west of the Elderwell.","Baharúd stares around in disbelief.","At last you have located Cúridwan!","You have found Cúridwan!","'Come, our destination lies to the south-west: the Elderwell. I remember Ulishár used to visit this place with Cúridwan, in happier times.'","'I spied crocodiles to the north-west as I climbed to this place. Collect their teeth and some samples of the blight near which they live, and bring them to me for study. My mind is awhirl with the possibility that this corruption can be beaten and its harm undone.'","'When I was younger, I was given to wandering. I met Cúridwan on one of these meanders, far from Sul Madásh, and she and I became dear friends. When the Ordâkhai came north and the pestilence was born in Adagím, she and I sought to prevent its spread. A few years ago I strayed too far in search of a cure, and... it is not important. I will say only that my wandering days were ended.'\
\
Ulishár frowns.\
\
'If Cúridwan came to these woods but avoided Sul Madásh, she must have had some reason. I am no adventurer, and would rather stay within these bounds, but my brother Baharúd would no doubt enjoy the search. Ask him if he will accompany you! You will find him at the entrance of the grove to the south-west.'","'If my brother is correct that Cúridwan may have skirted Sul Madásh, there is no need for us to look for her within view of the grove. We should travel south-east and see if we can pick up her trail in the further reaches. While we walk you can tell me about your adventures, for I judge that you have had a number of them!'","Cúridwan is no longer at the Elderwell","Chapter 14.8: Wandering Cúridwan","Collected crocodile teeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Baharúd agreed to travel south-east of Sul Madásh and to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> with you for Cúridwan.","Cúridwan is waiting at the Elderwell for you to return with the things she requested.","Baharúd believes that Cúridwan may have gone to Sul Madásh. You hope he is right!","'We should not go this way without allies beside us, ${PLAYER}. Some evil lurks in the south-eastern reaches of Adagím, and I fear its power outstrips our own. Orcs have taken up residence in that place, and I think they cannot be the most fearsome of the creatures who dwell there. Let us look elsewhere for Cúridwan.\
\
'My brother and Cúridwan strolled often in these woods. Perhaps she has gone to one of their old haunts? Ever since Ulishár returned from his captivity, he has not felt comfortable ranging from Sul Madásh; otherwise I would ask him to show us where he and the Golden Maiden once walked.'\
\
Baharúd falls silent.\
\
'My brother does not like to speak of it. I should not have said anything. Let us make our way through the swamps to the west and continue our search.'","You have found Sigileth again!","Sigileth has finished speaking with the elders of Sul Madásh.","Baharúd stands among the blighted trees, deep in thought.","Travel south-west to the Elderwell in search of Cúridwan","Baharúd is at the Elderwell in Adagím.","Talk to Baharúd at the Elderwell","Bring the crocodile teeth and blight samples to Cúridwan at the Elderwell","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> for Cúridwan","Talk to Baharúd in the swamps west of Sul Madásh","'Corudan told me you had come to Adagím, ${PLAYER}. I am glad to see you, but I hope you have better fortune on your errand than I have had on mine.'","Sigileth waves and calls you over to her","Collected blight samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2959]={"Talk to Cúridwan in Sul Madásh and ask that she explain herself","You have finally managed to track down Cúridwan. If fortune smiles, she will have the answers to Inkanûsh's questions.","'Why?' asks Cúridwan","'The Kinta elders of this grove have given me no means of freeing Silirtas from her fate. They believe this to be an unyielding truth: that a Kinta slain in battle is resigned to wander the land as one of the Väiri, a spirit of wrath and hatred. I refuse to believe it.'\
\
Sigileth grins without humour.\
\
'They have not taken to me very well, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Inkanûsh in Sul Madásh and go with him to speak to Cúridwan","Talk to Sigileth in Sul Madásh","'Then let us speak with Cúridwan before she wanders again into the forest!'","Inkanûsh is in Sul Madásh and ready to speak to Cúridwan.","'Curse the Thardúth for senseless slaughter! How many lives must their thralls destroy before it will be enough? Must this Kinta share the fate of Silirtas? \
\
'It is not fair! How can such a thing be? How many Kintai must be doomed to become wandering, wrathful Väiri, unable to find rest?'","The Utûgi have been driven away from Sul Madásh, but they leave sorrow in their wake.","Inkanûsh is in Sul Madásh.","Chapter 14.9: A Shared Mission","'Baharúd! Baharúd, I am sorry! I should have fought!\
\
'My brother... I am sorry!'","Talk to Ulishár in Sul Madásh","Talk to Inkanûsh in Sul Madásh","'It need not be the lot of this Kinta to remain unless he wishes it to be. Know you if that be his wish?'","Her words hang on the air","'What has brought you to Adagím, ${PLAYER}?'","Ulishár weeps for his brother, and you go unnoticed.","'Cúridwan has returned at last to the grove. Will you come with me to speak with her? I have questions to ask. May she be forthright in answering!'","Cúridwan stands in Sul Madásh."},
[2960]={"La Hueste Dorada está en peligro, ya que los ejércitos de Gathburz están a punto de ser desatados sobre Thangulhad.","Habla con Ellunen en Thangulhad","'¡Debemos resistir a los ejércitos orcos de Gathburz, ${PLAYER}! ¡Debes ayudarnos en la escaramuza contra sus avanzadas! ¡Debemos proteger Thangulhad!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo Solitario, Duo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o incursión usando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Capítulo 14: Thangulhad en peligro","'Este lugar pronto será el escenario de una escaramuza contra las fuerzas del enemigo. Tus habilidades como ${CLASS} serán de gran utilidad aquí, si las ofreces voluntariamente.\
\
'Los orcos esperan expulsarnos de este lugar con una derrota, pero juro por el poder que se me ha dado como líder de la Hueste Dorada, por el Señor Celeborn de Lórien mismo, que no caeremos hoy. ¡Lucha a nuestro lado, ${PLAYER}, y juntos protegeremos Thangulhad de las fuerzas del enemigo !'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo Solitario, Duo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o incursión usando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Ellunen está en Thangulhad, preparando su defensa.\
\
Ningloril te ha pedido que vengas a la defensa de Thangulhad y te ha dirigido a hablar con Ellunen.","Ellunen te espera para que participes en la defensa de Thangulhad.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo Solitario, Duo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o incursión usando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","'Ellunen está aquí en Thangulhad. Habla con él y prepárate para la batalla. Los ejércitos están marchando mientras hablamos, tú y yo, y cada momento que estás aquí es un momento perdido!'","Ellunen está en Thangulhad, el campamento de la Hueste Dorada en Gathburz.\
\
Has ayudado a defender Thangulhad y deberías ir a informar a Ellunen ahora.","'Thangulhad sigue bajo el control de la Hueste Dorada, lo que representa el símbolo de la intención del señor Celeborn y la dama Galadriel de oponerse a las fuerzas del enemigo. Estoy contento, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Resistimos su ataque. ¡Que ahora teman el nuestro!'","Completa la escaramuza: Los protectores de Thangulhad","'El explorador Lamwen informa que los orcos del norte de Gathburz han comenzado a moverse, y una gran tropa de criaturas marcha hacia nuestro campamento.\
\
'Thangulhad debe ser defendida, o las penas que hemos soportado hasta este punto habrán sido en vano. Esto no puede ser así, ${PLAYER}, ¡y no lo será!\
\
'Ellunen prepara las defensas. Habla con él y prepárate para la batalla. ¡Thangulhad no debe caer!'"},
[2961]={"'Where strayed the rest of the people who lived here?'","'After our argument, Wadu went to the halls of the corrach -- the dwarves -- in Thrór's Coomb, but what he saw there I do not know; he would say nothing to me when he returned.\
\
'Those halls have been abandoned for countless years, and have a fell reputation. No one goes there: corrach, Uch-lûth, or Draig-lûth. Did Wadu find this sword there? I cannot explain it. If you go to the dwarf-halls and learn what my brother saw there I will repay you with knowledge of these lands known only to the Uch-lûth.\
\
'I have never been to the halls of the corrach, but they can be found far to the east of here, in the northern mountains of Thrór's Coomb.'","'I do not know what my brother saw in the dwarf-halls in Thrór's Coomb, but he would not speak of it. I want to know what it was and why he went forth to his death. Go to the halls of the corrach far to the east of here, in the northern mountains of Thrór's Coomb.'","'There is an air of mystery about this place. I do not know what to make of it.'","'Frithgeir seems to take care of Nár, and his devotion seems to be very strong, but I have not been able to learn much about either of them.'","The ingredients needed by Frithgeir to make the brew can be found throughout Thrór's Coomb. He gave you a list of the ingredients and their locations to study.\
\
Frithgeir can make a brew that brings Nár back to awareness.","'The last one, eh? Good... good....'\
\
The dwarf nods contentedly, but makes no sign of having seen you.","'Ah, you have the ingredients, good. I will begin making the brew in just a moment.'","Collect handfuls of Hulwul-harâz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Chapter 14: The Distant Dwarf","'Frithgeir gave you a list of ingredients he needs in order to make a brew to make Nár more lucid? Well, I see no harm in gathering them together. They will be found throughout Thrór's Coomb? That seems simple enough.'","Talk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund","Frithgeir is in Zudrugund, the once-abandoned dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb.\
\
You have collected the ingredients needed by Frithgeir to make the brew that will restore Nár's awareness of his surroundings.","Collect Kibil-lawâz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected handfuls of Hulwul-harâz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Welcome to Zudrugund, traveller. I... I should apologize for Nár. He is very old -- I know not how old -- and his mind... wanders. He has experienced a great deal of hardship and pain, but he has remained here while all others have left him. All save Frithgeir, that is.'\
\
You explain why you have come and ask Frithgeir about Wadu. He nods with recognition.\
\
'Yes, the Dunlending. He came to speak with Nár some time ago. Nár was more aware that night than he usually is, so I marked the visit. The two ventured into the mine beneath these halls. I'm sorry, but I do not remember anything else peculiar about the visit.\
\
'There is a brew I can make of several ingredients found throughout Thrór's Coomb. The vapours of the brew seem to make Nár more aware of his surroundings. If you bring me these ingredients, the brew may allow you to speak with Nár directly. I will need several handfuls of the Hulwul-hurz herb, some Nijam-mujdu flowers, and the variety of nut called Kibil-luwz. Take this list of the ingredients and where they can be found.'","Explore the dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'I asked Golodir to explore this place with me, but he had other tasks before him.'","The dwarf-hall is located among the northern mountains of Thrór's Coomb, far to the east of Lhanuch, the Uch-lûth village in Nan Laeglin.\
\
Nona has asked you to journey to the dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb to learn what Wadu saw there that brought him to Fordirith and then to his death.","'Eh? Who's there? Who is it? Eh?'\
\
The dwarf peers forward, but his eyes seem unable to fix upon you.\
\
'The soup is cold! Hervin, the soup is cold! Set it atop the fire! Ah, yes, ah. Three and twenty!'\
\
The dwarf wheezes, his beard fluttering slightly with the exhalation. He brings his hand up to his mouth, as if holding a ladle, and sips at the air. He pays you no more heed.","Bring the list and ingredients to Frithgeir","'You found the various ingredients for which Frithgeir asked? Very good! Give them to him at once, and we will see if this brew has any effect at all upon Nár. I must admit I do not know what to expect, ${PLAYER}.'","Collected Najâm-mujdu flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect Najâm-mujdu flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I need a number of ingredients to make the brew that will bring Nár back to wakefulness: several handfuls of the Hulwul-hurz herb, some Nijam-mujdu flowers, and the variety of nut called Kibil-luwz. These all can be found throughout Thrór's Coomb. Consult the list of ingredients I gave to you for their locations.'","Collected Kibil-lawâz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'This hall is mostly abandoned, ${PLAYER}. Two dwarves seem to live here, but I have seen no sign of the rest of their people. Nár and Frithgeir, their names are, and Frithgeir seems normal enough, but as for Nár....\
\
'Well, see for yourself.'","Something Wadu saw in the abandoned dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb brought him to his death, and his sister Nona wants to learn what it was.","Two dwarves make their home in Zudrugund, the dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb, within Nár's Peak.\
\
One of the dwarves in the hall seems unable to focus upon you, but the other may be able to tell you what is going on."},
[2962]={"Collect blades from brigands in Kighân (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The road to An Shêru leads north-west of Zajâna.","Brigands appear to have tampered with this signpost as well","The Hold of Jalkhíla is located to the east in Kighân.","'Deprive those brigands of the blades and bows with which they trouble folk on the road, and we can meet up at Gadim-ûn where the road leads into An Shêru.'","Brigands may have tampered with the signpost north of Zajâna as well.","Travel north-east of Zajâna on the road to An Shêru","Repair the brigand-tampered signpost north of Zajâna","'We must remain alert for brigands as we make our way toward An Shêru.'","'An Shêru, the Height of the Sky, was once known for the loveliness of its high forests and flowering meads, but no longer. Now the plateau is parched and dry, a cracked waste among the high peaks of the Mûr. If Inkanûsh is correct that other vaults of the Thardúth remain, this would seem to be a likely place for them.\
\
'The road that runs from Zajâna to An Shêru has a reputation for danger. We must remain alert for brigands as we make our way north-east.'","Repair the brigand-tampered signpost","Amêsh leaps from hiding, unaware of your lack of surprise","The road to An Shêru has a reputation for danger, but that is the way you must go.","'Those brigands would surely have known not to trouble Shâra Mizâdi or her army, but most travellers have neither her numbers nor her ferocious mien! It is good you have shown them the road is not undefended.\
\
'I felt a chill when I arrived here, and my companions say they felt the same. I suspect more than brigands haunt these ruins.'","There is something suspicious about this signpost","Shouting defiantly, a brigand leaps out of hiding!","Rahâzi has arrived in the company of two Hamâti soldiers.","'Our paths cross once again, ${PLAYER}, and it seems they each lead to the Height of the Sky!\
\
'Shâra Mizâdi entrusted me and two of her soldiers to scout the plateau of An Shêru ahead of her army. We have not yet climbed high enough and already we have run afoul of brigands. I see you have as well!\
\
'The bandits came from the Hold of Jalkhíla to the east. If you deprive them of blades and bows with which they trouble folk on the road, you will be aiding the Shâra and any others who must travel this way. We can meet up at Gadim-ûn where the road leads into An Shêru and discuss our further plans.'","The road to An Shêru runs by Zajâna. You should begin by going to the north-east.","Collect bows from the Hold of Jalkhíla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should repair this signpost north of Zajâna as you repaired the other.","Continue further north-west along the road to An Shêru","Something strikes you as suspicious about the signpost north-east of Zajâna.","You survived Amêsh's ambush, and should repair this signpost as well","As you step back to admire your work, you feel eyes upon you","You survived, but he may have allies; if you repair the signpost you may save others","Examine the suspicious signpost north of Zajâna","Rahâzi asked you to meet up with her party at Gadim-ûn in An Shêru.","Collected bows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","If Dagûrum had allies, leaving the signpost as it is may help them ambush other travellers. You should repair the signpost and ruin their plans.","Bring the blades and bows to Rahâzi at Gadim-ûn in An Shêru","Examine the suspicious signpost north-east of Zajâna","Chapter 15.10: A Brigand-Haunted Road","Collected blades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You repair the signpost, making the road more safe for travellers","Talk to Rahâzi north of Zajâna"},
[2963]={"Talk to Corudan in Sul Madásh","Corudan has regretfully decided he cannot accompany you.","Wait for Corudan to depart","Chapter 15.1: Ulishár","Ulishár has joined your travelling companions for the journey south.","'I told the Wizard Inkanûsh I was willing to guide your party south into Mûr Ghala, and that is still true. It is... it is not an easy decision for me, but your arrival here has opened my eyes and thrown into disarray much that I thought certain!'\
\
Ulishár holds your eyes for a moment and then flinches suddenly away.\
\
'My brother Baharúd should have been the one to guide you south. He never lost the adventuring temperament as I did; he hungered still for the untaken road, ever desiring to see what lay beyond the furthest rise and over the horizon. I shared that mood with him, once...'\
\
The Kinta tries to meet your eyes again but cannot. Instead he stares away into the trees.\
\
'Some years ago I was captured by the Ordâkhai while travelling in the Mûr. Held in their distant city of Emax Dûl and put to harsh labour, I was certain I would die there. I still cannot believe I did not. Instead, with no small degree of fortunate happenstance I escaped from Emax Dûl and made my way home.\
\
'This was mere months ago, ${PLAYER}. I promised myself I would stray no longer from Sul Madásh... but now Baharúd is slain, and the Wizard Inkanûsh says a threat more terrifying than Ordâkh has risen. How can I remain in Sul Madásh when I know you and your companions need my help? I simply cannot.'","'Speak to Ulishár and judge his resolve for yourself.'","Ulishár takes a deep breath as he stares down the southward road","'I wish I could come with you, my friend, but I cannot. My sister is intent upon finding the shade that was once Silirtas, and I cannot leave her to accomplish this on her own. Perhaps once Sigileth is successful in this I can rejoin you... but I know not if her quest will be short or if it will be long.'\
\
Corudan lowers his voice and speaks only to you.\
\
'If it is from my heart I speak, I must confess this to you, ${PLAYER}: I am not certain I believe the conclusion for which my sister hopes is even possible. Silirtas perished some time ago before Utug-bûr, and if she now has become one of the Väiri, there is no assurance she will remember who she was in life. I fear Silirtas is gone, and this too: I must attend my sister closely or she may follow her to a careless death.\
\
'So this is farewell, for now. Good-bye, my friend.'","Ulishár stands here.","'Here the road winds south into Kighân as it approaches Mûr Ghala, the Ridge of Plenty. The Mûr itself is a line of sheer hills that runs from east to west and serves as the southern hospitable boundary of the land its people name Shagâna. Beyond the Mûr lies the Hatokáli River and the distant jungles of Abaníssa, from where the Ordâkhai come.\
\
'It is my understanding that Inkanûsh desires not to pass over the Mûr, but to visit the great libraries of Zajâna, the city that guards the road across the ridge. That is where we must first go.'","'We travel then to the west and to the south, for there the road leads from Adagím into Kighân... our first destination.'","Talk to Ulishár in Sul Madásh","'I am ready now to depart if your companions have finished their preparations. We must travel to the west and to the south, for there the road leads from Adagím into Kighân... our first destination.'","Corudan is by the southern entrance to Sul Madásh.","Ulishár stands where the road leads south-west into Kighân.","'When I requested a Kinta guide to accompany us into Mûr Ghala, I did not expect Ulishár to volunteer. Indeed, I asked him more than once if he was certain he wished to go with us into danger, so soon after the death of his brother. I deem he is made of stern material, as are all the Elves of my acquaintance. Yes, I now include the Kintai among that number, for if Ulishár is representative of that folk they seem as resilient as any of the Eldar!\
\
'Speak to him and judge his resolve in this for yourself.'","Ulishár agreed to show you where the road passes from Adagím into Kighân, south-west of Sul Madásh.","Baharúd's brother Ulishár has agreed to guide you on your road south into Mûr Ghala.","Ulishár is by the southern entrance to Sul Madásh.","Find the entrance to Kighân, south-west of Sul Madásh","'The Wizard Inkanûsh says a threat more terrifying than Ordâkh has risen. How can I remain in Sul Madásh when I know you and your companions need my help? I simply cannot.'","Talk to Ulishár on the road into Kighân"},
[2964]={"Talk to Glorfindel at Sormedân","Ulishár asked you to collect unblighted seed-pods from trees and defeat their corrupted roots at Shádhag, in Kighân.","Reassured villagers (1/2)","Inkanûsh is at the village of Sormedân.","Collect unblighted seed-pods from trees at Shádhag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The folk of Sormedân greeted me warmly, but they seem less friendly toward your companions Glorfindel and Inkanûsh. I know not the reason for it, but the farmers give them a wide berth. It is quite unlike the people of Sormedân to be so reserved.'","'This is not my first journey in these lands, ${PLAYER}, for I ventured south seeking tidings of Sauron, long ago. Much I learned in the lore-vaults of Zajâna, and it is there I wish to return. Let us not tarry in this farming village when there is knowledge to be gained in the libraries of the City of Gates!\
\
'But Glorfindel is not as accustomed to receiving such sour looks as I am! Distrust accompanies me in the south even as it does in the north, but he is an Elf-lord and travels fewer roads than I. What would old Barliman have to say of Glorfindel, I wonder?\
\
'Speak to one of these farmers and assure him that Glorfindel means him no harm, and at any rate our business will speed us along shortly. The people here have nothing to fear from us.'","Ulishár has come with you to Kighân, the Shornvale, but so too have tendrils of the blight that have taken root in Adagím.","Khâwaz at the village of Sormedân is reluctant to speak to you, but might be convinced.","Ulishár said he would wait for you at the village of Sormedân, to the south.","'See how the fungal blight within Adagím encroaches upon these lands? Can we seek unblighted seed-pods and cull some of the trees that have already been infected at Shádhag to the north-west?\
\
'We will meet up at Sormedân after the work at Shádhag is complete, or as near as we can make it. The blight always returns, but that is no reason not to combat it!'","'We will trust you, then. I hope you will be able to help us, as we helped Ulishár recover from his plight several months ago. If you are his friend, you are a friend to Sormedân, no matter how frightful the bearing of your companion.'","Reassure villagers of Sormedân (0/2)","Travel to Shádhag in Kighân","Khâwaz at the village of Sormedân has something to say to you.","Defeated fungal roots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Reassure villagers of Sormedân (1/2)","The trees at Shádhag may have been corrupted by the blight creeping into Kighân from Adagím.","'Your errand has put a smile on my face, ${PLAYER}, and that is no small thing in these dark days! The seed-pods you have brought me escaped the corruption of the blight, and that means they can be safely replanted further from Adagím, if that prove necessary. I have not given up hope that Cúridwan can find a cure for the blight... but until she does, we must remain practical. That was always my brother's advice, and now it must be mine as well.\
\
'The folk of Sormedân greeted me warmly, but they seem less friendly toward your companions Glorfindel and Inkanûsh. I know not the reason for it, but the farmers give them a wide berth. It is quite unlike the people of Sormedân to be so reserved.'","Talk to Khâwaz at Sormedân","It is as Ulishár feared: the trees have been corrupted by blight from Adagím","'When I escaped from Emax Dûl and fled homeward, I spent the last leg of my journey in the care of farmers at Sormedân, a village to the south. I will never forget the kindness they showed to me.\
\
'See how the fungal blight within Adagím encroaches upon these lands? A nearby grove to the north-west is threatened even now, and should it fall to that creeping corruption, the people of Sormedân will be endangered. Can we seek unblighted seed-pods and cull some of the trees that have already been infected at Shádhag? As we pass their village on the way to Zajâna, I would aid the farmers of Sormedân in memory of the kindness they showed me.\
\
'We will meet up at Sormedân after the work at Shádhag is complete, or as near as we can make it. The blight always returns, but that is no reason not to combat it!'","'Are the people of this village frightened of us, ${PLAYER}? It did not seem so elsewhere in Shagâna. For what reason might they fear us here?\
\
'It cannot be that they have never seen Elves before, for Ulishár is known to them and they greeted him warmly.'","Talk to Inkanûsh at Sormedân","Collected unblighted seed-pods (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Glorfindel is at the village of Sormedân.","'If you and he are friends of Ulishár, then I will trust your word that you hold no ill will toward us. Reassure my neighbours of this, and we will speak again... for there is something else that troubles me.'","Reassured villagers (2/2)","Defeat fungal roots at Shádhag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the seed-pods to Ulishár at the village of Sormedân, to the south","'My neighbours and I mean to cause no offence, stranger, but...'\
\
Khâwaz wrings his hands apologetically.\
\
'This Elf you are with has a presence about him we have never encountered before. The Kintai who dwell in the forest to the north rarely emerge, but those that do, such as Ulishár, have not his bearing. Is it rude to ask the age of an Elf, as it is to ask it of a man grown? For this Elf seems of an ancient kind, older even than the bones of the land.\
\
'If you and he are friends of Ulishár, then I will trust your word that you hold no ill will toward us. Reassure my neighbours of this, and we will speak again... for there is something else that troubles me.'","Chapter 15.2: Tendrils of the Blight","'Speak to one of these farmers and assure him that Glorfindel means him no harm, and at any rate our business will speed us along shortly. The people here have nothing to fear from us.'","'Are the people of this village frightened of us? It did not seem so elsewhere in Shagâna. For what reason might they fear us here?'","Villagers of Sormedân are frightened of Glorfindel, and need reassurance that he is a friend and can be trusted."},
[2965]={"Defeat spirits at Badrasâg (4/5)","'I will tell your companions where you have gone, if you truly will speak on my behalf before this invading Shâra of Hamât.'","Talk to Mizâdi at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân","After some thought, you decide Mizâdi will be reasonable","Mizâdi stands at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân.","The spirits at Badrasâg should be defeated to ensure the safety of Sormedân.","'You know I stand with you, Shâra Mizâdi, as was my mother's command. It was not her only command. This, too, she said to me: \\qSpeak always your heart, my daughter.\\q\
\
'And so it is I tell you this: you must control your soldiers, or the people of the Mûr, and of greater Shagâna, will treat you as an invading despot. Aye, even as the Ordâkhai themselves!'","'You have taken a long road to reach me, ${PLAYER}, but here you stand. Did the forest of the Kintai prove difficult to traverse? How else to explain this dour expression you wear?'\
\
You describe how a number of her soldiers slaughtered Rôkhasar's cattle and took the meat for themselves, and Mizâdi's own expression hardens.\
\
'Are my soldiers expected not to eat, then? An army must eat if it is to fight, ${PLAYER}, and there is no shortage of foes to face in Kighân and all along the Mûr. Foes enough to freeze the blood of this herdsman should he encounter them, I doubt not! Does he stand against the Ordâkhai? Or does he chafe only against those who oppose his foes, and grouse when they seek only enough food to keep them fed as they fight?'","The farmers of Sormedân are worried for one of their own, Rôkhasar, who may have strayed into danger.","Mizâdi's eyes flash angrily","Mizâdi and her advisors stand in the centre of much activity","'It is the custom of the farmers of Sormedân to let their herds graze upon the fields of Kighân. Pursuit of the longer grasses sometimes brings the cattle many hours or even days away from home, but it has been too long since one of my neighbours has returned. Rôkhasar is his name, and when we last caught sight of him he drove his cattle in the direction of Badrasâg, the Blade-horn.\
\
'That place has a dangerous reputation and he knows better than to bring his cattle so close, but I can think of no good reason he has not come back to Sormedân. Will you look for him by Badrasâg to the south-east, and quell whatever dangers you find there?'","'Will you look for Rôkhasar by the Blade-horn to the south-east, and quell whatever dangers you find there?'","Consider how Mizâdi will react to this situation","Chapter 15.3: Grazing Danger","Look for Rôkhasar near Badrasâg to the south-east of Sormedân","Defeat spirits at Badrasâg (${NUMBER}/5)","Talk to Rôkhasar below the Blade-horn","Defeated spirits (${NUMBER}/5)","Find Mizâdi at Ingar-garâsh in the southern reaches of Kighân","Someone calls for you from below the Blade-horn","Talk to Rahâzi at Ingar-garâsh","Standing nearby, Rahâzi grunts in disapproval","Khâwaz fears that Rôkhasar may have strayed too near Badrasâg, the Blade-horn south-east of Sormedân, in pursuit of his cattle.","Spirits dwell at Badrasâg and pose a danger to Sormedân","You heard someone calling for you below the Blade-horn. Could it be the missing farmer Rôkhasar?","'Well? Have you nothing to say?'\
\
You respond that the Shâra Mizâdi is known to you, and you believe if she is told of the injustice he has suffered, she will cure it. Rôkhasar stares at you with doubt on his face.\
\
'That would be the most unusual outcome of all, stranger, but if you are able to obtain some remedy for this injury, I will sing your praises from the sunrise to the sunset. But only then, and I expect it not.'\
\
Rôkhasar tells you the soldiers made for a camp to the south-west, and agrees to inform your companions where you have gone when he returns to Sormedân.","'Why do you strive against the spirits, stranger? All is hopeless! All is lost!\
\
'I drove my cattle to graze here against my better judgment, but it was not the evils of the Blade-horn that threatened them! No! Soldiers came from the west, and they laid claim to my creatures, butchering them and hauling away the meat to feed their army! They gave me nothing in return!'\
\
You ask Rôkhasar in whose name the soldiers claimed his cattle, and he shakes an angry fist at you.\
\
'Of what consequence is the name, stranger? Those were my beasts, taken without payment, and this wrong is unjust no matter in whose name it is performed! But I remember it, and curse it: the name was Mizâdi, some Shâra of Hamât. They must have taken me for a fool! Hamât is a dead kingdom, and can have no ruler.'","Mizâdi will be at Ingar-garâsh to the south-west, deep within Kighân.","Rôkhasar is below the Blade-horn, in Kighân.","You consider how Mizâdi will react to this situation.","'You have something to say, Rahâzi?'","Rahâzi stands at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân."},
[2966]={"Rahâzi is at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân.","'Shâra Mizâdi, mistake me not! I have seen the fire that drives you, and know why you fight to drive Ordâkh from these lands. I stood beside you at the Battle for Hamât, and my mother Girhâzi would not send me from Ambarûl in your train if she disbelieved in the rightness of your cause!\
\
'But the people that live alongside the Mûr have not seen these things. For how much longer have they lived nearer to their oppressors? Has any captain of Ordâkh hesitated to seize the land of this people, or the beasts that graze thereon?\
\
'You would gain much by treating this folk differently than have the Ordâkhai, my Shâra.'","Rahâzi believes the Shâra's response to this situation involving her soldiers will greatly impact the future of Renewed Hamât. How will Mizâdi respond?","Mizâdi stands at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân.","'I dispatched some soldiers to compensate the herdsman at Sormedân for his butchered cattle. Let the folk there see that the Shâra of Renewed Hamât is not like the other rulers with whom they have had dealings!\
\
'I thank you both for your words, and for the deeds you have done for me on this day, and on others.'","'I am pleased as well. I believe this is how my mother would have resolved the situation. Nothing is given for nothing, but especially not loyalty. That is earned.'","Collect meat from creatures in Kighân (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I thank you both for your words, and for the deeds you have done for me on this day, and on others.'","Mizâdi has charged you with the tasks her soldiers would have accomplished if they did not now need to provide aid and recompense to the farmers of Sormedân. These tasks include collecting eggs from nests at Khatzâla and collecting meat from creatures throughout Kighân.","Talk to Mizâdi at Ingar-garâsh","The provisioner Dunaïl stands at Ingar-garâsh.","'I thank you again for delivering this food to me. I will see that it is properly stored for the days to come.'","Bring the meat and eggs you collected to Dunaïl at Ingar-garâsh","'I hear wisdom in the words that Rahâzi speaks to me.\
\
'But if it is right that nothing should be taken for nothing, ${PLAYER}, you need be no sage to understand this truth, as well. If my soldiers owe something to the herdsman who could not control his own grazing animals, then I must send others to work off this debt; while they labour for him, they will be performing none of their own tasks for my army.\
\
'You will do their work, ${PLAYER}, while they go to compensate the herdsman for the meat that was taken on behalf of my army. It is only right.\
\
'Rahâzi knows the duties they must now neglect, and will tell you what to do.'","Chapter 15.4: Nothing For Nothing","'These are the duties the Shâra would have you complete: retrieve eggs from the bird-nests at Khatzâla to the east of Ingar-garâsh and hunt for meat from creatures throughout Kighân. Once you have done these things, you can bring the meat and eggs to Dunaïl, provisioner of the war camp.'","Talk to Rahâzi at Ingar-garâsh","Mizâdi is at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân.","'I knew Shâra Mizâdi would heed my words.\
\
'It will not take long for you to perform the tasks the soldiers were supposed to complete today, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps the burden will feel lighter knowing the herdsman you spoke with will be compensated for the meat that was taken from him?\
\
'These are the duties the Shâra would have you complete: retrieve eggs from the bird-nests at Khatzâla to the east of Ingar-garâsh, and hunt the meat from creatures throughout Kighân. Once you have done these things, you can bring the meat and eggs to Dunaïl, provisioner of the war camp.'","'Thank you for bringing me this meat and these eggs. I will ensure they are properly stored for the days ahead.'","'Rahâzi knows the duties the soldiers must now neglect. She will tell you what to do.'","Collected meat for the war-camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect eggs from nests at Khatzâla east of Ingar-garâsh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected eggs for the war-camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2967]={"Ulishár suggested that you travel to the cross-road north-west of the war-camp.","Ulishár stands by Khab Antâx, the Overgate, considering the city beyond.","Talk to Ulishár at the cross-road north-west of Ingar-garâsh","'Let us continue onward into the city.'","Ulishár stands here, observing the distant city.","Talk to Ulishár at Khab Antâx, the Overgate outside Zajâna","Ulishár suggested that you continue on into Zajâna itself.","Ulishár motions for you to halt","'This Kinta Elf has come in search of you, ${PLAYER}. He spoke with Shâra Mizâdi of a contagion in the forest to the north, and of his people's opposition to Ordâkh.\
\
'She invited him to join her army, but he says you and he have urgent business elsewhere?'","Travel to Khab Antâx, the Overgate outside Zajâna","Ulishár stands within the city, considering the buildings nearby.","'You must excuse me, ${PLAYER}, for my knowledge of the histories of Men is... sparse. Much of what I know of them I learned from the wagging tongues of my captors in Emax Dûl. But this must suffice!\
\
'The city you see before us was once named Jaghân, the City of Gates, but with the passage of time the name gradually changed, becoming Zaghâna. When a great conflagration of unknown origin burned much of the old city to the ground, the ruling Ibili, or Elders, established the First Triumvirate, a Council of Three to govern the reborn city. They gave it the name Zajâna, City of Keys, to herald the dawning of a new era for the city of the scholars.\
\
'But Ordâkh hungered for land and treasure, and when that empire seized the city more than one hundred and twenty years ago, they changed its name again: now it was Jajân, a puppet fiefdom held beneath the Hûl's distant boot. Gladly, the story does not end there! Let us proceed to Khab Antâx, the Overgate of the city, and I will tell you what happened only last year, and continues to this day.'","Ulishár is inside the city of Zajâna.","Ulishár stands beside the road that leads south-west to Zajâna.","Ulishár has come to Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân.","'Let us proceed to the gates and I will tell you what happened only last year, and continues to this day.'","'Despite its tumultuous history, Inkanûsh greatly desired to consult the libraries of Zajâna, for its scholars recorded much throughout the years that can be found in no other archive. He and Glorfindel have likely gone to search these troves for the knowledge they seek.'","Chapter 15.5: The Road To Zajâna","'This is the Overgate, one of the two famous gates that guards the pass through Mûr Ghala; the other lies in the southern wall of the city and blocks the road to the desert kingdoms beyond.\
\
'But I told you I would finish the tale. With so many of the soldiers of Ordâkh and Shagâna fighting away in the north during the last year, the people of Jajân rose against their oppressors. During this Scholars' Revolt, sometimes called the Second Blue Mutiny, they seized control of the western side of the city and pushed east until they were stopped by the remaining Ordâkhai garrison. Widespread fighting and ensuing fires split the city in twain, and it remains so today.\
\
'Now the free portion of the city is once again called Zajâna and it is ruled by a group of five: the Doorwards. The Ordâkh-controlled district of the city remains Jajân, and a new Triumvirate governs there. They believe this Second Blue Mutiny will end as did the first, crushed quickly by Ordâkh a hundred years ago, but as of yet it has not; the city remains divided.\
\
'Let us continue onward into the city.'","'Glorfindel and Inkanûsh have gone on ahead to Zajâna, and they sent me to find you, ${PLAYER}. If you have resolved matters here to your satisfaction, let us make for the city. I will tell you what I know of its history on the way.\
\
'The road to Zajâna lies north-west of here.'","Talk to Ulishár at Ingar-garâsh","Meet up with Ulishár at the cross-road north-west of Ingar-garâsh","Talk to Ulishár inside Zajâna","Ulishár stands by Khab Antâx, the Overgate outside Zajâna.","'Shâra Mizâdi invited him to join her army, but he says you and he have urgent business elsewhere?'","Continue on into Zajâna and meet up with Ulishár","Ulishár has come to Ingar-garâsh in search of you, bearing tidings about your companions' next road.","Ulishár suggested that you continue to the south-west until you reach Khab Antâx, the Overgate outside Zajâna.","'The road to Zajâna lies north-west of here. Glorfindel and Inkanûsh were eager to depart for the city.'"},
[2968]={"'You should learn the layout of Zajâna. Afterwards we will meet up with Glorfindel and Inkanûsh and determine our next course.'","Climb the stairs west to the commons of Zajâna","Chapter 15.6: City of Gates, City of Keys","Ulishár taps you apologetically on the shoulder","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the commons to learn the layout of the city","Ulishár suggested that you climb the stairs to the west and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the commons of the city, so you might learn the layout of Zajâna.","Glorfindel told you that Inkanûsh went to inspect Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate south of Zajâna.","Inkanûsh is at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate south of Zajâna.","Walk north into the scholar's district and find the stage","Find Inkanûsh at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate south of Zajâna","'We should be safe to explore the city, as long as you remain aware that the Ordâkhai control the elevated district on the southern rise. Why not climb to the west and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the commons of the city, ${PLAYER}? It will do you some good to learn the layout of Zajâna. Afterwards we will meet up with Glorfindel and Inkanûsh and determine our next course.'","'What is the matter?'","A bridge to the Ordâkhai-controlled district is beyond the arch to the south. The scholar's district is north","Zajâna the Splendid towers over Kighân, and visitors to the city are drawn to its libraries and cultural centres. Even so, peaceable travellers must avoid the presence of Ordâkh, which still attempts to control the city as it did before.","Glorfindel sees you approach and calls a greeting","Talk to Ulishár at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate","'Why not climb the stairs to the west and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the commons of the city, ${PLAYER}? It will do you some good to learn the layout of Zajâna. Afterwards we will meet up with Glorfindel and Inkanûsh and determine our next course.'","Glorfindel is by the stage in north-western Zajâna.","North of the commons lies the scholar's district of the city. Ulishár recommended that you go there and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the various sights of Zajâna.","Talk to Inkanûsh at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate","'I see that Ulishár was able to find you, ${PLAYER}! I am glad.\
\
'I have learned that a theatre troupe is about to perform an entertainment. Têrkar's Travellers, they are called, and if the talk I have overheard is to be believed, they are supposed to be quite skilled at their craft.\
\
'But the Wizard has little time for such things, and he wanted to inspect Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate of Zajâna, instead of waiting here for the show to begin. If you find him there, he will likely show you the fabled libraries of the city. I will tell you if Têrkar and his Travellers live up to their reputation when next we meet!'","'Inkanûsh has little time for such things, and he wanted to inspect the Nethergate of Zajâna instead of waiting here for the show to begin. If you find him there, he will likely show you the fabled libraries of the city. I will tell you if Têrkar and his Travellers live up to their reputation when next we meet!'","Talk to Glorfindel by the stage in north-west Zajâna","'Ah, yes, my friend. Ulishár told me he came with you to the city.'\
\
The Wizard gestures at the great southern gate.\
\
'Whether you name the city Jajân like the Ordâkhai or Zajâna like the Doorwards, it seems both groups agree on this one point: the Nethergate must remain sealed against the possibility of invasion by the Shoghór of the south.\
\
'You have already spoken with Glorfindel? He came not with you here; is there still time to visit the great library before we return to him?'\
\
You tell Inkanûsh that the Elf-lord agreed to report on the quality of Têrkar's Travellers' performance, but there should still be time to first visit the library of Zajâna.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the stage in the scholar's district","'I am sorry. Did you say the name \\qTêrkar's Travellers?\\q'\
\
You tell Ulishár you believe that is the name of the theatre troupe Glorfindel intends to watch perform elsewhere in the city, and the Kinta's eyes widen with surprise.\
\
'I know this group, ${PLAYER}, but I never thought to see them again! Têrkar and his theatre company were the very folk who aided me in my escape from Emax Dûl! I owe them my freedom, and my life!'","You have caught up with Inkanûsh and Ulishár at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate","Ulishár is at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate, and is very interested in something you have said."},
[2969]={"Talk to Inkanûsh at the Nethergate","Talk to Inkanûsh when you are ready to find the theatre troupe","'We came to this place to learn if the Thardúth pose a threat to these lands, and the great library of Zajâna, the Kalmakhíla, will aid me in this. The wisdom of many centuries is contained within. When last I walked these streets, it proved most informative on a great number of subjects!\
\
'But let none claim I am without feeling. To learn that Ulishár's absent friends have come to the city must delay our visit to the archives of Zajâna. My research can surely wait for the duration of their performance. How long could such a thing be? The Kalmakhíla has remained secure even while the city burned, so protective have its keepers been over the centuries!\
\
'Speak to me if you are amenable to this plan.'","'Then let us consume the day's entertainment, for Ulishár's sake, but also for our own. Afterwards we will go to the Kalmakhíla, the word-fortress of Zajâna.'","Ulishár has asked for permission to see the theatre troupe that has come to Zajâna.","Chapter 15.7: The Day's Entertainment","'It is good to learn the men of Têrkar's Travellers have returned safely from the war!'","'It was good of Inkanûsh to delay his plans so we might attend this performance, but now I have more questions than before!'","Talk to Ulishár by the stage in Zajâna","Ulishár is by the stage in Zajâna.","'I will always be in Têrkar's debt for the kindness he showed me. \\qOne last act of defiance before we march to their war,\\q he told me when we were safely out of Emax Dûl and heading eastward. That was a week before he and his men were to report to the northern march with the rest of the Shagâni conscripts from Mûr Ghala. They wished not to go, but it would mean death if they refused.\
\
'It is good to learn they have returned from the war!'","Inkanûsh is at the Nethergate south of Zajâna."},
[2970]={"Talk to Jêsamin in Zajâna","Ulishár is at the western market in Zajâna.","Retrieve the coin-purse from the Ordâkh-controlled district","'Retrieve the coin-purse from the Ordâkhai of this place and you will prove your friendship to Têrkar's Travellers. Hurry, now. The purse will be heavy with coin, for it contains all of our profit from the latest performance. The Zajâni love to hear about their resistance against Ordâkh, and they paid good coin for the privilege.'","Talk to Glorfindel at the western market in Zajâna","'There you are, ${PLAYER}. Inkanûsh sent me to bring word that he desires to speak with you.'","'I am Satagêra, the widow of Têrkar, and I am the playwright of this company of travelling players. I am pleased to meet any friend of Ulishár, for the Kinta is dear to us all, as he was to my husband. It was Têrkar's Travellers that smuggled him from the captivity of Ordâkh before most of our company were sent to war, did he tell you that?'\
\
Satagêra smiles fondly.\
\
'\\qOne last act of defiance,\\q my Têrkar called it. I am glad we did as he bade, for Ulishár's treatment in that city was hard. I think he would not have survived among the Ordâkhai for many more months.\
\
'I invite you to speak with the others of my company. A cloud hangs over us this day, but do not let it trouble you. It is a private matter, and one we can handle ourselves.'","Asharmûl is outside the Ordâkh-controlled district in south-east Zajâna.","Asharmûl and Zimêlkha asked you to retrieve from the Ordâkhai the coin-purse containing the money Têrkar's Travellers earned from their performance.","Zimêlkha stands with Asharmûl in Zajâna.","'Asharmûl and Zimêlkha can recover the stolen purse from the Ordâkh-controlled district of the city, but they will welcome your help if you offer it. Look for them in the residential district of Zajâna to the south-east.'","Talk to Imalêkh in Zajâna","'Does Satagêra think we two cannot retrieve the stolen purse? What say you, Asharmûl?'","Talk to Satagêra in Zajâna","'The Ordâkhai emptied the purse they took from us before you could retrieve it? That is a shame, my new friend.'\
\
Asharmûl smiles at you, a twinkle in his eye.\
\
'While you kept their attention, Zimêlkha and I took the opportunity to rob them anew. I think you will find that the number of coins we retrieved perhaps exceeds the number they took from us, but that is the price of thinking one might outwit Têrkar's Travellers!\
\
'Bring this fresh, newly-heavy coin-purse to Atâlsi, with our regards. I think she will be pleased.'","Talk to Atâlsi in Zajâna","Chapter 15.8: Têrkar's Travellers","Talk to Zimêlkha in south-east Zajâna","'Can we not help my friends recover their stolen purse of coins? I feel badly that the theft occurred as we watched the performance, and we noticed it not!\
\
'What says Satagêra to this? I have only ventured with you for a short time, ${PLAYER}, but already I know you for one who helps others when the chance comes!\
\
'We will not allow this to delay us overmuch; Inkanûsh will certainly understand, will he not?'","Asharmûl hands you a much heavier purse than the one you retrieved","You found the rest of Têrkar's Travellers outside the Ordâkh-controlled district","Talk to Mashkânu in Zajâna","Talk to Ulishár at the western market in Zajâna","'For Têrkar we served as guardians and enforcers of the peace when trouble called, and now that he is gone we do the same for his widow Satagêra. She doubts not our skill, Zimêlkha. She sees opportunity.'\
\
Asharmûl points toward the Ordâkh-controlled district of Zajâna, up the stairs to the south-east.\
\
'If you retrieve the coin-purse from the Ordâkhai of this place, you will prove your friendship to Têrkar's Travellers. Hurry, now. The purse will be heavy with coin, for it contains all of our profit from the latest performance. The Zajâni love to hear about their resistance against Ordâkh, and they paid good coin for the privilege.'","Bring the empty coin-purse to Asharmûl in south-east Zajâna","Ulishár is delighted to have encountered the theatre troupe that aided him during his escape from captivity, but he is troubled by their fewer numbers.","Têrkar's Travellers are at the western market in Zajâna.","Find Asharmûl and Zimêlkha in the residential district of Zajâna to the south-east","'I have spoken to Satagêra, and it is as I feared. Her husband Têrkar perished in the north, as did several others of the troupe. The fire-eater Zurûsh, the twins Dârjo and Orukhíl... no word has come back of Khazín or Urûnam, but Imalêkh fears they must also have died in battle. She was wounded during the retreat before the mighty city and saw them no more.\
\
'But the tidings are not all sad. Zimêlkha was held in reserve at the river-city and saw no fighting; her soldiers were driven south as Gondor advanced. And a fortunate star must shine upon Mashkânu, for Satagêra tells me he was wounded in the forest early during the fighting, and was not made to march upon Minas Tirith.\
\
'I mourn for the friends who were so kind to me, ${PLAYER}, and I honour their memory! Despite this sorrow, my heart fills to once again see those of Têrkar's Travellers who remain to bring joy to the folk of Shagâna!'","'I am Imalêkh, trick archer and juggler of the company, and it is a pleasure to meet any friend of Ulishár. Satagêra insists upon writing villainous roles for me: the deadly marksman who threatens the heroes, the brooding lieutenant of the evil king. I have prevailed upon her to give me something romantic next time, something bawdy!\
\
'We can all use a good laugh after what we went through in the north. I keep hoping Khazín or Urûnam will stroll up and demand a drink, but there has been no word. They were most skilled with their blades, but the foes arrayed against us were terrifying and numerous: frightening, mounted demons, bellowing for death.'","Bring the heavy coin-purse to Atâlsi at the western market in Zajâna","'When I knew Têrkar, it was customary after a performance for the company to gather at the nearest tavern to spend a portion of the day's coins on ale. I would like to see if that remains the case, ${PLAYER}! Let us look for them among the markets to the south-west, where it is possible they will acquire food and drink to sustain them following the performance!'","'A friend of Ulishár is a friend of mine!'","Find Têrkar's Travellers at the western market in Zajâna","The playwright Satagêra is at the western market in Zajâna.","Asharmûl and Zimêlkha went to the residential district of south-east Zajâna.","'We will not allow this to delay us overmuch; Inkanûsh will certainly understand, will he not?'","'Zimêlkha and Asharmûl have gone in search of the villain, but until they return with the right purse I will not be satisfied.'","'Bring that fresh, newly-heavy coin-purse to Atâlsi, with our regards. I think she will be pleased.\
\
'No, I trust you. You are a friend.'","The coin-purse feels empty, but you should return it all the same","Glorfindel is at the western market in Zajâna.","'A friend of Ulishár is a friend of mine! I am called Jêsamin, and I am a singer, tumbler, juggler, and player of drums for Têrkar's Travellers. What is it that you can do?'\
\
You tell Jêsamin that you are a ${CLASS} and an adventurer, and ask where she is from.\
\
'I live on the dusty road, friend, but I count myself among the Zajâni. I have not seen very many in Shagâna that look as I do, but that is fine with me! When Satagêra has need of someone to play a child, a goblin, or the legendary trickster Kêph, she can rely upon Jêsamin, for few indeed are as she is!'","'I am Atâlsi. Like Satagêra and our former leader Têrkar, I am from Zajâna.'\
\
The woman falls silent, but her eyes remain active, scanning the crowds.\
\
'Forgive me if I seem distracted. I collect the coins for our performances, and during our latest it seems some quick-fingered thief replaced our purse with one of similar heft and weight, but different contents: grey stones instead of shiny coins. Zimêlkha and Asharmûl have gone in search of the villain, but until they return with the right purse I will not be satisfied.'","'Asharmûl and Zimêlkha are capable of retrieving our stolen purse, but if you are willing to help I will not refuse it.\
\
'This is not the first time such a theft has occurred, and it will not be the last. Look for them in the residential district of Zajâna to the south-east, for the thief is likely to have fled for the Ordâkh-controlled district of the city.'","Zimêlkha is outside the Ordâkh-controlled district in south-east Zajâna.","Atâlsi is at the western market in Zajâna.","Ulishár stands by his friends in Zajâna.","'Who seeks Zimêlkha?'\
\
You explain that you are a friend of Ulishár the Kinta, and that Satagêra suggested you lend your aid to retrieve the stolen coin-purse.\
\
'Has our playwright's opinion of our skill fallen so low that she thinks we two unable to retrieve this stolen purse? Atâlsi should have kept a closer watch on it! She knows how often thieves think to rob us of our hard-earned profit!\
\
'What say you, Asharmûl?'","'We can all use a good laugh after what we went through in the north.'","'Tell me you have retrieved the stolen coin-purse, friend, and that Asharmûl and Zimêlkha encountered no difficulty among the Ordâkhai.'\
\
You place the coin-purse in her hand and Atâlsi almost drops it.\
\
'Thank you for your help, friend of Ulishár! But I must ask... did it always contain so many coins? I knew not that our performance was such a success! If you ever have need of assistance, you can count upon the friendship of Têrkar's Travellers!'","The coin-purse you were sent to retrieve has been emptied of its contents by the Ordâkhai, but you should return it to Asharmûl in south-east Zajâna.","'I mourn for the friends who were so kind to me, ${PLAYER}, and I honour their memory! Despite this sorrow, my heart fills to once again see those of Têrkar's Travellers who remain to bring joy to the folk of Shagâna!'","Ulishár has spoken with his friends, and wears a mournful expression","'I invite you to speak with the others of my company. A cloud hangs over us this day, but do not let it trouble you. It is a private matter, and one we can handle ourselves.'","Talk to Asharmûl in south-east Zajâna","'Inkanûsh is a figure of legend and myth, an odd wanderer and a troublemaker. Are you perhaps mistaken?'","'If you ever have need of assistance, you can count upon the friendship of Têrkar's Travellers!'","'I am the wardrobe-master of this company, and am called Mashkânu.\
\
'I caught sight of you from the stage, stranger. Who is the hooded man with whom you watched the performance?'\
\
You answer that your companion is the Wizard Inkanûsh, and he may have taken issue with his portrayal in the play. Mashkânu's eyes narrow.\
\
'Inkanûsh is a figure of legend and myth, an odd wanderer and a troublemaker. Are you perhaps mistaken?'","Têrkar's Travellers may be in the western market of Zajâna."},
[2971]={"'These tidings are unsurprising. I confess I expected Inkanûsh to remain here in Zajâna from the moment I set eyes upon the Kalmakhíla. Did he tell you about the Din of Stone?'\
\
You tell Glorfindel that the Wizard seemed certain the Din of Stone may have revealed more vaults of the Thardúth than Utug-bûr alone, and the Elf-lord nods.\
\
'He is rarely wrong, ${PLAYER}. These enchanted servants of Morgoth needed two things to threaten Middle-earth in the present age, and if Inkanûsh is correct they may have both of these things in Mûr Ghala: the end of their enchantment and access once again to the surface. We will take the road north-west as it climbs into An Shêru and keep watch for any sign of the Thardúth or their Utûgi warriors. Will Ulishár remain our guide on this road, or does he desire to remain in Zajâna with the travelling players now that they are reunited?'","Chapter 15.9: A Wizard In His Natural Environment","'I swore to slay him, if ever I could... but I am unable to carry out my vow!'","Inkanûsh stands in the Kalmakhíla.","Find Glorfindel at the Overgate outside Zajâna","Glorfindel is at the Overgate north of Zajâna.","You hear angry approaching footsteps","Inkanûsh has selected a tome and some pages for you to study in the Kalmakhíla.","Inkanûsh is in the Kalmakhíla in Zajâna.","'Will Ulishár remain our guide on this road, or does he desire to remain in Zajâna with the travelling players now that they are reunited?'","'Stand aside! The Wizard will pay for his crimes! I have come to slay this evil creature, this Mithrandir!\
\
'The Wizard will die at my hand!'","Mashkânu of Têrkar's Travellers has arrived in a rage","Without warning, Mashkânu bursts into tears","Mashkânu of Têrkar's Travellers has come to the Kalmakhíla, his weapon raised in anger.","'Know now the truth, my friend, and be healed, if such a thing can be possible.'","'I spoke to Glorfindel of this possibility, my friend. He will be waiting for you at the Overgate outside the city.'","'Though mine was a bittersweet reunion with Têrkar's Travellers, I was still most pleased to see them again! Even so, I made a commitment to guide you on the road through Mûr Ghala and I will not forsake that pledge!'\
\
Ulishár smiles.\
\
'In any event, Satagêra told me they must also take the westward road in a few days. She has been hired to write a new play for the Travellers to perform; it may be our paths will cross again.'","If you are able to <rgb=#00FF00>calm</rgb> Mashkânu, you might avoid the violence he intends in the Kalmakhíla.","'He has found his natural environment, as I knew he would! He has gone to the Kalmakhíla, the great library of Zajâna, and already he believes he has learned something of use, if not all of what he sought. He will tell you in person.\
\
'The entrance to this word-fortress, the Khíla, is to the north-east of here, beside the commons.'","'Be healed? I can never be healed, though my wounds have closed and I once again speak the words Satagêra has given to me, seeking applause and coin.\
\
'But so many of my friends returned not from the northern forest, or the fields outside the great city, or the Black Gate of Mordor. We were told that gate could never fall, but fall it did, and the vast armies of Barkhûsh and Ordâkh with it!'\
\
Mashkânu wipes his eyes.\
\
'When I beheld the Wizard Mithrandir earlier this day and learned he answered to the name Inkanûsh, I could not believe it. Inkanûsh is a figure of mischief and a troublemaker... but in none of the legends is he cruel, or destructive. It is a balm for my heart to learn the devastation I beheld was not caused by the trickster sprite of myth at whom I laughed in my youth, but was instead a final cruel consequence of Barkhûsh's evil.'","'I may have found part of the answer I sought. Look here!'","'I have not yet learned all that I sought by coming here, but I have confirmed one of my suspicions, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'It seems to my thinking that the Thardúth who lay hidden at Utug-bûr required two things to happen before they could trouble Middle-earth anew. First, they must pass beyond living memory of all who knew of them, and that was accomplished by the defeat of Sauron. Second, the chambers in which they lay buried must be brought to the surface by some geologic change: the movement of the earth, the diversion of the waters, the alteration of the rocks.\
\
'So it was at Utug-bûr, and ever my thought turned upon this matter: could it happen elsewhere? I may have found part of the answer. Look here!'","\\qThe sound was terrible and heard by all, but the devastation in the wake of the Urash-zâl was worst of all, and it changed the face of the land: cliffs crumbled, boulders fell from the height, great chasms opened in the earth along the whole of the Mûr. Even the great northern gate of Jajân cracked, so widespread were the effects of the tremors of the Urash-zâl.\\q","Glorfindel and Ulishár wait for you by the Overgate","Someone approaches, and they sound angry.","Remain on guard, just in case","Inkanûsh has gone to the Kalmakhíla, one of the most famous scholarly archives in all of Zajâna.","Glorfindel is at the Overgate outside Zajâna.","Talk to Inkanûsh in the Kalmakhíla","'Inkanûsh has gone to the Kalmakhíla, the great library of Zajâna, and already he believes he has learned something of use, if not all of what he sought. He will tell you in person.\
\
'The entrance to this word-fortress, the Khíla, is to the north-east of here, beside the commons.'","Someone approaches, and their anger is evident","Ulishár is at the Overgate outside Zajâna.","Talk to Mashkânu in the Kalmakhíla","Mashkânu's rage has been replaced with sorrow.","'You have provided a balm for the pain of my heart.'","Read the open book on the table in the Kalmakhíla","<rgb=#00FF00>Calm</rgb> Mashkânu in the Kalmakhíla","Have your efforts borne fruit?","Talk to Inkanûsh in the Kalmakhíla in north-west Zajâna","'I cannot...' he weeps, his body seized by tremendous shuddering cries as tears stream down his face.\
\
'Friend of Ulishár... how can one such as you... befriend this monster? This is no man... he is a creature of death! I swore to slay him, if that could be in my power... but...'\
\
Mashkânu struggles to speak through wracking sobs.\
\
'I was pierced by an arrow in the side, loosed from in hiding by green-garbed men in the northern forest. Others of my company marched on the great city, and fell during the fighting, but I retreated with others of the wounded to Mordor. From the shadow of the Black Gate I witnessed as the armies of the West approached, and I saw the fighting's end! So it was I witnessed the arrival of this man you defend, and heard his name spoken aloud by the Men of Gondor. \\qMithrandir,\\q they called him, and even from so far away I knew him for a Wizard.'\
\
Mashkânu's bloodshot eyes flare with anger and with fear.\
\
'I watched as the Wizard Mithrandir threw his arms into the air, and the very earth rocked beneath his feet! \\qThe hour of doom!\\q I heard him command over the tumult. In answer to his spell, the mighty towers and rampart of the Black Gate crumbled into dust! Wherever he looked, death came to his enemies, and those that could not escape perished! I fled... but still I can hear the terrible voice of the Wizard and the death he caused!\
\
'I swore to slay him, if ever I could... but now my sword-arm freezes... and I am unable to carry out my vow!'","'I would remain and speak with Mashkânu a little longer, ${PLAYER}. Furthermore, my research is not yet complete. I must search for more information about the Urash-zâl, the Din of Stone, within the Kalmakhíla. I believe you should continue without me on the western road as it climbs into An Shêru. I will catch up to you when I have finished my studies in Zajâna, but until I have done so you must remain alert for the presence of the Thardúth in Mûr Ghala.\
\
'I spoke to Glorfindel of this possibility, my friend. He will be waiting for you at the Overgate outside the city.'","'The people of Mûr Ghala named it Urash-zâl: the Din of Stone. It was a terrifying noise that could be heard all along the Ridge of Plenty, and its tremors changed the face of the land, opening great chasms, diverting the course of rivers, and drying lakes to their very beds. This was the cause of the Great Dearth that so affected much of Shagâna.\
\
'One hundred and twenty years ago, the Hûl of Ordâkh committed a terrible act of change with effects that would ripple throughout all of Shagâna. His purpose was to open the way for his armies to conquer the lands to the north, but as we saw at Utug-bûr, I fear this act cleared the way for even greater evils. Now these ancient servants of Morgoth, these Thardúth, have broken loose from the enchantment that kept them preserved for thousands of years, and they stir again in the darkness beneath the earth.\
\
'The Din of Stone revealed the hidden temple of Utug-bûr in which the Thardúth slept. How many other such hidden places might it have revealed elsewhere in Shagâna, ${PLAYER}?'","Inkanûsh is in the Kalmakhíla in north-west Zajâna, beside the commons.","Read the pages on the table in the Kalmakhíla","'You are one of the theatre players who worked to free Ulishár from captivity when he was held by the Ordâkhai? I know you from the recent performance, and from the stories he has told to us of your company. Your name is Mashkânu, wardrobe-master of Têrkar's Travellers? But no one is one thing alone; you were a soldier pressed into service, forced to fight for Sauron against the Host of the West through threat or falsehood.\
\
'You have been deceived again, Mashkânu, this time by your own eyes. It was no spell of mine that brought low the Black Gate or the Towers of the Teeth on the edge of Mordor. A great weapon of Sauron's was unmade, and its undoing heralded the destruction of all he had wrought, despite his terrible power.\
\
'Some who had been held spell-enslaved by the Dark Lord of Mordor threw themselves into pits or fought desperate last stands, but many were of like kind as you, Mashkânu: held in thrall not by enchantment but by the fear of cruel commanders from Ordâkh and their tales of horrible monsters from Gondor and the North. Know now the truth, my friend, and be healed, if such a thing can be possible.'","Talk to Glorfindel at the Overgate","Talk to Ulishár at the Overgate","The pages of the open book are weathered and faded, but still legible.\
\
\\q...would not have believed it ever ran so deep had I not seen it myself only months before, but the flow of the river was greatly diminished. By the third day following the great tremors it had slowed to a trickle. My friend insists that the Usâl and the Agâl too will never flow again as they had, and even the lake of Idagâl is now a cracked and dry basin. He named it Khadagâl, the Dry-whelm, but the herdsmen insist that is a name of ill omen and the lake must return. I think they are both right and wrong: I believe the name is ill-starred, but the waters of the lake have gone forever.\
\
'Were the great tremors of the Urash-zâl a natural event, like the rising and setting of the sun or the passing of the seasons, or was it inflicted upon us by the whim of the Ghursâti? What could we have done to incur such wrath and vengeance?\
\
'My friend thinks Shurash Hûl of Ordâkh is somehow to blame for the Urash-zâl, for the drying of the rivers has removed the last barrier to the northern progress of his armies. I say it must be happenstance, for the quakes were felt along the entirety of the Mûr. How could one man so change the face of the land, even one so ambitious as the Hûl?\\q","In Mashkânu's eyes you see more than rage. You see fear"},
[2972]={"'I will set about making the brew, ${PLAYER}, if you do not mind waiting. Let me know if that is fine.'","'There is a Ranger by the entrance. Tell him that Nár means no harm by his words, from wherever they come.'","'It will be a few moments. Find a comfortable place to wait.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>","'There is something very peculiar about this place.'","'I do not know, ${PLAYER}! Nár has often said peculiar things, but it is difficult sometimes to determine what he means by them. He has had an extremely long and extremely painful life, as I understand it, and only faithful Frithgeir remains now to help him continue it.\
\
'These Men with you, these Rangers...they seem disturbed by what Nár has said. Can you ease their minds? I fear they will do him some harm, and I cannot allow that!'","'I do not know what to make of these dwarves!'","Talk to Corunir in Zudrugund","You have brought the ingredients Frithgeir needs to make a brew that will restore Nár's awareness of you so you can ask him what he said to Wadu.","'Frithgeir is going to make the brew for Nár? Good. I hope it is enough to make him understandable for us. Speak with Frithgeir and see how goes the work.'","Talk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund","Corunir is at Zudrugund.\
\
Frithgeir wants you to speak to Corunir and assure him that Nár means no harm.","Chapter 15: An Echo of Days Past","Frithgeir is in Zudrugund, the once-abandoned dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb.\
\
Frithgeir is preparing to make the brew that will restore Nár's clarity so you can ask him questions.","'I am completely at a loss, ${PLAYER}. How can Nár have known what Elrond said to his sons before we departed Rivendell? And what does it mean that he does know it?'\
\
Corunir sighs, and you realize that it has become a familiar sound. He catches your look and smiles bitterly.\
\
'It feels like we are mired in something we do not fully understand. We cannot afford to ignore this mystery, for it may threaten the very purpose of our journey, but what will we discover?\
\
'We must take a rest, in any event. We can talk this over later, and hope things will be more clear.'","'What does it mean, ${PLAYER}? I do not know what the words of Nár must signify, but they fill me with dread! Speak with Frithgeir about this! Demand that he tell us what this means for the Grey Company!'","Talk to Frithgeir and wait for him to make the brew for Nár","Frithgeir is in Zudrugund, the once-abandoned dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb.\
\
You have travelled with Nár into the mine beneath Zudrugund and witnessed some peculiar things that the Dúnedain are hard-pressed to explain."},
[2973]={"Habla con Ningloril en Thangúlhad","Completa la Escaramuza: Forzar la Puerta del Nigromante","'El hecho de que Thangúlhad siga bajo nuestro control y que la Hueste Dorada siga oponiéndose a los espectros que gobiernan esa fortaleza son ambos testimonios de tu destreza y la nuestra. ¡Enviemos un mensaje a los que residen dentro de esas paredes!\
\
'Ha llegado el momento de atacar con fuerza la fortaleza del Enemigo, . Goldagnir ha ideado un plan para hacerlo, y lo hemos estado discutiendo. Él te dirá los detalles si le informas que estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a luchar.'","Los Elfos de la Hueste Dorada están preparados para lanzar su asalto a la fortaleza de Dol Guldur.","Goldagnir está en Thangúlhad.\
\
Se te ha dicho que hables con Goldagnir sobre los detalles del plan para atacar la fortaleza de Dol Guldur.","Goldagnir está en Thangúlhad, esperando para comenzar la segunda etapa del asalto a Dol Guldur.\
\
Has participado en la escaramuza en la puerta de la fortaleza y ahora deberías hablar con Goldagnir para conocer sus planes para la siguiente etapa de la batalla.","'Ningloril está aquí en Thangúlhad. Ha estado preguntando por ti. Es mejor no hacerla esperar, porque cuando su mente está decidida, nada la disuade de pensar en ello.'","'La próxima escaramuza llevará a la Hueste Dorada detrás de las murallas de Dol Guldur, al mismo escondite de los Espectros del Anillo que ahora residen dentro de la fortaleza. ¡No temas a los males fantasmales! ¡La Hueste Dorada estará contigo!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Dúo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Ha llegado el momento de lanzar el ataque contra Dol Guldur. La primera escaramuza tendrá lugar en la puerta de la fortaleza.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Dúo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","'La fortaleza de Dol Guldur se encuentra en la cima de la torre rocosa, hacia el este, ${PLAYER}. No será fácil abrirnos camino más allá de las murallas, porque el Enemigo nos verá venir desde una gran distancia.\
\
'Los que logremos llegar a la puerta tendremos que soportar la carga del combate para todo el ejército, porque estamos seguros de que no tenemos los números necesarios para una victoria fácil.\
\
'¡Tomar el control de la puerta es solo el comienzo, pero concentrémonos en el inicio de la campaña antes de planificar el final!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Dúo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","'Hemos tomado el control de las puertas, pero puede que no las mantengamos por mucho tiempo. Debemos actuar rápidamente y lanzar el segundo ataque contra la fortaleza.\
\
'Esta escaramuza tendrá lugar dentro de las murallas de Dol Guldur; no sé qué peligros enfrentaremos allí, pero ese es el destino de la Hueste Dorada y debemos enfrentarlo sin vacilar.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Dúo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","'La Hueste Dorada ha tenido éxito en el primer ataque contra la fortaleza, ${PLAYER}, pero ahora ha llegado el momento de hacer lo que vinimos a hacer.'","'La primera escaramuza en nuestro ataque contra Dol Guldur tendrá lugar en la puerta de la fortaleza. ¡No vaciles en tu determinación!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Dúo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Goldagnir está en Thangúlhad.\
\
Has participado en la segunda escaramuza en Dol Guldur y deberías informar a Goldagnir.","'¡La batalla va bien, ${PLAYER}! Quizás veamos el final de esta canción después de todo y tengamos bardos dispuestos a cantarla, y gente viva para escucharla.\
\
'Ningloril estaba pidiendo verte de nuevo. Ahora que la Hueste Dorada ha llegado tan lejos en la torre rocosa, ella cree que puede ser posible lograr otro de nuestros objetivos aquí en el Bosque Negro, uno que se dejó de lado hace días.'","Completa la Escaramuza: Asalto a la Guarida de los Espectros del Anillo","Capítulo 15: Asalto a Dol Guldur","'Goldagnir tiene el plan de batalla para atacar la fortaleza de Dol Guldur. Él te lo mostrará si estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a participar en la batalla. Ya he visto lo suficiente de tus habilidades para saber que estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}; no puede haber ninguna duda al respecto.'","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, el campamento de la Hueste Dorada en Gathbúrz.\
\
Ningloril te ha pedido que vuelvas a verla sobre un encargo secreto.","Habla con Goldagnir en Thangúlhad","La batalla por Dol Guldur continúa, con la próxima escaramuza teniendo lugar detrás de las murallas de la ciudad.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Dúo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>"},
[2974]={"Talk to Asharmûl in south-east Ahâba","'It is a good plan. Remain calm and confident, and all will be well.'","It is time for Têrkar's Travellers to perform Satagêra's masterpiece, and for you to complete your mission and learn how the plans of Ordâkh and the Thardúth intertwine.","'I am as ready as ever I will be. Let us find Asharmûl and tell him we are prepared to go.'","'Let us find Asharmûl and tell him we are prepared to go.'","Talk to Asharmûl and go with Têrkar's Travellers into Emax Dûl","Asharmûl is in south-east Ahâba.","Chapter 16.10: The Great Triumph of Mordor and Ordâkh","'You are ready, then? Once we depart for Emax Dûl there will be no turning back. Let me know if you are certain.'","The time has come for you to go with Asharmûl and the rest of Têrkar's Travellers into the guarded fastness of Emax Dûl.","'What did you learn? Quickly, now!'\
\
Inkanûsh listens closely as you describe what you learned about Sûg Nidar, the Fearwater, and the long creation of the Song of Waves and Wind. The Wizard strokes his beard, deep in thought.\
\
'I should have known, ${PLAYER}. When the Din of Stone shook the Mûr, it collapsed a great cavern to the east of Ikorbân. The river rushed into the chasm, creating a vast lake that showed on no map. After Thorongil destroyed the Corsair fleet at Umbar, Sauron demanded a new fleet be built; the Fearwater proved the perfect location. Had he not loosed his war too soon, and waited for the Song to be complete, things might have turned out differently. That the fleet was kept secret from all may have prevented the Masters of Mordor from attempting to harness it against us.'\
\
Inkanûsh tilts his head to one side, thinking.\
\
'Secret from all, did I say? No. Azagath knew of this fleet, this Song of Waves and Wind, and so did Nakási Wave-reaper. This may be a problem.'","Inkanûsh must be told what you have discovered.","Talk to Inkanûsh on the island in the centre of the oasis of Ahâba"},
[2975]={"Talk to Rahâzi in Khanâg Valoyar","Chapter 16.11: A Journey Into Danger","Ulishár will remain in Idagâl to stand alongside Têrkar's Travellers","'To Khanâg Valoyar, then, and without delay!'","Rahâzi stands here.","Glorfindel will remain in Idagâl to stand against the Thardúth","'Then we must quickly conceal ourselves within the departing waggon!'","Your companions assemble in Ahâba to discuss these fresh dangers.","With dangers looming in two directions, the time has come to make a difficult choice: some must remain in Idagâl to oppose the Thardúth, and some must return north to combat this last evil of Sauron.","Talk to Rahâzi outside the waggon that brought you to Sûg Nidar","According to what you learned in Emax Dûl, supply-waggons for Sûg Nidar depart from Khanâg Valoyar, south of Jiret-menêsh, in An Shêru.","Fortunately, there is no sign of the Temámir who accosted you during your last visit","Rahâzi will journey with you and oppose this last evil of Sauron","'I will accompany you on this journey, ${PLAYER}. Such a fleet as you describe threatens my home and my people, and no daughter of Iridír could let this danger remain unmet and unopposed!\
\
'Supplies depart for Sûg Nidar from the khanâg south of Jiret-menêsh, Khanâg Valoyar? That is where you encountered that impolite Temámir, is it not? If we are fortunate, he may unwittingly drive us to the harbour where the Song of Waves and Wind is under construction!\
\
'To Khanâg Valoyar, then, and without delay!'","Return to Khanâg Valoyar in An Shêru","'I must remain with Inkanûsh to face the Thardúth of Damudûr, if it comes to that. But fear not, my friend: I know you have the courage and the skill to end the threat posed by the Song of Waves and Wind.\
\
'I will see you again when you return in victory!'","<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>\
\
Rahâzi is outside the waggon that brought the two of you to Sûg Nidar, the Fearwater.","'From your account it sounds like the Song is nearing completion, but is not yet ready to sail. We are fortunate. If goods and supplies travel by waggon from Khanâg Valoyar to Sûg Nidar, one or two secret stowaways might gain access to the harbour where the Song is being constructed.\
\
'Can I count upon you to do this, ${PLAYER}? You must prevent the Song from setting sail. I will remain here to combat the Thardúth, but I do not ask you to travel alone. Any who seek to go with you on this journey into danger will have my approval.'","Talk to Glorfindel in Ahâba","'You must prevent the Song from setting sail. I will remain here to combat the Thardúth, but I do not ask you to travel alone. Any who seek to go with you on this journey into danger will have my approval.'","Talk to Ulishár in Ahâba","Rahâzi is at Khanâg Valoyar in An Shêru.","Talk to Rahâzi in Ahâba","'Luck is with us. According to these papers, a waggon is soon to depart for Sûg Nidar. Are you ready to go? It will be some time before we return to these lands!\
\
'Let me know if you are prepared!'","'If you ask me to go with you I will, ${PLAYER}, but my heart tells me to remain with Têrkar's Travellers while they stay in this land. I owe them a debt of friendship for all they have done, and I want to stay and fight the Thardúth, if Inkanûsh asks it of me.\
\
'My heart has also not stopped racing since we passed within Emax Dûl! I am not sure it could handle another mission of secrecy so soon after the last!'","Talk to Rahâzi in Khanâg Valoyar and sneak aboard the next waggon to depart","'We made it. This is Sûg Nidar, the Fearwater.'","Rahâzi is at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru. She has identified the next waggon to depart, and is prepared to sneak aboard it with you."},
[2976]={"'If this man has something to say, he should say it to my face!'","'The air is thin and cold in An Shêru. I like it not! I much prefer the warmth and life of Ambarûl to this desolate height. Are pleasant villages so few here that we must shelter among crypts and tombs? But it was Shâra Mizâdi's command to scout this place for her foes, and we will do it.\
\
'I understand one of my companions met you some time ago, ${PLAYER}. His name is Shenzâmin, and he speaks most highly of you. The other is named Kishâtal, and he has proven a sturdy ally to me as well, besting a number of brigands that thought to ambush us between Ingar-garâsh and the road through Kighân.'","You have come to An Shêru, the Height of the Sky, and must now brave the dangers of this inhospitable land.","Wights stalk Naxar Dâl in northern An Shêru.","Wights stalk the heights of Naxar Dâl","It would appear Mashdagâl has something he wants to say.","Talk to Shenzâmin in Naxar Dâl","Chapter 16.1: Hallows In The Height","The man leaning against a nearby wall snorts in derision","Talk to Shenzâmin at Gadim-ûn","You hear one of the Hamâti soldiers calling for you within Naxar Dâl","You picked up a parchment covered in a sorcerer's mad ravings.","Defeat wights at Naxar Dâl (5/6)","Examine the corpse of the sorcerer of Ordâkh in Naxar Dâl","'This slain man wears the distinctive robes of a sorcerer from Ordâkh. What led him to his death among these ruins? Search his body and we may learn the answer, or if his allies are nearby.'","'I am Shenzâmin of Kûr Anzar, ${PLAYER}. We last spoke outside the town of Urmâkh, in Imhûlar. I did not expect to see you again so far from where last we met, but the surprise is a pleasant one!\
\
'It is Shâra Mizâdi's command that we watch the road through An Shêru for any sign of foes that might endanger her army as it travels. Rahâzi of Iridír says she does not like this place; I echo her thoughts, for the thin air and the cold fills me with unease.'","'I found something, ${PLAYER}. Look here! This slain man wears the distinctive robes of a sorcerer. Did he come here in search of treasure? I said nothing back at Gadim-ûn, but I think that unmannerly scoundrel might be a treasure-seeker himself, if not an outright brigand. Should we tell him of this man's fate, it may encourage him to seek another profession!\
\
'This corpse tells us the Ordâkhai have already pressed forward into An Shêru, and this man, at least, ran afoul of the wights. Has he anything upon him that might tell us the movements of his allies?'","Read the parchment you recovered from the sorcerer of Ordâkh","Shenzâmin discovered the corpse of a man of Ordâkh wearing sorcerous robes in Naxar Dâl.","Mashdagâl told you that if you want to help so badly, you might deal with creatures of evil at Naxar Dâl.","'You found a parchment on the slain sorcerer of Ordâkh? What does it say?'","'If Mizâdi really wants to aid the people who must live in An Shêru, her followers must prove her good intentions. There are wights to be found at Naxar Dâl. Have you the courage to face them?'","'I understand one of my companions met you some time ago. His name is Shenzâmin, and he speaks most highly of you.'","Rahâzi has introduced you to the Hamâti soldiers with whom she travels. They can be found at Gadim-ûn in An Shêru.","Defeat wights at Naxar Dâl (${NUMBER}/6)","Find Naxar Dâl to the north of Gadim-ûn","You find a parchment covered in mad ravings","Shenzâmin is in Naxar Dâl. What has he discovered?","'This is not the first talk of this sort I have overheard. Every new ruler thinks to better the lives of their people, but when the time comes to make good on such promises they are found wanting!\
\
'Is this Mizâdi any different? If she really wants to aid the people who must live in An Shêru, her followers must prove her good intentions. There are wights to be found at Naxar Dâl. Have you the courage to face them?'\
\
You ask Mashdagâl why he ventures so near to tombs known to be inhabited by wights, and he chuckles.\
\
'That is my own business, stranger. If they prove too fearsome for you to handle, I am certain your warrior-queen will be along shortly to recover your equipment and your body. I hear this Mizâdi is different than the others.'","'The Elf-lord Glorfindel will want to see that parchment, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps he will know what those ravings could mean.'","Talk to Mashdagâl in Gadim-ûn","Glorfindel will want to see the writings of the sorcerer of Ordâkh. The Elf-lord waits for you in Gadim-ûn.","Talk to Kishâtal at Gadim-ûn","'What have you found, my friend? From the look in your eye I deem you have discovered something that must concern us.'\
\
You hand the ravings of the Ordâkhai sorcerer to Glorfindel, and he closely studies the parchment. After a moment he looks up at you.\
\
'These words remind me of the Dagor Carlanthir, ${PLAYER}. To me this writing sounds like someone with less fortitude than Inkanûsh experiencing the mind-tampering of the Thardúth.'","Defeated wights at Naxar Dâl (${NUMBER}/6)","'It is Shâra Mizâdi's command that we watch the road through An Shêru for any sign of foes that might endanger her army as it travels.'","'Shâra Mizâdi entrusted us with scouting the Height of the Sky for any sign of Ordâkhai aggression. We are also to treat with the Temámir dwarves that are said to dwell in this place, and to offer them the friendship of Renewed Hamât.'\
\
Kishâtal smiles with wry amusement.\
\
'Shenzâmin and I have spoken of this curiosity before: that neither of us knew ourselves to be Hamâti before the rise of Shâra Mizâdi. Now each of us would die for her, and for Renewed Hamât. I hope it will not come to that, but if it does I will die knowing my death will be of some use for the Shâra and the welfare of my people, and hers.'","Bring the parchment you found to Glorfindel in Gadim-ûn"},
[2977]={"You picked up another parchment covered in a sorcerer's mad ravings.","'What evils have you brought to this place? Did your warrior-queen not intend to aid us? Instead you speak of ancient sorcerer-kings tampering with our very thoughts!'","Read the mad scratchings of the sorcerer of Ordâkh","Travel to the Crypts of Khâb Daku south-west of Gadim-ûn","You discover a parchment covered in rantings and ravings","Ulishár is at Gadim-ûn, and wishes to speak to you.","Glorfindel will want to see the writings of this sorcerer of Ordâkh as well. The Elf-lord waits for you in Gadim-ûn.","'This raises a question in my mind about the reach of the Thardúth. For these servants of vanished Morgoth to threaten the people of An Shêru in this way... they must have either travelled from Utug-bûr, as we did, or they awoke within a vault somewhere within Mûr Ghala, as Inkanûsh supposed. We must find out.\
\
'Something drove that sorcerer mad, and he was unable to resist as it clawed its way inside his mind. He would have been our enemy, there is no doubt, but none should perish as he did.'","Talk to Ulishár at Gadim-ûn","You heard the cries of hyenas and a scream to the east, near Spoiler's Crag.","'Before you returned and Glorfindel's words replaced his bombast with fear, Mashdagâl spoke of wights to the south-west. There we may find more information about the Thardúth, and if not we will at least combat the danger such creatures pose to the folk of An Shêru with their continued presence.'","The Dead walk at the Crypts of Khâb Daku, as they did at Naxar Dâl","Defeated wights or shades (${NUMBER}/6)","'Creatures prying into your mind, driving you mad? This is nonsense, surely?'\
\
Mashdagâl's eyes are wild, his fear evident.\
\
'What evils have you brought to this place? Did your warrior-queen not intend to aid us? Instead you speak of ancient sorcerer-kings tampering with our very thoughts!'","Defeat wights and shades at the Crypts of Khâb Daku (5/6)","Hurry east to Spoiler's Crag and find the source of the scream","Search the body of the slain sorcerer at Spoiler's Crag","It is your duty to face the wights at the Crypts of Khâb Daku, and wherever you find them.","A sorcerer of Ordâkh has fallen victim to the hyenas of Spoiler's Crag","Defeat wights and shades at the Crypts of Khâb Daku (${NUMBER}/6)","Talk to Mashdagâl at Gadim-ûn","The slain sorcerer at Spoiler's Crag may have something of interest on his person, as did the other you found.","'Something drove that sorcerer mad, and he was unable to resist as it clawed its way inside his mind. He would have been our enemy, there is no doubt, but none should perish as he did.'","'The ill fortune of these Ordâkhai sorcerers continues? They should never have come to the Height of the Sky!'\
\
Glorfindel studies the parchment you found.\
\
'I think our Wizard's supposition was correct, ${PLAYER}. There is another vault of the Thardúth, and it is located within An Shêru.'","Mashdagâl has become increasingly agitated by the talk in Gadim-ûn.","The Crypts of Khâb Daku are south-west of Gadim-ûn.","The ravings of a slain sorcerer of Ordâkh point to the presence of the Thardúth in An Shêru.","Chapter 16.2: Something Else Inside","'This is my understanding of Glorfindel's words: the Ordâkhai came here in search of something, and the Thardúth ensnared them. If the slain sorcerer you found was not alone, his allies may have perished nearby. They might also tell us what happened to them, as he did. Alive, if they be more fortunate than he.\
\
'Before you returned and Glorfindel's words replaced his bombast with fear, Mashdagâl spoke of wights to the south-west. There we may find more information about the Thardúth, and if not we will at least combat the danger such creatures pose to the folk of An Shêru with their continued presence.'","Bring the parchment you found to Glorfindel in Gadim-ûn","You hear the cries of hyenas to the east, followed by a piercing scream!"},
[2978]={"Glorfindel stands here.","Investigation completed: 'A Difficult Step'","Work with Glorfindel and complete 'The Madness at Damudûr'","Glorfindel believes that terrible evils slept within An Shêru, but they must now be awake. You must determine the dangers lurking within the Height of the Sky and aid your companions with their duties.","Your companions within Gadim-ûn have a number of investigations with which they need your help.","The Hamâti soldier Kishâtal in Gadim-ûn has something he wishes to say to you.","Talk to Rahâzi on the road toward Idagâl","'Did the tremors caused during the Din of Stone unseal the path to a second vault of Morgoth's servants? It seems likely to me, ${PLAYER}, and I believe one of the slain Ordâkhai has given us a name to this place: Damudûr.\
\
'We have some work to do. Once we have learned what we can in An Shêru we will travel westward, where the road leads to Idagâl.'","'If we all work together we can both carry out our duties and search An Shêru for the evils that threaten its people.'","Investigation completed: 'A Song of Shurug-nîn'","Work with Rahâzi and complete 'A Song of Shurug-nîn'","'Mashdagâl fled this place while you were away, but unless he leaves An Shêru entirely I fear he will not escape the reach of the Thardúth. Did the tremors caused during the Din of Stone unseal the path to a second vault of Morgoth's servants? It seems likely to me, ${PLAYER}, and I believe one of the slain Ordâkhai has given us a name to this place: Damudûr.\
\
'We have some work to do. Once we have learned what we can in An Shêru we will travel westward, where the road leads to Idagâl.'","Rahâzi is on the road toward Idagâl.","Talk to the Hamâti soldier Kishâtal in Gadim-ûn","'The Ordâkhai who control Emax Dûl are being manipulated by the Thardúth. I am certain of it.'","Meet with your companions on the road toward Idagâl","Work with Shenzâmin and complete 'Emissaries to Jiret-menêsh'","'Shenzâmin and I cannot let these terrors distract us from the mission given to us by Shâra Mizâdi. We will help you investigate An Shêru, but we must also carry out our own duties.'","'Ever since we departed Zajâna, I suspected our road would bring us to Emax Dûl in Idagâl. I did not expect the situation with which we are now threatened, that the Ordâkhai who control that city might be manipulated by the Thardúth.'","Investigation completed: 'Emissaries to Jiret-menêsh'","Talk to Glorfindel on the road toward Idagâl","Chapter 16.3: Investigations In An Shêru","Having aided your companions with their investigations, you should now meet them where the road leads toward Idagâl.","Work with Ulishár and complete 'A Difficult Step'","'Shenzâmin and Kishâtal have set out for Kighân to bring word back to Shâra Mizâdi. I will remain with you, ${PLAYER}, for I fought at the Sabûdamar, the red-rush battle, and I know the danger posed by the Thardúth.\
\
'For fallen Surdûsha and the honour of the Dumûri, I will fight alongside you against them!'","Glorfindel is on the road toward Idagâl.","Investigation completed: 'The Madness at Damudûr'"},
[2979]={"'Of our company, only Ulishár has walked into Idagâl. Will he tell us what to expect, and where first we should go?\
\
'Even mighty Shurug-nîn would hesitate to knock upon the gates of Emax Dûl, knowing the Ordâkhai and the Thardúth have joined hands within!'","Ulishár stands by the road into Idagâl.","'Emax Dûl has borne many names over the span of its history, each chosen by the power that controlled it: the Menûns of Nísaka, the Khôrthan League, and now the Ordâkhai.\
\
'But Rahâzi is right. We should not make directly for Emax Dûl. Instead let us pass into Idagâl and follow the road northward. There we will find a pleasant settlement beside a green oasis. It is called Ahâba, and the Beltáni herdsmen who dwell there showed me kindness while I wandered, a few years before I was imprisoned by the Ordâkhai. If Malgârzor lives there still, he may help us. I knew him not, but by his reputation he was a man of influence among those who live by the water.'","Defeated brigand \\qvultures\\q (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What says Ulishár about our course as we pass into Idagâl?'","Rahâzi is at Ahâba in Idagâl.","Defeated vultures (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Ordâkhai \\qvultures\\q (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Your next destination is the small village of Ahâba located by the oasis in Idagâl.","'Outsiders are often drawn to Ahâba by the oasis. It is the custom of my people to welcome any who desire water or food, if they come in peace and offer work in exchange for these gifts.\
\
'We have had difficulty with vultures of late. Should you do something about them, you will have the friendship of the people of Ahâba.'\
\
You ask Malgârzor to describe the vultures and tell you where you can find them, and he smiles broadly at you.\
\
'Some of these vultures fly upon wings, and are at the Fane of Shahûru. But others bear swords of Ordâkh, and these too are unwelcome; they reside at the Wither-watch. Still other vultures might once have called Ahâba their home, but now they live at Kidu-bâla and prey upon their former neighbours. I am pleased you understand me.'","Travel to the village of Ahâba by the oasis in Idagâl, and introduce yourself to Malgârzor","'We have had difficulty with vultures of late. Should you do something about them, you will have the friendship of the people of Ahâba.\
\
'Some of these vultures fly upon wings, and are at the Fane of Shahûru. But others bear swords of Ordâkh, and these too are unwelcome; they reside at the Wither-watch. Still other vultures might once have called Ahâba their home, but now they live at Kidu-bâla and prey upon their former neighbours. I am pleased you understand me.'","Defeat vultures at the Fane of Shahûru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Ulishár on the road into Idagâl","Talk to Malgârzor in Ahâba","Defeat brigand \\qvultures\\q at Kidu-bâla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Ordâkhai \\qvultures\\q at the Wither-watch (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The herdsman Malgârzor in Ahâba asked you to defeat \\qvultures\\q of different kinds.","'Rahâzi is right. We should not make directly for Emax Dûl. Instead let us pass into Idagâl and follow the road northward. There we will find a pleasant settlement beside a green oasis. It is called Ahâba, and the Beltáni herdsmen who dwell there showed me kindness while I wandered, a few years before I was imprisoned by the Ordâkhai. If Malgârzor lives there still, he may help us. I knew him not, but by his reputation he was a man of influence among those who live by the water.'","Your companions are prepared to advance further into the Ordâkhai-held territory of Idagâl.","'The Din of Stone that drained the lake of Idagâl occurred before even the eldest resident of Ahâba was born. The basin has stood empty for the longest lifetime among Malgârzor's people.\
\
'He tells me the bones of great beasts can be seen in the dry lake-bed. These must be the remains of the dragons slain by Shurug-nîn, so long ago!'","'I understand you dealt with both the vultures and the \\qvultures,\\q friend of Ahâba. I thank you for aiding my people in this way.\
\
'Your companion Rahâzi asked some questions while you were away, and I have answered her as best I may. Her knowledge of the old stories exceeds even my own, though her home be far away.'","Chapter 16.4: The Vultures Circle","Talk to Rahâzi at Ahâba","The oasis-village of Ahâba is green and pleasant","The herdsman Malgârzor in Ahâba eyes you cautiously.","The herdsman Malgârzor in Ahâba will be interested to hear that you dealt with the vultures, as well as the \\qvultures.\\q","'I have answered Rahâzi's questions as best I could. Her knowledge of the old stories exceeds even my own, though her home be far away.'"},
[2980]={"'I would see the bones of these dragons, ${PLAYER}. Will you accompany me to the centre of the lake, that we may see this evidence of Shurug-nîn's great triumph?'","'The Dawn-warden is a most impressive construction even when seen from afar, but more so when seen from below! I understand a similar statue stands to the north, in Khûd Zagin, but that one lies in ruin.\
\
'In his own language Malgârzor named this great statue \\qUzûr\\q and said many wayfarers and pilgrims travel great distances to see it. Perhaps you can speak with some of these travellers and learn what they can tell us of the Ordâkhai presence in Idagâl. They will likely not know anything concerning the Thardúth... but keep open your ears.'","'So many wayfarers come to this statue to appeal to the Menundâri for his return. They leave various keepsakes at the base of the statue as offerings for him, but I call it a futile endeavour! The Eternal Ruler will return at a time of his choosing, not of ours. Until that moment, all we can do is watch over his sacred sites.\
\
'At night I have heard a terrible wailing, as of an anguished wind, and in the morning assorted items have been taken from the base of Uzûr. I care not for the keepsakes that are taken, but sometimes stones go missing, and because they belong to Uzûr they are sacred.\
\
'I have never caught them doing it, but I suspect the scavenging beasts called kergrim are to blame for these thefts. If you retrieve these sacred stones from their dens to the north-east, you will prove yourself a friend to the people of this land, and to the memory of the Menundâri.'","Defeat kergrim at the Tombs of Khâb Ishil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Glorfindel stands here.","The Dawn-warden towers over the surrounding lands of Idagâl","'Malgârzor named this great statue \\qUzûr\\q and said many wayfarers and pilgrims travel great distances to see it. Perhaps you can speak with some of these travellers and learn what they can tell us of the Ordâkhai presence in Idagâl. They will likely not know anything concerning the Thardúth... but keep open your ears.'","Rahâzi stands here.","Rahâzi stares at the dragon-bones in awe","Bring the sacred stones to Kindrígi at the Dawn-warden","Talk to Bâlamar at the Dawn-warden","Kindrígi asked you to defeat the creatures at the Tombs of Khâb Ishil and recover the stones they stole from the site of the Dawn-warden.","Collected sacred stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Rahâzi by the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm","Kindrígi is waiting to hear news of your success, and to accept delivery of the sacred stones the kergrim stole from the Dawn-warden site.","'I dare not hope the Menundâri will return during my lifetime. Why has he not already come back to us? What more suffering could be required before he will take pity upon us? Has there not been war and bloodshed enough to merit his return?'","Travel to the feet of the Dawn-warden statue north-west of the Dry-whelm","'I believe Maethriel stood beside Shurug-nîn when she faced the dragons, ${PLAYER}, but she appears in no further tale; when Akhízi chased Shurug-nîn north to Urash Dâr, the Shagâni warrior fought alone.\
\
'Let us leave Rahâzi to contemplate the dragon bones in peace. I would take a closer look at the great statue that stands beyond the edge of the lake-bed to the west. Malgârzor named it the Dawn-warden, and it watches over this land from a great height.'","'Let us leave Rahâzi to contemplate the dragon bones in peace. I would take a closer look at the great statue that stands beyond the edge of the lake-bed to the west. Malgârzor named it the Dawn-warden, and it watches over this land from a great height.'","'I suspect the scavenging beasts called kergrim are to blame for these thefts. If you retrieve these sacred stones from their dens to the north-east, you will prove yourself a friend to the people of this land, and to the memory of the Menundâri.'","Talk to Glorfindel at the Dawn-warden","Glorfindel is in the Dry-whelm.","'Will you accompany me to the centre of the lake, that we may see this evidence of Shurug-nîn's great triumph?'","'It is one thing to hear the songs, ${PLAYER}, but to see such evidence of them so near! The dragons were so large, and yet Shurug-nîn faced them beside the lake of Idagâl, and with the sword Orotheg she brought them low.'\
\
Rahâzi falls silent. When she speaks again, her voice is a whisper.\
\
'Three were the children of Akhízi. Know now their names: Ahûshu, Nuzêru, and Rabûg. Now forget them, for only Shurug-nîn remains.'","Talk to Kindrígi at the Dawn-warden","Chapter 16.5: A Reminder of Ancient Days","A number of wayfarers have made pilgrimages to the Dawn-warden statue in Idagâl.","Collect sacred stones from the Tombs of Khâb Ishil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am pleased a stranger would help us in this way. I thank you for it.\
\
'When the Menundâri returns, he will look favourably upon you.'","Glorfindel is interested in seeing the Dawn-warden statue to the north-west of the Dry-whelm up close.","Rahâzi stares at the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm.","Rahâzi wants to examine the dragon-bones said to lie within the Dry-whelm, west of Ahâba.","Glorfindel is at the Dawn-warden statue in Idagâl.","'Have you come from afar to worship Uzûr, the great statue of Izighûz Menundâri, the Eternal Ruler? The time of his return is nearly at hand, when he will deliver Shagâna from its enemies!'","The lake-bed in the centre of Idagâl has borne witness to a great deal of history, some tragic and some triumphant.","Defeated kergrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Meet with Rahâzi by the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm, west of Ahâba","'Three were the children of Akhízi. Know now their names: Ahûshu, Nuzêru, and Rabûg. Now forget them, for only Shurug-nîn remains.'","Talk to Dimûzga at the Dawn-warden","Talk to Glorfindel by the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm"},
[2981]={"Satagêra is in north-east Ahâba.","'Ever since the Dagor Carlanthir was fought, I have believed the Thardúth must possess more hidden vaults than the one we discovered at Utug-bûr. After all, a fox might gain access to one hen-house, and if that is where you keep all of your hens, you will soon find yourself without eggs. The hobbits of the Shire with whom I am well-acquainted would not risk a breakfast without eggs, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'No, it seemed clear to me the Thardúth must possess more than one hidden vault. Like Utug-bûr, another vault would be concealed within the rocks, the better to protect the Thardúth until the enchantment that preserved them came to its end. And also like at Utug-bûr, this vault would not be accessible unless the face of the land was to be changed.\
\
'Shurash Hûl of Ordâkh knew nothing of the Thardúth, but the Din of Stone he caused would enable them to emerge when the time was right. I suspected the location of this second vault might be within An Shêru, but I see you have confirmed it for me.'","Talk to Ulishár in north-east Ahâba","'The sight of these dragon-bones will never leave my memory, ${PLAYER}. I am glad we could spare the time to see them.\
\
'I am ready to return to the oasis at Ahâba. When we have arrived at the central island within the oasis, we will plan our next course of action.'","'Comparing the records I found in the Kalmakhíla with the tales of the Kintai of Sul Madásh, I have come to a realization, ${PLAYER}. I believe the Din of Stone unleashed the fungal blight that now consumes Adagím.\
\
'Note my use of the word \\qunleashed,\\q rather than \\qcreated.\\q For I think the entity the Kintai name Sívigush, the Earth-terror, dwelt beneath Nisigím for untold ages of the world. It would have remained there forever, had not the Ordâkhai cracked the earth during the Din of Stone. It may be the fungal blight was fed by newly-flooded caverns beneath the Mûr, but of that I am less certain.'","'Thank you for indulging me in this detour, my friend. Let us return to the dry lake-bed and collect our companion who remained behind. I am certain Rahâzi will have appreciated the time she spent in contemplation, but now we must decide our next course.'","'We must make our plans, and make them well. For now, go to north-east Ahâba and ask Ulishár what he can tell us.'","'I have written more plays than I can count on ten fingers, ${PLAYER}, but this one is proving more difficult than those others.'\
\
Satagêra shakes her head with disgust.\
\
'The Ordâkhai have commissioned us to perform a new play that will inspire their people. They want it to be called \\qThe Great Triumph of Mordor and Ordâkh,\\q and it is intended to convey that their defeat in the war was actually a victory, and their greatest triumph is still to come!\
\
'Coin is coin, ${PLAYER}, and the performance of this play will keep Têrkar's Travellers fed and comfortable for many months... but these are all lies!'","Chapter 16.6: Making Connexions","Talk to Rahâzi by the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm","Listen to what Inkanûsh has discovered","'The ritual commanded by Shurash Hûl of Ordâkh damaged bastions along the entirety of Mûr Ghala, from Emax Dûl to the northern gate of Zajâna. Much of this damage was superficial, causing a spider's web of cracks to form along the outside of buildings and knocking items off of shelves.\
\
'It was worse for the Temámir. The Din of Stone collapsed mines up and down the entirety of the Ridge, and thousands of dwarves were lost. Jiret-menêsh survived, but its ruler sealed the fortress in the following years and took little notice of events in the wider world.\
\
'Agents of the Temámir that dared to leave Jiret-menêsh attained much influence elsewhere in Middle-earth. I wonder if Khôltekh would have become a Kinsman of the Kindred of the Coins in Umbar if the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh had played a larger role in the region in the years following the Din of Stone?'","Inkanûsh stands here.","'I told you we would see Têrkar's Travellers again!'","Talk to Glorfindel at the Dawn-warden","'In the year 2890 of the Third Age, Shurash Hûl of Ordâkh raged against the River Usâl, for it blocked the passage of his armies north. With the aid of agents of Mordor, his sorcerers devised and cast deadly spells that cracked the earth about the springs of the river. The rituals triggered great tremors in the foundation of Mûr Ghala, collapsing reservoirs beneath the surface and causing the Usâl to run dry.\
\
'The quakes continued for weeks, one after another, and the ensuing noise caused by the shifting of the rocks came to be known as the Din of Stone, which the Zajâni scholars I have read named Urash-zâl. I showed you some of these accounts, ${PLAYER}; there are others, which shed more detail upon the scope of the injury inflicted during the Din of Stone.\
\
'The Usâl was not the only geologic casualty of Ordâkh and Mordor's fell cooperation. The wells of the Usâl's sister-river, the Agâl, were partially-blocked, and the Idagâl lake emptied, becoming a ruin of cracked and broken mires. More than one hundred years after the Din of Stone, the lake has shown no sign of restoration. Where the water might have gone, I cannot say; perhaps great caverns beneath the surface are now flooded where once they were not. The sorcerers of Ordâkh have much for which to answer.'","Rahâzi is by the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm.","'Let us return to the dry lake-bed and collect our companion who remained behind. I am certain Rahâzi will have appreciated the time she spent in contemplation, but now we must decide our next course.'","Ulishár stands here.","Inkanûsh is at the village of Ahâba.","Talk to Satagêra in north-east Ahâba","Return to the village of Ahâba in Idagâl, and meet your companions on the central island of the oasis","'Because you have aided me on this day, I will give you some advice, stranger. The fighting strength of Ordâkh is greatly diminished following Barkhûsh's war... but it is not eliminated. He would have wisdom who avoids Emax Dûl, the last great redoubt of Ordâkh in the Mûr. They say the Hûl died upon a distant field during the war, but no empire can last without its leader. A new Hûl will come to power in Ordâkh. The surest sign of our fortunes changing would be for the Menundâri to return to us first!\
\
'Go in peace, and remember: the Ordâkhai remain a danger in the Mûr, despite their defeat in the north.'","'I told you we would see Têrkar's Travellers again!\
\
'They have been employed to perform a new play for the Ordâkhai, but Satagêra has been having some trouble finishing it to her satisfaction.'","Inkanûsh suggested you join your companions at north-east Ahâba.","The situation in Idagâl merits further investigation, particularly the relationship between the Ordâkhai of Emax Dûl and the Thardúth of Damudûr.","Inkanûsh waits at the village of Ahâba, eager to tell you what he has discovered.","Rejoin your companions in north-east Ahâba","'I trust you were not sight-seeing, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You explain that you were gathering information about the Ordâkhai presence in Idagâl and their relationship with the newly-awoken Thardúth of Damudûr, and the Wizard chuckles.\
\
'My chiding was unserious, my friend; but I see you have already learned some of what I came to tell you! It was with haste that I joined Têrkar's Travellers after I finished my investigation in the Kalmakhíla. Their road aligned with mine, for their next engagement is within the walls of Emax Dûl itself, and I knew your search would bring you near to that city.\
\
'Listen now to what I have learned! I have made some connexions between subjects about which we knew little, and now I know a great deal!'","Ulishár is in north-east Ahâba.","Glorfindel is at the Dawn-warden in Idagâl.","A familiar face wears a familiar expression: kindness tempered by impatience","Inkanûsh has come to Ahâba.","Talk to Inkanûsh at Ahâba","'After the defeat of Sauron during the War of the Ring, the Thardúth tested the will of any who strayed too near their vault in Damudûr. Did they compel the soldiers and sorcerers of Ordâkh to seek them out, to finish what the Din of Stone had begun, clearing the blocked way into Damudûr? I feel certain they did, ${PLAYER}, but some to whom they spoke may have resisted. The pryings of the Thardúth are ungentle; an unprepared mind could not withstand such invasion, and with resistance would be broken.\
\
'But we have an advantage, my friend. The Thardúth slumbered within their vaults for thousands of years, and during that time these servants of Morgoth possessed no knowledge of the outside world. They emerged from their hidden vaults like children, children who know nothing of present days and who must be taught. The Thardúth have chosen the Ordâkhai to teach them, and while the Empire of Ordâkh remains a danger to us, it still reels from Sauron's defeat during the War of the Ring.\
\
'If the Thardúth are to learn the state of things from their Ordâkhai teachers, their classroom is sure to be within the fortress of Emax Dûl. You will need to find a way inside, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'For now, go to north-east Ahâba and ask Ulishár what he can tell us.'","Your companions agreed to meet back at the village of Ahâba in Idagâl, on the central island in the oasis.","'I am ready to return to the oasis at Ahâba. When we have arrived at the central island in the oasis, we will plan our next course of action.'","'Go in peace, and remember: the Ordâkhai remain a danger in the Mûr, despite their defeat in the north.'"},
[2982]={"Satagêra is in north-east Ahâba.","Satagêra gave you another part of the script she has written.","Talk to Ulishár in north-east Ahâba","'We have performed plays for the Ordâkhai before. Their coins spend just as well as any others... perhaps better!'","Imalêkh is in north-east Ahâba.","'I fought on the field before the great city in the north. The nobles of Ordâkh who commissioned this play would not pay for a true account of what befell their soldiers there.\
\
'But Jêsamin is right about this. Even an untrue play may accomplish some good. Had Satagêra not written \\qBite of the Black Serpent,\\q we would not have met Ulishár, and Têrkar would not have asked us to spirit him to freedom.'","'I know these for lies because my friends were there, ${PLAYER}, and they have told me how it was. What the Ordâkhai have asked me to write is nothing near the truth. This has never been a problem for me before now! Think you my plays were always true? It is not so!'\
\
Satagêra sighs heavily.\
\
'I say I cannot understand, but that is also a falsehood. I know why I struggle so with this one. It is because my husband Têrkar died in service of their war, as did so many of my friends; those that returned were not the same. I wish you could have known Mashkânu before he fought in the north. He speaks not of it to any of us, but whatever he saw changed him. Only rarely now does he laugh, when before he was always merry.\
\
'For me to write the Ordâkhai's words feels like a betrayal. Here! See for yourself!'","Chapter 16.7: The Lies","Read the script Satagêra gave to you","'Read the portion I gave to you and see for yourself!'","'My companions are as supportive as ever, but by itself that puts no words on the page! I will keep at it.\
\
'I fear \\qThe Great Triumph of Mordor and Ordâkh\\q will not live up to my other works, ${PLAYER}. Let us hope the nobles who commissioned it believe otherwise!'","'The only true word on that parchment is \\qdespairing,\\q ${PLAYER}. Many were the lies that sent my friends marching north to Barkhûsh's war, and now I add another: that victory is near at hand, despite the grave defeats I know were suffered.\
\
'Here, see another portion of my script.'","Talk to Satagêra in north-east Ahâba","Satagêra gave you part of the script she has already written.","Talk to Imalêkh in north-east Ahâba","Satagêra has some thoughts about the play she has been tasked with writing.","Read another part of the script Satagêra gave to you","'I fear \\qThe Great Triumph of Mordor and Ordâkh\\q will not live up to my other works, ${PLAYER}. Let us hope the nobles who commissioned it believe otherwise!'","You have read portions of Satagêra's script and should return them to her.","Ulishár is in north-east Ahâba.","Jêsamin is in north-east Ahâba.","Return the pages she gave you to Satagêra in north-east Ahâba","'It cannot be that bad, can it?\
\
'We have performed plays for the Ordâkhai before. Their coins spend just as well as any others... perhaps better!\
\
'If we had not performed \\qBite of the Black Serpent\\q in Emax Dûl we would not have met Ulishár, and he might still be imprisoned there, or slain!'","Talk to Jêsamin in north-east Ahâba","'But Jêsamin is right about this. Even an untrue play may accomplish some good. Had Satagêra not written \\qBite of the Black Serpent,\\q we would not have met Ulishár, and Têrkar would not have asked us to spirit him to freedom.'","'It has been nice to catch up with Têrkar's Travellers, but we should no longer delay our work.'"},
[2983]={"Talk to Ulishár in north-east Ahâba","Glorfindel has also come to scout the defences of Emax Dûl.","Scout the approach to the main entrance to Emax Dûl","'The guards of the city seem much more vigilant now than before.'","'We need to scout the approach to Emax Dûl and learn if there is a way past the sentries. Perhaps there is an unguarded location to the left or right of the main entrance that will allow you to scale one of the walls?'","With regret, Ulishár has bid farewell to Têrkar's Travellers so you can continue your urgent errand: scouting the approaches to the Ordâkhai-held Emax Dûl.","'After you have played your part, you can then sneak away to search the keep. Once you find whatever it is Inkanûsh seeks within those walls, you can return to us and we will all leave together!'","'We may need to fight our way inside. Let us return to Inkanûsh and tell him what we have learned.'","Glorfindel quietly arrives as you survey the approach to Emax Dûl","Chapter 16.8: A Guarded City","Jêsamin claps her hands together","The approach to the main entrance of Emax Dûl must be scouted for some weakness in the defences.","'The city is guarded, and I see little chance of sneaking in past the sentries.\
\
'We may need to fight our way inside. Let us return to Inkanûsh and tell him what we have learned.'","Talk to Zimêlkha in north-east Ahâba","'We were able to sneak Ulishár out of the city... why not do the same, but in the other direction?'","'It is not enough. ${PLAYER} does not know the interior of the keep.' \
\
Ulishár takes a deep breath before he continues, and when he speaks his voice is low and quiet.\
\
'Someone must accompany you who knows the layout of the keep, someone who has been there before. I need to go with you. Otherwise you will not be able to search the keep before the performance ends.'","Glorfindel fears that fighting your way in to Emax Dûl may be the only option available to you, but Inkanûsh in north-east Ahâba will not like that answer.","'Glorfindel suggests that you fight your way in to Emax Dûl? Has he taken leave of his senses? Such an attack will raise the alarm through the entire city, and we will learn the plans of neither Thardúth nor Ordâkhai!\
\
'Always an Elf-lord suggests the direct approach. It will not serve us here!'","Talk to Inkanûsh in north-east Ahâba","Study the main entrance of Emax Dûl from the low wall atop the hill","Emax Dûl looms high above the cliffside","The approach to Emax Dûl must be scouted for some weakness in the defences.","Talk to Glorfindel outside Emax Dûl","'I have it!'\
\
Jêsamin quivers with excitement.\
\
'If our friend has a part to play in the performance, the guards will have to let ${PLAYER} in!'\
\
Jêsamin beams at you excitedly.\
\
'After you have played your part, you can then sneak away to search the keep. Once you find whatever it is Inkanûsh seeks within those walls, you can return to us and we will all leave together!'","Scout the approach to Emax Dûl above the cliffside","Talk to Mashkânu in north-east Ahâba","Mashkânu in north-east Ahâba has an idea.","Mashkânu looks around at his companions before meeting the eyes of the Wizard that once frightened him so.\
\
'I have had an idea, Inkanûsh.\
\
'What if we sneak ${PLAYER} into the city the same way we snuck out Ulishár? When we go to perform Satagêra's new play, ${PLAYER} could be hidden among the costumes, beneath a hooded cloak.'","Study the defences of Emax Dûl from the low wall by the cliffside","Ulishár is in north-east Ahâba.","Zimêlkha is in north-east Ahâba.","'The direct approach will not serve us here!'","The main entrance to Emax Dûl appears heavily-guarded","Jêsamin in north-east Ahâba knows what needs to be done.","'That will not work this time, Mashkânu. The guards of the city seem much more vigilant now than before. They will search our things, and if ${PLAYER} is hidden among them, our secret passenger will be discovered.'","Talk to Jêsamin in north-east Ahâba","It will be difficult, if not impossible, to enter Emax Dûl from this side","Mashkânu clears his throat, drawing your attention"},
[2984]={"'Satagêra wanted me to give you some advice about performing before an audience? Such a thing is difficult to learn in a single lesson! You must demonstrate confidence, ${PLAYER}. An audience can tell if you believe what you are showing to them.'\
\
Mashkânu laughs humourlessly.\
\
'With this particular play that may be difficult for all of us. The lords and ladies of Emax Dûl want us to convince their people that the victory of Ordâkh is near at hand... but any of us who were there know otherwise. Some of us may still be there, lost in the north, like Urûnam or my beloved Khazín! And others of my friends are known to be slain, cut down in the forest like Têrkar, or trampled before the great city like Zurûsh.\
\
'Had we not a purpose to accomplish here, I might have taken advantage of this moment to slay at least one of these lords of Emax Dûl, ${PLAYER}. For months I blamed the Wizard \\qMithrandir,\\q who is Inkanûsh, for the death of my friends and my family... but it was Ordâkh and Barkhûsh who sent us to that war. Barkhûsh is gone, but Ordâkh remains. If you can learn something that will hurt them, I will not rue the staying of my hand.'","Satagêra is in north-east Ahâba.","You have only known Têrkar's Travellers for a short time, but you are reasonably certain they would want you to <rgb=#00FF00>point</rgb> at the largest of the mûmakil.","'This is why I have come with you, my friend. I knew it not when we departed Sul Madásh, but I know it now. This certainty gives me the courage to return to that place. Worry not for me.\
\
'I will be fine, and you will learn whatever it is that Inkanûsh believes Ordâkh is hiding within the keep.'","Find Inkanûsh in south-east Ahâba","Satagêra is in north-east Ahâba, waiting for your response to her script.","'I have been remembering the time of my captivity, ${PLAYER}. For two years I laboured in the mines, but as my health worsened the overseers came to realize I could not survive much longer beneath the earth. In the early days they delighted to send a Kinta belowground, but as my speed suffered they decided my slow toil was not worth the jest. They sent me to Emax Dûl to serve the nobles who dwelt there, lords and ladies unaccustomed to wielding weapons; there was no call for them to march north with the Hûl when the Black Serpent departed for the war Barkhûsh commanded.\
\
'The work was lighter than in the mines, but my health remained poor, and the punishments I endured were just as severe. Had I not encountered Têrkar that night, I am certain I would have died within the keep of Emax Dûl.\
\
'And now I return. If we learn something to undermine the plans of Ordâkh and the Thardúth who slew my brother, it will be worth it. This will truly be Satagêra's masterpiece, ${PLAYER}.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Point</rgb> at the mûmak you want from the Scardelve","'What do you want? Speak quickly or I will summon the guards.'\
\
You hand Shâdugan Gânda the pass and he breaks the wax seal upon it. Sweat breaks out upon his brow as he reads the contents. At last he looks up, a relieved smile upon his face.\
\
'I saw many of these notices at the start of the year, stranger. So many of my mûmakil were outfit with harness and armour and sent north to the war. Only the smallest were deemed unfit for battle; they were left behind to haul stone and timber. I am glad the mûmak you seek will not be asked to fight!\
\
'<rgb=#00FF00>Point</rgb> out which of my creatures you would like to join these travelling players for their performance before the Lords of Emax Dûl.'","Satagêra hands you some fresh pages of her script","'We need a mûmak. Don't ask.'\
\
You tell Atâlsi that Satagêra has requested you help her attain the things that will be needed for the performance, and the playwright is hoping for as large a spectacle as possible.\
\
'I admit I am not surprised. It is most easy for Satagêra to write these things into her plays, but who must then arrange for them to be found? Atâlsi and Mashkânu, most of the time!\
\
'I have already attained a pass from the Ordâkhai allowing us to use one of their mûmakil for our purpose. I will give you the pass and you can show it to Shâdugan Gânda, the mûmak-keeper. Find him at the Scardelve, south of Ahâba. I would have selected a small one, but knowing Satagêra she will want the biggest we can get!'","Return the script to Satagêra in north-east Ahâba","Talk to Inkanûsh in south-east Ahâba","Talk to Shâdugan Gânda at the Scardelve","'I will see what I can do. You have chosen one of the more obstinate creatures of this herd!\
\
'But your travelling players will have a mûmak when they need one. I hope their performance will show to the Lords of Emax Dûl the value of raising mûmakil even in time of peace, and the quality of their minders!'","Inkanûsh stands here.","'The interior of the keep of Emax Dûl is a confusing maze of stairs and hallways, but I have not forgotten its layout. How could those passages leave my memory? During the years of my captivity I would be punished if the food I brought from the kitchen to the chambers of the lords and ladies grew cold while finding my way. I can navigate the maze for you, and bring you directly to the inner sanctum of whoever now rules in Emax Dûl.\
\
'This is why I have come with you, my friend. I knew it not when we departed Sul Madásh, but I know it now. This certainty gives me the courage to return to that place. Worry not for me, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I will be fine, and you will learn whatever it is that Inkanûsh believes Ordâkh is hiding within the keep.'","'The writing goes slowly, but I have incorporated both you and Ulishár into an early scene. After the two of you have been seen by the audience, it will then be your task to slip away and search the keep while we hold their attention upon us. The mûmak I asked Atâlsi to get for us should prove useful!\
\
'Here, ${PLAYER}. Your part is labelled \\qHero of Gondor,\\q and Ulishár will be \\qNorthern Elf.\\q Read this portion of the script and commit it to your memory. I have already shown it to Ulishár. He insists he will have no trouble with his own part, and yours should be easy enough. The difficult task will begin after the two of you slip away, of course.'","Inkanûsh stands in south-east Ahâba, deep in thought","'The Hûl of Ordâkh and his sons fell during the War of the Ring, but no empire can remain leaderless. If a new Hûl has come to power in the south, he or she may have much to fear from these newly-awakened creatures of evil. They served Morgoth. They will serve no other, and certainly not a Hûl of Ordâkh.\
\
'This is the sort of thing I need you and Ulishár to learn.'","Têrkar's Travellers are willing to help you gain access to the inner keep of the guarded city of Emax Dûl, but the plan is not without its dangers.","No... not big enough!","Talk to Satagêra in north-east Ahâba","They said big, but that one is TOO big, and equipped for war!","Inkanûsh has gone to south-east Ahâba to think about the plan.","Read the new portion of the script Satagêra gave to you","Talk to Mashkânu in south-east Ahâba","'It will take me some time to revise the play to include you and Ulishár, ${PLAYER}. If I can do this in such a short time perhaps this will be my greatest masterpiece, after all... despite the lies of Ordâkh contained within!\
\
'I jest, but as we travelled from Zajâna with Inkanûsh he spoke of the terrible ancient creatures he opposes. If your mission proves instrumental in defeating these villains, these Thardúth, the play I now write must be considered my masterpiece, in truth! For it also to undermine the goals of those who sent my husband and my friends to their deaths in war... I admit that sweetens the sweet-cake.\
\
'While I work to include you and Ulishár in the play, you can help me by aiding Atâlsi. She is arranging some of the things we will need for the play. I already intended it to be full of spectacle, but now it is doubly-important the attention of the Ordâkhai be held while you and the Kinta slip away. If Atâlsi proves stubborn, tell her that your life and Ulishár's life might depend upon the size of the creature....'","'If Atâlsi proves stubborn, tell her that your life and Ulishár's life might depend upon the size of the creature....'","Atâlsi hands you a pass with a wax seal to give the mûmak-keeper","Shâdugan Gânda gives you a grim smile","'Your travelling players will have a mûmak when they need one. I hope their performance will show to the Lords of Emax Dûl the value of raising mûmakil even in time of peace, and the quality of their minders!'","Inkanûsh stands in south-east Ahâba, deep in thought.","Bring the pass to Shâdugan Gânda, the keeper of the mûmakil, at the Scardelve","Talk to Ulishár in south-east Ahâba","Mashkânu crosses his arms.\
\
'The nobles who reside within Emax Dûl know the play they have asked Satagêra to write is full of falsehoods, just as we do. Which of us will first admit it? That is the game, ${PLAYER}.'","Ulishár is in south-east Ahâba.","'I am glad the mûmak you seek will not be asked to fight! <rgb=#00FF00>Point</rgb> out which of my creatures you would like to join these travelling players for their performance before the Lords of Emax Dûl.'","Talk to Atâlsi outside the western entrance to Ahâba","'Read the portion of the script I gave to you and commit it to your memory. I have already shown it to Ulishár. He insists he will have no trouble with his own part, and yours should be easy enough. The difficult task will begin after the two of you slip away, of course.'","'Yes, I am worried. This plan will get you inside the keep of Emax Dûl, but its true success depends upon something else: whether the attention of the Ordâkhai and of the Thardúth are sufficiently held by the performance. You and Ulishár need time to search the inner sanctum for the plans of the Thardúth and the Ordâkhai.\
\
'But secrecy is our ally, ${PLAYER}, and lends us the advantage. The Thardúth that departed Damudûr and accompanied the Ordâkhai to Emax Dûl will expect no such intrusion. Glorfindel and I cannot join you, for our presence would risk drawing their attention. If they remain unalerted, I believe we can learn where next the Thardúth intend to send their Utûgi. I suspect they will desire to destroy Gondor and the kingdoms of the north... but there is another possibility.\
\
'The Hûl of Ordâkh and his sons fell during the War of the Ring, but no empire can remain leaderless. If a new Hûl has come to power in the south, he or she may have much to fear from these newly-awakened creatures of evil. They served Morgoth. They will serve no other, and certainly not a Hûl of Ordâkh.\
\
'This is the sort of thing I need you and Ulishár to learn.'","'I gave you the pass already. Show it to Shâdugan Gânda, the mûmak-keeper at the Scardelve, south of Ahâba.'","Shâdugan Gânda, the keeper of the mûmakil, is at the Scardelve, south of Ahâba.","Satagêra has given you some fresh pages of her script to read.","Atâlsi is outside the western entrance of Ahâba.","Mashkânu is in south-east Ahâba.","Chapter 16.9: Satagêra's Masterpiece","'I hope you suffer not from the fright of being on stage, ${PLAYER}. I understand you have faced some terrible foes and engaged in many a difficult battle... but the act of performing before an audience can be daunting in its own right. Mashkânu may give you some advice; he has done both.\
\
'But that reminds me. Inkanûsh wanted to speak to you before the performance. I last saw him to the south-east.'","'Inkanûsh wanted to speak to you before the performance. I last saw him in south-east Ahâba.'"},
[2985]={"Habla con Ningloril en Thangúlhad","'Vinimos aquí para liberar al enano Bori de su cautiverio, y aún no lo hemos hecho. Ahora que hemos luchado más allá de los muros de Dol Guldur, ¿qué puede detener a la Hueste Dorada de hacer lo que la Guardia Oculta se propuso hacer?\
\
'Nos infiltraremos en las mazmorras después del anochecer con una pequeña fuerza de Elfos y rescatamos a Bori. Habla conmigo cuando puedas partir.'","Habla con Ningloril e infiltrate en las mazmorras de Dol Guldur","'La torre Nothgar está aquí en Thangúlhad. Bori está dentro, esperando para agradecerte por su rescate.'","Bori está dentro de Nothgar, la torre central de Thangúlhad.\
\
Bori te espera para agradecerte por su rescate.","'${PLAYER}, no puedo agradecerte lo suficiente; pensé que te había visto por última vez en Zabadgathol, en las profundidades de Moria. Ser rescatado así... no tengo palabras para decírtelo.\
\
'¡Pero no basta con ser libre, mientras el Enemigo aún posee Zigilburk por mi culpa! Debemos recuperar el hacha de mithril antes de que pueda ser usada para algún gran mal, ¡y debemos ver a Gorothúl derrotado!'","Capítulo 16: Las Mazmorras de Dol Guldur","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, el campamento de la Hueste Dorada en Gathbúrz.\
\
Has rescatado a Bori de las mazmorras de Dol Guldur y ahora deberías hablar con Ningloril, quien organizó el esfuerzo de rescate.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para embarcarte en la misión de rescatar a Bori de las mazmorras de Dol Guldur?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no se puede completar con una Comunidad.</rgb>","Habla con Bori en Nothgar, en Thangúlhad","'Después de tanta pérdida de vidas, por fin hemos logrado lo que la Guardia Oculta se propuso hacer, ${PLAYER}. El enano Bori está libre de las mazmorras de Dol Guldur. La única tarea que queda ahora es que la Hueste Dorada asedie la fortaleza durante el mayor tiempo posible para proporcionar la distracción que el señor Celeborn deseaba.\
\
'Bori está dentro de Nothgar, la torre central de Thangúlhad. Desea agradecerte por su rescate.'","En las profundidades de las mazmorras de Dol Guldur, Bori sigue cautivo en una celda de prisión. Es hora de liberarlo.","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, el campamento de la Hueste Dorada en Gathbúrz.\
\
Ningloril te espera para viajar contigo a las mazmorras de Dol Guldur y rescatar a Bori de su cautiverio."},
[2986]={"The Temámir Habâti has set up a shop for the Ordâkhai in the central tent of Khomar Bóha.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FFFF00>MEDIUM</rgb>.","You should walk calmly out of Khomar Bóha without arousing further suspicion.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>.","'If you cause no trouble, no trouble will come to you. That is something the Orcs could stand to learn, and the Corsairs would do well to remember!'","A map just to the north seems promising.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FFFF00>MEDIUM</rgb>.","'None saw us arrive, ${PLAYER}. Might we use this to our advantage?\
\
'I doubt not that the bounds of this land are watched by sharp-eyed guards, but the Temámir who drove this waggon is known to them. He has carried us, all unknowing, to a place where it must be assumed every person belongs.\
\
'I hear the sounds of an encampment to the north-west. What if we simply walk among these people and see what we might learn of their purpose here, and how near this secret fleet may be to completion?'","'What do you think you're doing? You should not be lingering in this place!\
\
'Habâti the Dwarf has just arrived, but instead of going to see him you insist upon poking into places where you do not belong? What were you looking at just now?'\
\
You tell Jóla that you were just about to go see Habâti, but you were worrying that you would not be able to afford his unreasonable prices. She stares at you suspiciously.\
\
'Go on, then. Into the main tent with you.'","'Hmmm... are you certain we have not met?'","The Ordâkhai camp of Khomar Bóha is to the north-west of the waggon in which you arrived.","You should walk calmly out of Khomar Bóha without arousing further suspicion","The soldiers at Khomar Bóha do not seem suspicious of you... yet","You have no choice but to go inside the central tent of Khomar Bóha","Rahâzi is outside the Ordâkhai camp of Khomar Bóha.","'The Temámir has set up his wares inside the main tent! Hurry now, or you will miss him.\
\
'Delay will not lower his prices for you, or for anyone. Go on, then.'","You should see what is being stored in the amphorae located on the eastern side of Khomar Bóha.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>.","Walk calmly out of Khomar Bóha and arouse no further suspicion\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>","Even as you commit the map to memory, a woman calls out to you!","Talk to Rahâzi outside the Ordâkhai camp of Khomar Bóha","Report to the vendor inside the central tent of Khomar Bóha\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FF0000>HIGH</rgb>","'How fared you within the enemy encampment, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You describe to Rahâzi the map you memorized, and she nods agreeably, assigning names to locations in her head.\
\
'I too have learned some things that may be of use to us. The Ordâkhai are not alone in Sûg Nidar, and they are not happy about it.'","Examine the amphorae to the east\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>","Onúkho is in the centre of Khomar Bóha.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>.","Capítulo 17.1: Extraños Desde Lejos","Jóla has caught you examining the map of Sûg Nidar, and she demands to hear your explanation!\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FF0000>HIGH</rgb>.","'Carefully approach the camp to the north-west and we will test this supposition of mine.\
\
'They will have no reason to be suspicious of us, unless we give them one.'","Talk to Onúkho in Khomar Bóha\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>","'Hoy, stranger! You must be new here. All glory to the Hûl!'\
\
You repeat the sentiment, and Onúkho nods pleasantly.\
\
'It warms my heart to hear it! The Orcs claim to share our purpose here, but I do not believe it. If they thought Mordor had the advantage they would turn on us in the span of a breath! And the Corsairs down at Bâkhridar and at Starkhaven mumble their oaths, but they resent the Hûl, I am sure of it. I wish Ordâkh had no need of either, but this great work began before I was even born, and I was not consulted! It has taken great cost in lives to build the Song of Waves and Wind, and now we wait only for the signal to sail!\
\
'You are fortunate to join us today, stranger. Habâti the Dwarf has just arrived, and he brings goods and provisions from far away. He comes back every few weeks and sets up shop. His arrival is always welcome... it helps to break up the monotony of our days, which are spent mostly in waiting. His prices could be lower, though, I admit it.'","'Do I know you, stranger? You look familiar to me for some reason.'\
\
You assure Habâti that you and he have never met, but before he can respond the Ordâkhai erupt in a chorus of complaints.\
\
'There is a line,' Habâti says, and you step back before you draw any further attention to yourself.","Travel north-west to the camp of Khomar Bóha","Talk to Jóla and explain yourself\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FF0000>HIGH</rgb>","Examine the nearby map of Sûg Nidar\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FFFF00>MEDIUM</rgb>","You and Rahâzi have arrived at Sûg Nidar, the Fearwater, and must now learn of some way to prevent the Song of Waves and Wind from setting sail.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>","A line has formed inside the central tent","The amphorae contain fresh, easily-transportable water for the use of the Ordâkhai","Talk to Habâti in the central tent of Khomar Bóha\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FFFF00>MEDIUM</rgb>","You have no choice but to go inside the central tent of Khomar Bóha.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FF0000>HIGH</rgb>."},
[2987]={"Rahâzi stands alongside an unexpected friend near the outer palisade of Drushkála.","Corudan stands outside the Orc-encampment of Drushkála, a good distance from where last you saw him.","Having slain many Orcs at Drushkála, you should return to the entrance of the Orc-encampment and see if you have drawn the attention of your potential ally.","Capítulo 17.2: No Estás Solo","Defeat Orcs at Drushkála (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We should get closer to the Orc encampment. But be cautious, and remain alert for anything out of the ordinary!'","'We should get a closer look at this encampment of Orcs to the east.'","You and Rahâzi have learned that the various groups working to complete the Song of Waves and Wind are not as unified as they might be.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>","Talk to Corudan near the entrance to Drushkála","'I did not expect to see you here, my friend, but it is a welcome surprise! We must each share the paths we have trod to arrive in this place, but quickly, for the days are dangerous and time is short! I believe the Kindred of the Coins has allied with Orcs of Mordor and the Empire of Ordâkh to construct this fleet of warships.\
\
'Using this fleet, the Song of Waves and Wind, its masters might threaten all of Middle-earth!'","Rahâzi asked you to descend the slope and approach the Orc-encampment of Drushkála, remaining alert for anything out of the ordinary.","'So many ships, and they all ready for war! You told me what you learned in Emax Dûl, that the fleet has been in construction for so many years... but it is different entire to see the evidence with my own eyes!\
\
'Let us descend the slope toward Drushkála. Go carefully! Remain alert for anything out of the ordinary.'","What slew this Orc so near to the entrance of Drushkála?","'Look who I found: an unexpected friend!\
\
'Corudan tells me that his sister Sigileth and Cúridwan the Golden Maiden are elsewhere in Sûg Nidar; the three of them followed troubling signs to this place, but now that they have laid eyes upon the Song of Waves and Wind, they intend to counter it, if such a thing is possible. Together we will do this!'","'Look who I found: an unexpected friend! Corudan, his sister Sigileth, and Cúridwan the Golden Maiden are elsewhere in Sûg Nidar. Now that they have laid eyes upon the Song of Waves and Wind, they intend to counter it, if such a thing is possible. Together we will do this!'","An Orc lies dead a short distance from the outer palisade of Drushkála","Rahâzi has suggested that you travel east toward the Orc-encampment of Drushkála so that you might learn more.","Rahâzi stands alongside a familiar figure","'Look there!'","Rahâzi stands west of the Orc-encampment of Drushkála and stares at the ships of the Song moored off the shore.","'Look who I found!'","This Orc was slain by an Elf-arrow. Might you have allies hereabout?","Return to the entrance of Drushkála and look for your potential ally","Approach Drushkála and remain alert for anything out of the ordinary","Talk to Rahâzi west of Drushkála","You should slay Orcs at their encampment of Drushkála and look for signs of your potential ally.","Rahâzi slows to a halt and stares out at the ships of the Song","Talk to Rahâzi near the entrance to Drushkála","'By listening to the conversation of the Ordâkhai, I have learned something of their associates in the Fearwater. Orcs have established an encampment to the east of here at Drushkála, a fort that was drowned when the lake of Sûg Nidar was formed. During the reign of Barkhûsh, the Orcs and the Ordâkhai were made to work together; now that he is gone, the two groups find it more difficult to coexist, and there has been fighting between the two.\
\
'The map you saw contained markings on the other side of the river for a place called the Haven of Bâkhridar, which seems to be a Corsair encampment. The Ordâkhai need crews to sail the ships, but I am not certain how they convinced these sailors; there is little love between Umbar and Ordâkh these days. Beyond Bâkhridar, the wharfs and jetties of Starkhaven must serve as the primary shipbuilding location for the Song.\
\
'Let us first travel eastward toward Drushkála. After we have seen the Orcs, we will turn our attention to the other side of the river.'","Travel east in the direction of the Orc-encampment of Drushkála","Defeated Orcs at Drushkála (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Search the Orc for some sign of what killed him"},
[2988]={"'Search the crates within the Heirsworn camp and we may learn how prepared they are to sail. I will meet you on the other side of the camp!'","<rgb=#00FF00>When you accept this quest, you will travel with Corudan to the opposite shore.</rgb>\
\
'My sister and I departed Sul Madásh after you left with Inkanûsh and Glorfindel, making once again for Utug-bûr. Sigileth believed we could put the spirit of Silirtas to rest, but alas we found no sign of her. What we found instead set our course: waggon-tracks, ${PLAYER}, waggon-tracks sunk deep into the rocky ground from the weight of the goods they carried. The tracks travelled from west to east, and when I convinced my sister that we must learn from where they came, my deepest fears were realized. The guards at Ashâgir were slain, and the stockpile of Narghâk contained within was gone. Few only knew of the dangerous substance held within Ashâgir, and only one might command such waggons to transport it away. They were waggons of Temámir design, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Nakási Wave-reaper has taken command of this fleet, and Khôltekh has supplied it with Narghâk, the Hungry Fire. We may not yet know their full purpose... but I can make some guesses. That is the bad news! There are good tidings as well: Sigileth and I encountered Cúridwan as we followed the road towards Sûg Nidar, and with her aid we were able to slip past the border-guards. Let us walk to the other side of the river and we will speak more about what we have learned.'","Talk to Rahâzi south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar","Corudan asked you to search supply crates within the Haven of Bâkhridar and then meet him and Rahâzi on the other side.","This crate is packed with stoppered glass jars, currently empty","Corudan and Sigileth have come to the Fearwater, bolstering your ability to destroy the Song of Waves and Wind.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>","You have travelled with Corudan to the opposite shore, very near to the Haven of Bâkhridar, an encampment of Heirsworn within Sûg Nidar.","'And so the three of us came to the Fearwater, where we have worked to sow dissent among the groups that labour to finish the fleet. As a result, each group is now alert to anything suspicious... I am afraid you will not be able to walk among them without combat any longer, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'I have seen Balakhâd, the son of Balakhôr, from afar; he seems to command the Corsairs of this place. I know not where Nakási may be found, but my sister believes she might have established a command post on the island to the south-east. If Khôltekh is with her, he has remained out of sight. It is also possible he remains in Umbar, and arranged for the delivery of the Narghâk only through his agents.\
\
'We have arrived outside the Haven of Bâkhridar, which seems to be an encampment of Corsairs loyal to the Heirs of Castamir who have now sworn to follow Balakhâd. Let us search the camp and see how well-supplied the Corsairs are, and if they are ready to sail. Then we will meet up on the other side of the Heirsworn camp.'","This crate contains wrapped portions of ship's biscuit","'These Corsairs are ready to sail for war, if it is commanded of them. We must do something about any who might issue such a command!'","This crate contains several folded maps showing navigable rivers","'My study of this camp has revealed to me some things of interest. The Corsairs support Balakhâd; they believe he has picked up the mantle set down by his father Balakhôr, and they think he will lead them to victory over Gondor and over Ordâkh alike. They are uncertain of Nakási's loyalty, and they hate the Orcs. They believe she is the one forcing them to work alongside the creatures, and they resent her for it. Many hope Balakhâd will break ties with her and seize control of the Song for himself.\
\
'I agree with Rahâzi. If we can kill or capture these leaders, we will have struck a major blow against those who might wield the Song of Waves and Wind against us.'","Rahâzi and Corudan agreed to meet up with you south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar.","Search supply crates within the Haven of Bâkhridar (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Capítulo 17.3: Tras los Pasos de su Padre","Talk to Corudan outside the Haven of Bâkhridar, in Sûg Nidar","Meet with Rahâzi and Corudan south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar","Corudan stands south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar.","'What have you learned of the Heirsworn Corsairs? Are they prepared to sail?'\
\
You tell Rahâzi that the Corsairs spend their time in idleness, but that supply crates within the Haven of Bâkhridar have much of what they would need to set sail on the ships of the Song.\
\
'They will go nowhere until their leaders tell them to depart. If we put an end to Nakási and to Balakhâd, they will be content to remain here. Has not the fleet lingered here, unused, for many years?'","Rahâzi stands south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar.","Talk to Corudan south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar"},
[2989]={"'Welcome to Sûg Nidar, ${PLAYER}. I have taken this campsite from the soldiers who made it. I have named it Fearwater Notch, and it is now mine. Should they return they will not live long enough to inform anyone of our presence here. These others dislike the Ordâkhai as much as we do, and have offered their services to us. For now they have my trust.\
\
'Did my brother tell you that we encountered Cúridwan on the road to this place? She has gone down to the water north-east of here, intending to perform an investigation of some sort. I pressed her not on the subject, but what I understood from her mumblings and musings was that she hoped to find some means of sinking the Song to the bottom of the lake?\
\
'You should see if the Golden Maiden found success. Such a thing would be very helpful to us!'","Your allies have returned to Fearwater Notch","'You have joined us?'","'You should look for Cúridwan by the water's edge to the north-east.'","'The light of hope shines upon Sûg Nidar! It may yet become a watery grave for the Song of Waves and Wind!'","You have found Sigileth's encampment in the Fearwater","Talk to Cúridwan north-east of Fearwater Notch","Sigileth is by the camp-fire at Fearwater Notch, on the island of Kasukhín.","Sigileth stands at Fearwater Notch, awaiting news.","Sigileth and Cúridwan intended to set up camp on the island that holds the ruins of Kasukhín, but the bridge leading there lies beyond Starkhaven.","You should return to Fearwater Notch with news of Cúridwan's investigation.","Find Cúridwan north-east of Fearwater Notch, by the shore of Kasukhín","You have found Cúridwan, standing by a small, sunken row-boat","'Sigileth intended to make camp on the island to the south-east, in the shadow of the ruined keep. A lone bridge stretches to the island, and it will be a long journey to the south-east along the shore to reach it. Take special care as you pass through Starkhaven; that place is surely crawling with both Heirsworn and Ordâkhai.'","Return to Fearwater Notch with news of Cúridwan's potential solution","Talk to Sigileth at Fearwater Notch","Make your way to the island on which stands the ruins of Kasukhín, and find Sigileth","Cúridwan went to perform an investigation north-east of Fearwater Notch, on the shore of Kasukhín.","'Has Cúridwan found what she sought, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You briefly relate what you understand of the Golden Maiden's discovery, and its potential use for sinking the warships before they depart the Fearwater.\
\
'A means of utilizing the blight to destroy the Song of Waves and Wind? Let us hope she is right, for our sake and for that of all Middle-earth! But it is not enough to sink the ships. We must also combat the crews here mustered, and the leaders who drive them to war.'","Cúridwan stands by the water's edge north-east of Fearwater Notch.","Before you can confront the Song of Waves and Wind, you must rejoin Sigileth and Cúridwan.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>","'But we should not get ahead of ourselves: first we must rejoin my sister and Cúridwan. Sigileth intended to make camp on the island that lies to the south-east of here. High atop that rocky place stands the ruin of Kasukhín, and my sister suggested making camp somewhere in its shadow. Cúridwan says the fort once perched atop a hill that was a meeting-place for travellers, but that was before the floods claimed the valley.\
\
'A single bridge stretches to the island, and it will be a long journey to the south-east along the shore to reach it. Find my sister beneath Kasukhín, but take special care as you pass through Starkhaven; that place is surely crawling with Heirsworn and Ordâkhai alike.'","'I see you found your way here. Have you brought the Wizard Inkanûsh with you? He will be most interested to hear what I have learned!'\
\
You tell Cúridwan that, regretfully, Inkanûsh remained behind when you came in search of the Song of Waves and Wind, but you are also interested to hear of her discoveries. Cúridwan motions at the submerged boat.\
\
'After you and Inkanûsh left Sul Madásh, my steps took me to Laivárth, and the Kinta Shadalith spoke to me of her experimentation with the Lâg Dávrit. She told me that you helpfully provided a number of blight samples, ${PLAYER}, but when you added them to water, in time they damaged the integrity of the bucket that held it; the wooden slats of the bucket fell apart, spilling the water onto the ground.\
\
'I have done the same with this row-boat I found moored alongside this island. In a matter of moments, a small sample of the blight has damaged the seals that held together this boat, causing it to take on water and sink. Most curious.\
\
'I am ready to return to Fearwater Notch, if you are. My investigation here is complete, and in it I see a means to destroy the fleet these enemies of the natural order think to wield against the Kintai and the other peoples of Shagâna. Sûg Nidar may yet become a watery grave for the Song of Waves and Wind!'","Capítulo 17.4: A la Sombra de Kasukhín"},
[2990]={"Talk to Cúridwan at Fearwater Notch and complete 'Evil's Uses'","Talk to Corudan at Fearwater Notch and complete 'The Stockpile'","'Together we may yet defeat the schemes of Nakási and Balakhâd, but it will not be easy. Aid each of our companions with the task they choose for themselves, and together we may be able to ensure the Song of Waves and Wind can never leave Sûg Nidar!'","'Aid the companions with their objectives, and we will end the threat of the Song of Waves and Wind.'","Your companions at Fearwater Notch on the island of Kasukhín have several objectives you must achieve if you are to prevent the Song of Waves and Wind from endangering Middle-earth.","Sigileth is at Fearwater Notch on the island of Kasukhín.","'We are almost finished now, ${PLAYER}. Only one thing remains to be done: we must put an end to Nakási and Balakhâd.'","Capítulo 17.5: Silenciar la Canción","Talk to Sigileth at Fearwater Notch","Talk to Rahâzi at Fearwater Notch and complete 'Even A Single Sword'","In order to prevent the Song of Waves and Wind from threatening Middle-earth, you and your companions must achieve several important objectives.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>"},
[2991]={"Talk to Rahâzi on the island of Kasukhín","Talk to Sigileth at Fearwater Notch and go with her to confront the leaders of the Song","'I am ready if you are. They will not long hide from us.'","Capítulo 17.6: En la Cima de la Isla","Rahâzi is atop the island of Kasukhín.","If you and your companions can defeat Nakási and Balakhâd, you will deprive the Song of Waves and Wind of its leaders and its purpose.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>","Sigileth is waiting for your signal to confront Nakási and Balakhâd atop the island of Kasukhín.","'Are you ready to deprive this fleet of its leaders, ${PLAYER}? You have only to give the word and we will search the ruins for Nakási and Balakhâd. They cannot escape the four of us: you, me, my brother, and the Dumûri warrior Rahâzi.\
\
'Meanwhile, Cúridwan will continue to use the blight to damage the seaworthiness of the Song. It will not be long before every vessel lies at the bottom of the lake! We must give her time enough to distribute the blight to every vessel of the fleet.'","'This is bad, ${PLAYER}! Corudan lies bleeding, and Balakhâd and Nakási escape us! They will sail the surviving ships of the Song of Waves and Wind downriver... to war!'"},
[2992]={"Habla con Ningloril en Thangúlhad","Encuentra y recorre el pasaje secreto hacia los cimientos de Dol Guldur","Bori ha recordado la mención de Gandalf, hace mucho tiempo, de un camino secreto hacia los cimientos de Dol Guldur, y cree que si se pudiera encontrar, podría ser utilizado en beneficio de la Hueste Dorada.","Sigileth está en Nothgar, la torre situada dentro del campamento de Thangúlhad.\
\
Bori ha recordado algo que podría ser útil: un camino secreto hacia Dol Guldur utilizado por Gandalf hace mucho tiempo.","'El enano puede estar en lo cierto, ${PLAYER}. También recuerdo las historias de Mithrandir, y aunque la difícil situación de los enanos no era algo que nos preocupara en el pasado, he escuchado el relato del que habla. Más que eso, ¡un amigo nuestro jugó un papel en ello!\
\
'El pobre e infeliz Raddir viajó con Mithrandir en esa antigua búsqueda a las mazmorras del Nigromante. Habló, en una ocasión, de los caminos que recorrieron juntos, y que haya un camino secreto hacia los cimientos de la fortaleza me parece una certeza.\
\
'Debemos encontrarlo, ${PLAYER}. Debe estar en algún lugar de la base del espolón rocoso sobre el que se encuentra Dol Guldur, ya sea en Gathbúrz o en los Pasajes de Ceniza.'","Habla con Sigileth en Nothgar en Thangúlhad","'¡Gandalf debió haber tomado un camino secreto hacia los cimientos de Dol Guldur! Busca la entrada en algún lugar de la base del espolón rocoso sobre el que se encuentra la fortaleza.'","'¡Imagina nuestra ventaja si la Hueste Dorada pudiera infiltrarse en Dol Guldur por este camino secreto! Debes encontrarlo, ${PLAYER}, si existe. La entrada seguramente se encuentra en algún lugar de la base del espolón rocoso sobre el que se encuentra la fortaleza.'","'¡Gandalf debió haber tenido algún camino secreto hacia Dol Guldur por el cual pudo hablar con el padre de Thorin, Thrain, ¿no es así? Si podemos encontrar este camino secreto, podríamos usarlo para infiltrarnos en la fortaleza y recuperar Zigilburk!'","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad.\
\
Has descubierto el camino secreto utilizado por Mithrandir para entrar en Dol Guldur hace mucho tiempo y deberías informar ahora a Ningloril.","'Durante mi encarcelamiento, ${PLAYER}, para pasar el tiempo, me recité a mí mismo las historias que Bróin y yo escuchábamos durante nuestra infancia: principalmente relatos de Khazad-dûm y de la Búsqueda del Dragón en la que se aventuraron nuestros abuelos.\
\
'A lo largo de las largas horas de mi cautiverio, llegué a recordar detalles de esas historias que había olvidado hace mucho tiempo. Recordé cómo Gandalf llevó a Thorin Escudo de Roble la llave y el mapa que le dio el padre de Thorin, Thrain... quien entonces era prisionero en las mazmorras del Nigromante, en las mazmorras de Dol Guldur.\
\
'¿Cómo llegó Gandalf a esas mazmorras? ¡Pues, ${PLAYER}, debió haber encontrado un camino secreto!'","Capítulo 17: Recuerdos de Mithrandir","'¡Lo has logrado, ${PLAYER}! ¡Este camino secreto hacia los cimientos de Dol Guldur es justo lo que la Hueste Dorada necesita para tomar la fortaleza por sorpresa!\
\
'Tanto Raddir como Mithrandir nos han ayudado, incluso en la muerte.'","El misterioso camino secreto hacia los cimientos de Dol Guldur que Gandalf debió haber utilizado se encuentra seguramente en algún lugar del espolón rocoso sobre el que se encuentra la fortaleza."},
[2993]={"Talk to King Elessar in the graveyard and learn how he was wounded","You have encountered Tatháta by the docks. She may have seen Aphadaer","Pursue Aphadaer to the northern docks of the burning Harlond","Aphadaer will seek to join Balakhâd by the Heirsworn ship moored at the docks!","Tatháta is by the northern docks of the burning Harlond, near the flagship of the Song.","'What treacherous snake has dared harm the King?'","Talk to Tatháta by the northern docks of the burning Harlond","'What treacherous snake has dared harm the King? If this worm thinks to join his master, he will make for the Heirsworn ship moored at the docks!'","'We must end this. Now.'\
\
You ask Tatháta if she has seen Aphadaer, the man you pursued to the docks.\
\
'He is just ahead,' she responds. 'But he is no one. We must put an end to his masters.'","The King has been wounded!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>","'We must end this. Now.'","King Elessar lies in the graveyard, wounded. What happened while you were away?","Aphadaer ran for the docks, intending to join Balakhâd and be rewarded for the death of King Elessar.","Chapter 18.10: A Knife in the Smoke","'My King! My King! Who has done this to you?'","King Elessar grimaces with pain, and blood trickles from beneath his chestplate.\
\
'${PLAYER}, my friend... heed my words...\
\
'It was Aphadaer... my groom of horses...\
\
'He stood close by... and whispered in my ear. \\qFor the Heirs of Castamir!\\q hissed he, and his knife found a gap... in the plates of my armour.\
\
'He must have been... the traitor we suspected...'\
\
Elessar laughs quietly, but the action causes him pain.\
\
'I thought such a one... would be higher in my counsels...'"},
[2996]={"'Do not make the King wait! He wants to speak to you and hear that the battle is ended!'","Talk to Ioreth in the Harlond infirmary","'Speak to Jajax and return with him to Umbar. I must know the state of that city, and the position of its ruling Kindred.'","Queen Arwen and the healer Ioreth arrive at the King's bedside","The threat posed by the Song of Waves and Wind has been met, and now those wounded during the attack must work to recover their wounds and rebuild their homes.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>","Jajax is in the Harlond infirmary.","The King smiles at you, and you are reassured to see the return of his strength.\
\
'My friend, I am glad to see you survived the battle! The reports I have heard tell me the threat of the Song is ended.'\
\
You tell King Elessar that Aphadaer has paid for his treachery, and both Nakási and Balakhâd perished during the fighting. He nods.\
\
'Would that we could have dissuaded them from this course, but alas! Only rarely is that possible. I confess to you it never occurred to me that Aphadaer could have been the supporter of the Heirs of Castamir whose presence we suspected in Minas Tirith. The gaze of my suspicion turned always to those who wielded greater power than my groom of horses! And yet the Heirsworn prized his reports, believing he was always only moments away from wielding the blade that would end my life. Surely there were opportunities to be had before today, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'This I believe, for it seems to fit every fact. While the Harlond burned, Aphadaer stood near enough to me to whisper his battle-cry in my ear. \\qFor the Heirs of Castamir!\\q he said as he slipped his knife beneath my armour, and I all unsuspecting. How then did his blade not pierce a vital organ? How could he inflict this wound with such murderous intent and yet not spill the last of my life's blood?\
\
'I think our tour of King's Gondor planted a seed, ${PLAYER}. When he travelled with us to Anfalas and to Pinnath Gelin, he did so intending to serve the interests of the Heirs of Castamir, but I think our journey caused a sapling to grow within his heart. When today he saw the opportunity to carry out his intention, I believe he was unable to fully wield the blade that could end my life, and his aim went astray, despite his purpose.\
\
'None can say if this be truly so, but that is my belief. I weep not for Aphadaer, but I hail him for my life, even as he sought the taking of it.'","Talk to Jajax in the Harlond infirmary","Queen Arwen smiles at you and turns her attention to her injured husband.","Queen Arwen and Ioreth the Healer have come to the Harlond infirmary.","You can tell the King will not long remain abed. Already he desires to get up and move around, despite the instructions of his healers! You advise that he lay still and not aggravate his injury, and he shakes his head with amusement.\
\
'The battle has ended, but there is something I need you to do, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Nakási's attack on Gondor must reshape the Kindred of the Coins, for it is my understanding that some of that body supported her in this and others did not. Belondor died in our defence, but Rothog and Tatháta also fought on our behalf, and they survived. What befell those who remained behind in Umbar?\
\
'I ask that you speak to Jajax here in the infirmary and prepare to return with him to his city, ${PLAYER}. We must learn what we can of the situation in Umbar now that the threat posed by the Song of Waves and Wind has been eliminated.'","Arwen smiles at you warmly.\
\
'I am once again in your debt, dear ${PLAYER}! My husband is ever eager to charge near and far in support of his people. Perhaps this bed will keep him from embarking upon foolish errands for a time!\
\
'A short time only, I suspect. I am told his wound is shallow, and it would take one of more severity to keep him from tending to the needs of his people! But today he will rest, and for that I am grateful.'","Ioreth sputters madly, for once at a loss for words.\
\
'The Queen asked me to attend her as she came to the Harlond. Is it true that Aphadaer thought to attack the King? Oh me! Oh my!'\
\
You tell Ioreth that the groom attempted to kill the King, but was unsuccessful in the attempt and perished defending Balakhâd, son of Balakhôr. She nods sagely, overcoming her surprise.\
\
'I always suspected he was a villain, ${PLAYER}. Did I not tell you as we journeyed in Outer Gondor that he was up to no good? Let none say Ioreth fails to see things as they are!'","Ioreth sputters to herself with disbelief.","'He has asked to see you. Disturb him not overlong! But I would not dare to keep you from him, lest I risk either your ire or that of the King!'","Chapter 18.13: The Peace Restored","Talk to King Elessar in the Harlond infirmary","<rgb=#00FF00>When you complete this quest, you will sail back to Umbar with Jajax to carry out King Elessar's wishes.</rgb>\
\
'Yes, I understand. When we sailed from Umbar Baharbêl, the city was in turmoil, and my brother was somehow in the middle of it! Let us return to the Sail-haven and learn what happened while we were gone. I will speak with you not far from the Beacon-gate when we have arrived. I have many questions.\
\
'Does the Kindred rule still? Might there be a reward for those of us who fought to protect both Gondor and Umbar from the ravages of the Song? King Elessar is not the only one who wants answers, ${PLAYER}! Let us go at once!'","Talk to Queen Arwen in the Harlond infirmary","'I mourn the loss of so much life, but I am grateful for such heroes as you, my friend. Without your aid the cost of this day would have been much worse.'","King Elessar recovers from his wound in the Harlond infirmary."},
[2998]={"Talk to Tasâdi the Rumourmonger","Talk to Daxamat by the pool","'You must hurry on to Umbar! Bring your warning to the guards at the gate, and I will follow behind you!'","The guardsman would not listen. You should hurry to the Waterway Market and <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> for the folk by the pool to heed you.","Ride west to Umbar Baharbêl and give your warning to the guardsmen at the White Gate","'What is this I hear, ${PLAYER}? Tell me what I can do!'\
\
You ask Daxamat to spread the word to the people of the city that a fleet of dangerous ships carrying Orcs and Ordâkhai soldiers approaches from Ikorbân.\
\
'I will! You should find my brother Jajax at the forum of Bith Gabâr... he will know what to do!'","Chapter 18.2: The River Gate","'I will arrange for the defence of the city!'","'How foolish! How absurd!'","'It is not much, Dax, but you can stay here as long as you need. I have lived here ever since Kinsman Belondor ordered my release from the gaol following his return from Ikorbân. Many of my fellows were freed as well. I know not what Belondor saw there, but I am grateful for it!\
\
'You can stay here until you learn what happened to your brother. There has really been no word of him since he and ${PLAYER} went to Dâr Laja?'","Daxamat hurries off to warn the folk of the city about the approaching threat.","Jajax stands at the forum of Bith Gabâr in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Mother Phúrsi","The folk near the Waterway Market must be warned of the approaching danger!","'I know you for a friend of the city, ${PLAYER}. If you say a hostile fleet approaches Umbar Baharbêl, then it must be so.\
\
'We must arrange for the defence of the city! We must get everyone away from the river!'","Daxamat and the others run off to warn the folk of the city!","'What did you say? A secret fleet sails toward the city? And I was not informed?'\
\
You tell Jajax that Nakási Wave-reaper and Balakhâd have taken control of the Song of Waves and Wind and equipped its ships with dangerous Narghâk weapons. If it is not kept from leaving the Ikorbân River, all of Middle-earth will be in danger.\
\
'You need the Kindred of the Coins to close the river gate? You will want my help with this, ${PLAYER}. Let me know when you are ready for us to speak with them.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Beckon</rgb> the people nearby to heed you","The people of Umbar Baharbêl must be warned about the danger that approaches them from the east!","According to his brother, you will find Jajax at the forum of Bith Gabâr.","Find Jajax at the forum of Bith Gabâr and warn him of the danger","'You must hurry on to Umbar, ${PLAYER}! Bring your warning to the guards at the gate, and I will follow behind you!'","Will they heed you?","Talk to Guardsman Phârex by the fountain","You can waste no time. Warn the folk at the Waterway Market!","Talk to Itûr within the refuge he has offered you","At last some of the folk give you their attention","'A fleet of ships manned by the Heirsworn approaches from the River Ikorbân? How can this be?'","A familiar voice calls to you as Daxamat pushes through the crowd","Phârex stands at attention, worried by the tidings you have brought to his city.","'A hostile fleet sails toward us down the River Ikorbân? That is absurd! What proof have you of this?'","'A hostile fleet approaches from the river? Can this be so?\
\
'I will share these tidings throughout the city!'","<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>\
\
Itûr has given you a place to shelter until you can learn what happened to your brother and your friend within Dâr Laja.","Talk to Ushrin the Purchaser","Daxamat stands by the fountain, a worried expression upon his face.","'The Kindred of the Coins will listen to me, you will see. No one can refuse Jajax!'","You must hurry to the eastern gate of Umbar Baharbêl and warn the guardsmen there of the approaching danger.","'Are we... are we in danger?'","Talk to Jajax and go with him to warn the Kindred of the Coins about the approaching danger","Pass through the gate and hurry to the court by the nearby pool"},
[2999]={"Two residents of the city have come to the refuge. But why?","Talk to Itûr in the left storage room","Talk to Khâsha in the entrance to the refuge","Talk to Phêlex in the entrance to the refuge","'You can leave your belongings in the storage room. Go through the door behind me into the hall; the storage room is the door on the left.'","Until he can learn what happened to his brother and his adventuring friend, it is up to Daxamat to make sense of things!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>","Chapter 18.3: Daxamat Takes The Lead","'I may be able to contact someone who can get a message to the prisoners. I will return and let you know.'","'You need a way to pass unseen from this refuge without being seen by spies loyal to the Kindred of the Coins? I would not call this day fortunate... but perhaps in this matter alone I have some good fortune to share.\
\
'Pass through the door behind me and take the stairs down to the cellar. You will see what I mean.'","Explore the cellar beyond the southern hallway of the refuge","You have never met this Temámir before. Why does he ask for you?","Birûk nods pleasantly at the boat in the water.","Itûr told you about a useful feature of the refuge: a cellar beneath a trapdoor at the far end of the south hall.","You hear Itûr's footstep behind you as he enters the storage room","'Ah, I see what your friend has in mind. I know a waterway to Umbar-môkh when I see one. With this I can enter and leave the refuge without detection by spies loyal to Hármelak.'\
\
Birûk shakes his fists in the air.\
\
'I still cannot believe Khôltekh would endanger the city in this way! I have never known  to lie, and ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} was most clear that a hostile fleet sails down the river toward us!\
\
'I may be able to contact someone who can get a message to the prisoners. I will return and let you know if I succeed.'","Talk to Itûr by the entrance to the refuge","'You are Daxamat, the brother of Jajax? I have been looking for you! I have tidings of him you should hear. I spoke to many people hoping to find you, but at last a rumour-monger directed me to this place. Now hear what I have seen!\
\
'I was in Dâr Laja when your brother and my friend  petitioned the Kindred of the Coins to close shut the river gate and prevent the approaching fleet from passing the city. Almost did I leave, but curiosity stayed my feet, and I watched from afar as they were seized by the guards! They were brought to the gaol, and are now captives of Hármelak... even Khôltekh has sided with her! I can think of no just reason for him to do this!\
\
'I fear the Kindred of the Coins has betrayed the city. Even now I hesitate to return to the streets; they may keep watch for any who witnessed their duplicity!  proved a friend to many of us in the city... how can they justify imprisoning ${PLAYER:her[f]|him} after such monumental deeds on behalf of Umbari and Temámir alike?'","A Temámir dwarf has come in search of you. But why?","'Word spreads through the city that a hostile fleet approaches on the Ikorbân River, and that  has been imprisoned for trying to stop it. Can this be true?\
\
'My wife Khâsha and I name  a friend. Any who seek to harm ${PLAYER:her[f]|him} must answer to us! My deadliest days are behind me, but I have mates enough throughout the Shield Isles and the Cape to make things difficult for the Kindred of the Coins if they truly have betrayed the city, as the whispering suggests.\
\
'If the word of the advance scouts can be trusted, it seems likely: they say you can hear Orkish voices from at least one of the approaching ships.'","You hear the sound of a door closing in the distance, and voices drift from above","'Pass through the door behind me and take the stairs down to the cellar. You will see what I mean.'","'There is someone here for you, Dax... a Temámir dwarf I have never seen before.\
\
'If he is not a friend of yours, I will send him away. If it is true that an enemy fleet approaches the city, we should not draw attention to this place.'","Itûr stands in the entrance to the refuge, awaiting your answer.","A small boat bobs in the water beside the platform","Itûr told you a Temámir dwarf has come to the refuge asking for you.","What would they do if they were here?","'I fear the Kindred of the Coins has betrayed the city. Even now I hesitate to return to the streets; they may keep watch for any who witnessed their betrayal!'","'If this Temámir is not a friend of yours, I will send him away.'","'Rumours spread like wildfire throughout the Lower Ward. Is it true that  has been imprisoned by the Kindred of the Coins? I can think of no reason for ${PLAYER:her[f]|him} to languish in the gaol, especially if ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} sought to warn us about this approaching danger! Why would the Kindred support this attack?\
\
'My husband owes a great deal to Tumúldo Fierce-water, who convinced him not to join Balakhôr during the war... but that was a different Kindred, and people say Tumúldo is slain.\
\
'People also say you and your brother are 's close companions, Daxamat. Tell us what we must do to help, and we will do it!'","Return to the entrance of the refuge to speak with the new Temámir arrival","Leave your belongings in a corner of the left storage room","Itûr clears his throat, surprising you. He has a knack for moving unseen!","'The people turn to you for guidance, Dax!'\
\
You stammer to Itûr that you don't know what to do. He rests an assuring hand on your shoulder.\
\
'Ask yourself what ${PLAYER} and Jajax would do, if they were here.'","Itûr has returned to the entrance of the refuge, and has some information for you and the Temámir Birûk.","Have more people come to the refuge? You should return to the entrance and learn who has arrived and for what purpose.","Itûr stands in the entrance to the refuge, assessing the new arrivals.","'Yes! That is exactly right, Dax!\
\
'Today we begin to fight against those who would betray us! For ${PLAYER}, and for Jajax!'","Itûr has followed you into the left storage room. He has a worried expression on his face.","Return to the entrance of the refuge and learn the identity of the new arrivals","What would they do in this situation, if they were here?","They would fight. They would fight!","Itûr offered you a place in the left storage room of the Refuge. He said to open the southern door and then the storage room would be on the left side of the hall.","More new arrivals: a man and a woman you have not met before","Talk to Birûk, the newly-arrived Temámir dwarf","Talk to Itûr in the entrance to the refuge","Talk to Birûk in the cellar of the refuge"},
}
